nextest|Test|ovrcr-protocol|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Atheme_appearance_metadata_groups_every_existing_theme|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-protocol,lib,unit,settings::tests::theme_appearance_metadata_groups_every_existing_theme,default,crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/settings.rs,1974,1992,"[""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/settings.rs:1088-1171""]","Six dark and two light themes assert their ThemeAppearance, and the two lists total eight.","A theme reporting the wrong appearance, so the Dashboard groups it under the wrong picker section.",1,2,0,3,25,35,31,crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/settings.rs:1088-1171 is appearance metadata; a wrong grouping is cosmetic.,Only eight of eighty themes are checked and no negative exists.,"Row 14 asserts appearance for every theme against the shipped manifest, including all eight here, so there is no extra boundary.",Production appearance() for the checked themes.,high,consolidate,"Fully subsumed by row 14 (theme_catalog_matches_the_exact_approved_manifest), which iterates all 80 themes and compares appearance against the manifest; retain that test rather than this eight-theme subset.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-protocol|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Atheme_catalog_matches_the_exact_approved_manifest|default""]",two short lists,0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2320 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,protocol-terminal-002,independent-protocol-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|fixture%20result%20receipt%20appears%20only%20after%20its%20complete%20JSON%20is%20written|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,fixture result receipt appears only after its complete JSON is written,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,13,56,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A preloaded fs.writeFileSync interposer observes the fixture's receipt write at its open-for-write boundary: the receipt path does not exist at that moment, the write then completes, and the receipt parses as {details:{published:true}}.","If the fixture's toolOutput wrote the receipt in place instead of temp+rename, a Rust parent polling for the file could read a truncated body and fail or misparse; if it renamed before writing, the receipt would become visible empty.",1,3,1,0,25,40,34,"The subject is the test fixture's receipt writer; a regression makes other suites read partial results and fail confusingly, i.e. a maintenance consequence with no product path (tests/fixtures/pi/pi_host.mjs:177-180).","It observes the real write boundary via a preload rather than inferring it, and asserts both non-visibility at open time and the final parsed content (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:13-56).","No other test asserts the atomicity of the fixture's receipt publication; the delegation suites depend on it implicitly but never check the window; the handler it drives is tests/fixtures/pi/pi_host.mjs:177-180, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The subject is a stand-in: the fixture's own writer is instrumented with a mock fs module and a stubbed extension, so no production behaviour is exercised (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:20-36).",high,keep,"Fixture-qualification coverage: F=0 and C=1 fail the improve gate and usefulness 35 exceeds the prune floor of 25, so the rubric leaves it as grounded infrastructure coverage rather than a prune candidate.",[],0.046s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.046,0.046,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 45.988459 at macOS-job.log:4191; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_workflow_tracker.mjs|the%20bounded%20tracker%20stub%20exposes%20duplicate%20attempts%20and%20refuses%20parent%20modification|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs,node,unit,the bounded tracker stub exposes duplicate attempts and refuses parent modification,default,tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs,33,41,"[""tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs:1-40""]","A repeated identical issue create succeeds then fails with status 1, issue close of the parent and a graphql api call both fail, and the ledger shows two issues with two create attempts while the parent record is unchanged.","If the stub accepted a duplicate create or let the parent be modified, the reconciliation suites could not distinguish an idempotent publisher from a broken one, and a test could silently mutate its own parent fixture.",1,3,1,0,25,40,34,"Again the subject is the fixture: its value is that other suites can rely on duplicate refusal and an immutable parent (tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs:24-28, 42-44).","It asserts the success/failure sequence, the refusal of close and graphql, and the ledger's issue and attempt counts (tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs:33-41).","The lost-reply row covers the other stub behaviour; this row covers duplicate refusal and parent immutability, which the stub's callers depend on; the handler it drives is tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs:20-44, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Stand-in subject: the assertions read the fixture's ledger after driving the fixture CLI (tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs:14-32).,high,keep,Fixture qualification; retained for the same rubric reason as the sibling row.,[],0.135s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.135,0.135,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 134.854333 at macOS-job.log:4335; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,independent-extensions-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adesktop_confirmed_without_unread_does_not_queue|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::desktop::tests::desktop_confirmed_without_unread_does_not_queue,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs,2083,2097,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-688"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/ready.rs:43-52""]",A ResponseReady activity sample with quality Confirmed and unread None queues no alert.,"The body cannot distinguish Confirmed quality from any other quality because unread is None, so the claimed defect (Confirmed treated as Ready) would still pass; only the missing-unread rule is exercised.",2,1,0,3,50,25,35,"If Confirmed were wrongly delivered the consequence is one misleading alert (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-688, crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/ready.rs:43-52).","The fixture sets unread=None, which alone blocks the queue at crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:642-660, so the asserted length cannot detect the named Confirmed-quality defect.","Fully subsumed by desktop_does_not_queue_when_unread_is_absent:2072-2081, whose fixture differs only by the unused quality field. Counterpart: nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adesktop_does_not_queue_when_unread_is_absent|default.","Runs the production observer, but the claim about quality is never reached. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-688.",high,consolidate,"Retained protection: nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adesktop_does_not_queue_when_unread_is_absent|default uses the same snapshot(2,""a"",ResponseReady) input with unread None and asserts the same empty queue at crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:2073-2080; crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/unread.rs:23-26 returns false before any quality is consulted, which proves the Confirmed claim is never exercised. C=2, so no high-criticality invariant depends on a separate row.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adesktop_does_not_queue_when_unread_is_absent|default""]",[],0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2961 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-001,independent-tui-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|startup_offers_are_recognised_only_while_waiting_for_their_answer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,startup_offers_are_recognised_only_while_waiting_for_their_answer,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,963,982,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:928-960"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:908-925""]","waiting_startup_decision returns the offer title only when the screen shows an 'OVRCR · startup' prompt whose last line is one of the known answer forms, returns None when the offer is answered or not yet drawn, and errors on an unknown title so the harness never answers an offer it does not recognise.","A laxer parser that matched the answer line without the known title set would let the GUI tests auto-decline a new offer such as 'Restart OVRCR server - all running sessions will stop', silently changing the state under test; a stricter one would never decline and the GUI tests would time out.",1,3,1,1,25,45,37,"The subject is test-harness code, so a regression can only mislead or stall the GUI suites; no product path changes, which is a maintenance consequence (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:928-960).","Four cases cover both branches: two recognised offers, an answered and an undrawn screen returning None, and an unknown title returning an error (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:963-982); the alternate-screen early return in decline_test_startup_prompt (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:909-916) and the send path are untested.",The product-side offer vocabulary is covered by tests/client_startup.rs and the GUI acceptance tests at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:693-906 fail if this helper stops recognising offers; only the strictness assertion (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:944-956) is extra here.,The subject (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:928-960) is a #[cfg(test)]-only helper fed three hand-written screen strings at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:963-982; no live vt100 screen is read and the sending half of the harness (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:908-925) is not exercised.,high,keep,"It guards the harness that the two GUI acceptance tests depend on; the pragmatic call is keep rather than improve, because the product behaviour it mirrors is covered by the client_startup suite and the harness fails loudly (timeout) if recognition breaks.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclient_startup|dashboard_startup_offers_missing_hooks_and_decline_preserves_profiles|default""]",0.025s one hosted attempt; pure string parsing of three literal screens,0.025,0.025,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2223 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|terminal_fonts_render_mockup_glyphs_or_default_symbols|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,terminal_fonts_render_mockup_glyphs_or_default_symbols,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,158,186,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:98-156"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:34-57"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:59-96""]","install_terminal_fonts loads Apple Symbols and the JetBrains Nerd Font styles from the home font directory into egui, and the test asks the font atlas whether each of the four TerminalFonts FontIds covers the dashboard's status glyphs - the nerd set when the nerd family was installed, otherwise a single braille spinner.","A font wiring regression that pointed bold, italic or bold-italic at a family without the dashboard status glyphs (or that dropped the symbols fallback) would render the spinner, check and arrow glyphs as replacement boxes in the GUI terminal.",1,1,2,3,25,45,37,"The failure is limited to the appearance of status indicator glyphs in the GUI; no state, routing or ownership depends on them, so the consequence is cosmetic (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:49-57).","The accepted symbol set changes with the developer's ~/Library/Fonts: without the nerd font install_terminal_fonts returns current_monospace where all four FontIds are the same monospace id (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:34-48, 108-110), so the style mapping is unasserted and only one braille glyph is checked; it also relies on Fonts::has_glyphs, the API paint_terminal explicitly distrusts (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1052-1060).","No other test exercises install_terminal_fonts' family selection (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:98-156): the paint tests at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:196-260 and src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:388-427 cover glyph output, never which family each style is bound to.","The production install path (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:98-156) and a real egui Context are used, but the assertion stops at atlas coverage (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:158-186) rather than painting a cell, so the claim 'renders the glyphs' is only partially exercised.",medium,improve,"S=1: on a machine without the nerd fonts the test degenerates to one braille glyph and the style mapping is vacuous, while the behaviour it claims still needs protection - assert per-style family identity from a fixture font directory and paint one status cell instead of querying has_glyphs.",[],0.046s one hosted attempt; reads the developer's ~/Library/Fonts and builds a real egui font atlas,0.046,0.046,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2224 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acli|dashboard_selection_frames_skip_only_quota_telemetry|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::cli,integration,integration,dashboard_selection_frames_skip_only_quota_telemetry,default,tests/cli.rs,1425,1492,"[""tests/cli.rs:1409-1422"", ""tests/cli.rs:1302-1407""]","Feeds a socket pair with four expected production messages, interleaving QuotaChanged events (and a recorded Quota event after index 2) before each, and asserts the local next_skipping_quota helper returns exactly the four expected messages.","The test-local frame filter skipping a non-quota message (for example SettingsChanged) or failing to skip quota telemetry, which would make every dashboard-based CLI test flaky or wrong.",1,2,2,1,25,45,37,The subject is a test helper; a defect weakens other tests but has no product or data consequence.,"The exact sequence is compared, and the interleaved quota frames exercise both the skip and the pass-through branches.","Only exercises next_skipping_quota; the sibling row covers non-quota events but through the same helper, so the distinction is which frames are fed.",The filter is test-local plumbing; no production component is driven.,high,improve,"F=1 plumbing test: add an assertion against a real server attach that a non-quota Recorded event and SettingsChanged are delivered in order, instead of relying solely on the local filter.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acli|quota_filter_preserves_other_events_and_responses|default""]","[""UnixStream pair"", ""synthetic frames only""]",0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:792 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-002,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acli|quota_filter_preserves_other_events_and_responses|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::cli,integration,integration,quota_filter_preserves_other_events_and_responses,default,tests/cli.rs,1495,1543,"[""tests/cli.rs:1409-1422""]","Writes six non-quota messages (Titles and Settings recorded events, ScreenDirty, Output, HierarchyChanged, a Response) through a socket pair and asserts next_skipping_quota returns each unchanged and in order.","The test-local filter dropping or reordering any non-quota event, which would hide a real production frame-ordering regression from the Dashboard tests.",1,2,2,1,25,45,37,Test-helper behavior only; the product path is not exercised.,"Each variant is asserted individually and in order, so a broad skip predicate fails; the assertion set is otherwise small.",Same helper and same defect class as the sibling row; this row adds the non-quota event variants.,Local helper over a socket pair; no product code runs.,high,improve,F=1 plumbing test: drive the real Dashboard attach path and assert these event kinds survive in the client's frame order rather than only through the private filter.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acli|dashboard_selection_frames_skip_only_quota_telemetry|default""]","[""UnixStream pair"", ""synthetic frames only""]",0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:805 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-002,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|palette%3A%3Apaste_into_repository_field_refreshes_the_listing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,integration,palette::paste_into_repository_field_refreshes_the_listing,default,tests/tui/palette.rs,1984,1995,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1743-1963"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:3105-3425""]",Pasting a directory path ending in a slash lists its child child.,The listing not refreshing after paste.,1,2,1,3,25,45,37,Only the completion listing is incidental.,One substring for the refreshed child.,Paste refresh is a small distinction already exercised by the Tab listing tests.,Real filesystem listing through the path picker.,high,keep,Keep: One substring for the refreshed child. Paste refresh is a small distinction already exercised by the Tab listing tests.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|palette%3A%3Atab_on_a_leaf_path_advances_to_the_next_field|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|palette%3A%3Atabbing_to_workspace_root_refreshes_its_derived_listing|default""]","[""tempdir""]",0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1927 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-003,independent-dashboard-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|mouse%3A%3Aterminal_mode_keeps_dashboard_mouse_capture_without_a_ready_session|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,mouse::terminal_mode_keeps_dashboard_mouse_capture_without_a_ready_session,default,tests/tui/mouse.rs,434,451,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:2952-3040"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:3261-3360""]","A dashboard with no session and no acknowledged screen receives a click at 50,10 and must not emit PtyBytes(Vec::new()).",A click with no focused/ready session being encoded as empty or partial PTY bytes instead of staying in dashboard capture.,2,1,1,2,50,30,38,Losing mouse capture is a bounded UI misrouting.,"Only assert_ne against PtyBytes(Vec::new()) passes for almost any action, including non-empty PtyBytes or Detach, so most wrong outcomes escape.",No distinct input beyond the capture tests; the named Terminal-mode boundary is not constructed.,"The fixture never enters Terminal mode (it has no session), so the claimed state is replaced by a Browse-mode click on an empty dashboard.",high,improve,Strengthen to assert Redraw/None and mouse_capture_required with a real unready session in Terminal mode; the current inequality accepts non-empty PTY bytes and Detach.,[],[],0.031,0.031,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1845 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adefault_session_label_tests%3A%3Adirect_agent_executable_matches_kind_when_label_omitted|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,server::default_session_label_tests::direct_agent_executable_matches_kind_when_label_omitted,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs,3251,3262,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:3174-3180""]","For an Agent codex session with argv ['codex'], an omitted label resolves to 'codex'.",Only a completely empty or unrelated label value; both plausible producers (kind name and argv basename) yield 'codex' for this input.,2,1,0,4,50,30,38,Same bounded mislabelling consequence as the other label fixtures (2).,"crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:3251-3262 asserts a string that equals the result under either the kind or the argv implementation, so it cannot reject the defect the sibling fixtures exist for.","The input cannot distinguish the branches, and the Agent branch is already protected by the pi and claude fixtures (0).","Direct production function call, which is why the pure-algorithm allowance applies.",high,consolidate,"No independent expectation: merging it into the Agent-kind representative loses nothing, and the existing pi and claude fixtures already guard the same invariant.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adefault_session_label_tests%3A%3Amanaged_pi_launcher_uses_agent_kind_not_ovrcr_argv0|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adefault_session_label_tests%3A%3Amanaged_claude_launcher_uses_agent_kind_not_ovrcr_argv0|default""]",pure string formatting,0.010,0.010,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2507 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-server-session-001,independent-runtime-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|empty_dashboard_response_preserves_complete_frame_after_peer_close|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,unit,empty_dashboard_response_preserves_complete_frame_after_peer_close,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,6178,6190,"[""tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6135-6177""]",A UnixStream pair receives one complete protocol frame and then its peer closes; the test-side dashboard response reader returns exactly that frame rather than an error.,"The reader helper could reject a fully received frame when the peer closes immediately afterwards, failing unrelated dashboard tests.",1,3,1,2,25,50,40,"Only harness correctness: no product state is protected, but false failures cost maintenance (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6135-6177).","Exact frame equality for the complete-frame case, though the helper itself is the subject (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6150-6160).",One of three helper cases; the partial-frame and open-peer cases are separate rows (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6178-6224).,"Real socket pair with the real protocol codec, but the asserted component is a test helper, not the dashboard path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6135-6145).",high,keep,Grounded helper coverage; no retention or pruning gate applies.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|empty_dashboard_response_rejects_closed_peer_without_a_complete_frame|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|empty_dashboard_response_keeps_open_peer_reads_bounded|default""]","[""UnixStream::pair"", ""real frame codec""]",0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1528 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_workflow_tracker.mjs|lost%20create%20reply%20is%20attributable%20through%20ordinary%20issue%20list%20without%20a%20duplicate%20publication|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs,node,unit,lost create reply is attributable through ordinary issue list without a duplicate publication,default,tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs,21,31,"[""tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs:1-40""]","With the stub's lose-once mode, an issue create exits 124, an ordinary issue list finds exactly one issue whose title and body match the approved ticket, its url is the created number and blockedBy contains the parent, the ledger shows one create attempt and the parent issue unchanged.","If the fixture did not drop the reply exactly once, or if a retry could publish a second issue, the reconciliation test it supports would prove nothing about attributable publication; the blockedBy assertion also relies on the stub returning fields the real gh list --json projection would omit.",1,3,2,0,25,50,40,"The subject is the command-boundary fixture, so a regression misleads the suites that rely on the lost-reply scenario; no product path is exercised (tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs:1-2, 20-40).","It asserts the timeout status, exactly one matching issue, the url, blockedBy and the ledger attempt count (tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs:21-31); the blockedBy check is not faithful to gh's field projection because the stub returns the whole issue object for any --json list.","The sibling row exercises the same stub's duplicate refusal and parent immutability; together they qualify the stub, and no other suite asserts its projection behaviour.","The subject is a stand-in: the test drives tests/fixtures/pi/workflow-gh.mjs, an explicit 'command-boundary fixture only' that never contacts GitHub, so production tracker behaviour is out of scope (tests/pi_workflow_tracker.mjs:12-13).",high,keep,"Fixture qualification only: F=0 and C=1 fail the improve gate, and usefulness 50 exceeds the prune floor of 25, so the rubric keeps it as grounded infrastructure coverage.","[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_workflow_tracker.mjs|the%20bounded%20tracker%20stub%20exposes%20duplicate%20attempts%20and%20refuses%20parent%20modification|default""]",0.062s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.062,0.062,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 62.080125 at macOS-job.log:4329; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,independent-extensions-check-1
