nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atask_tui|unicode_prompt_render_is_safe_while_another_field_has_focus|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::task_tui,integration,unit,unicode_prompt_render_is_safe_while_another_field_has_focus,default,tests/task_tui.rs,623,630,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/task_tui.rs:430-560"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/task_tui.rs:1225-1490""]",Opening the editor on a task whose prompt contains CJK text while the Name field is focused draws without panicking.,A panic or a misaligned render when a unicode prompt is stored but not the focused field.,2,1,2,3,50,45,47,A panic in the task editor would take down the dashboard while it is being used (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/task_tui.rs:1225-1490).,"The body only calls draw_tasks once: it asserts no panic and nothing about the rendered text, cursor or field layout (tests/task_tui.rs:623-630).","Adjacent render tests assert field labels and narrow footers; this one adds no assertion beyond not panicking (tests/task_tui.rs:258-289,763-802).","Real renderer with a real TasksView, but the claimed behavior is only smoke-checked (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/task_tui.rs:1225-1490).",high,improve,"Name promises a safe unicode prompt render while another field has focus, but the body only draws once and asserts nothing; add an assertion that the stored prompt text ('界 hello') is rendered intact in the Prompt field and that the focused Name field's cursor/text stays correct, on the draw path at crates/ovrcr-tui/src/task_tui.rs:1225-1490.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atask_tui|multiline_cursor_edits_unicode_without_corruption|default""]",One 80x24 render,0.016,0.016,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1687 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-007,independent-integration-final-check-1
