nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aloopback_requests_bypass_the_login_gate|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::loopback_requests_bypass_the_login_gate,default,src/remote/mod.rs,775,779,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:144-166"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:703-710""]","authorized() accepts a request whose Host is 127.0.0.1:<port> or localhost:<port> even when a tailnet login is configured, without requiring a tailscale-user-login header.","A gate that demanded the login header for loopback Hosts would 403 the local browser and the settings path that probes http://127.0.0.1:<port>/api/state, making the remote dashboard unreachable from the machine that runs it.",2,2,1,3,50,45,47,Wrongly demanding a login breaks local access to one optional surface with a workaround (send the tailnet header or use the desktop UI); it does not itself expose session state (src/remote/mod.rs:144-166).,"Two positive spellings are asserted and nothing else: an over-permissive host parse such as host.contains(""localhost"") would still pass this test and both negative gate tests, because their hosts ('node.example.ts.net') contain neither token (src/remote/mod.rs:775-779).","tests/remote_web.rs:30-41 drives real loopback requests through the same gate and asserts 200, so the allow direction is already exercised end to end; only the 'localhost' spelling and the no-header case are extra.","Gateway::authorized is the production decision function, but it is fed a hand-built http::Request with already-lowercase header names, so the parser's name normalisation is bypassed (src/remote/mod.rs:761-773).",high,keep,"Cheap and still the clearest statement of the loopback branch, but its evidence is largely duplicated by the acceptance GETs; a later consolidation could fold it into the gate tests.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aremote_web|remote_gateway_follows_the_settings_toggle|default""]","0.018s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:566 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|terminal_paints_reserved_icon_cell_before_foreground_glyph|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,terminal_paints_reserved_icon_cell_before_foreground_glyph,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,388,427,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1017-1041"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1051-1092""]","paint_terminal fills the whole terminal and both cells of a wide private-use icon glyph in its background pass with the terminal background colour, and only then draws the icon's foreground glyph or mesh.","Running the background fill after the glyph pass, or filling only one cell of the wide icon, erases the icon or half of it, leaving an invisible or clipped sidebar icon in the GUI terminal.",1,3,2,3,25,65,49,"Only the icon's visibility changes; no text, state or control path is affected, so the consequence is cosmetic (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1017-1041).","It asserts exactly three background rects of the terminal colour and that every one precedes the first text or mesh shape (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:404-426), which rejects both ordering defects; a glyph drawn with the wrong width or a transparent icon still passes.","Distinct from the native-image test at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:196-260: this one (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:388-427) pins the two-pass ordering and the two-cell reservation for a wide icon, which no other test observes.","It paints through the real paint_terminal (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1007-1113) with a real vt100 screen, but the icon's pixels are never inspected at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:388-427 - only shape ordering - so the visual result is only indirectly covered.",high,keep,Cheap assertion of a specific painting-order defect not covered elsewhere; keep.,[],0.210s one hosted attempt; one paint of a 1x2 vt100 screen with hidden cursor,0.210,0.210,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2226 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
