nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Abuild_identity%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afingerprint_detects_byte_changes_with_same_length_and_preserves_open_build|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,server::build_identity::tests::fingerprint_detects_byte_changes_with_same_length_and_preserves_open_build,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs,266,275,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:56-113""]",executable_build over a 130000-byte file returns a different ExecutableBuild after one byte at offset 70000 is rewritten to 8 with the length unchanged.,A fingerprint that keys only on file length or a prefix of the file and so reports an unchanged build after an in-place same-length replacement.,2,2,1,4,50,50,50,The fingerprint decides whether a client is offered a restart against a changed build; a false match is a bounded detection failure (2).,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:266-275 asserts one before/after inequality; stability across repeated captures and the 'preserves_open_build' half of the name are not exercised.,"Differs only in length and byte offset from crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:278-291, which also rewrites bytes and compares whole ExecutableBuild values at 3/65535/65536/65537/131079 including two-block files.",Direct call to production executable_build over a real file.,high,consolidate,The changed-bytes invariant is fully and more strictly covered by the block-boundary matrix; folding this case into that loop keeps the same protection without a second 130KB writer.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Abuild_identity%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acapture_covers_small_files_and_fixed_block_boundaries|default""]",writes a 130000-byte file twice,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2479 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-server-session-001,independent-runtime-check-1
