nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|native_glyph%3A%3Anative_raster_retains_style_scale_and_opacity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,native_glyph::native_raster_retains_style_scale_and_opacity,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs,233,279,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:281-355"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:108-123""]","rasterize renders 界 and 🙂 through CoreText at scale 1 and 2 so the image doubles when DPI doubles, uses the bold-italic Menlo face for styled text, and applies the colour's alpha to the CGContext so a dimmed colour keeps partial opacity.",Rasterizing at point size instead of the pixel scale blurs every retina glyph; ignoring bold/italic in the CTFont name makes styled characters render regular; dropping CGContextSetAlpha makes dim cells full brightness and loses the dimmed-state cue.,1,3,2,4,25,70,52,"The consequences are visual - blur, lost style, lost dimming - with no state or control effect, so this is a cosmetic contract (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:281-300).","Size doubling is checked per dimension with a one-pixel tolerance, styled pixels must differ, dim alpha must land in (0,128], and a null CF value must map to None (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:233-279); a bold/italic swap still passes because only 'differs' is asserted.","Distinct from the paint test at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:196-260: this one (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:233-279) pins DPI scale, font traits and alpha inside rasterize, which the mesh and colour assertions cannot see.","rasterize is called directly against real CoreText and CoreGraphics, so the platform boundary the claim is about is fully exercised (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:281-355).",high,keep,"Direct, precise coverage of the rasterizer's three stated properties with real OS frameworks; keep.",[],0.343s one hosted attempt; six CoreText rasterizations at two pixel scales,0.343,0.343,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/mac