nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aagent_labels_are_readable|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::agent_labels_are_readable,default,src/remote/mod.rs,859,864,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:615-629"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:500-505""]","agent_label maps omp to 'Oh My Pi', cursor-agent to 'Cursor Agent', shell to 'Shell', and capitalises the first character of any other name (claude to 'Claude').","A fallback that returned the raw name, or a lost special case, would put the wrong harness label on the session the phone shows after remote creation, so the user cannot tell which agent owns the session.",1,3,2,4,25,70,52,"The only effect is the label text on a session summary (src/remote/mod.rs:500-505); no state, ownership or routing depends on it, so the consequence is cosmetic.",Four exact equalities cover both branches - three special cases and the default capitalisation (src/remote/mod.rs:859-864) - so any mapping change is rejected; the empty-name branch is unreachable from create_session and untested.,"tests/remote_web.rs:294-300 asserts the omp label end to end, and the runtime/tui label tests cover a different label contract (harness rendering, not src/remote/mod.rs:615-629); the cursor-agent, shell and default cases are unique here.","agent_label is the production function called by launch_for, tested directly on its full mapping (src/remote/mod.rs:615-629).",high,keep,Cheap exact coverage of a user-visible label mapping whose other cases have no test; it does not meet the prune threshold (usefulness 70).,[],"0.019s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.019,0.019,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:560 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Akeys_and_ids_are_validated|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::keys_and_ids_are_validated,default,src/remote/mod.rs,884,894,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:689-701"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:664-672"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:250-270"", ""crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/key.rs:76-131""]","valid_key accepts only ':name:' whose body is 1-46 characters of lowercase ASCII letters, digits or dash, and parse_id accepts only a 1-20 digit, non-zero decimal session id.","Accepting ':Escape:' or ':hello world:' would forward a keystroke name the server's parse_keystroke rejects (crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/key.rs:76-131), turning a bounded 400 into an error after a session round-trip, and accepting '0' or a 21-digit id would address a session that cannot exist.",1,3,2,4,25,70,52,"A regression only produces a worse error path or an extra round-trip for a malformed phone request (src/remote/mod.rs:250-270); no session is created, killed or misaddressed.","Both helpers get exact positive and negative cases - prefix and suffix colons, uppercase, spaces, dash, zero, negative, non-numeric (src/remote/mod.rs:884-894) - so a loosened shape or id range is rejected; the 46-character and 20-digit ceilings are only probed incidentally.","The key-name half duplicates the strictness already asserted at crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/key.rs:227-247, but the id half (zero, negative, non-numeric) is unique to this row.","Both are pure production functions tested directly (src/remote/mod.rs:664-701), and the keystroke shape they pre-filter is the same contract the terminal crate's parser enforces at crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/key.rs:76-131, so the real behaviour is exercised.",high,keep,"Cheap validation test whose id half is unique; its overlap with the terminal key tests is partial, so it stays as the gateway-side statement of the contract.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-terminal|key%3A%3Atests%3A%3Akeystroke_names_are_strict|default""]","0.013s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:563 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,
