nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahermes_detection_uses_managed_launch_and_preserves_explicit_override|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::agents::tests::hermes_detection_uses_managed_launch_and_preserves_explicit_override,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs,454,501,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-34"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:72-122"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:124-174"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:176-191""]","A detected hermes executable is wrapped through agent run with no auto-trust flag, an explicit hermes override replaces it exactly, and chmod 0644 removes hermes from detection entirely.",Launching hermes bare loses its process supervision; detecting a non-executable hermes would launch a file that cannot run. Both are rejected by exact argv and the post-chmod absence.,2,3,1,4,50,60,56,One agent's launch route (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-34); a bad argv fails that session's start and the picker is the workaround.,"Exact wrapped argv, exact override argv and the negative detection after chmod. Assertion anchor: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:460-496.","Managed launch and bare baseline are asserted identically by crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:359-451, and the 0644 skip repeats crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:241-287's gemini case; only the hermes name is new.",Real temp executable and chmod through production detect_agents/apply_overrides. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-34.,high,consolidate,"Retained protection: nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amanaged_agents_launch_through_the_agent_run_route|default asserts hermes' exact wrapped argv in the same MANAGED_AGENTS loop at agents.rs:402, and nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adetects_executables_then_shell_then_custom|default asserts the same 0644 non-executable skip through executable_in at crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:250-277; fold the hermes override case into crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:436-450. C=2, so no high-criticality invariant depends on a separate row.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amanaged_agents_launch_through_the_agent_run_route|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adetects_executables_then_shell_then_custom|default""]","[""tempdir with chmod stub""]",0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2904 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-001,independent-tui-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Ahttp%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aparses_a_body_and_reports_a_missing_content_length_as_zero|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::http::tests::parses_a_body_and_reports_a_missing_content_length_as_zero,default,src/remote/http.rs,313,319,"[""src/remote/http.rs:168-210""]","read_request takes exactly Content-Length bytes of body, truncating anything beyond it and reading more only while short, and reports an empty body when no Content-Length header exists.","A body-assembly regression - using only the bytes read with the head, ignoring content-length, or failing to truncate - would hand /api/session/<id>/send and POST /api/session bodies that are empty or carry trailing bytes, so the gateway would either 400 every remote action or type unintended text into a session.",2,2,2,4,50,60,56,"A broken body boundary degrades the remote send and create surface only; prompts can be re-sent or the command run locally, so the failure is bounded (src/remote/mod.rs:240-255).","It asserts the happy path and the absent-Content-Length default (src/remote/http.rs:313-319), but both bodies arrive in the same read as the head, so the 'while body.len() < content_length' loop and the exact MAX_BODY boundary are never exercised and an off-by-one there would pass.","The acceptance create test posts a real body with Content-Length through a socket (tests/remote_web.rs:43-56), so that half is covered; the 'no Content-Length means zero' default is asserted only here.","The production read_request runs unmodified over a Cursor holding head and body bytes, so the real framing code is what the assertions observe (src/remote/http.rs:119-210).",high,keep,"Distinct framing default with no acceptance coverage; the incremental-read gap is a coverage limitation rather than redundancy, so the test earns its place.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aremote_web|remote_gateway_creates_an_agent_session_from_the_phone_payload|default""]","0.014s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.014,0.014,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:555 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,
