24 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_attention%3A%3Aattention_compact_unicode_name_preserves_title_identity_and_session_id|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_attention::attention_compact_unicode_name_preserves_title_identity_and_session_id,default,tests/tui/agent_attention.rs,291,320,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7295-7345"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:340-377""]","At 24x9 the compact Agents row keeps the Agent name and its (#id) inside the display-column budget for names of ten e-acute, five CJK 界 and five 🙂 characters.","The width budget measured in bytes or in code points while 界/emoji occupy two columns, so clipping drops the (#id) suffix or cuts a multibyte name and two rows become indistinguishable.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Narrow-terminal identity confusion among equal titles; the user can widen the terminal or reopen the picker (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7330-7335).,Counts occurrences of the name's first character in the drawn row (must equal the name's char count) and requires both 'age' and '#2' for three width classes (tests/tui/agent_attention.rs:291-320).,The Unicode display-width boundary of the compact suffix is distinct; the same 24x9 compact row is exercised for duplicate titles by attention_maximum_population (tests/tui/agent_attention.rs:411-453).,"Real palette layout and clipping on a 24x9 TestBackend; the drawn buffer is what is asserted, with fixture snapshots only as input (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7295-7345).",high,keep,Only coverage of multi-byte/wide Agent names in the compact picker row.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_attention%3A%3Aattention_maximum_population_offscreen_filter_and_compact_duplicate_identity|default""]",Three 24x9 TestBackend draws,0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1725 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_empty_filter_and_cancellation_never_reopen_or_write|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_empty_filter_and_cancellation_never_reopen_or_write,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,802,842,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7287-7300"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1710""]",Enter in Browse enters Terminal and s becomes terminal input; an agent filter with no match shows 'No matching agents' and Enter does nothing; Esc returns to Browse; with every other agent stopped the picker says 'No other running agents' and Enter does nothing.,"Enter on an empty result switching to a stale candidate, the picker re-opening itself, or keys written to the pty while the palette is open.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Bounded key-routing failure; other keys and Esc recover (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7287-7300).,Six negative assertions across three picker states plus pty byte checks (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:802-842).,The empty 'No other running agents' state is also asserted by excludes_each_inactive_phase; the empty-filter path and cancellation are distinct (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1309-1330).,"Real key dispatch, palette rendering and terminal encoding; no stand-in for the mode gate (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7287-7300).",high,keep,Covers empty-result Enter and the picker's own cancelled state.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_each_inactive_phase_and_archived_records|default""]",Five full renders and two terminal-mode transitions,0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1733 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_current_shells_and_inactive_agents_across_projects|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_excludes_current_shells_and_inactive_agents_across_projects,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,708,734,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1698"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:3110-3140""]","The Agents picker lists only other running agent sessions across projects (no focused session, no plain shells, no exited session), matches a multi-word case-insensitive query across workspace/title, and Enter on the match requests only that session's view and closes the picker.","The picker offering a shell or the focused session as a destination, or a case/word mismatch hiding or mis-selecting an agent, or the palette left open over a terminal.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,"Bounded destination filtering: an invalid destination is refused at confirm time, so the cost is a wasted selection (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1698).","Exclusion positives and negatives, a mixed-case multi-word filter, the exact SetView target, palette closed and Terminal mode plus pty bytes (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:708-734).","Exclusion of non-agent sessions is partly covered by agent_search_excludes_each_inactive_phase_and_archived_records and search by palette::ux_search_keeps_session_identity_and_filters_complete_context; the cross-project running-agent enumeration is distinct (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140,1661-1698).","Real hierarchy enumeration, picker filter and confirm path through the real Dashboard; fixtures provide the sessions (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:3110-3140).",high,keep,Protects the running-agent predicate and the multi-field filter in one flow.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_each_inactive_phase_and_archived_records|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|palette%3A%3Aux_search_keeps_session_identity_and_filters_complete_context|default""]",Two full palette renders and one acknowledged view,0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1734 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_each_inactive_phase_and_archived_records|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_excludes_each_inactive_phase_and_archived_records,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1309,1330,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140""]","Each of Paused, Stopped, Interrupted, Exited and the archived current agent is excluded: the picker says 'No other running agents' and Enter does nothing.","Offering an agent that cannot accept a view, or listing archived records as destinations.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,"Bounded: an invalid destination would be refused, but the picker misleads (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140).","Four phases plus the archived flag, each with the empty-state text and a refused Enter (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1309-1330).",Overlaps the running_agent predicate in the current-shells test; the phase matrix and archived bit are distinct (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140).,Real hierarchy events and picker rendering through the Dashboard (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:136-140).,high,keep,Covers the full inactive-phase and archived matrix.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_current_shells_and_inactive_agents_across_projects|default""]","Five iteration states, each with one palette render",0.045,0.045,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1735 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_reaches_collapsed_workspace|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_reaches_collapsed_workspace,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1289,1306,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1664-1672""]",Folding the selected project and workspace rows away does not hide their agents from the picker: the filter finds agent-title-1 and Enter requests its view.,"Picker enumerating only expanded/visible rows, so agents in collapsed workspaces cannot be reached.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Bounded usability: the user can expand the workspace as a workaround (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1664-1672).,Proves the selection is a container after the folds and that Enter yields SetView focused 1 (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1289-1306).,The hierarchy_rows(true) enumeration is also implied by the cross-project test; the collapsed-row input is the distinction (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1664-1672).,"Real fold state, picker enumeration and confirm path (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1664-1672).",high,keep,Covers the folded-away destination case.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_excludes_current_shells_and_inactive_agents_across_projects|default""]",Two fold transitions and one view request,0.019,0.019,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1744 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_removal_fallback_disables_newly_focused_candidate|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_removal_fallback_disables_newly_focused_candidate,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1248,1269,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:172-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1711-1721""]","When the focused session is removed and focus falls to a frozen candidate, Enter refuses it as 'already focused' instead of switching.",Confirming a candidate that has become the current session; focus movement would silently substitute for the user's choice.,2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Bounded: the refusal is truthful and nothing is switched (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:180-187).,Asserts the 'already focused' reason and that Enter leaves the picker open (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1248-1269).,Another AgentCandidate::reason cell; the fallback-focus wording is asserted only here (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:172-190).,"Real hierarchy removal, focus fallback and confirm path (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:172-190).",high,keep,Covers the already-focused reason after a server-side removal.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_filtered_workspace_removal_never_substitutes_neighbor|default""]",One hierarchy update and one palette render,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1746 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,independent-dashboard-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acommand_modifier_does_not_start_the_verified_control_hold|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::command_modifier_does_not_start_the_verified_control_hold,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,490,514,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1145-1160"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/keymap.rs:228-250""]","A LeftSuper modifier press does not start the Control hold and Cmd+2 is not accepted as a label digit: no labels are drawn, focus is unchanged and nothing is requested.","The Command modifier matched as a Control edge, so pressing Cmd labels agents and swallows Cmd+digit shortcuts.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Bounded gesture confusion; no navigation or input occurs while the wrong hold is active (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1145-1160).,"Two explicit negatives (Super press, Super+digit) plus focus and outbox assertions (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:490-514).",The bare Super-press negative is unique; command_shortcut_cancels_control_hold only covers a Super key during an existing hold (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:402-432).,Real modifier-edge matching and keymap; the Dashboard dispatch is the subject (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1145-1160).,high,keep,Covers the Command-is-not-Control edge directly; no other test presses LeftSuper alone.,[],Two full sidebar renders,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1751 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acontrol_hold_labels_visible_running_agents_without_moving_the_title_column|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::control_hold_labels_visible_running_agents_without_moving_the_title_column,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,92,162,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1064-1100""]","While Control is held the first nine visible running Agent rows get [1]..[9] badges without changing the status/title columns or the row count, and releasing Control restores the unlabelled rows.","A badge inserted before the glyph shifting every title column, an extra row per label, or the focused agent left unlabelled so Ctrl+1 does not exist.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,"A mislabeled or shifted row makes the user pick a different agent than the badge shows; the hold can be released harmlessly, so it is bounded (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330).","Compares each labelled row's text after five cells with the pre-hold row, asserts the row count is unchanged, checks labels [1]/[2]/[3], and checks the unlabelled restore (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:92-162).","The skip(5) geometry, row count and per-row labels are covered by tests/tui/session_jump_single_digit.rs:191-254, and label hiding after a full release by tests/tui/agent_search.rs:337-346. The named tests/tui/session_jump_single_digit.rs:338-349 release case only asserts the absence of ""[01]"", which is vacuous for single-digit labels, so the restore assertion at tests/tui/agent_search.rs:150-161 is not covered by the named retained tests.",Real sidebar renderer and the real modifier-event path on a TestBackend; the badge placement is the subject (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330).,high,keep,"Partial redundancy only: the two named session_jump_single_digit tests cover badge geometry/labels but not release restoration, and the cited release test cannot observe a lingering [1]. Keep the row instead of consolidating on the stated evidence.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Afirst_nine_labels_follow_drawn_title_rows_in_wide_and_narrow_frames|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Areleasing_without_a_digit_cancels_without_selecting|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acontrol_keys_share_one_hold_and_hidden_sidebar_never_intercepts|default""]",Three 120x40 renders per phase and two modifier events,0.041,0.041,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1753 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,independent-dashboard-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acontrol_labels_preserve_geometry_at_wide_and_narrow_sizes_with_unicode_titles|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::control_labels_preserve_geometry_at_wide_and_narrow_sizes_with_unicode_titles,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,244,311,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1064-1100""]","The Control-hold badge keeps the status glyph and the Unicode title '界e◌́🙂' columns identical and leaves pane rects unchanged at 120x40, 80x24 and 60x24.","Badge width computed without Unicode display width, so a wide or combining title shifts and the advertised PTY size changes.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Layout/identity drift at supported sizes; the copy is visually wrong but navigation still works (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330).,"Per size it asserts the labelled suffix equals the pre-hold suffix, the row count is unchanged, and pane_rects is identical (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:244-311).","session_jump_single_digit::single_digit_badges_preserve_stacked_unicode_rows_and_clipped_metadata and first_nine_labels_follow_drawn_title_rows_in_wide_and_narrow_frames assert the same columns and geometry for the same Unicode title at these sizes (tests/tui/session_jump_single_digit.rs:191-254,427-483).",Real render and pane geometry at each size on a TestBackend; no stand-in for the layout (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:1300-1330).,high,keep,"session_jump_single_digit asserts the same Unicode column equality, but not that pane_rects and the advertised PTY size stay fixed; that assertion is unique here, so removal loses a boundary (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:244-311).","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Asingle_digit_badges_preserve_stacked_unicode_rows_and_clipped_metadata|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Afirst_nine_labels_follow_drawn_title_rows_in_wide_and_narrow_frames|default""]",Six full TestBackend renders (two per size),0.123,0.123,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1760 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Along_visible_agent_list_uses_first_nine_single_digit_labels_and_search_stays_available|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::long_visible_agent_list_uses_first_nine_single_digit_labels_and_search_stays_available,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,659,705,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1064-1100"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1710""]","Sixteen visible agents get only single-digit badges 1-9 (no [01]/[10]), the footer advertises Ctrl+1–9 while held, and the Agents search still opens after release.","Two-digit or tenth labels, or a footer advertising a digit range that does not exist.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,A wrong range makes the user press a digit that selects nothing or the wrong agent; bounded (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1064-1082).,"Asserts [1] and [9] present, [01] and [10] absent across rows, the footer text, then a real 's' open (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:659-705).","tests/tui/session_jump_single_digit.rs:57-104 asserts the single-digit rule, footer and per-id labels across counts 0/1/9/10/50, and tests/tui/session_jump_single_digit.rs:191-254 covers the ninth cutoff. Neither presses and releases Control before opening Agents search, which is the assertion at tests/tui/agent_search.rs:698-704.","Real render, footer and picker entry; the badge count rule is the subject (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1064-1100).",high,keep,"Most of the single-digit contract is duplicated, but post-release availability of the Agents palette (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:698-704) is not exercised by the named retained tests. Keep rather than consolidate.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Avisible_count_uses_only_single_digit_labels_from_zero_to_fifty|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Afirst_nine_labels_follow_drawn_title_rows_in_wide_and_narrow_frames|default""]",Two full 120x40 renders and a release event,0.070,0.070,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1761 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,independent-dashboard-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|cards%3A%3Aa_split_shows_the_card_in_the_pane_the_selection_emptied|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,cards::a_split_shows_the_card_in_the_pane_the_selection_emptied,default,tests/tui/cards.rs,214,242,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:56-84"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:248-262""]","In a split, moving up from the focused session to its workspace empties that pane and the card names the workspace; j reopens the local session and the now-empty other pane falls back to the projects card.","The emptied split pane going blank, the card rendered in the wrong pane index, or j opening the session in the wrong pane.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,"Bounded split UX: the session is still reachable, but the user can be confused about which pane is which (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:56-84).","Asserts focus movement, both panes' card contents, and hint presence/absence (tests/tui/cards.rs:214-242).",Card content duplicates the unit tests; the empty-pane placement and titled header in a split are the distinction (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:248-262).,"Real split state, pane rects and card renderer on a TestBackend (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:56-84).",medium,keep,The split empty-pane card placement is unique; the pane-selection internals were not read in full.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|split%3A%3Asplit_state_focus_and_close_preserve_sessions|default""]",Three full 120x40 renders and two view pumps,0.076,0.076,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1772 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|cards%3A%3Acards_are_display_only_and_enter_still_folds_the_row|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,cards::cards_are_display_only_and_enter_still_folds_the_row,default,tests/tui/cards.rs,101,130,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:248-331"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:444-510""]",A card is display-only: drawing it emits no request and the empty pane refuses input; Enter still folds the workspace and the card switches to 'Enter expand to reach its sessions' with no open hint.,"A card action emitting a request as a side effect, the empty pane accepting keystrokes, or Enter no longer folding.",2,3,2,3,50,65,59,Bounded: a stray request or accepted input from an empty pane can leave the UI in an unexpected state (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:248-331).,"Two empty-outbox assertions, the no-input assertion, the replaced hint and the absence of 'open' (tests/tui/cards.rs:101-130).",the_open_hint_names_what_the_next_row_key_selects covers the collapsed hint text; the no-request and no-input guarantee is distinct (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:896-918).,"Real empty-pane draw, fold and input gate; no stand-in for the Dashboard (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/cards.rs:248-331).",high,keep,The display-only/no-input invariant is asserted only here.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Acards%3A%3Atests%3A%3Athe_open_hint_names_what_the_next_row_key_selects|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Acards%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acards_are_drawn_only_where_a_pane_has_no_session|default""]",Two full renders and one terminal-input probe,0.043,0.043,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1773 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
