nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Ainput%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adrag_released_outside_ends_at_the_last_reported_cell|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,gui::input::tests::drag_released_outside_ends_at_the_last_reported_cell,default,src/gui/input.rs,2196,2228,"[""src/gui/input.rs:236-453""]","Press on cell (2,1), drag to (3,1), then release outside the terminal: the release report uses the last dragged cell.","Releasing off the terminal with no report, leaving the child app's drag selection live forever.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,A stuck selection in the child is a bounded interaction failure (input.rs:236-453).,"Exact bytes for press, drag and the off-terminal release (input.rs:2196-2228).",Off-terminal variant of the drag test; distinct ending behaviour; nearest neighbour drag_is_forwarded_in_button_motion_mode is at src/gui/input.rs:2087-2109,Production adapter and held-state tracking (input.rs:236-453).,high,keep,Distinct off-terminal release.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Ainput%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adrag_is_forwarded_in_button_motion_mode|default""]","[""three mouse events""]",0.017,0.017,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:512 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-gui-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Ainput%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aspecial_keys_carry_modifiers|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,gui::input::tests::special_keys_carry_modifiers,default,src/gui/input.rs,2312,2327,"[""src/gui/input.rs:236-453""]","Ctrl-Up encodes the modified arrow, Shift-Enter the CSI-u enter, and Alt-Backspace the meta form.","Special keys losing their modifiers, so Ctrl-Up scrolls panes instead of moving the cursor and Shift-Enter sends a bare Enter.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,Wrongly modified special keys change pane/cursor behaviour but are recoverable (input.rs:236-453).,Three exact byte strings for distinct key families (input.rs:2312-2327).,Generic modifier encoding; overlaps the Command-specific tests on Backspace but uses the ordinary path; asserted at src/gui/input.rs:2312-2327,Production encoder (input.rs:236-453).,high,keep,Cheap coverage of ordinary modified special keys.,[],"[""three encoder calls""]",0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:529 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-gui-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Ainput%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aunmodified_letter_keeps_its_text|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,gui::input::tests::unmodified_letter_keeps_its_text,default,src/gui/input.rs,2346,2360,"[""src/gui/input.rs:883-932"", ""src/gui/input.rs:1017-1029""]","An unmodified A press encodes nothing while the following Text event forwards 'a', so the filter must leave ordinary text alone.","The composed-text filter dropping ordinary text, so unmodified typing produces nothing in the child.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,Lost typing is visible immediately and recoverable by retyping (input.rs:874-932).,Asserts the filtered non-empty encoding is exactly 'a' (input.rs:2346-2360).,Negative complement of the Option-composition test; nearest neighbour alt_letter_encodes_meta is at src/gui/input.rs:2330-2343,Production filter and encoder (input.rs:874-932).,high,keep,Cheap guard against over-filtering.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Ainput%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aalt_letter_encodes_meta|default""]","[""one frame""]",0.020,0.020,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:532 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-gui-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afocus_reporting_observer_ignores_other_modes|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,gui::tests::focus_reporting_observer_ignores_other_modes,default,src/gui.rs,687,699,"[""src/gui.rs:27-50""]","Feeds the mouse-mode enable and disable ([?1000h, [?1000l) and asserts focus reporting stays off.","Conflating DEC mode numbers by prefix, so enabling mouse reporting makes the GUI send focus events the application did not request.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,Spurious focus reports confuse the application's focus state but are recoverable (gui.rs:27-50).,Two negative cases that differ only in mode number (gui.rs:687-699).,Negative complement of the split enable/disable test; nearest neighbour focus_reporting_observer_tracks_split_enable_and_disable_sequences is at src/gui.rs:671-684,Real observer function (gui.rs:32-50).,high,keep,Cheap mode-number guard.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afocus_reporting_observer_tracks_split_enable_and_disable_sequences|default""]","[""two feeds""]",0.014,0.014,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:535 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-gui-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Atests%3A%3Akeyboard_mode_observer_ignores_different_flags|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,gui::tests::keyboard_mode_observer_ignores_different_flags,default,src/gui.rs,664,668,"[""src/gui.rs:27-50""]",Feeds kitty push and pop sequences with key flags other than 15 and asserts the observed flag stays off.,"Prefix matching too loosely, so any kitty sequence enables enhanced encoding even though the application negotiated different flags.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,Wrong keyboard mode is a bounded input-fidelity failure (gui.rs:27-50).,Two negative cases with exact byte sequences (gui.rs:664-668).,"Negative complement of the split-sequence test; same contract, different flags; nearest neighbour keyboard_mode_observer_tracks_split_push_and_pop_sequences is at src/gui.rs:648-661",Exercises the real observer (gui.rs:32-50).,high,keep,Cheap negative guard.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr|gui%3A%3Atests%3A%3Akeyboard_mode_observer_tracks_split_push_and_pop_sequences|default""]","[""two feeds""]",0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:537 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-gui-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Ahttp%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aparses_get_and_headers_case_insensitively|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::http::tests::parses_get_and_headers_case_insensitively,default,src/remote/http.rs,301,310,"[""src/remote/http.rs:31-46"", ""src/remote/http.rs:119-210"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:144-166""]","read_request parses the request line of 'GET /api/state?x=1 HTTP/1.1' into method and target, path() drops the query, query(""x"") returns ""1"", and header() finds 'X-Test: yes' and a capitalised 'Host' through case-insensitive comparison.","A parser that stored header names with their wire case but looked them up case-sensitively, or a path() that kept the query string, would make authorized()'s header(""host"") lookup (src/remote/mod.rs:144-166) miss and return 403 for every request including loopback, and would route /api/session/3/screen?... to the 404 fallback: the whole remote web surface would be unusable.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,"Failure is bounded to the optional remote web gateway; the desktop and TUI keep working, so it is a feature outage with a workaround rather than lost state or an authority breach (src/remote/mod.rs:126-166).","Five assertions pin the stated boundaries: method, query-free path, query extraction, a lowercase lookup of 'X-Test' and an uppercase lookup of 'HOST' (src/remote/http.rs:301-310); no malformed-head or duplicate-header case is included, but each claimed property is positively checked.","The end-to-end path in tests/remote_web.rs:30-41 also sends a capitalised 'Host' and gets 200, so name normalisation is covered elsewhere; the query-string extraction and the mixed-case X-Test lookup are asserted only here.","read_request is the production parser itself (src/remote/http.rs:119-210), driven through its generic Read+Write with a Cursor; the socket seam is not part of parsing, so the full algorithm is exercised.",high,keep,"Grounded unit coverage at a parser boundary the acceptance harness does not reach (query extraction, mixed-case lookups), and it does not depend on the remote_web suite staying green.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aremote_web|remote_gateway_follows_the_settings_toggle|default""]","0.020s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.020,0.020,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:556 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Ahttp%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awrites_a_response_with_security_headers_and_honours_head|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::http::tests::writes_a_response_with_security_headers_and_honours_head,default,src/remote/http.rs,333,347,"[""src/remote/http.rs:212-239"", ""src/remote/http.rs:21-23"", ""src/remote/http.rs:274-286""]","write_response emits the status line, Connection: close, Content-Type, Content-Length, Cache-Control, Content-Security-Policy, nosniff and Referrer-Policy, then CRLFCRLF and the body; head_only omits the body so a HEAD reply ends at the blank line.","Dropping the CSP (or the whole security header block) leaves the gateway's dashboard page, which renders agent output and holds a live /api/state control channel, without the browser restriction that stops injected script from reading terminal content; emitting a body for HEAD breaks HTTP framing.",2,2,3,4,50,70,62,The headers are defence in depth around the served page: losing them does not by itself expose state but removes the barrier that makes an injection in rendered agent output harmless (src/remote/http.rs:21-23).,"It checks that the CSP header name is present and that a HEAD reply ends at the blank line, but never the policy value, nor nosniff, Referrer-Policy or Content-Length despite the test name (src/remote/http.rs:333-347); an empty or weakened CSP still passes.","No other test inspects response headers: tests/remote_web.rs:30-56 looks only at the status line, body text and the font Content-Type, so header emission is protected only here.","write_response is the production writer run over a Vec<u8> sink, so the exact bytes the gateway sends under serve() are produced (src/remote/http.rs:212-239).",high,keep,"Sole coverage of the response header contract; the unchecked policy value is an improvement opportunity, not evidence that the test is redundant.",[],"0.020s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.020,0.020,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:559 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alaunch_kind_and_prompt_follow_the_agent|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::launch_kind_and_prompt_follow_the_agent,default,src/remote/mod.rs,821,856,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:598-628"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:33-56"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:14-25""]","launch_for maps a Shell entry to SessionKind::Terminal with no label and an unchanged argv, maps omp to SessionKind::Agent{omp} with label 'Oh My Pi' and appends '--' plus the trimmed prompt, and leaves a non-task agent (hermes) argv unchanged.","Adding hermes, cursor-agent or opencode to TASK_AGENTS, dropping the explicit '--' separator, or skipping the trim would start a remote-created session with an argv its CLI rejects (hermes takes a task only via -z) or with the task parsed as a flag or subcommand: the requested task would never run, or would run with unintended launcher options.",2,3,2,4,50,70,62,"A mis-built argv makes one remotely created session start wrongly; the user can recreate it from the desktop, so it is a bounded feature failure rather than lost work (src/remote/mod.rs:425-500).","Three agent shapes are asserted exactly - kind, label and argv bytes (src/remote/mod.rs:821-856) - so a separator loss, a trim loss or a task-agent list change is rejected; an empty prompt (which must not append '--') and the Custom-source rejection live in create_session and are untested here.","The omp task injection is exercised end to end by tests/remote_web.rs:294-320, which reads the stub's argv; the shell kind, the no-label rule and the hermes exception are asserted only here.","launch_for and with_task are pure production functions tested directly, including the TASK_AGENTS constant that decides the behaviour (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:33-56).",high,keep,"Distinct boundaries (shell, task agent, non-task agent) that the acceptance test cannot cover without stubs for th