nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_attention%3A%3Ajump_key_visits_input_then_unread_in_sidebar_order_and_the_strip_counts_them|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_attention::jump_key_visits_input_then_unread_in_sidebar_order_and_the_strip_counts_them,default,tests/tui/agent_attention.rs,456,486,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:18-35"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:53-118"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:121-166"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/hints.rs:44-60""]","The i key visits Input-needed entries before Unread ones in sidebar order, wraps, and emits a SetView; the strip directly above the quota section and the footer name the same queue, and a Busy session with an older Unread is skipped.","Jump and strip computed from two different classifications, or an Unread under a Busy session visited early, sending the user to an agent that is not waiting.",3,3,1,3,75,55,63,Attention routing in the sidebar: a wrong queue sends the user to a busy agent and leaves the one needing an answer unvisited (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:53-118).,"Asserts the exact visitation sequence [8,9,1,2,8,9], the exact strip text ' ? 3 need input · ✓ 1 ready' at row 32, the footer 'i Next input needed', and a SetView in the outbox (tests/tui/agent_attention.rs:456-486).","The same order, counts, strip position and footer are asserted by the attention.rs unit tests jump_visits_input_then_ready_in_tree_order_and_wraps, strip_sits_above_the_quota_section_and_a_click_jumps_like_the_key and browse_footer_names_the_jump_only_while_a_session_needs_you; only the legacy-rollup fixture differs (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:380-520).","Real Dashboard keys, tree and render; protocol fixtures are the input, and the integration draws the same screen the unit tests do (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:121-166).",high,keep,"Overlap with the attention.rs unit tests is partial, not subsuming: they use a different fixture (no legacy-rollup conflict) and the key-driven walk from a quiet row is only here. Removing it would lose that fixture and the 120x40 strip/footer composition (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:380-520).","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ajump_visits_input_then_ready_in_tree_order_and_wraps|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astrip_sits_above_the_quota_section_and_a_click_jumps_like_the_key|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abrowse_footer_names_the_jump_only_while_a_session_needs_you|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainput_outranks_unread_and_only_a_running_session_waits|default""]",Six i dispatches and three 120x40/88x38 TestBackend renders,0.038,0.038,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1730 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
