nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Aextension%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asession_start_and_model_select_publish_the_reported_model_for_both_harnesses|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::extension::tests::session_start_and_model_select_publish_the_reported_model_for_both_harnesses,default,src/report/extension.rs,1758,1797,"[""src/report/extension.rs:539-585"", ""src/report/extension.rs:418-440""]","For Pi and Omp, session_start carrying model=grok-4.7 publishes that model, a later model_select with claude-sonnet-4 replaces it, and an identical model_select on a fresh sequence is accepted but publishes nothing.","Inventing or dropping the reported model, republishing an identical model, or failing to replace it on a mid-session switch.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,The sidebar model is display metadata; a wrong value misleads but does not change execution (2).,"src/report/extension.rs:1758-1797 asserts ACCEPTED for all three frames and the exact observed model sequence [grok-4.7, claude-sonnet-4] for both harnesses.",Only model-publish sequence test across harnesses; the no-model and pre-binding rows cover other arms.,Production Events with the scripted supervisor.,high,keep,Covers both harnesses' announce and switch paths with no republish on equality.,[],two harness runs with three frames each,0.101,0.101,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:644 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Aextension%3A%3Atests%3A%3Athe_settled_quality_is_the_harness_claim_about_its_own_boundary|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,report::extension::tests::the_settled_quality_is_the_harness_claim_about_its_own_boundary,default,src/report/extension.rs,1723,1755,"[""src/report/extension.rs:335-360"", ""src/report/extension.rs:40-47""]","For Pi and Omp the same session_start/agent_start/agent_settled sequence publishes ResponseReady with quality Confirmed for Pi and Observed for Omp, matching each harness's settled_quality claim.","A single shared settled quality, or a provider's weaker boundary reported as Confirmed, which would let Omp's non-final stop hook look like a settled response.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"Quality labels how final the reported boundary is; a wrong Confirmed overstates a weaker harness signal, a bounded reporting-fidelity failure (2).","src/report/extension.rs:1723-1755 asserts the exact last observed state and quality for both harnesses, so a uniform quality fails one side.",Only assertion tying Harness.settled_quality to published observations.,Production Events logic with the scripted supervisor; both harness constants are the real ones.,high,keep,Only evidence for the per-harness settled-quality claim.,[],two scripted-supervisor runs,0.099,0.099,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:651 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,independent-report-check-2
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20same-file%20reload%20is%20a%20switch%20that%20names%20the%20conversation%20it%20is%20already%20on|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a same-file reload is a switch that names the conversation it is already on,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,111,122,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A session_switch without a preceding startup, whose previousSessionFile names the current session, emits one session_start frame with previous = its own id, not null.","If the extension suppressed 'previous equals current' as a no-op, a same-file reload would leave the receiver without the expectation it needs, or would emit a startup-style frame with no previous id and bind the conversation as new.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"The frame is the only binding evidence for a reload; emitting previous = null makes a reload indistinguishable from a startup, which resets the receiver's expectations (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:47-48).","It asserts the single frame's event, session_id and previous (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:111-122); the same-value case is a real boundary the other switch rows do not cover.","Distinct input from the resume row: here previous id equals the current id and no startup precedes it, so the assertion separates 'same file reload' from 'switch left a conversation'; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:47-48, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The production announce path and idOf run against a synthesized event; the assertion reads the delivered frame (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:118-121).,high,keep,A distinct boundary of the same switch contract with no other test; keep.,[],0.011s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 10.814334 at macOS-job.log:3729; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20tool%20error%20followed%20by%20a%20successful%20assistant%20response%20is%20a%20successful%20cycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a tool error followed by a successful assistant response is a successful cycle,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,399,416,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","An agent_end whose messages end with a toolResult error followed by a successful assistant message reports outcome ok, and the tool output text never reaches the record.","If outcomeOf scanned for any failed message rather than the last assistant message, a recoverable tool error would mark the whole turn failed, so a successful result would be reported as an error.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,Misclassifying a recovered tool error flips a completed turn to failed in the sidebar and blocks the user's normal collect path (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:8-20).,"It asserts the ok outcome on end and settled for a mixed message list and excludes the tool output text (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:399-416), the exact case a naive any-error scan breaks.","The Pi suite asserts the same mixed-message case over its own cycle (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:254-273); shared classification logic, distinct emission paths.",Real handler and outcomeOf with synthesized messages; delivered frames are read from the record (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:405-415).,high,keep,Distinct classification boundary (recovered tool error) on the OMP path; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20tool%20error%20followed%20by%20a%20successful%20assistant%20response%20is%20a%20successful%20cycle|default""]",0.017s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.017,0.017,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 16.584208 at macOS-job.log:3831; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|error%20and%20aborted%20ends%20settle%20as%20error%20and%20aborted%3B%20no%20assistant%20message%20is%20none|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,error and aborted ends settle as error and aborted; no assistant message is none,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,379,397,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Across three cycles the last assistant stopReason decides the outcome: error, aborted, and none for no assistant message, each reflected in agent_end and agent_settled, with the user prompt text excluded.","If outcomeOf were missing or read the first assistant message, an errored turn would be reported ok (or vice versa), so the Dashboard would show success for a failed turn and the user would collect nothing.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,The outcome field is what the sidebar and phone show for a finished turn; a wrong outcome hides a failure as success (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:8-20).,"Three outcome classes across three runs, each asserted on both end and settled, plus a prompt-content exclusion (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:379-397).","The Pi suite asserts the same outcomeOf contract for its own cycle rows (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:168-186); the shared helper is covered twice, but the OMP emission path is distinct.",Real handlers and the real outcomeOf over synthesized message arrays; frames from a real helper (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:385-396).,high,keep,Covers the outcome classification on the OMP path; retained since the OMP end path differs from Pi's settled path.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|error%20and%20aborted%20outcomes%20come%20from%20the%20last%20assistant%20message%3B%20a%20second%20run%20increments|default""]",0.049s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.049,0.049,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 49.408959 at macOS-job.log:3825; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|registers%20OMP%27s%20lifecycle%20and%20switch%20events|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,registers OMP's lifecycle and switch events,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,76,87,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","The factory registers exactly agent_end, agent_start, model_select, session_shutdown, session_start, session_switch, session_tree, tool_approval_requested, tool_approval_resolved, tool_execution_end, tool_execution_start, registers no session_before_switch or session_compact, and exposes one command, ovrcr-reattach.","A later change adding a pre-switch or compaction subscription, or dropping a lifecycle event, would silently change what OMP may block or when OVRCR pauses; a fabricated plugin-refresh binding would claim an event the host never fires.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"The registered set is the extension's whole hook surface: an added cancellable pre-switch could pause a conversation, and a dropped tool lifecycle handler re-enables OMP's speculative tool execution (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-108).","An exact sorted list plus two explicit 'must not include' checks and the command list (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:76-87) reject additions and removals; it cannot detect a handler whose body is wrong, which the behavioural rows cover.",The Pi extension's registration list is asserted in a different test against a different module (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:140-149); OMP's exact list has no other coverage.,The production factory is loaded from the materialized source and its real pi.on/registerCommand calls are recorded by the fixture's API (tests/fixtures/pi/pi_host.mjs:33-57).,high,keep,Exact structural guard on the provider's hook surface; keep.,[],0.001s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.001,0.001,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 1.398 at macOS-job.log:3717; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|shutdown%20reports%20once%20with%20reason%20quit%20and%20disables|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,shutdown reports once with reason quit and disables,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,442,450,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A session_shutdown with reason 'replaced' emits one session_shutdown frame with reason 'quit', and the following agent_start/agent_end emit nothing because the producer is disabled.","If shutdown did not disable the producer, a reload's late lifecycle events would report into a producer the receiver has already retired, and the reason would leak the host's replacement vocabulary instead of the canonical quit.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"A retired producer that keeps reporting double-counts cycles for the session until the receiver fences it (src/ovrcr-reporting-extension.mjs:117-121, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:134-144).","It asserts both the single frame and the canonical reason, then the post-shutdown silence (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:442-450).",The Pi suite asserts its own shutdown drain and disable (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:207-218); the OMP shutdown path is a separate handler with a fixed reason.,Real handlers and the real flush path with a helper child; the record proves both the frame and the silence (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:446-450).,high,keep,Distinct shutdown contract for OMP; keep.,[],0.008s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.008,0.008,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 8.303792 at macOS-job.log:3843; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|retry%20rejects%20a%20FIFO%20intent%20before%20a%20blocking%20open%20can%20wait%20for%20a%20writer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,retry rejects a FIFO intent before a blocking open can wait for a writer,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,421,456,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","With parent-intents/fifo.json a FIFO, ovrcr_retry returns Refused with the regular-bounded-private-owned-file reason and never blocks waiting for a writer.","If the reader opened the intent without O_NONBLOCK and a regular-file check, a FIFO would block the filesystem worker forever, wedging the tool call and the session's intent recovery.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"A blocked open stalls the retry path indefinitely; the consequence is a hung tool call rather than lost state, so it stays below the authority band (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:283-302).","It uses a real mkfifo, a 2 s release timer that records whether a writer was ever needed, and the exact refusal reason (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:421-456), which distinguishes a non-blocking refusal from a hang.","No other row uses a non-regular intent file; the symlink and growing-file cases assert different guards; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:274-350, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real readPrivate opens the real FIFO with O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK; the assertion is on the observed non-blocking return (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:283-302).,high,keep,Only coverage of the FIFO/non-blocking intent guard; keep.,[],0.017s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.017,0.017,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 17.202041 at macOS-job.log:3969; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_package_bootstrap.mjs|standalone%20package%20diagnoses%20managed%20launch%20without%20manufacturing%20tools|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs,node,unit,standalone package diagnoses managed launch without manufacturing tools,default,tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs,45,49,"[""pi/extension.ts:1-6"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:33-93""]","Calling the real package entry with no OVRCR channel registers only a session_start handler, and that handler notifies one warning matching 'requires a managed Pi launch' with zero tool or command registrations.","If the package entry registered tools or reporters outside a managed launch, an ordinary Pi install would expose delegation tools that cannot work and the agent would call them and fail.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"A package that manufactures a control owner in an unmanaged session produces tool calls that cannot reach a Server, and the diagnosis is the only feedback (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:33-38, 69-77).","It asserts the single session_start registration, zero registrations and the notice text (tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs:45-49).","The other bootstrap rows supply metadata; this row is the no-channel branch, which no other test covers; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:33-46, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real pi/extension.ts entry and initializeOvrcr run; the Pi API is a fixture that records registrations and notifications (tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs:14-44).,high,keep,Only coverage of the unmanaged package diagnosis; keep.,[],0.001s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.001,0.001,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 1.429833 at macOS-job.log:4119; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20hung%20helper%20is%20killed%20at%20the%20deadline%20and%20the%20handler%20still%20resolves|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a hung helper is killed at the deadline and the handler still resolves,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,229,237,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","With a helper that sleeps five seconds, agent_start resolves between 800 and 2500 ms, i.e. the transport killed it at its 900 ms deadline instead of waiting for the child.","Without the deadline the handler would block for the helper's full lifetime, so a wedged helper would stall Pi's event loop path and every later event for the session.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"The one-second callback budget is what keeps a lost helper from stalling the host; the deadline enforces it (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:44-44, 88-95).","The elapsed-time window brackets the 900 ms deadline from both sides (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:229-237); it cannot distinguish a kill from a close that happened for another reason, and the bound is loose.","No other row exercises the deadline; the overflow and drain rows exercise queue behaviour, not the per-helper timer; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:82-144, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real deliver() timer and real spawn of a hanging helper run; the assertion is on observed elapsed time (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:232-236).,high,keep,Only coverage of the per-helper deadline; keep.,[],0.915s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.915,0.915,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 914.582041 at macOS-job.log:4245; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20tool%20error%20followed%20by%20a%20successful%20assistant%20response%20is%20a%20successful%20cycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a tool error followed by a successful assistant response is a successful cycle,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,254,273,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","An agent_end ending with a successful assistant after a toolResult error reports ok on both end and settled, and the tool output text is absent from the record.","If outcomeOf scanned for any failed message, a recovered tool error would mark a completed turn failed and the user would not collect a good result.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,The classification decides the published outcome of a turn; a false failure hides a usable result (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:8-20).,It asserts the three-frame run/outcome sequence and excludes the tool output (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:254-273).,"The OMP suite asserts the same classification over its own end path (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:399-416); duplicated logic, different emission path.",Real handlers and outcomeOf with a real helper child recording frames (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:262-272).,high,keep,Covers the recovered-tool-error boundary on the Pi cycle path; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20tool%20error%20followed%20by%20a%20successful%20assistant%20response%20is%20a%20successful%20cycle|default""]",0.026s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 26.279792 at macOS-job.log:4257; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20transition%20names%20the%20conversation%20it%20left%20by%20id%2C%20never%20by%20its%20file%20path|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,"a transition names the conversation it left by id, never by its file path",default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,324,344,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A resume with a long Pi session path delivers previous '11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555', a startup delivers null, and a resume whose filename has no bounded id also delivers null; no timestamp or '.pi/agent' text appears.","If idOf truncated or accepted the timestamp, the receiver would pause on a conversation that does not exist or on a stale path-derived id; leaking the path would carry the user's home layout into the channel.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,The previous id decides which conversation the receiver pauses on a transition; a truncation or a path would pause the wrong one (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:27-32).,"Three previous values including the null-for-unparseable case, plus two body exclusions (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:324-344), reject truncation, path copying and invented ids.",The OMP suite covers the same helper with an OMP-shaped filename (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:89-109); the 100-character unparseable-name boundary is unique here.,The real idOf helper runs through the real announcement handler with a real helper child recording frames (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:334-343).,high,keep,Covers the unparseable-name boundary of the shared redaction helper; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20switch%20names%20the%20conversation%20it%20left%20by%20id%2C%20never%20by%20its%20file%20path|default""]",0.021s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.021,0.021,1,0,ho