node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20unavailable%20optional%20Pi%20API%20preserves%20ordinary%20reporting|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an unavailable optional Pi API preserves ordinary reporting,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,124,138,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","With ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts replaced by a module whose loader returns undefined, a full cycle still delivers session_start, agent_start (with interrupt 'Unavailable'), agent_end and agent_settled with outcome ok.","If a missing optional keybinding API aborted registration, a Pi build without pi-tui would lose all reporting; if it aborted after registering some handlers, the receiver would see frames without a settled event.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,"Optional-API absence must degrade only the interrupt field, otherwise a whole class of installs loses lifecycle reporting (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:86-88, 106-112).","It asserts the four-event sequence, the interrupt field value and the settled outcome (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:124-138); the interrupt semantics themselves are covered by the interrupt suite.","No other test replaces the optional module with an unavailable one; the interrupt suite tests inspectPiInterruptBinding directly but never the registration path; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-124, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real runtime and transport run with a substituted optional module and a real helper child, so the degraded path is exercised end to end in-process (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:127-136).",high,keep,The only end-to-end test of optional-API degradation in the registration path; keep.,[],0.034s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.034,0.034,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 34.20125 at macOS-job.log:4209; run 