node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|continuations%20inside%20one%20cycle%20keep%20the%20run%3B%20the%20last%20end%20before%20settled%20decides%20the%20outcome|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,continuations inside one cycle keep the run; the last end before settled decides the outcome,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,188,205,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A start/end(error)/start/end(stop)/settled sequence keeps run 1 for all five frames, settled carries outcome ok (the last end), and a start after settled opens run 2.","If each continuation opened a new run, the receiver would see several turns where Pi ran one; if settled carried the earlier error, a successful continuation would be reported failed.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,"The continuation rule is the whole reason the extension owns the cycle span; breaking it splits one prompt into several published turns (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:1-9, 106-124).","It asserts the five-event order, run equality across them, the settled outcome and the next-run boundary (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:188-205).","The OMP suite has no continuation-in-one-cycle row (its agent_end without willContinue closes the cycle), so this semantic is Pi-only; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-124, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport; frames recorded by a real helper child (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:198-204).,high,keep,Pi-only continuation accounting with no counterpart; keep.,[],0.037s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.037,0.037,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 37.111333 at macOS-job.log:4227; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
