node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|non-tui%20modes%20never%20spawn%20a%20helper%3B%20shutdown%20reports%20once%20then%20disables|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,non-tui modes never spawn a helper; shutdown reports once then disables,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,207,218,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","In mode rpc, agent_start and agent_settled emit nothing; after the mode flips to tui, one session_shutdown with reason 'reload' is delivered and a later agent_start emits nothing.","If the mode guard were absent, a rpc-mode session would spawn helpers for events it never shows; if shutdown did not disable, a reload's events would report from a retired producer.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,"Mode gating keeps reporting to the terminal UI, and the post-shutdown disable prevents a retired producer reporting into the next factory (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:108-108, src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:148-153).","It asserts empty output in rpc mode, then the single shutdown frame with its canonical reason and the silence after (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:207-218).","The OMP suite covers print-mode inertness but not a mode transition in the same producer; no other row asserts the disable-after-shutdown ordering; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:108-134, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport; the record file proves the absence of helper spawns (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:211-217).,high,keep,Distinct mode-transition and disable-ordering coverage; keep.,[],0.014s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.014,0.014,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 13.781167 at macOS-job.log:4233; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|one%20response%20cycle%3A%20start%2C%20end%2C%20settled%20carry%20run%2C%20outcome%20and%20ordered%20sequence|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,"one response cycle: start, end, settled carry run, outcome and ordered sequence",default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,140,166,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","The exact registration and command lists, then a startup/start/end/settled cycle delivering sequence 1-4 with run 1, outcome none->ok, schema 1, mode tui, owner_pid, session id and a 32-hex instance, and no prompt content.","If sequencing were assigned at delivery time or run were not opened at agent_start, the receiver would reject or reorder the cycle; a copied prompt message would leak user content into the channel.",2,4,2,3,50,75,65,"The sequence is the receiver's deduplication key, and run/outcome is what the Dashboard shows for the turn (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:65-80, src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-124).","It pins the exact (event, sequence, run, outcome) tuples, a per-frame metadata sweep and a secret-prompt exclusion (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:140-166), a complete cycle invariant.","The OMP suite has its own cycle rows over a different protocol (continue semantics instead of settled); the Pi settled protocol is protected only here; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-124, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real runtime handlers and transport with a real helper child; instance and owner_pid are asserted against the live process (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:154-162).,high,keep,Complete invariant for the Pi cycle protocol; keep.,[],0.033s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 33.06775 at macOS-job.log:4215; run 42429838269 jo