python-unittest|Relocated%20pinned%20Cursor%20dependency%20and%20passive%20CLI%20diagnostics|tests%2Fcursor_bridge_install.py%3A%3AInstallation|test_reinstall_reuses_valid_pin_without_downloading|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics,python-unittest,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py::Installation,unittest,acceptance,test_reinstall_reuses_valid_pin_without_downloading,default,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py,42,46,"[""tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:42-46"", ""scripts/install-cursor-bridge.py:44-48""]",A second install with no archive argument and PATH=/nonexistent returns 0 and does not invoke curl because the installed archive already matches the pin.,"A reinstall that always downloads (failing here) instead of reusing a verified pin, or one that reuses a mismatching file.",2,3,3,3,50,75,65,A needless download is a bounded operational failure; the verified-pin short-circuit is the invariant (2).,"tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:42-46 forces the no-download path with a PATH that cannot contain curl and asserts success plus the absence of 'curl' in stderr, which the download implementation cannot satisfy.",Only cache-reuse test for this installer.,Real installer in a temp HOME with the real pinned archive; the download tool is made unreachable by PATH.,high,keep,Only evidence that a verified pin short-circuits the download path on reinstall.,[],runs the installer twice with a constrained PATH,,,,,unmeasured,no per-method timing; unittest prints one aggregate: macOS-job.log:3669 'Ran 6 tests in 2.076s' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics'),packaging-installers-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aoperator_auth|dangling_credential_links_are_rejected|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::operator_auth,integration,integration,dangling_credential_links_are_rejected,default,tests/operator_auth.rs,395,406,"[""src/operator/auth.rs:207-270"", ""src/operator/auth.rs:856-899""]",A credential path symlinked to a missing target yields Storage.,"A dangling link being treated as an empty/new record, silently replacing the link.",3,2,2,4,75,60,66,"The body only requires status() to return AuthError::Storage for a dangling credential link (tests/operator_auth.rs:395-406). exists() uses symlink_metadata (src/operator/auth.rs:898-904) and a followed dangling link would also fail ENOENT as Storage, so the assertion proves the tampered path is not silently read as an empty credential record that reports signed out; that is a bounded credential-store integrity/diagnosis failure (C=3). The sibling real-target test (tests/operator_auth.rs:376-393) carries the C=4 breach protection.",One Storage assertion for status.,Dangling-link handling is a small distinct case of link rejection.,Real filesystem symlink.,high,keep,Keep: One Storage assertion for status. Dangling-link handling is a small distinct case of link rejection.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aoperator_auth|storage_refuses_insecure_directory_and_symlink_credentials|default""]","[""real fs""]",0.138,0.138,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:982 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-004,independent-integration-mid-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aregistry_migration|corrupt_sqlite_refuses_startup_and_offline_without_legacy_fallback|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::registry_migration,integration,acceptance,corrupt_sqlite_refuses_startup_and_offline_without_legacy_fallback,default,tests/registry_migration.rs,190,194,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:85-235""]","A file containing non-sqlite bytes is refused at startup and offline, leaving both files unchanged.",Overwriting a corrupt database or falling back to legacy and losing its contents.,3,2,2,4,75,60,66,Destroying a user's database file is irreversible.,Refusal and byte equality from the same helper as the incompatible case.,Corruption is a small distinct input of the refuse-existing matrix.,Real binary and filesystem.,high,keep,Keep: Refusal and byte equality from the same helper as the incompatible case. Corruption is a small distinct input of the refuse-existing matrix.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aregistry_migration|incompatible_sqlite_refuses_startup_and_offline_without_legacy_fallback|default""]","[""real fs""]",0.684,0.684,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1377 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aregistry_migration|nonempty_unversioned_sqlite_refuses_startup_without_legacy_fallback|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::registry_migration,integration,acceptance,nonempty_unversioned_sqlite_refuses_startup_without_legacy_fallback,default,tests/registry_migration.rs,197,207,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:85-235""]",A sqlite with a foreign sqliteX table and no OVRCR version is refused without importing the legacy file.,Adopting an unrelated database as OVRCR's registry.,3,2,2,4,75,60,66,Adopting/overwriting another tool's database destroys data.,Refusal plus unchanged source bytes.,Unversioned-nonempty is a distinct metadata state.,Real sqlite and binary.,high,keep,Keep: Refusal plus unchanged source bytes. Unversioned-nonempty is a distinct metadata state.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aregistry_migration|corrupt_sqlite_refuses_startup_and_offline_without_legacy_fallback|default""]","[""real sqlite""]",0.902,0.902,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1383 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|harness_default_claude_launches_without_catalog_or_model_override|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,harness_default_claude_launches_without_catalog_or_model_override,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,470,574,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:604-616"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/auto_trust.rs:54-90""]",A HarnessDefault CreateAgentSession over the dashboard socket launches a fake Claude that records its argv; the retained terminal contains --dangerously-skip-permissions and does not contain --model.,"The HarnessDefault path could inject a model override the user did not choose, or could drop the auto-trust flag and block the managed launch.",3,3,1,4,75,60,66,Launching a managed agent with a wrong or missing privilege/model flag is a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:605-614).,"Asserts absence of --model and presence of the auto-trust flag in the recorded argv, but not the rest of the command line (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:556-572).",The no-model HarnessDefault leg repeats tests/server_lifecycle.rs:409-432; only the skip-permissions assertion is not already made there.,"Real compiled server process, PTY and dashboard socket with a scripted native Claude (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:474-508).",high,keep,Small distinct assertion (managed auto-trust flag) keeps it above full subsumption by the detected-model test.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|detected_claude_model_launch_revalidates_alias_and_workspace_identity|default""]","[""spawns detached compiled server with a fake claude on PATH"", ""real PTY plus Unix dashboard socket"", ""polls terminal text""]",3.534,3.534,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1535 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asave_uncommitted_work_defaults_off|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,settings::tests::save_uncommitted_work_defaults_off,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs,1037,1047,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-160""]","An empty document reports save_uncommitted_work as value 'false' from SettingSource::Default, owned by the Server, with the SAVE_UNCOMMITTED_WORK_OFF explanation.","A default-on regression that would let the server commit the user's uncommitted work without consent, or a missing/misowned off-state explanation.",3,3,1,4,75,60,66,"The setting authorizes touching uncommitted work in the user's checkout (settings/mod.rs:145-160); a default-on regression mutates user work without consent, a durable-work/consent failure at C=3.","Four exact row assertions (value, source, owner, off_state) at 1037-1046; it does not re-check behavior when a document sets it (covered by full_document). Assertions at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1040-1043.",Mostly redundant with the off_state assertion inside nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aempty_document_is_all_defaults_and_consent_settings_say_how_to_turn_on|default and the default rows in nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|matrix_covers_every_declared_setting|default; the only extra evidence is that the owner is SettingOwner::Server. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1162-1243.,Direct call to production parse with an empty document (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-160.,high,keep,The unique owner assertion plus the consent-oriented framing keep it; usefulness stays above any prune gate.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aempty_document_is_all_defaults_and_consent_settings_say_how_to_turn_on|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|matrix_covers_every_declared_setting|default""]",empty document parse,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2799 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-002,
