nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_keeps_already_configured_native_value_formatting|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,acceptance,codex_setup_keeps_already_configured_native_value_formatting,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,1025,1045,"[""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:55-133"", ""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:191-212""]","Takes a fresh setup output, rewrites `type = ""command""` into native single-quoted form with a trailing comment, feeds it back to setup and asserts the emitted bytes are exactly the input.","Reserializing already-configured TOML, which would change quoting/formatting, drop the user's comment and churn a Codex hook trust hash on every setup run.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"Formatting churn forces re-trusting hooks and creates noisy config diffs, but the hooks still work.",Byte equality is a decisive no-change invariant for this claim and would fail on any reserialization.,The formatting dimension is not asserted by the composition or repair rows.,Real CLI and real TOML file.,high,keep,Exact fixed-point assertion on an otherwise unobservable formatting contract; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_preserves_handlers_trust_and_quotes_noop_helper|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_repairs_stale_owned_handler_and_preserves_comments|default""]","[""two setup invocations"", ""string replacement of the whole document"", ""temp HOME""]",0.050,0.050,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:681 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
