nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|matrix_covers_every_declared_setting|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,unit,matrix_covers_every_declared_setting,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,372,437,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/settings.rs:326-340""]","The loader's row catalog is exactly the documented 35 setting keys in order with their exact kinds, and every test-side sample/unset/enum table names a declared setting.","A setting silently disappearing from the loader catalog or changing type without the matrix noticing, so its generated cases vanish.",2,3,3,4,50,80,68,Catalog drift affects settings visibility and the breadth of the generated matrix (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-200).,"Asserts the complete ordered key list and the complete kind list, plus that every matrix table key is declared.",No other test snapshots the whole catalog; the loader unit tests cover individual settings (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1050).,Reads the real loader's default rows (settings::parse) and compares them with the documented catalog.,high,keep,Only whole-catalog snapshot test.,[],"[""generated from the production loader rows""]",0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2878 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|quota_in_instance_identity_is_one_finding_and_configures_nothing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,integration,quota_in_instance_identity_is_one_finding_and_configures_nothing,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,778,803,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:48-130"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1-80""]",A legacy identity file containing [quota] yields one finding keyed 'quota' at line 3 saying it belongs in dashboard.toml while rows stay at defaults; beside a full document the document's values win and the finding persists.,Quota settings in the instance identity file being applied (ghost configuration) or the finding disappearing when a dashboard document exists.,2,4,2,4,50,80,68,The identity-file quota table is inert by design; honoring it would duplicate or override the real consent setting (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:75-95).,"Asserts the single finding key/line/message, rows default with no document, and document values plus the same finding when a full document exists.",tests/provider_quota.rs quota_table_in_instance_identity_is_a_finding_and_starts_no_worker proves the same claim end to end including the worker not starting (tests/provider_quota.rs:598).,Real legacy identity file and document paths through the production loader.,high,keep,Retained for the loader-level rows/finding coexistence assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aprovider_quota|quota_table_in_instance_identity_is_a_finding_and_starts_no_worker|default""]","[""real legacy identity file and document""]",0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2881 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|read_only_document_is_still_read|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,integration,read_only_document_is_still_read,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,849,860,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:48-130""]",A 0444 dashboard.toml loads its full settings with no findings.,"Refusing to read a read-only settings document, so the user sees defaults and believes their configuration was lost.",2,3,3,4,50,80,68,Settings display only; a read-only file is a plausible dotfiles/Nix setup (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:48-90).,Asserts empty findings and row equality with the document's values.,write.rs edits_refuse_dangling_links_and_read_only_targets covers refusing edits to a read-only target; reading it is the complement (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:1073-1131).,Real 0444 file through the production loader.,high,keep,Only read-only read coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Awrite%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aedits_refuse_dangling_links_and_read_only_targets_and_keep_links|default""]","[""one 0444 document""]",0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2883 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|unknown_enum_spelling_is_one_finding_not_a_silent_default|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,unit,unknown_enum_spelling_is_one_finding_not_a_silent_default,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,713,739,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-320""]","Each documented enum spelling loads with no findings, while every near miss in every background yields one finding naming the key/line and containing the misspelling, with only that setting on its invalid row.",An unknown enum spelling silently falling back to the default (for example a near-miss delegation harness or provider appearing to work).,2,4,2,4,50,80,68,Enum near misses are settings-display errors; the user sees the finding in the editor (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-320).,Asserts the accepted spelling has no findings and each near miss produces exactly one named finding plus the invalid row.,settings::tests::unknown_enum_spelling_is_a_finding_not_a_silent_default covers two settings; this covers every enum template and background (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1446).,Runs the production loader over generated enum documents.,high,keep,Broader enum matrix retained; the loader test covers only two settings.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aunknown_enum_spelling_is_a_finding_not_a_silent_default|default""]","[""generated enum matrix""]",0.336,0.336,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2892 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_accepts_exact_payload_limit|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,agent_runner::tests::invocation_channel_accepts_exact_payload_limit,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs,616,638,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:313-420"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:579-599""]","A client that authenticates with the channel token and sends a 65,536-byte request frame gets exactly one handler call with a 65,536-byte input and the handler's reply is written back verbatim.","An off-by-one limit that rejects the documented maximum hook payload, so a maximal hook input is silently dropped and the agent's activity never reaches the server.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"The invocation channel is the hook path that carries agent activity into a session (agent_runner.rs:381-412); a wrong limit loses one report, a bounded failure with the agent still running, so C=2.","The handler asserts `input.len() == 65_536`, the counter must be exactly 1, and the client must read `accepted\n` (agent_runner.rs:622-637) — an inclusive-boundary invariant that fails on either a short read or a premature rejection.","The paired negative at nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_rejects_payload_above_limit_without_allocating_or_dispatching|default covers the other side of the same boundary; accepting the exact limit is the only positive side, so this cannot be dropped. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:641-661.","Real InvocationChannel with a real UnixListener, a connected UnixStream and the production read loop (agent_runner.rs:323-420); the socket framing is the subject (F=4).",high,keep,Exact boundary assertion over the real channel; the counterpart covers rejection only.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_rejects_payload_above_limit_without_allocating_or_dispatching|default""]","Unix socket pair, channel thread, in-process handler",0.198,0.198,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2338 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_rejects_payload_above_limit_without_allocating_or_dispatching|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,agent_runner::tests::invocation_channel_rejects_payload_above_limit_without_allocating_or_dispatching,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs,641,661,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:381-412""]","A declared frame length of 65,537 bytes is refused before allocation or handler dispatch: the connection closes with an empty response and the handler is never called.","Removing or loosening the `length > 65_536` guard, which would allocate an attacker-chosen size and dispatch an oversized hook payload.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"The guard bounds memory and hook work per connection (agent_runner.rs:389-392); a regression costs a rejected hook report or a large allocation, bounded and not durable, so C=2.","`response.is_empty()` and `calls == 0` after the client half-closes (agent_runner.rs:657-660) prove both no reply and no dispatch; a guard that allocated but did not dispatch would still pass, which is the stated limit.",The rejection side of the same limit covered by nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_accepts_exact_payload_limit|default; both sides are needed because either can regress independently. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:616-638.,Real socket against the production accept loop (agent_runner.rs:368-415) (F=4).,high,keep,The negative boundary is asserted through the real listener.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|agent_runner%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvocation_channel_accepts_exact_payload_limit|default""]","Unix socket pair, channel thread",0.064,0.064,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2339 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,claude_recovery::tests::saved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs,189,220,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115""]","Claude launch_options keeps --model and --permission-mode with values, drops a trailing prompt and everything after `--`, and errors for inline --system-prompt/--append-system-prompt/--agents/--settings/--mcp-config values.","Replaying a saved private prompt when a session is resumed, or admitting inline instructions/configuration that would replace the file-reference policy.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"Recovery argv decides what a resumed Claude session is instructed with (claude_recovery.rs:48-115); a wrong option changes that session's behavior but is visible to the user and re-runnable, so C=2.","The exact resulting vector (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:189-201) rejects any kept prompt or lost flag, the trailing-prompt case (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:202-206) pins the empty result, and five per-option errors (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:207-219) pin the refusal set.","Claude-specific option grammar; the same contract for Codex and Pi/Omp lives in nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arecovery_preserves_controls_but_drops_prompts_and_rejects_unsafe_options|default and nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|extension_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arecovery_preserves_explicit_controls_but_never_prompts_or_selectors|default, which have different flag names and error sets. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:267-340.",Direct call to the production launch_options (F=4); no filesystem or process is involved in this branch. Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115.,high,keep,Exact argv equality and per-flag refusals; provider-specific.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arecovery_preserves_controls_but_drops_prompts_and_rejects_unsafe_options|default""]",argument vector construction only,0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2352 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_settings_are_exact_file_references_and_missing_files_fail|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,claude_recovery::tests::saved_settings_are_exact_file_references_and_missing_files_fail,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs,223,254,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115""]","A saved --settings path is canonicalized and emitted as the same file path with spaces preserved, and a settings file that no longer exists makes launch_options fail.","Copying the settings content into argv, substituting a different path, or silently dropping a missing settings file so the resumed session runs without its saved policy.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"The settings file carries the session's permissions/status-line configuration (claude_recovery.rs:48-115); losing it changes the resumed session's policy but is reported and repairable, so C=2.","The exact vector compares against `settings.canonicalize()` (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:223-244) and the post-deletion call must be Err (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:245-253), rejecting both content copying and silent fallback.",Settings-file handling is one distinct option family; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aassigned_read_policy_recovery_retains_disabled_builtins_and_one_exact_mcp_file|default covers --tools/--strict-mcp-config/--mcp-config instead. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:256-292.,"Real temp file with a space in its name, canonicalized by the production function (F=4); the filesystem reference is the subject. Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115.",high,keep,Exact path equality plus the missing-file failure branch.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aassigned_read_policy_recovery_retains_disabled_builtins_and_one_exact_mcp_file|default""]","temp file create, canonicalize, delete",0.019,0.019,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2353 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amanaged_daemon_pid_reads_codex_daemon_pid_file|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,codex_recovery::tests::managed_daemon_pid_reads_codex_daemon_pid_file,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs,395,403,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:209-235""]","managed_daemon_pid accepts a daemon pid file object with pid 1792397 and rejects pid 1, non-JSON and an empty object.","Treating an unrelated or init process recorded in the pid file as the managed Codex daemon, or accepting a malformed file.",2,3,3,4,50,80,68,"The pid identifies which daemon the runtime considers managed (codex_recovery.rs:209-235); a wrong answer could target an unrelated process, but pid 1 and malformed inputs are explicitly refused and the consumer only inspects, C=2.","Four inputs pin the parse and the three rejections (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:394-403); a permissive parser that returned pid 1 or 0 would fail, though a syntactically valid but unrelated pid is still accepted by design.",Only test of the daemon pid parser; the history and argv tests cover different recovery data. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:209-235.,Direct call to the production parser with raw text (F=4); file reading is the caller's concern. Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:209-235.,high,keep,Specific positive and negative parse results for the guard against pid 1.,[],string parsing only,0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2367 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_maps_config_alias_to_parent_directory|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,config::tests::home_maps_config_alias_to_parent_directory,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,693,706,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:71-92"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:192-202""]","Without OVRCR_HOME, an OVRCR_CONFIG=/x/config.toml alias resolves the instance home to its parent /x, records the alias path in notes, and the finding text tells the user to set OVRCR_HOME=/x.","Mapping the alias to the file itself (or to the wrong parent) so the instance directory becomes a file path, and dropping the migration finding that names the replacement variable.",2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"The alias is the compatibility path for existing installations (config.rs:71-92); a wrong parent puts the registry beside the wrong directory, a bounded misconfiguration with the documented OVRCR_HOME fix (C=2).","`assert_eq!(home, Path::new(""/x""))`, `notes.config_alias == Some(""/x/config.toml"")` and the finding containing `OVRCR_HOME=/x` (config.rs:700-705) pin the parent mapping and the guidance text together.","Distinct branch from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_prefers_ovrcr_home_over_config_alias|default (alias present, no explicit home) and from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_defaults_to_platform_config_directory|default (no env at all); the three inputs partition the function. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:681-690.","Direct call to production home_from_env plus config_alias_finding (config.rs:71-92, 192-202); no stand-in (F=4).",high,keep,Every asserted value comes from the production paths and is specific to this branch.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_prefers_ovrcr_home_over_config_alias|default""]","pure function call, no filesystem or process",0.010,0.010,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2372 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_prefers_ovrcr_home_over_config_alias|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,config::tests::home_prefers_ovrcr_home_over_config_alias,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,681,690,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:71-92"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:192-202""]",home_from_env gives an explicit OVRCR_HOME priority over the deprecated OVRCR_CONFIG alias and returns no config_alias note.,Reversing the precedence (or treating the alias as a directory) so a leftover OVRCR_CONFIG selects a different instance while the explicit home is ignored.,2,4,2,4,50,80,68,"Instance selection decides which registry and retained sessions a server opens (config.rs:71-92); choosing the wrong instance points at another instance's durable registry, but the remedy is to unset the alias, so C=2.","`assert_eq!(home, Path::new(""/inst""))` and `assert!(notes.config_alias.is_none())` (config.rs:688-689) reject any precedence inversion and any stray alias note on the explicit-home path.","The other two branches of the same function are covered by nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_maps_config_alias_to_parent_directory|default and nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_defaults_to_platform_config_directory|default, so this is one distinct input of an already covered contract rather than a new failure mode. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:693-706.","It calls the production home_from_env directly (config.rs:71-92) with all three inputs; the decision is pure environment parsing, so the function is the entire subject (F=4).",high,keep,Grounded in the function and its assertions; the branch is unique to this test and no gate applies.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahome_maps_config_alias_to_parent_directory|default""]","pure function call, no filesystem or process",0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2373 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
