nextest|Test|ovrcr-protocol|agent%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areadiness_providers_are_codex_pi_omp_and_claude|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-protocol,lib,unit,agent::tests::readiness_providers_are_codex_pi_omp_and_claude,default,crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/agent.rs,790,804,"[""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/agent.rs:57-68""]","Asserts supports_readiness() for all nine providers: true for Codex, Pi, Omp, Claude, Hermes, CursorCloud and Operator; false for Grok and Cursor.","Flipping which providers may produce reviewable Ready cycles, for example making Grok reviewable without native turn identity or dropping Hermes, which changes alert and review eligibility.",3,3,2,3,75,65,69,"crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/agent.rs:57-68 decides which response cycles become Ready, Unread and review targets, so a wrong provider set misroutes review ownership.","Exhaustive over the enum with exact booleans, so any added or removed provider is visible; it pins the policy table rather than derived behavior.","Row 6 checks the same predicate only for a five-provider subset through validate(), so the full table is distinct but inside an already-covered contract.",Direct production predicate call.,high,keep,Pins the readiness policy for every provider; overlaps row 6 only for a subset.,[],nine-entry provider table loop,0.014,0.014,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2233 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,protocol-terminal-001,
