node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|the%20reattach%20command%20re-announces%20a%20disabled%20producer%20once%20and%20says%20so|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,the reattach command re-announces a disabled producer once and says so,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,365,380,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","After a shutdown disables the producer (a later agent_start emits nothing), ovrcr-reattach delivers one session_start with reason 'reattach', run null and idle true, notifies 'OVRCR reporting reattached', and reporting resumes with a following agent_start.","If reattach did not re-enable the producer, the operator's only in-place recovery would silently do nothing and the live session would stay invisible until it is relaunched, losing the conversation.",3,3,2,3,75,65,69,"Reattach is the recovery path for a retired/dead producer; without it the session must be restarted, which loses the running conversation (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:155-169).","It asserts the disabled state first, then the reattach frame's reason/run/idle, the notice, and the resumed reporting (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:365-380).",The OMP reattach row starts from an open cycle rather than a disabled producer (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:150-164); the re-enable branch is unique here.,"The real command handler, the real transport reattach and a real helper child run; only ctx.ui.notify is recorded by the fixture (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:371-379).",high,keep,Only test of re-enabling a shutdown producer; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|the%20reattach%20command%20re-announces%20this%20producer%20once%20and%20says%20so|default""]",0.023s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.023,0.023,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 22.609583 at macOS-job.log:4293; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|native_glyph_cache_evicts_entries_unused_last_frame|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,native_glyph_cache_evicts_entries_unused_last_frame,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,306,385,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:164-173"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:175-225"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:124-158""]","With the entry cap lowered to 4, four frames over two sets of six glyphs show that frame two keeps set A cached (12 entries), frame three sweeps A down to B's six entries without a re-raster, and frame four rasterizes A again - i.e. the sweep retains entries stamped in the previous frame only.","A sweep that evicted entries in the frame they were used, or no sweep at all, would either re-rasterize every glyph on every frame or grow the cache and its GPU textures without bound over a long session, ending in a stall or memory exhaustion.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"Unbounded texture growth degrades and eventually crashes the GUI process, but sessions live in the server and the user can restart the window, so this is a bounded failure (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:124-134).","The four-frame assertion sequence separates all three plausible defects - no sweep (len stays 12), a too-aggressive sweep (frame three re-rasters B), and a sweep that does nothing until the cap is exceeded - with counts and lengths after each frame (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:340-384).","Only src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:306-385 asserts the sweep; the other cache test at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:264-302 proves hit reuse at the production cap, so the retention rule (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:166-173) has no other protection.","The sweep logic is the production one, but the test-only with_max_entries(4) substitutes the threshold, so the production 4096 cap and a real screen's churn are not exercised (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:147-162).",high,keep,"The only test of the eviction rule, with a decisive frame-by-frame signal; the lowered cap is a scale limit, not redundancy.",[],0.139s one hosted attempt; four paints against a lowered four-entry cache cap,0.139,0.139,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2221 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
