nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aserver_refusals_read_in_plain_words_and_expected_limits_are_not_errors|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::tests::server_refusals_read_in_plain_words_and_expected_limits_are_not_errors,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs,4682,4738,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:937-995"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:905-936""]","Server refusals are rewritten into plain words: a sessions-remain limit names project, branch and session title without a code and stays muted; a conflict becomes an ERROR line in red; paths that merely contain an id are never rewritten; quoted and bare ids resolve correctly.","A real filesystem path being rewritten as a workspace identity, or an expected limit presented as an error (or the reverse), misleading the user's recovery.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,Message presentation is bounded (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:937-995); a misread limit changes which action the user takes next.,"Asserts two exact footer strings and colours, plus five preserved-path cases and three rewrite cases (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs:4682-4735).",The failed-recovery row covers one error classification; the path-preservation and identifier-rewrite matrix is unique (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:937-995).,Calls production plain_error and the footer draw path through TestBackend (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:937-995).,high,keep,"Kept: criticality 2 and derived usefulness 85 do not meet the prune gate, and no test named in the uniqueness note covers the same assertion and input (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:937-995).","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aa_failed_recovery_relaunch_is_an_error_not_a_limit|default""]","[""TestBackend 120x24 footer reads""]",0.025,0.025,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3360 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-006,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20next%20start%20racing%20an%20un-awaited%20end%20opens%20a%20new%20cycle%3B%20the%20settled%20end%20keeps%20run%201|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a next start racing an un-awaited end opens a new cycle; the settled end keeps run 1,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,452,469,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","When agent_end is not awaited and the next agent_start lands while its helper is in flight, the wire order is start 1, end 1, settled 1, start 2: the settled frame belongs to run 1 even though run 2 has already opened.","If the settled frame captured producer.run at delivery time instead of framing it synchronously, it would carry run 2 and the receiver would settle the new cycle instead of the finished one.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"A settled frame attributed to the wrong run closes the wrong cycle, so the finished turn stays open and the new turn is reported complete (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:59-72, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:65-80).",The exact four-frame event/run sequence under a real race (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:452-469) is precisely the case that a delivery-time frame build breaks.,"The will-continue row covers sequential continuations; this row covers the concurrent start/end race, which is a distinct ordering boundary; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:59-72, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport with real helper children; the race is produced by not awaiting the emit (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:459-467).,high,keep,Only test of the concurrent start/end frame attribution; keep.,[],0.025s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.025,0.025,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 24.808625 at macOS-job.log:3849; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20switch%20names%20the%20conversation%20it%20left%20by%20id%2C%20never%20by%20its%20file%20path|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,"a switch names the conversation it left by id, never by its file path",default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,89,109,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A startup announcement carries previous = null, and a resume switch carries previous = 'sess-a' extracted from '/private/x/2026-09-13T00-00-00-000Z_sess-a.jsonl', with no directory, timestamp or .jsonl suffix anywhere in the frame body.","If idOf were replaced by the raw filename, the frame would carry a user path and timestamp; a receiver that also paused on the wrong conversation would stop the wrong session, and the path is the kind of host detail this channel must never carry.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"The previous-conversation expectation decides which conversation OVRCR pauses on a switch; a path or a wrong id pauses or binds the wrong one (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:47-48, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:27-32).","It asserts the exact previous values for startup and resume and then three body-level exclusions (directory, timestamp, .jsonl) from the recorded bytes (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:89-109), which catches both a wrong id and a leak.","The Pi analogue covers the same transport helper with a UUID-shaped name (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:324-344); OMP's session_switch carries the file itself, so this branch is distinct.","The real extension and the real idOf helper run; only the host event is synthesized, and the assertion reads the actual delivered JSON (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:97-108).",high,keep,Decisive positive and negative assertions on the switch identity; keep.,[],0.018s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 17.524792 at macOS-job.log:3723; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20end%20that%20will%20continue%20keeps%20the%20cycle%20open%3B%20the%20final%20end%20settles%20it%20as%20observed%20work|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an end that will continue keeps the cycle open; the final end settles it as observed work,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,350,377,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A willContinue end emits agent_end with run 1, outcome ok and will_continue true without closing the cycle; the next start stays run 1, the final end emits will_continue false followed by agent_settled in the same run, and a later start opens run 2, with schema/mode/pid/session/instance asserted on every frame.","If a willContinue end closed the cycle, OVRCR would publish a settled Ready for a turn OMP is still continuing, so the Dashboard would show completed work and the user's follow-up would race the running turn.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,The cycle boundary decides when OVRCR reports a response as ready; a premature settled event is a false completion signal that the receiver treats as observed work (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:59-72).,The six-frame event/run/outcome/will_continue sequence plus a per-frame metadata sweep and the run-2 tail (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:350-377) is a complete cycle invariant.,"The Pi provider closes cycles on agent_settled instead (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:119-124), so OMP's continue semantics are a different protocol and have no other test.","Real handlers and transport; frames delivered by a real helper, with the instance/owner_pid asserted against the actual process (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:364-371).",high,keep,Complete cycle-accounting invariant for OMP's continuation protocol; keep.,[],0.046s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.046,0.046,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 46.036375 at macOS-job.log:3819; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|tree%20navigation%20invalidates%20the%20response%20cycle%20and%20carries%20only%20idleness|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,tree navigation invalidates the response cycle and carries only idleness,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,124,148,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","After agent_start opens run 1, a session_tree emits cycle_invalidated with run 1 and idle false, then the next agent_start opens run 2, and leaf ids, the old leaf and the summary text never appear in any frame.","If tree navigation left the cycle open, a later agent_end would settle a turn for a conversation branch the producer no longer owns, and a frame that copied newLeafId/summaryEntry would publish branch content OVRCR never asked for.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,A cycle that survives tree navigation makes OVRCR publish a Ready for a discarded branch; the carried idleness is what lets the receiver show the session as idle rather than running (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:111-116).,"The exact event/run/idle triples plus three secret-substring exclusions (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:124-148) reject a missing invalidation, a wrong run and any content leak.",Same handler shape exists for Pi (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:346-363) but over a different module and event payload; neither covers the other's file.,"The real session_tree handler runs against a synthesized event carrying the secrets, and the assertions inspect the frames actually delivered by the helper (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:130-147).",high,keep,Decisive invalidation-and-redaction assertions; keep.,[],0.031s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.031,0.031,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 31.140083 at macOS-job.log:3735; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|current%20continuation%20and%20scoped%20legacy%20gaps%20both%20reach%20startup%20context|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,current continuation and scoped legacy gaps both reach startup context,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,78,88,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","A response with one workflow plus scoped legacy gaps reconciles the workflow (epoch 4) and the injected before_agent_start context carries the objective, a handle, the gap's original request and its reason.","If scoped gaps were dropped when a workflow was found, the model would act without knowing that some legacy work could not be certified, and would not reconcile it.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"Missing gap context makes the resumed model act on incomplete reconciliation; the workflow itself is correctly restored, so the consequence is incomplete context rather than wrong authority (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:33-40, 71-79).","It asserts both the state and four substrings in the injected context (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:78-88), covering the merge of workflows and gaps.","The legacy-only row covers no workflow; this row is the both-present case, which a 'gaps only when no workflow' implementation passes the other test with; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real reconcile merge and the real context builder run with a fake response (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, 71-79).",high,keep,Distinct merge boundary of workflow plus scoped gaps; keep.,[],0.000290042s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.000290042,0.000290042,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.290042 at macOS-job.log:3903; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_interrupt_extension.mjs|missing%2C%20uninitialized%20or%20broken%20optional%20APIs%20produce%20a%20bounded%20unavailable%20result|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,node,unit,"missing, uninitialized or broken optional APIs produce a bounded unavailable result",default,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,36,50,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:1-59"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-112""]","Undefined, null, getting a null manager, a manager without getDefinition, a throwing getter, a manager whose getDefinition returns undefined, and malformed getKeys values all yield 'Unavailable'; a throwing matches also yields 'Unavailable'.","If a broken optional API threw out of the inspection, it would abort the agent_start reporting path; if it returned 'Escape' on a missing definition, OVRCR would claim an interrupt the host does not have.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"The inspection runs inside the reporting handler; an escaped exception or an optimistic result degrades a report or overstates control, bounded to the interrupt field (src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:36-56).",Ten degraded shapes including oversized and empty key lists and a throwing matches are asserted to collapse to one bounded value (tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs:36-50).,"The Escape and preemption rows cover valid managers; the broken-shape enumeration is unique; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:36-56, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real try/catch and shape checks run; only the manager is a fixture (src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:36-56).,high,keep,Comprehensive negative coverage of the optional API contract; keep.,[],0.000206584s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.000206584,0.000206584,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.206584 at macOS-job.log:4041; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_observation_extension.mjs|wait%20AbortSignal%20cancels%20observation%20only%20and%20disconnection%20wake%20carries%20no%20error%20body|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,node,unit,wait AbortSignal cancels observation only and disconnection wake carries no error body,default,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,109,122,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:1-147"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:236-239""]","An explicit wait rejects with AbortError when its signal aborts, no non-Observe call is made, and after a failed observation the wake carries status 'disconnected' with no error text.","If the abort were treated as a control failure the observer might retry control or notify an error body; if disconnection produced no wake, the parent would never learn that observation stopped.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"Cancellation must not mutate control, and a disconnect must still surface a content-free signal so the parent can reconcile later (src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:111-123, 90-99).","It asserts the AbortError name, the Observe-only call list, the disconnected status and the absence of 'error' in the content (tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs:109-122).","The synchronous-delivery-failure row covers a throwing sendMessage; this row covers an aborted wait and a transport rejection; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:111-123, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real wait()/start() abort plumbing runs against the fixture's abortable call stub (tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs:14-35).,high,keep,Only coverage of wait cancellation and disconnection signalling; keep.,[],0.001s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.001,0.001,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.747792 at macOS-job.log:4077; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|resume%20and%20fork%20announce%20the%20conversation%20without%20a%20cycle%3B%20a%20run%20whose%20last%20assistant%20errored%20is%20an%20error|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,resume and fork announce the conversation without a cycle; a run whose last assistant errored is an error,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,275,291,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A resume session_start delivers reason 'resume', run null, no previousSessionFile field and no path text; the following cycle is run 1 and settles error because the last assistant errored.","If the announcement kept the host's previousSessionFile or opened a run, the receiver would treat a resume as a turn and could pause on a path it was never meant to see; a wrong outcome hides the error.",2,4,3,3,50,85,71,A resume announcement must reset cycle state (run null) while still carrying the conversation; conflating it with a turn corrupts the published sequence (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:94-104).,"It asserts the reason, run null, the absence of the previousSessionFile key and old-path text, then the three-frame error cycle (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:275-291).","The OMP suite has no resume/fork announcement row; the continuation suite covers fork's pointer behaviour, not the reporting frame; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:94-104, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport with a synthetic resume event and a real helper child (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:280-290).,high,keep,Only coverage of the resume announcement contract; keep.,[],0.028s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.028,0.028,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 27.979708 at macOS-job.log:4263; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|cache-hit-local-profile%3Aln221|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,cache-hit-local-profile:ln221,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,221,221,"[""native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:221-221"", ""scripts/package-startup.sh:26-62""]","With an intact local payload whose source.sha256 matches the local-profile fingerprint, the check runs the real scripts/package-startup.sh --local-development and requires exit 0, no builder invocation, payload bytes unchanged, no leftover stage directory and no process left in the spawned group.",A cache that rebuilds on every request (or leaves a stage/child behind) when the pinned fingerprint and the relocated validator already agree.,2,4,3,3,50,85,71,"A spurious rebuild costs build time and could publish a different artifact, but it is not a wrong-target install; bounded (2).","native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:196-220 asserts the exit code, an exact 65536-byte output bound, byte-identical payload, empty stage glob and empty owned process-group listing, plus the absent builder call.",Only cache-hit test for package-startup.sh.,"Runs the real script with the real fingerprint/validator, but the build step is an intercepted fail-closed fake (the script's comment says it never reaches Swift, signing or a native lifecycle).",high,keep,"Only cache-hit test for package-startup.sh, including no-build, unchanged payload and no lingering process group.",[],spawns package-startup.sh with a symlinked PATH and a fake builder; scans ps and payload hashes,,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|doctor_reports_partial_config_proof_and_any_version_without_secrets|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,acceptance,doctor_reports_partial_config_proof_and_any_version_without_secrets,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,187,266,"[""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:472-531"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:532-554"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:555-643"", ""src/report/admission.rs:215-232"", ""src/report/versions.rs:13-31""]","Loops four Claude version strings (including the untested 2.1.293) through `agent doctor claude --json --session 1 --executable`, with an async Stop hook, a private permissions value and OVRCR_HOOK_TOKEN set; asserts probe_status, version, tested_versions, version_gate none, absence of version_compatible/compatible_versions, resume forms, the Stop async issue, session_not_found, no secret substring and no socket; then probes a missing executable.","Reintroducing a version gate (version_compatible fields or refusing an untested release), drifting tested_versions, certifying an async hook, fabricating a session state, echoing the hook token or a settings value into JSON, or starting a server during doctor.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Doctor JSON is the repair surface for managed reporting; a false certified configuration leaves sessions untracked, and the reporter token is a credential that must never appear in output.","Four version cases plus a missing-executable branch assert exact positive and negative fields, and a whole-stdout scan rejects the secret; the version matrix partly repeats row 12.",Its unique contribution is configuration issues plus redaction plus session status in one Claude doctor run; the version evidence overlaps row 12 and tests/cli.rs claude_doctor_reports_exact_version_and_both_resume_forms.,Real CLI spawned against a synthetic claude executable; the provider is a controlled fixture but the diagnostic path is real.,high,keep,Grounded coverage of the doctor contract including credential redaction; overlapping version assertions are partial and do not replace the config/secret assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|doctor_reports_tested_releases_as_evidence_and_gates_no_version|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_doctor_defaults_dispatch_and_reports_versions_without_gate_server_or_secrets|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acli|claude_doctor_reports_exact_version_and_both_resume_forms|default""]","[""spawns doctor four plus one times"", ""spawns a fake claude shell per case"", ""temp HOME""]",0.186,0.186,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:689 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_repairs_stale_owned_claude_statusline_without_wrapping_it|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,integration,setup_repairs_stale_owned_claude_statusline_without_wrapping_it,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,909,920,"[""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:311-470"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:266-294""]","Supplies a marked statusLine pointing at `/old installation/ovrcr` with `--render-command 'printf renderer'` and refreshInterval 15, then asserts setup replaces the stale path, keeps the renderer argument and the interval, and is idempotent.","Wrapping an already-marked statusline in a second `--render-command` (nested invocation), dropping the user's renderer or refreshInterval, or leaving the deleted installation path in place.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"A double-wrapped statusline breaks context/quota reporting while the configuration still looks owned, and a stale path points at a binary that no longer exists.","Repair, renderer retention, interval retention and an idempotent rerun are asserted; there is no negative case for multi-marked commands.",Repairs a distinct branch (marked prefix repair) from row 0's arbitrary renderer and row 1's legacy migration.,Real CLI and real settings file; no simulation of the claim.,high,keep,Small but non-redundant branch with a precise retention assertion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_preserves_settings_and_external_renderer_bytes_once|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_migrates_only_exact_legacy_statusline_and_marks_hooks|default""]","[""two setup invocations"", ""temp HOME""]",0.048,0.048,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:696 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
