nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|restore_without_reporting_executes_native_picker_in_shell|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,restore_without_reporting_executes_native_picker_in_shell,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,2516,2518,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1515-1690"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/recovery.rs:89-205"", ""tests/retained_sessions.rs:2526-2580""]","A restored agent without reporting runs the provider's native resume picker inside the surviving shell; after the agent exits, the same terminal accepts shell input.",The restore replacing the shell (so no interactive terminal remains) or running the wrong command.,3,3,2,4,75,70,72,A restored session must land in a usable shell; losing it strands the user's workspace (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/lifecycle.rs:600-650).,"Asserts the initial exit output, the native picker output after reopen, and a following shell command's output (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2516-2518 with assert_native_picker_in_shell at 2526-2580).",The sh-shell native-picker case is one shell variant of the helper test; the zsh case covers the other (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2522-2524).,"Real binary, real shell and a real provider fixture; the process boundary is the subject (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/lifecycle.rs:600-650).",high,keep,Covers the sh restore path end to end.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|restore_native_picker_in_zsh_after_loading_user_configuration|default""]",A real shell and two PTY interactions,4.084,4.084,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1434 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-006,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_short_resume_on_2_1_268_preserves_argv_and_lifecycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_admission_short_resume_on_2_1_268_preserves_argv_and_lifecycle,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9361,9363,"[""src/report/admission.rs:88-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]","The same resume flow with the short `-r` flag on Claude 2.1.268: argv starts with -r and the canonical uuid, the matching resume root binds, and the lifecycle through clear/branch transitions matches the long-flag case.","Short-form resume could be missed by eligibility parsing, so the invocation is treated as a fresh session and usage/identity diverge.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Mishandling -r breaks resume for users of the short flag, resuming as a new conversation (src/report/admission.rs:88-190).","Asserts argv and the bound conversation, but not the usage totals that the long-flag row also checks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9535-9560).",Distinct short-flag input within the resume contract already covered by the long-flag row (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9356-9363).,Real native fixture and real resume callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9370-9410).,high,keep,The only short-flag resume input; cheap and distinct.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_explicit_resume_preserves_argv_and_collects_conversation_usage|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_later_patch_preserves_resume_identity_and_lifecycle|default""]","[""real native fixture"", ""resume callbacks"", ""env_lock serialization""]",5.375,5.375,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1449 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_startup_registration_is_visible|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,agent_hook_startup_registration_is_visible,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,931,950,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:958-1000"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:466-479""]",A hook child that reports Busy during startup makes activity Busy visible through List before the terminal prints HOOK_READY; after KillSession the retained terminal still contains HOOK_READY and the process group is absent.,"Startup reports could be lost or not published before the first listing, so the dashboard shows Unknown for a busy agent; kill could drop final terminal text.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Lost startup activity leaves the sidebar claiming an idle agent while it works, a major workflow misreport (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:968-985).",Asserts only the Busy value plus final terminal text; it does not assert revision or ordering of the SessionChanged publication (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:935-948).,Distinct startup timing within the report contract already covered by the ordering test (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:931-950).,"Real ignored test-binary child, PTY and server socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5936-5998).",high,keep,Small but genuine startup-visibility boundary not covered by the sequencing test.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_sequence_does_not_regress_state|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_round_trip_survives_dashboard_reconnect|default""]","[""ignored test-binary hook child"", ""real PTY and Unix socket"", ""polling terminal text""]",2.669,2.669,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1452 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_doctor_names_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_doctor_names_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17595,17662,"[""src/cli/managed.rs:40-80"", ""src/report/admission.rs:240-300""]","Claude doctor reports bound/Connected with no reason when healthy; after a branch it reports reporting_unavailable and identity_transition_unavailable with unchanged binding, and remediation naming the foreground conversation and a fresh supervised invocation but not configuration repair; a later prompt leaves the freeze; the session stays Running.","Doctor could advise a configuration repair that cannot fix an identity freeze, or report a frozen reporter as connected.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,Wrong remediation sends users through futile repair while reporting stays frozen (src/cli/managed.rs:40-80).,Asserts JSON status/health/reason and three remediation substrings plus post-freeze stability (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17600-17660).,"Claude doctor variant; codex and pi rows assert their own remediation text (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14122-14219, :15748-15820).",Real compiled doctor CLI against a real claude session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17597-17620).,high,keep,Grounded provider-specific remediation assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_doctor_inspects_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_doctor_reports_bound_lifecycle_activity_and_transport_loss|default""]","[""two doctor CLI runs"", ""claude helper callbacks""]",3.332,3.332,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1459 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_doctor_inspects_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,codex_doctor_inspects_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,14122,14219,"[""src/cli/managed.rs:40-80"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:520-560""]","`agent doctor codex --json` for a healthy binding reports bound/Connected with no reason and no conversation or invocation fields; after an unsupported fork it reports reporting_unavailable with identity_transition_unavailable, the same binding, and remediation naming the foreground conversation, configuration non-recovery and the exact launch command; a later prompt leaves the freeze in place.","Doctor could print private conversation fields, or report a frozen reporter as healthy / suggest an ineffective configuration repair.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Misdiagnosing reporting health leads users to restart or repair the wrong thing, and leaked conversation ids expose private sessions (src/cli/managed.rs:40-80).","Asserts JSON fields and absence of the two conversation ids, plus three remediation substrings and post-freeze stability (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14125-14215).","Provider-specific doctor variant; the pi and claude doctor rows assert different lifecycle fields (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15748-15820, :17595-17662).",Real compiled doctor CLI against a real bound codex session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14130-14150).,high,keep,Grounded diagnostic assertions with a privacy check; distinct provider output.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_doctor_reports_bound_lifecycle_activity_and_transport_loss|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_doctor_names_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default""]","[""compiled doctor CLI runs"", ""real hook callbacks""]",3.503,3.503,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1472 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_duplicate_hello_does_not_write_from_reader_thread|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,dashboard_duplicate_hello_does_not_write_from_reader_thread,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,6097,6133,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:186-215"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:431-450""]","First dashboard hello succeeds; a second connection hello receives a Conflict response within 250ms, proving the refusal is written through the dashboard writer rather than from the reader thread.","A duplicate hello answered from the reader thread could interleave frames with the writer, corrupting the dashboard stream, or a second dashboard could claim the slot.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Two writers on one dashboard socket corrupt every subsequent frame, breaking the only UI path (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:186-215).","Asserts the Conflict response arrives promptly, which is the observable of writer-side delivery; it does not inspect which thread wrote (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6097-6130).",Overlaps the same-connection sole-writer row; only the second-connection variant is distinct (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6227-6272).,Real server thread and two real Unix connections (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6099-6115).,high,keep,Grounded second-connection refusal; the writer-thread attribution is inferred from timing.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|duplicate_dashboard_hello_uses_the_sole_writer|default""]","[""real server thread"", ""two dashboard sockets"", ""250ms response deadline""]",1.273,1.273,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1490 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|duplicate_dashboard_hello_uses_the_sole_writer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,duplicate_dashboard_hello_uses_the_sole_writer,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,6227,6272,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:186-215"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:147-175""]","A dashboard hello returns a hierarchy and consumes the settings reading; a second hello on the same connection is answered Conflict through the same writer, after which the connection is torn down.","A repeated hello on the owning connection could create a second writer or be answered out of band, corrupting the stream.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,A second writer or out-of-band answer on the dashboard socket corrupts the UI stream (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:186-215).,"Asserts the first greeting, the queued settings reading, and the Conflict for the duplicate hello (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6227-6270).","Same-connection variant of the duplicate-hello contract, which the reader-thread row also covers (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6097-6133).",Real server thread and real dashboard connection with settings publication (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6229-6245).,high,keep,Grounded owner-connection refusal with greeting and settings ordering.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_duplicate_hello_does_not_write_from_reader_thread|default""]","[""real server thread"", ""dashboard socket"", ""event draining helper""]",1.820,1.820,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1526 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|fast_exit_session_is_retained_as_exited|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,fast_exit_session_is_retained_as_exited,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2679,2722,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1643-1686"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:643-700""]","A session that prints and exits immediately is observed as Exited and can be acknowledged and removed; then the remaining local shell is killed, removed, and the workspace is removed successfully.","A fast exit could race retention so the record or its output is lost (or the row sticks forever), blocking workspace removal.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Lost fast-exit records lose user-visible output and block cleanup, a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1643-1686).","Asserts Exited observation and the full acknowledge/remove/teardown sequence, but not the retained output text (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2683-2720).","Fast-exit trigger is distinct, though the retained-row contract is already covered by the restart test (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2187-2224).",Real PTY that exits immediately and real retention/registry teardown (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2685-2690).,high,keep,Grounded race coverage of exit-vs-retention ordering.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_without_kill_allows_retained_exited_records|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|control_lifecycle_enforces_every_removal_gate|default""]","[""real fast-exit PTY"", ""full teardown sequence""]",2.843,2.843,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1532 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_managed_launch_inserts_its_extension_and_removes_it|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,omp_managed_launch_inserts_its_extension_and_removes_it,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17709,17761,"[""src/report/omp.rs:24-47"", ""src/report/extension.rs:48-95""]","An omp managed launch prepends exactly one -e with an ovrcr-omp-reporting.mjs path, keeps --model x/y, exits 17, and removes the materialized extension file and directory afterwards.","The extension could be inserted twice or left behind, leaking the reporting entrypoint and polluting later launches.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,A leaked extension file or duplicate -e changes the native launch and can report from a stale entrypoint (src/report/extension.rs:48-95).,"Asserts argv prefix/tail, exact extension basename and directory removal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17715-17755).","Omp launch-shape row; the pi row additionally asserts env, RPC mode and plain launch (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11542-11629).",Real compiled agent run with a scripted omp that records its argv (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17710-17735).,high,keep,Grounded launch cleanup check; small but distinct provider entrypoint.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_launch_preserves_argv_exit_and_environment_and_plain_launch_is_untracked|default""]","[""real compiled CLI session"", ""filesystem polling""]",3.006,3.006,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1550 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_ready_alerts_once_and_creates_unread|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,omp_ready_alerts_once_and_creates_unread,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17665,17706,"[""src/report/omp.rs:24-47"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-700""]",Omp: a settled cycle delivers one host alert and Unread; a repeated end reaches no open cycle and republishes nothing; CLI list matches the Unread; the visible focused-pane case still alerts.,"A repeated end could re-alert and replace Unread, or a visible pane could suppress a genuinely new completion.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,Duplicate completions create phantom attention and a missed one hides finished work (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-700).,"Asserts host-call count, snapshot equality after the duplicate, and CLI Unread equality (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17670-17700).",Omp ready-alert row; the larger omp extension row covers cycle semantics without a host (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15882-16022).,"Real omp host, dashboard host record and real PTY (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17665-17680).",high,keep,Grounded alert-once evidence for omp.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_managed_extension_reports_observed_ready_continuations_switches_and_child_inertness|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_ready_alerts_once_creates_unread_and_explicit_review_clears_only_presented|default""]","[""node omp host"", ""dashboard host record""]",3.861,3.861,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1551 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_shutdown_cleans_stopped_groups|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_shutdown_cleans_stopped_groups,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4013,4062,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1988-2095"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1560""]","Two paused sessions are shut down with kill:true; both groups report TERM_ACK plus descendant final markers, both groups disappear, the server joins and the socket is removed.",Server shutdown could leave paused groups behind (shutdown returns Ok while children survive) or skip SIGCONT for stopped groups.,3,3,2,4,75,70,72,Paused groups surviving shutdown leave orphaned processes after the terminal is gone (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2035-2095).,"Asserts acknowledgements for four peers, group absence for both, server join and socket removal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4017-4060).",Shutdown path over paused groups; kill semantics themselves are covered by the paused-kill row (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:3931-4010).,Real paused process groups and a real server shutdown (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4015-4055).,high,keep,"Grounded shutdown coverage for stopped groups, distinct entry point.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_kill_terminates_sessions_concurrently|default""]","[""four stopped real peers"", ""datagram acknowledgement collection"", ""server join wait""]",3.088,3.088,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1557 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_doctor_reports_bound_lifecycle_activity_and_transport_loss|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_doctor_reports_bound_lifecycle_activity_and_transport_loss,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15748,15820,"[""src/cli/managed.rs:40-80"", ""src/report/extension.rs:98-180""]","Pi doctor: unbound reports a run-pi remediation; after session_start it reports bound, provider Pi, extension loaded_and_bound, delivery observed, activity Idle, Connected, unread false, version tested; after a cycle activity ResponseReady and unread true; after shutdown:quit health still Connected; after native exit Unavailable with a fresh-launch remediation while unread stays true.","Doctor could report an unbound session as bound, mislabel delivery health, or claim a review/response state that does not exist.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,Wrong lifecycle diagnosis leads users to restart healthy sessions or trust a dead reporter (src/cli/managed.rs:40-80).,"Asserts seven lifecycle fields across four states, including quit-not-loss and loss-keeps-Unread (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15755-15815).","Pi doctor variant; codex and claude rows assert different remediation/fields (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14122-14219, :17595-17662).",Real compiled doctor CLI against a real pi host session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15750-15770).,high,keep,Grounded diagnostic contract with state transitions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_doctor_inspects_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_doctor_names_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default""]","[""four doctor CLI runs"", ""node pi host""]",3.790,3.790,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1560 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
