python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|local-production-validation-rejected%3Aln108|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,local-production-validation-rejected:ln108,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,108,109,"[""native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:108-109"", ""native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:18-38""]","A relocated local-development payload is passed to the validator without --local-development, and because the copied expected-contract.json sets local_development=true the validator must exit nonzero.","A validator that ignores the contract's local_development field or the profile argument, so a local-profile payload validates as a production release.",3,3,2,4,75,70,72,"Accepting a local-development build as production ships the wrong profile (its marker and identity differ), an untrusted/wrong artifact (3).",native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:108-109 invokes the real validator through the reject_validation helper and increments the check count only on a nonzero exit; native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:32-34 asserts the contract profile matches the invocation.,"native/bridge/check-installer.py:753-766 covers production-refuses-local at the installer gate; this row is the validator gate on a relocated copy, a distinct boundary (2).",Real relocated bundle plus the production validator subprocess.,high,keep,Only validator-level evidence that a local contract cannot pass production validation on a relocated copy.,"[""python-unittest|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-installer.py%3A%3AInstallerTests|test_local_refuses_production_artifact|default""]",copies a payload tree; spawns the validator subprocess,,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|missing-entitlements-rejected%3Aln56|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,missing-entitlements-rejected:ln56,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,54,57,"[""native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:20-89""]",Deleting the payload's entitlement resource makes the validator reject the relocated bundle.,A payload shipping without its entitlement file accepted (automation would fail at signing/authorization).,3,4,1,4,75,70,72,The entitlement file is required at the pinned resource path (native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:62).,"Asserts rejection after removal, then restores the bytes.",Same removal on the local payload (native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:54-57).,Real payload mutation and validator.,high,keep,Mostly redundant with the production case; kept as the local-payload execution.,[],"[""copies the packaged payload to a temp dir and runs the validator""]",,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|native_glyph_cache_keeps_a_screen_of_distinct_glyphs|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,native_glyph_cache_keeps_a_screen_of_distinct_glyphs,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,264,302,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:147-225"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1013-1020""]","Painting a 40x30 screen of 600 distinct CJK glyphs rasterizes exactly 600 glyphs on the first frame, and a second paint of the same screen reuses the cache with zero further rasterizations.","A cache that misses on repeated frames (a per-paint map, or a key that includes the cell or rect) would run 600 CoreText rasterizations and texture uploads every frame for a CJK or emoji screen, collapsing the GUI's frame rate on exactly the content this fallback exists for.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"The consequence is GUI performance on non-ASCII screens, recoverable by using the TUI; it does not corrupt state, so it stays below the major-workflow band (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:147-160).","It is a complete invariant for the cache-hit claim: exactly 600 rasters on frame one and an unchanged count on frame two (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:283-301), so any per-frame re-rasterization or missed reuse is caught.","Distinct from the eviction test at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:306-385: this one (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:264-302) proves hit reuse at the production cap, while the eviction test proves the sweep with a lowered cap; no other suite touches NativeGlyphs (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:129-225).","paint_terminal and NativeGlyphs::paint run for real against CoreText; the only test instrument is the cfg(test) rasterize_calls counter, which observes rather than replaces the behaviour (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:129-135, 190-193).",high,keep,Decisive invariant for a real GUI performance failure mode with no other protection; keep.,[],"0.450s one hosted attempt; rasterizes 600 distinct CJK glyphs through CoreText in one paint, twice painted",0.450,0.450,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2222 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|terminal_paints_missing_unicode_as_native_images|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,unit,terminal_paints_missing_unicode_as_native_images,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,190,193,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1007-1113"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:175-225"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:281-355""]","paint_terminal paints CJK and emoji cells missing from the outline font through the CoreText fallback as exactly two image meshes, each inside its wide cell, keeping the terminal red for the CJK glyph and the emoji's own colours; it does this both with the nerd fonts installed and with plain monospace.","A fallback that stops producing native artwork (replacement galleys instead), draws at the wrong column, stretches a glyph into one cell, or drops the cell foreground turns 界 and 🙂 into white boxes or misplaced glyphs, making non-Latin terminal output unreadable in the GUI.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"Reading CJK or emoji output is a real workflow, but only non-ASCII content is affected and the same session can be read in the TUI, so this is a bounded feature failure (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:1051-1092).","The assertions are decisive: exactly two meshes, per-column bounds with a one-pixel tolerance, the clip rect, non-empty texture pixels, red foreground for 界 and a colour gradient for 🙂 (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:224-259), so a mesh-free fallback, a one-cell draw or a monochrome emoji is rejected.","Only src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:196-260 checks what the native fallback paints; the cache tests at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:264-302 and src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:306-385 count rasterizations, and the icon test at src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:388-427 checks shape ordering, so glyph placement and colour fidelity are protected here alone.","It runs the production paint_terminal and rasterize with real CoreText and real egui texture upload, i.e. the full OS text-rendering boundary the claim is about (src/bin/ovrcr-gui/native_glyph.rs:281-355).",high,keep,"Precise, high-fidelity protection of the native fallback's placement and colour, with no equivalent coverage; keep.",[],0.137s one hosted attempt; two full paints including real CoreText rasterization of the CJK glyph and the emoji,0.137,0.137,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2225 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|a_live_managed_claude_session_suppresses_the_probe|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,acceptance,a_live_managed_claude_session_suppresses_the_probe,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,720,839,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:27-39"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:100-143"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/claude_allowance.rs:110-145""]","With the probe enabled and a dashboard not yet attached, asserts no probe ran and that the probe count is still zero after a 300 ms settle; then starts a managed Claude session through a real `agent run` child that reports a statusline payload with rate_limits, selects the session, waits for a Current row whose source is Session, asserts the five_hour window is present, and requires the probe count to stay zero.","Running the hidden probe even though a live managed Claude session already supplies quota (duplicate provider use and contradictory rows), or failing to surface the session-sourced reading.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"A missing suppression spends one extra probe prompt and leaves a hidden conversation in the user's Claude history (docs/provider-quota.md:28) and can show a probe row instead of the session row; both are bounded and avoidable with quota.claude.probe=false (tests/claude_quota_probe.rs:720-838), so C=2.","Waits for an exact source/state pair with window identity, and the probe count is checked before attach, after the session reports, and after a 400 ms settle.","The only end-to-end session-suppression test for fresh_managed_claude (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:27-51); the attach-gating and cadence siblings cover other branches, so the failure mode is distinct but the suppression preconditions are partially covered (U=3).","Real server, real managed `agent run` session and PTY, and a real probe-absence check (tests/claude_quota_probe.rs:720-838); the fake native Claude is the controlled provider and the suppression decision itself is the subject (F=4).",high,keep,Covers the highest-precedence quota source end to end; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_does_not_run_before_a_dashboard_attaches|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_waits_for_usage_after_the_startup_callback|default""]","[""creates a managed agent session through an ignored helper test binary"", ""dashboard select"", ""probe count polling"", ""6.08 s observed""]",6.078,6.078,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:734 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
