nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|context_snapshot_survives_dashboard_reattach|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,context_snapshot_survives_dashboard_reattach,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,1381,1540,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:958-998"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:104-200""]",A context report raises a SessionChanged event carrying the snapshot; an equal-count resend updates only received_unix_ms; after a half-close and drain the reconnected hello carries the same snapshot; on exit the retained row keeps it and a later report is refused with Conflict.,A dashboard reconnect could lose the context snapshot or restamp unchanged values; a late report could mutate an exited record.,2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Lost or restamped context display is a bounded feature failure with a dashboard reattach workaround.,"Asserts event snapshot, strict timestamp advancement, equality after reattach, and refusal with the retained value intact (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1390-1525).","Only row covering the dashboard event plus reattach path for context, distinct from summary-only reads (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1381-1540).","Real dashboard socket with half-close and drain, real server and hook session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1400-1445).",high,keep,Grounded reattach/event coverage with precise state-preserving assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|context_report_replaces_snapshot_and_preserves_activity|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|context_report_rejects_old_and_invalid_samples|default""]","[""ignored test-binary hook child"", ""dashboard socket half-close and drain"", ""event loop reads with timeouts""]",2.610,2.610,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1488 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_queued_ready_and_input_without_replay|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_queued_ready_and_input_without_replay,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18547,18632,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:86-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130""]","With one delivery gated, a queued session readies then starts work, opens an input request and closes it; when the gate releases, only the first completion is delivered; later accepted input and Ready produce exactly three deliveries (first, later input, later Ready) with the queued cancelled candidates absent, each carrying sound tap and correct session body.",Cancelled queued ready/input candidates could still reach the host later (stale notifications) or cancel the wrong in-flight delivery.,2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Replayed cancelled notifications are a bounded annoyance; the strong invariant is ordering against the delivery barrier (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130).,"Asserts exact delivery count, titles in order, per-request sound, session body ids and absence of independent audio (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18600-18630).",Only row covering cancellation of queued ready+input candidates (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18547-18632).,"Real gated host process, real dashboard PTY and real callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18549-18570).",high,keep,Grounded cancellation ordering with exact title sequence.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_each_in_flight_lane_and_preserves_the_persistent_host|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_managed_completion_reaches_host_once_including_visible_sessions|default""]","[""gated host process"", ""dashboard PTY"", ""many callback steps""]",5.372,5.372,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1500 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_installation_failures_are_actionable_without_settings_or_fallback|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_installation_failures_are_actionable_without_settings_or_fallback,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18349,18389,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:840-880""]","For host statuses missing, incompatible and wire_mismatch, the dashboard shows the specific notice (missing host, needs updating), issues no deliver and, for the two present-but-wrong hosts, only status controls; a completion is consumed with Unread and no record or fallback, and detach works.",An incompatible bridge could be used for delivery (dropped alerts) or the dashboard could silently fall back rather than telling the user to repair.,2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Wrong-host handling is a bounded notification failure with the dashboard and an explicit notice as workaround (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:840-880).,"Three status cases assert exact notices, expected control sequences, absent records/fallback and Unread (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18355-18385).",Only row covering incompatible/wire-mismatch host statuses; runtime removal is separate (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18043-18075).,Real dashboard PTY with host fixtures per status (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18351-18365).,high,keep,Grounded failure-status coverage without fallback.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_missing_host_tool_preserves_response_and_dashboard_controls|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_denied_settings_are_explicit_and_never_modal_or_automatic|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_pending_permission_does_not_repeat_or_block_input|default""]","[""three dashboard PTY iterations"", ""bridge control record""]",12.886,12.886,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1513 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_default_off_and_disabled_events_do_not_replay_on_enable|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_default_off_and_disabled_events_do_not_replay_on_enable,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17848,17884,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:601-700"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:205-230""]","With notifications off by default, completions are consumed (output shown) but no host call occurs; enabling delivers exactly one; disabling suppresses again; re-enabling delivers only new completions, never replaying the disabled ones.",Enabling notifications could replay old completions (stale alerts) or the default could be on despite the setting.,2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Replayed alerts for old completions are a bounded annoyance; the workaround is dismissing them.,Uses shown output as proof of consumption plus exact host-call counts across three toggles (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17850-17880).,Only row covering the enable/disable replay boundary (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17848-17884).,Real dashboard PTY toggling settings through the real key path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17850-17870).,high,keep,Grounded no-replay assertions on the toggle path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_managed_completion_reaches_host_once_including_visible_sessions|default""]","[""dashboard PTY"", ""host record counts""]",5.207,5.207,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1514 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_managed_completion_reaches_host_once_including_visible_sessions|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_managed_completion_reaches_host_once_including_visible_sessions,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17764,17845,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:601-700"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130""]","A managed codex completion delivers exactly one host call; thereafter duplicate, stale, child, interrupted and later turns produce exactly one more call; a focused visible pane still delivers; a retargeted visible pane delivers; a hidden split pane still delivers; after detach and reattach a later completion delivers once.","Completions could be replayed per visibility change or suppressed for visible panes, and duplicate events could double-notify.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Notification delivery is a bounded feature with a workaround (the dashboard itself); duplicates or misses degrade but do not destroy state.,"Host-call counts are asserted after every event group, including hidden splits and a reattach (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17770-17840).",Only row covering the visibility/focus matrix for completion delivery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17764-17845).,"Real dashboard PTY, real host record and real codex callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17766-17780).",high,keep,Grounded count-based delivery matrix.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_queued_completion_still_delivers_when_its_pane_becomes_visible|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_default_off_and_disabled_events_do_not_replay_on_enable|default""]","[""dashboard PTY and host record"", ""~20 callback steps"", ""split resize""]",7.371,7.371,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1518 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_sound_in_flight_preference_changes_cancel_clients_without_replay_and_keep_host_alive|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_sound_in_flight_preference_changes_cancel_clients_without_replay_and_keep_host_alive,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,19479,19556,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:86-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130""]","For both a sound-flag change and a choice change while a delivery client is gated: the started client is cancelled promptly (<1s, not at its ordinary timeout), the persistent host survives, the gated banner is not admitted, the next fresh completion delivers with the new preference, and the saved document matches.","An in-flight preference change could leave a stale banner delivered, keep the old client hung, or kill the persistent host.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Preference changes affecting an in-flight notification are bounded; the persistent-host invariant is the meaningful part (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130).,"Asserts prompt group absence, elapsed bound, persistent host existence, delivery count and new sound value per change type (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19485-19550).",Only row covering in-flight preference-change cancellation for both sound and choice (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19479-19556).,Real gated client and persistent host process groups plus dashboard PTY (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19481-19500).,high,keep,Grounded cancellation and preference-propagation assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_each_in_flight_lane_and_preserves_the_persistent_host|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_sound_queued_ready_uses_latest_choice_without_cancelling_the_control_client|default""]","[""two full iterations"", ""persistent host process"", ""wall-clock bounds""]",8.885,8.885,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1521 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|settings_set_without_a_server_writes_the_document_a_later_server_loads|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,settings_set_without_a_server_writes_the_document_a_later_server_loads,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,20109,20194,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:1-140"", ""src/cli/mod.rs:71-130""]","With no server, `settings set` edits the resolved document in place, preserves comments/other keys, never starts a server, and reports the path; invalid type/key/reset edits fail with specific messages and leave the file unchanged; --json reset returns path and document; a later server loads those values and subsequent edits go through the server with the same refusals.","Offline settings edits could start a server, write a different document, drop comments, or accept invalid values that a later server silently ignores.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"Offline settings corruption is bounded and reversible by editing the file, though it changes later launch defaults (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:1-140).","Asserts exact file contents, no-socket fact, five refusal messages, JSON output and server-side loading (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20115-20190).",Only row covering offline settings writes and later server load (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20109-20194).,Real compiled settings CLI and real server restart over the same document (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20111-20130).,high,keep,Grounded offline-write and reload coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_hello_carries_the_servers_settings_and_toggles_save_through_the_request|default""]","[""several compiled CLI runs"", ""server restart"", ""document comparisons""]",2.017,2.017,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1578 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_failure_reports_server_log|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,startup_failure_reports_server_log,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,1688,1735,"[""src/client.rs:72-140"", ""src/client.rs:160-178""]","With a corrupt registry, connect_or_start fails quickly with an error containing the parse failure, the server log path and ""exited during startup""; the log file is mode 0600 and contains the parse error; no socket remains.","Startup failure could surface as an opaque timeout, hiding the real cause, or the log could be world-readable and leak registry contents.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"Opaque startup failures are a bounded diagnosability failure with a workaround (run the server manually), though log mode is privacy-relevant (src/client.rs:160-172).","Asserts four error substrings, a time bound, log mode 0600 and log content plus socket absence (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1688-1735).",Only row covering startup-failure reporting and log permissions (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1688-1735).,Real spawned server process with stderr redirected by connect_or_start (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1688-1700).,high,keep,Grounded failure-path coverage including a privacy-relevant file mode.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_stale_socket_is_recovered|default""]","[""spawns compiled ovrcr server"", ""corrupt registry fixture"", ""global env mutation under env_lock""]",0.660,0.660,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1587 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|keyboard_protocol%3A%3Aalternate_key_reporting_preserves_quick_message_control_shortcuts|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,acceptance,keyboard_protocol::alternate_key_reporting_preserves_quick_message_control_shortcuts,default,tests/terminal_acceptance/keyboard_protocol.rs,73,97,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:6-57"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/text_cursor.rs:178-243""]","In Quick message, Ctrl-D (reported with alternate keys as 99:67 modifier 6) inserts `_SUFFIX` without deleting, and Ctrl-E (modifier 5) submits/clears the draft.",Alternate-key control events could be misread as their base character (typing a literal `C`) or fail to trigger the control shortcut (Ctrl-D deleting text).,2,4,3,4,50,90,74,"Misdecoded control keys in the composer can delete a draft or submit unintended text (bounded, recoverable) (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:6-57).",Asserts the exact draft text after Ctrl-D as a character and the cleared composer after Ctrl-E (tests/terminal_acceptance/keyboard_protocol.rs:73-97).,Only row covering alternate-key control shortcuts in the composer (tests/terminal_acceptance/keyboard_protocol.rs:73-97).,Real dashboard PTY with real CSI-u control-event bytes (tests/terminal_acceptance/keyboard_protocol.rs:75-90).,high,keep,Grounded control-key decoding assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|operator_quick_outer_pty_modifiers_paste_escape_restore_terminal|default""]","[""outer PTY dashboard"", ""key sequences""]",1.606,1.606,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1705 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|control_punctuation_and_modified_keys_encode|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,control_punctuation_and_modified_keys_encode,default,tests/tui/main.rs,640,681,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:6-62""]","Ctrl punctuation (space/@, backslash/4, ]/5, ^/6, _/7) encode to the terminals' control bytes, Ctrl-c keeps 0x03 under every modifier combination, and Shift/Alt/Ctrl arrows, Enter, Backspace and PageUp produce their CSI sequences.","A wrong table entry sending a different control byte or CSI sequence, so programs misinterpret modified keys (e.g. Ctrl-Space vs NUL collisions, Shift-Enter submitted as plain Enter).",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Wrong bytes to a program are a bounded feature failure inside the pane.,A wide exact-byte matrix with independent expected values and a modifier sweep.,Punctuation and modified-key encodings are distinct inputs from the Ctrl-g/Ctrl-c reservation test.,Direct full production encode_key invocation (pure encoder).,high,keep,Exact matrix protects the terminal input contract.,[],[],0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1778 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|mouse%3A%3Amouse_encode_legacy_boundaries|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,mouse::mouse_encode_legacy_boundaries,default,tests/tui/mouse.rs,221,301,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:60-160""]","Legacy X10 encoding emits ESC[M + offset bytes for (0,0), accepts 222 and rejects 223 for Default, accepts 2014 and rejects 2015 for UTF-8, encodes U+07FF for Utf8, keeps SGR coordinates at u16::MAX, and encodes release as button 3.","Off-by-one limit arithmetic or invalid bytes emitted for coordinates past 223/2015, producing corrupt mouse reports in legacy programs.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Corrupt legacy mouse reports affect a bounded interaction.,Exact boundary triples at each limit with accept and reject sides.,Legacy/UTF-8 boundary encoding is a distinct input space from SGR encoding.,Direct full production encode_mouse invocation (pure encoder).,high,keep,Only coverage of legacy encoding limits.,[],[],0.039,0.039,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1836 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|mouse%3A%3Amouse_encode_sgr_events|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,mouse::mouse_encode_sgr_events,default,tests/tui/mouse.rs,6,134,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:60-160""]","SGR encoding for down/up (m suffix), middle/right buttons, four wheel directions, drag/motion codes, >223 coordinates and Shift/Alt/Ctrl modifier bits all match the expected byte strings.","Wrong SGR button/release/modifier/coordinate codes, e.g. a release reported as a press or wheel codes off by one, so child programs act on phantom clicks.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Wrong mouse bytes affect a bounded interaction inside the pane.,"Exact byte assertions across every button, release, wheel, motion and modifier combination, including a coordinate beyond the legacy limit.",SGR event encoding is distinct from protocol-mode filtering and legacy-encoding boundary tests.,Direct full production encode_mouse invocation (pure encoder).,high,keep,Complete exact SGR matrix.,[],[],0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1837 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|mouse%3A%3Amouse_encode_tracking_filters|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,mouse::mouse_encode_tracking_filters,default,tests/tui/mouse.rs,137,218,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/input.rs:60-160""]",Mode filtering: None emits nothing; Press mode emits only presses; PressRelease adds releases but no drag/motion; ButtonMotion emits drags but not motion; AnyMotion emits motion; wheel events are suppressed in x10 Press mode.,"Events leaking past the negotiated tracking mode, so a program receives drags/ups/wheels it never requested.",2,4,3,4,50,90,74,Wrong tracking mode bytes affect a bounded program interaction.,"Full matrix over seven event kinds against four protocol modes, including the negative cases per mode.",Mode filtering is a distinct invariant from event code encoding.,Direct full production encode_mouse invocation (pure encoder).,high,keep,Decisive mode-filter matrix.,[],[],0.039,0.039,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1838 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-002,
