nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|claude_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,claude_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,3009,3118,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:174-215"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-375""]","In a fixture with no title_model, retains a matching Claude history and asserts no call and an unchanged name; in a second fixture whose provider exits 2, asserts the name and identity survive with attempt_count 1.","Spawning the model without a configured title_model for a Claude session, or a failed call changing the name and retrying.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,The missing-model half guards against unauthorized provider use; the failure half prevents retry loops.,The no-call half is negative only; the failure half asserts attempt_count 1 plus name and identity.,"Mirrors row 43 for Claude; same orchestration path with a different provider string, so the unique value is small.",Real server and Claude-format history; fake provider.,high,keep,Retains the Claude-specific missing-model evidence alongside a stronger sibling; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_model_missing_mismatches_terminal_and_grok_do_not_spawn_pi|default""]","[""two server fixtures"", ""3 s and 1 s settles"", ""12.17 s observed""]",12.170,12.170,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:703 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_history_change_without_recorded_switch_keeps_title|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,codex_history_change_without_recorded_switch_keeps_title,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2795,2880,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:250-345"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:905-915"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:784-800""]","Titles a Codex session, replaces the history file content with a session_meta naming a different conversation without recording a switch, appends more work and asserts the original subject is still displayed, the other conversation has no subject row, identity is unchanged and at most one additional call was made.","A silent history change (same path, different session_meta id) being treated as a conversation switch, accepting a new subject or attributing it to the other conversation.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Path-based identity is the switch signal; treating content drift as a switch would attribute a different conversation's topic to the session.,"The kept topic, zero rows for the other conversation, display and identity are decisive; the call allowance is deliberately loose (`<= before+1`), so an extra provider call would not fail.",Only test of silent history change with an unchanged path; row 39 covers recorded switches.,"Real server, Codex-format history and fake provider.",high,keep,Covers a path-versus-content identity edge that no other row asserts; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_matching_session_meta_shows_subject_replacing_creation_name_until_rename|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acodex_reference_unchanged_keeps_subject_when_only_history_path_would_differ|default""]","[""file rewrite plus append"", ""5 s settle"", ""SQLite reads"", ""9.63 s observed""]",9.632,9.632,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:704 (PASS attempt 1); run 4242983