nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,codex_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2683,2792,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:174-215"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-375"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1462-1470""]","In one fixture with no title_model, retains a matching Codex history and asserts no provider call and an unchanged name; in a second fixture with a provider that exits 2, retains a matching history and asserts the name and identity survive with attempt_count 1.","Spawning the model when title_model is unset for a Codex session, or a failed call changing the name and retrying.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,The missing-model half guards against unauthorized provider use; the failed-call half prevents retry loops and name churn.,"The no-call check is negative only, while the failure half asserts attempt_count 1 plus name and identity.","Mirrors row 47 for Claude; the Codex-specific missing-model path is the same code path with a different provider string, so the distinction is modest.",Real server plus Codex-format history and a fake provider.,high,keep,Retains the Codex-specific failure evidence even though it parallels the Claude row.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|claude_missing_model_or_failed_title_call_leaves_current_name|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_failures_mismatches_and_missing_binary_do_not_change_rows_or_retry|default""]","[""two server fixtures"", ""fake provider scripts"", ""3 s and 1 s settles""]",11.296,11.296,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:708 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_archive_is_not_saved_or_shown|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,late_title_result_after_archive_is_not_saved_or_shown,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1499,1553,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:217-345"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302""]","Starts a title call whose provider sleeps two seconds, closes the terminal before the reply, waits three seconds and then reads the archived row through `terminal list --archived`, requiring the original name.","A late model reply being saved or surfaced for a session that was archived while the call was in flight, reviving a stale title on a stopped session.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,The archived listing is the user's record of finished work; a late title overwrites a name the user may be relying on and implies the archived session is still active.,"The archived CLI read is decisive for the shown-name claim, but no subject-row assertion proves nothing was saved to the DB.","Archive race is distinct from rename, clear and switch races covered by rows 36, 38 and 40.","Real server, real close/archive and real CLI read; fake provider supplies the delayed reply.",high,keep,"Meaningful race coverage; keep, with the DB-write half left implicit.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_clear_is_dropped|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_recorded_switch_is_dropped|default""]","[""provider sleeps 2 s"", ""3 s settle"", ""CLI archived listing""]",7.388,7.388,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:711 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_clear_is_dropped|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,late_title_result_after_clear_is_dropped,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2355,2399,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1330-1360"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:858-890"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-380""]","Starts a provider call that answers after two seconds, clears the title while the call is in flight, waits three seconds and asserts the creation name is displayed, the conversation is dismissed and its topic is not the late topic.",A late result after Clear being saved (re-titling a session the user just cleared) or clearing the dismissal flag.,3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Clear is the user's explicit 'stop naming this' action; a late save defeats it and re-exposes a topic the user removed.,"Dismissal and topic are asserted separately, and the display name is checked, though the topic assertion is only inequality with the late value.",Clear race is distinct from row 37's dismissal scope and row 38's timing path is the only late-after-clear case.,"Real server, SQLite and delayed fake provider.",high,keep,Grounds the clear/late-result race; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|clear_restores_original_dismisses_current_subject_and_keeps_other|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aclear_without_existing_subject_still_drops_late_result|default""]","[""provider sleeps 2 s"", ""3 s settle"", ""SQLite read""]",7.598,7.598,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:713 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
