nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_attention%3A%3Aattention_exact_priority_ties_effective_input_and_current_exclusion|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_attention::attention_exact_priority_ties_effective_input_and_current_exclusion,default,tests/tui/agent_attention.rs,172,192,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1710"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:399-475"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/agent.rs:290-298""]","The Agents picker orders a session whose effective activity is WaitingInput (any open input_requests on a Connected reporter) ahead of an Unread-only session, keeps ties in tree order, excludes the currently focused session, and renders each candidate's own clause (input needed, Unread, response ready, error observed, unknown observed, unavailable reason).","Picker sorted by the legacy SessionSummary.activity rollup instead of AgentSnapshot::effective_activity, so an agent with an open Input request drops below an Unread agent; or the focused session is offered as a destination.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Attention routing on a working dashboard: the agent that needs an answer must be first; a wrong order delays the user's answer while other agents wait (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1661-1710).,"Walks all eight queue positions, asserting the highlighted identity, that the focused #1 never appears, and the exact clause for each activity/health state (tests/tui/agent_attention.rs:172-192).","Ordering by effective input and the current-session exclusion are asserted only here; the per-state clause wording is also covered by status_table and unread tests, so the distinct part is the picker order (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1687-1706).","Drives the real Dashboard through the s key into the real palette renderer on a 120x40 TestBackend; protocol snapshots are fixtures, and the picker is the subject (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7300-7390).",high,keep,"The picker-order invariant (effective input first, tree-order ties, current excluded) has no other test.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Astatus%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astatus_table|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainput_outranks_unread_and_only_a_running_session_waits|default""]",Eight full 120x40 TestBackend renders plus one Down dispatch per candidate,0.113,0.113,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1726 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_attention%3A%3Aattention_live_status_and_titles_refresh_without_reordering_or_reviewing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_attention::attention_live_status_and_titles_refresh_without_reordering_or_reviewing,default,tests/tui/agent_attention.rs,195,288,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1711-1721"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:4777-4790"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7300-7390""]","An open Agents picker keeps its candidate order and highlighted identity across a live HierarchyChanged while refreshing the displayed title, the Unread/health clauses and the searchable identity; Enter requests the frozen id and R sends MarkReviewed with the ReadyObservation captured when the picker opened.","A live refresh re-sorts the picker so the highlighted row changes under the user, or R acknowledges the newest observation instead of the one the row displayed, reviewing a turn the user has not seen.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Marking a different ReadyObservation reviewed acknowledges a response the user never saw and silently clears the newer Unread (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:4777-4790).,"Asserts the new title and 'Unread Unavailable' after the event, the SetView target, MarkReviewed expected equal to the captured observation in a rebuilt dashboard, and that the old title no longer matches the filter (tests/tui/agent_attention.rs:195-288).","Frozen-picker live refresh with a captured review identity is distinct; new-candidate freezing is covered by agent_search_snapshot_defers_new_candidates_until_reopening, and R semantics by the unread suite (tests/tui/unread.rs:45-127).",Real Dashboard key/event dispatch and palette rendering with in-memory protocol fixtures; the picker plus view request is the subject (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7300-7390).,high,keep,Only test that refreshes a frozen picker in place and pins MarkReviewed to the displayed observation.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Astatus%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astatus_table|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|unread%3A%3Aunread_review_key_captures_visible_observation_without_optimistic_clear|default""]",Two 120x40 renders and a second rebuilt 120x40 dashboard per half,0.078,0.078,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1727 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,independent-dashboard-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_filtered_workspace_removal_never_substitutes_neighbor|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_filtered_workspace_removal_never_substitutes_neighbor,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1197,1217,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:172-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1711-1721"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:7290-7300""]","With a filter active, removing the selected candidate's workspace keeps the selected identity visible with 'session removed' and Enter refuses instead of choosing the neighbour.","The selection index clamped onto the next candidate after removal, switching to an agent the user did not choose.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"A silent neighbour substitution is a wrong-target switch, and the switch path can then carry input (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:172-190,7290-7300).","Asserts the '› agent-title-3' selection, the removal reason text, and that Enter leaves the picker open (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1197-1217).",Removal under an active filter with identity preservation is unique; removal_fallback covers the unfiltered fallback (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1248-1269).,"Real hierarchy update, candidate snapshot refresh and confirm path (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:1711-1721).",high,keep,Covers identity preservation when the filtered destination disappears.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_removal_fallback_disables_newly_focused_candidate|default""]",Two palette renders plus one hierarchy update,0.031,0.031,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1738 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_rapid_choices_coalesce_and_require_a_fresh_a_to_b_to_a_view|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_rapid_choices_coalesce_and_require_a_fresh_a_to_b_to_a_view,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1007,1035,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1353-1380"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/view_handshake.rs:1-140""]","Choosing 2, then 3, then 2 again coalesces to one replacement SetView with a higher revision focused on 2; typing starts only after that view is acknowledged.","The older in-flight view for 2 satisfying the A-to-B-to-A intent, so Terminal opens on B's pane or without a fresh revision.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,Wrong-pane input after a rapid multi-choice; bytes typed after the switch land in the wrong session (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1353-1380).,"Asserts exactly one follow-up, a higher revision, focused 2, and that typing is allowed only after its acknowledgement (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1007-1035).",split::split_review_replaces_a_b_a_and_rejects_old_completions covers the same A-B-A coalescing for split panes; the picker path is distinct (tests/tui/split.rs:2102-2215).,Real handshake revision tracking and coalesced view request through the Dashboard (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/view_handshake.rs:1-140).,high,keep,The picker-specific A-B-A coalescing and fresh-revision requirement.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|split%3A%3Asplit_review_replaces_a_b_a_and_rejects_old_completions|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aagent_confirmation_enters_terminal_only_after_complete_acknowledgement|default""]",Three confirms and one acknowledged view,0.032,0.032,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1743 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Aagent_search_reaches_hidden_sidebar_and_reuses_other_pane|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::agent_search_reaches_hidden_sidebar_and_reuses_other_pane,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,1333,1366,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:4373-4384"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:2600-2700""]","With the sidebar hidden and a split open, the picker still switches agent 1 into the focused pane (two panes preserved), then Tab to the other pane requests a view with panes [1,4] focused on 4.","The picker limited to visible sidebar rows, switching an agent already shown elsewhere creating a duplicate pane owner, or Tab losing the retargeted pane.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Pane ownership: a duplicate owner or a lost pane splits one session's input across panes (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:2600-2700).,"Asserts both panes, focus, Terminal entry, then the post-Tab view contents and order (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:1333-1366).",Hidden-sidebar plus split retarget integration appears only here (tests/tui/split.rs:81-110).,"Real split state, picker confirm and view request through the Dashboard (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:4373-4384).",high,keep,Only test of the picker from a hidden sidebar into a split.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|split%3A%3Asplit_state_focus_and_close_preserve_sessions|default""]",Split creation plus two acknowledged views,0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1745 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acontrol_keys_share_one_hold_and_hidden_sidebar_never_intercepts|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::control_keys_share_one_hold_and_hidden_sidebar_never_intercepts,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,314,399,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1234-1330"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/keymap.rs:440-470""]","Either Control key keeps the hold alive and releasing both ends it; with the sidebar hidden no labels are drawn and Ctrl+digit is not intercepted — in Browse it does nothing, in Terminal it stays the NUL byte for Ctrl+2 with no dashboard request.","Releasing the left Control ending a hold started with the right one, or the hidden sidebar swallowing Ctrl+2 so a program loses its NUL input.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Terminal Ctrl+digit is real program input; intercepting it loses bytes the program expects, and a shared-hold bug hides the gesture mid-selection (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1234-1330).","Left/right release sequencing, hidden-sidebar negatives, then a Terminal-mode PtyBytes([0]) positive with an empty outbox (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:314-399).","The hidden-sidebar versus Terminal-mode routing of Ctrl+digit appears only here; operator_control_jump_does_not_reveal_its_on_demand_sidebar covers the Operator sidebar, not NUL routing (tests/tui/operator.rs:252-330).","Real modifier state machine and terminal-mode encoding; the outbox is checked instead of a real PTY, which the claim does not require (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1234-1330).",high,keep,Unique protection for the hidden-sidebar Ctrl+digit passthrough and the two-key hold.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|operator%3A%3Aoperator_control_jump_does_not_reveal_its_on_demand_sidebar|default""]",Multiple full sidebar renders and a split-free terminal entry round trip,0.045,0.045,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1754 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|agent_search%3A%3Acontrol_label_selects_its_frozen_agent_and_waits_for_release_and_readiness|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::tui,integration,unit,agent_search::control_label_selects_its_frozen_agent_and_waits_for_release_and_readiness,default,tests/tui/agent_search.rs,165,241,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1234-1330"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1385-1445"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/hints.rs:12-18""]","Ctrl+2 selects the frozen second target exactly once (one SetView, footer 'Session selected'), refuses further keystrokes and a second digit while the view is acknowledged but Control is still held, and after release refuses the queued input with 'input was not sent'.","Typing reaching the new agent before Control release or before the view drains, a second destination accepted while the first is in flight, or queued input replayed into the new agent.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Wrong-ownership input: bytes typed for the old agent could be delivered to the newly selected one (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1234-1330,1385-1445).","Asserts one SetView, DashboardAction::None for the held keystroke, an empty outbox, the repeat-digit refusal, and the 'input was not sent' footer after release (tests/tui/agent_search.rs:165-241).",Only test here of one-destination-per-hold plus the post-release input refusal; session_jump_retained covers release-and-ack gating for retained runs with a different fixture (tests/tui/session_jump_retained.rs:184-248).,"Real event dispatch, sidebar-jump state machine and outbox; the model-level outbox is the correct boundary before the PTY (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/hints.rs:12-18).",high,keep,Protects the single-destination and post-release input boundary that no other test asserts.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Atui|session_jump_retained%3A%3Arunning_selection_from_retained_browse_waits_for_release_and_the_view_ack|default""]",Two full sidebar renders and one acknowledged view round trip,0.052,0.052,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1755 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-dashboard-001,
