nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Agrok%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aa_refused_bind_leaves_the_native_arguments_alone|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::grok::tests::a_refused_bind_leaves_the_native_arguments_alone,default,src/report/grok.rs,296,321,"[""src/report/grok.rs:125-175""]","When the supervisor refuses the Bind, admit() returns None, leaves the launch argv byte-identical, closes the reporter, retains nothing, and receiver(None) leaves argv untouched.","Injecting --session-id or retaining history after a refused bind, which would start a session the server does not own.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"A refused binding must not rewrite the native launch; doing so starts work the server cannot attribute (wrong ownership, 3).","src/report/grok.rs:296-321 asserts argv equality in both the refused and no-reservation cases, reporter.closed(), and no Retain event.",Complementary refusal arm; the successful row cannot prove the untouched-argv invariant.,Production admit()/receiver() with the scripted supervisor.,high,keep,Guards the wrong-ownership failure the success path cannot express.,[],scripted supervisor; two argv constructions,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:650 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,independent-report-check-2
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aa_publication_that_cannot_be_delivered_disables_the_reporter|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::a_publication_that_cannot_be_delivered_disables_the_reporter,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,350,367,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:656-683""]","A publish whose delivery fails returns UNAVAILABLE, closes the reporter and clears the binding, and a subsequent publish still returns UNAVAILABLE; only the first activity was observed.","Keeping a connected reporter after delivery uncertainty, so the server believes it is still current while reports are being dropped.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,A reporter that keeps claiming continuity after an undelivered report leaves the session's state silently stale (3).,"src/report/reporter/tests.rs:350-367 asserts UNAVAILABLE twice, the closed and unbound state, and exactly one observed activity.",Only delivery-failure publish test.,Production Reporter with a scripted refusing supervisor.,high,keep,Only evidence that delivery uncertainty disables rather than continues.,[],scripted supervisor run,0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:659 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afinalize_settles_a_bound_invocation_and_only_releases_an_unbound_one|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::finalize_settles_a_bound_invocation_and_only_releases_an_unbound_one,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,411,441,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:771-815""]",A bound invocation's finalize publishes the final accounting as revision 2 (after activity at 1) and closes; an unbound invocation's finalize sends only a Release with no Finalize report.,"Numbering the final accounting outside the revision set (so the server rejects it), or finalizing an invocation that never bound.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Final accounting is the last durable metrics write; a wrong revision loses it, and a wrong finalize confuses an unbound reservation (3).","src/report/reporter/tests.rs:411-441 asserts the finalized revision vector [2] and, for the unbound case, a Release with no Finalize observed.",Only finalize test.,Production Reporter with the scripted supervisor.,high,keep,Only coverage of final accounting numbering and the unbound release.,[],two scripted-supervisor runs,0.055,0.055,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:663 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Apolling_never_promotes_pending_retention_to_a_replacement_generation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::polling_never_promotes_pending_retention_to_a_replacement_generation,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,537,581,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:443-520""]","For both a conversation switch and a forced rebind, a failed retention left pending is not resubmitted by a poll or native-completed event against the replacement generation; exactly one Retain is observed.",Polling or the completion callback promoting a stale pending retention to whatever binding is now current.,3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"A promoted pending retention persists old metadata under a new generation (durable-state and recovery identity, 3).",src/report/reporter/tests.rs:537-581 runs both force modes through Poll and NativeCompleted and asserts the retained count is 1.,Only poll and native-completion retention test.,Production Reporter with a scripted supervisor and a no-op Frames handler.,high,keep,Covers the asynchronous retry paths the direct retention row never reaches.,[],two scripted-supervisor runs with poll and completion events,0.075,0.075,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:669 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,independent-report-check-2
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aunacknowledged_health_disables_and_an_unbound_reporter_has_none_to_report|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::unacknowledged_health_disables_and_an_unbound_reporter_has_none_to_report,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,370,387,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:719-770""]","An unbound reporter's health() returns true without sending anything; a bound reporter whose health command is refused returns false, closes, and the supervisor observed the Unavailable health report.","Disabling an unbound reporter for having no health to send, or ignoring an unacknowledged health report so a stale pause state persists.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Health drives the paused and uncertain state; a wrong result either disables a healthy launch or leaves a false pause (3).,src/report/reporter/tests.rs:370-387 asserts both ends: true with no binding and false/closed with the observed health report.,Only health-failure test.,Production Reporter with scripted supervisors.,high,keep,Covers both the unbound no-op and the acknowledged-failure arms.,[],two scripted-supervisor runs,0.046,0.046,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:672 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20denial%20closes%20the%20approval%20exactly%20as%20an%20allow%20does|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a denial closes the approval exactly as an allow does,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,209,217,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A resolution with approved=false still emits input_open then input_close for approval:c1, and the denial reason ('denied by user') never appears in the record.","If the close depended on approved being true, a denied approval would stay open and the session would look permanently blocked while OMP has already moved on.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"A denied approval that never closes is the same stuck session state as a missed allow, and the human decision text has no business in the channel (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:90-93). The receiver derives the namespace from the request-id prefix and IGNORES an open whose id does not carry it (src/report/extension.rs:396-420, src/report/extension.rs:688-696), so a wrong id or a mismatched close leaves the prompt invisible while the child blocks on the human answer.","It asserts the two events for the denied case and excludes the denial reason (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:209-217); the allow case's exact ids are the previous row, so this row is the branch distinction.","Same request shape as the allow row, but the approved=false branch is a distinct authority outcome; without it a truthiness regression on `approved` passes; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105, which no other reviewed case exercises.","Real handlers, real transport and helper; the assertion reads the delivered bytes (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:212-216).",high,keep,Covers the denial branch that the allow row cannot; keep.,[],0.045s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.045,0.045,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 44.533292 at macOS-job.log:3759; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20tool%20that%20is%20not%20ask%20emits%20nothing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a tool that is not ask emits nothing,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,260,267,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]",A tool_execution_start/end for a non-ask tool (bash) produces no frames at all.,"If the toolName filter were dropped, every bash or edit call would open a question request and never close it (the close is filtered by the same name), so the session would look permanently blocked after the first tool call.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"A spurious question frame is indistinguishable from a real pending question to the receiver, so the human-facing input state becomes unusable (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:98-105).",It asserts a completely empty record for a non-ask tool pair (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:260-267); both the start and end guards are exercised by the same pair.,"No other row sends a non-ask tool through the question handlers; the approval rows use approval events; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105, which no other reviewed case exercises.","Real handlers and transport with no helper spawn, which the empty record proves (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:265-267).",high,keep,Covers the negative branch of the ask filter; keep.,[],0.002s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.002,0.002,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 2.255916 at macOS-job.log:3783; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20approval%20requested%20and%20resolved%20in%20one%20tick%20is%20delivered%20open%20before%20close|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an approval requested and resolved in one tick is delivered open before close,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,301,320,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Emitting the approval request and its resolution without awaiting the first keeps the wire order open then close with ascending sequence numbers, i.e. the transport FIFO preserves the emit order.","If report() delivered out of order when two handlers were invoked in one tick, the close would reach the receiver before the open and be discarded as unknown, leaving the approval pending.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,Out-of-order frames corrupt the receiver's request state machine; the same-tick case is the one OMP produces on a no-interactive-UI resolution (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:107-131).,"It asserts both the event order and the ascending sequence numbers (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:301-320), which is the decisive evidence that the FIFO, not luck, ordered the frames.","The Pi suite asserts the same one-tick ordering for its own emission path (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:140-166 covers sequence, and the analogous prompt rows), so the transport invariant is covered twice across providers.","Real handlers, real transport with its single-in-flight queue, and a real helper child that records each frame (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:310-319).",high,keep,"Mechanism-level ordering coverage, but the transport invariant is asserted for both providers; retained rather than consolidated because the OMP event pair differs.","[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|one%20response%20cycle%3A%20start%2C%20end%2C%20settled%20carry%20run%2C%20outcome%20and%20ordered%20sequence|default""]",0.026s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 26.211125 at macOS-job.log:3801; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20ask%20execution%20that%20starts%20and%20ends%20in%20one%20tick%20is%20delivered%20open%20before%20close|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an ask execution that starts and ends in one tick is delivered open before close,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,322,338,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]",Starting and ending an ask execution without awaiting the start still delivers input_open then input_close for question:q1 with ascending sequence numbers.,"An out-of-order delivery would drop the close for an unknown request, leaving the question pending after the tool already returned.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,"Same receiver state machine as the approval case, but on the ask/question namespace, which is a separate handler path (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:98-105). The receiver derives the namespace from the request-id prefix and IGNORES an open whose id does not carry it (src/report/extension.rs:396-420, src/report/extension.rs:688-696), so a wrong id or a mismatched close leaves the prompt invisible while the child blocks on the human answer.",It asserts the ordered event pair and the sequence comparison (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:322-338); the ordering evidence is explicit rather than inferred from array order alone.,The approval one-tick row covers the other namespace of the same transport FIFO; the Pi suite covers the transport for its own emissions.,Real handlers and real transport queue; frames recorded by the helper child (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:330-337).,high,keep,Distinct namespace of the same ordering mechanism; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20approval%20requested%20and%20resolved%20in%20one%20tick%20is%20delivered%20open%20before%20close|default""]",0.027s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.027,0.027,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 27.025916 at macOS-job.log:3807; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20end%20that%20failed%2C%20timed%20out%20or%20aborted%20still%20closes%20the%20question|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,"an end that failed, timed out or aborted still closes the question",default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,285,299,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A tool_execution_end for ask with isError true still emits input_close for question:q1, and neither isError nor the answer text appears in the record.","If the close depended on a successful tool result, an errored, timed-out or cancelled ask would leave the question open forever, blocking the session's input state after the failure.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,The tool's end is the end of the wait whatever its outcome; gating the close on success turns every failed ask into a stuck prompt (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:102-105).,It asserts the open/close pair for the error case and excludes isError and the answer body (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:285-299); the timeout/abort variants are represented by the same isError path rather than separately.,"Same handler as the ask-lifetime row but the failure outcome is a distinct boundary that a success-gated close passes without; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport with a real helper; assertions read the delivered bytes (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:290-298).,high,keep,Distinct failure-outcome boundary of the question close; keep.,[],0.012s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 12.144542 at macOS-job.log:3795; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|the%20reattach%20command%20re-announces%20this%20producer%20once%20and%20says%20so|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,the reattach command re-announces this producer once and says so,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,150,164,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","With an open run 1, running the ovrcr-reattach command emits one session_start with reason 'reattach', idle false and run null, notices 'OVRCR reporting reattached' at info level, and the following agent_start opens run 2.","If reattach did not reset producer.run/open, the receiver would treat the announcement as part of the old cycle, and a reattach that kept the open run would make the next start a continuation of a turn that no longer exists.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Reattach is the operator's only in-place recovery for a dead producer; a wrong run/open state leaves the session permanently mis-sequenced, which the receiver rejects as a repeated identity (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:146-158).","It asserts the frame triple, the notice text and level, and that a later start is a new run (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:150-164); the failure branch (unavailable) is the next row.","The Pi analogue (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:365-380) starts from a disabled producer rather than an open cycle, so the reset semantics exercised here are distinct.",The real registerCommand handler and the real transport reattach run; only ctx.ui.notify is a fixture recorder (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:154-163).,high,keep,Only recovery-path coverage for OMP reporting; keep.,[],0.029s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.029,0.029,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 29.3875 at macOS-job.log:3741; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|two%20approvals%20overlap%3A%20each%20frame%20carries%20its%20own%20tool%20call%20id|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,two approvals overlap: each frame carries its own tool call id,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,230,244,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Two approvals c1 and c2 queue independently: both input_open frames appear in order with their own request ids, and their closes arrive in resolution order with matching ids.","If the extension remembered a single current tool call id, the second open would reuse c1 and the first close would close the wrong request, leaving one prompt permanently pending.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Overlapping approvals are the normal case when a child asks twice; a shared id mismatches open and close and blocks the session's input state (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-93). The receiver derives the namespace from the request-id prefix and IGNORES an open whose id does not carry it (src/report/extension.rs:396-420, src/report/extension.rs:688-696), so a wrong id or a mismatched close leaves the prompt invisible while the child blocks on the human answer.","It asserts the full four-frame id sequence (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:230-244), which rejects a single-id implementation and any reordering.",The Pi prompt-span row asserts two distinct request ids for nested prompts (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:293-312); the OMP approval naming has no other coverage.,Real handlers and transport with a real helper child; the ordering is read from the record (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:236-243).,high,keep,Distinct concurrency boundary of the approval identity; keep.,[],0.043s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.043,0.043,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 42.872667 at macOS-job.log:3771; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|failed%20publication%20preserves%20original%20pointer%20and%20unresolved%20assignments|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,failed publication preserves original pointer and unresolved assignments,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,54,64,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","When the Save call rejects, continuation.save() rejects and the previous state (including handles and pointer) is unchanged, with no second pointer appended.","If a failed save cleared or replaced state, the session would lose the continuation index and the unresolved assignments it had already reconciled, so pending work would be forgotten after one storage error.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,Lost continuation state means unresolved assignments are never surfaced again; the reconciliation is the only record the extension holds (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:82-95).,It compares a structured clone of the state before and after the rejection and counts appended entries (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:54-64).,"Only this row asserts state preservation on a failed publication; the retirement rows cover generation fencing; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:82-95, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real save() path runs with a fake call that rejects for Save, and the state/appendEntry observables are the module's own (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:82-95).",high,keep,Covers the failed-publication state-preservation boundary; keep.,[],0.002s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.002,0.002,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 2.062667 at macOS-job.log:3891; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|ordinary%20failed%20or%20ambiguous%20recovery%20never%20asks%20for%20fresh%20logical%20routing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,ordinary failed or ambiguous recovery never asks for fresh logical routing,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,111,119,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","For a rejected Recover and for a two-workflow (ambiguous) response, the module reports a gap with no fresh reset (resets == [false]) and null state.","If an ordinary Server error or an ambiguous reply reset the routing generation, every live tool would be retired and the workflow identity replaced, orphaning pending work on a transient failure.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,A reset retires live tool routing (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:243-250); triggering it on an ordinary failure turns a transient error into lost authority over running work (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:47-62).,It drives both the thrown-error and the ambiguous-array branches and asserts the absent fresh reset plus a non-empty gap (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:111-119).,"No other row asserts resets == [false]; the fork/new rows assert the opposite; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:47-62, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real restore error path runs with fake responses, and the reset callback is the production hook the runtime supplies (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:47-62).",high,keep,Protects the no-reset-on-ordinary-failure rule; keep.,[],0.001s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.001,0.001,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.522667 at macOS-job.log:3921; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_interrupt_extension.mjs|each%20turn%20samples%20current%20loaded%20bindings%3B%20config%20drift%20alone%20has%20no%20authority|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,node,unit,each turn samples current loaded bindings; config drift alone has no authority,default,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,52,62,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:1-59"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-112""]","Calling the inspector per turn returns 'Escape' initially; a config object on disk changes nothing; after the manager's binding changes to empty it returns 'Unsupported', and after restoring escape it returns 'Escape'.","If the result were cached across turns, a mid-session rebind would leave OVRCR claiming an interrupt it can no longer deliver; if it read config files, a stale file would override the live manager.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"Per-turn sampling is what keeps the claim true after a user rebinds keys during a session (src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:1-2, 41-54).",It asserts the sample-after-change transition in both directions plus the no-config property (tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs:52-62); the 'no file consulted' claim is proven only by the absence of a path argument.,"The other interrupt rows call the inspector once; the re-sampling contract is unique here; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:41-54, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real inspector is called through a getter returning the same live manager, whose binding is mutated between calls (tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs:53-61).",high,keep,Covers the per-turn sampling contract; keep.,[],0.000158417s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.000158417,0.000158417,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.158417 at macOS-job.log:4047; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_observation_extension.mjs|65%20pending%20identities%20drain%20in%20bounded%20batches%20without%20a%20new%20state%20change|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,node,unit,65 pending identities drain in bounded batches without a new state change,default,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,124,139,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:1-147"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:236-239""]","Sixty-five pending handles are delivered as one 64-handle wake and then one single-handle wake, with 65 distinct handles across the two, and the extra handles are watched without a new state change.","If the batch were unbounded, the wake content and details could exceed Pi's message limits and be dropped, losing the reconciliation for tens of assignments.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"BATCH=64 bounds each wake; exceeding it silently loses pending identities, i.e. assignments that never surface (src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:3-3, 25-40).","It asserts the 64/1 split, the union size of 65 and that only one continuation was outstanding before the acknowledge (tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs:124-139).","The TRACKED capacity (4096) is not exercised; the 64-batch boundary is asserted only here; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:3-4, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real deliver() slicing and pending-set bookkeeping run with fixture observations (src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:25-40).,high,keep,Only coverage of the batch bound; keep.,[],0.084s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.084,0.084,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 84.144708 at macOS-job.log:4083; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
