tion tool schemas; keep.,[],0.098s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.098,0.098,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 98.47975 at macOS-job.log:4173; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20prompt%20can%20open%20while%20no%20cycle%20is%20running%20and%20never%20touches%20the%20cycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a prompt can open while no cycle is running and never touches the cycle,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,314,322,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A prompt span emitted before any agent_start delivers input_open/input_close with run null, and the following agent_start is run 1.","If the prompt path opened or incremented a run, a question asked outside a turn would fabricate a cycle that never settles, and the receiver would show a permanently running turn.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,A prompt is not a turn; letting it touch the cycle state creates a run with no end that the receiver publishes (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:130-124).,"It asserts run null on both prompt frames and run 1 on the later start (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:314-322), the exact boundary that separates input from work.","The prompt-span row above has a cycle open; this row is the no-cycle case, which a run-reading implementation would pass in the other test; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:130-141, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real prompt handlers and transport; the frames are delivered by a real helper (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:318-321).,high,keep,Distinct no-cycle boundary of the prompt contract; keep.,[],0.021s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.021,0.021,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 21.127833 at macOS-job.log:4275; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20shutdown%20drain%20discards%20the%20queue%20and%20delivers%20only%20the%20final%20frame%20in%20one%20deadline|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a shutdown drain discards the queue and delivers only the final frame in one deadline,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,382,394,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","With a helper that answers only the drain, five queued agent_starts plus a session_shutdown complete in under 1200 ms and the record contains exactly one frame, session_shutdown.","If flush waited for each queued frame, a shutdown behind five stalled helpers would take five deadlines and blow the callback budget, delaying or dropping the final shutdown frame.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,The drain deadline is what guarantees the shutdown frame is delivered inside one budget; a per-frame budget multiplies the stall and can drop the final frame entirely (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:134-144).,"It asserts one absolute deadline via elapsed time plus the single-frame record (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:382-394); the 1200 ms bound is a proxy, but the frame count is exact.","The overflow row tests the queue bound; this row tests the discard-and-send-one drain, which no other test covers; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:82-144, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real flush path and real spawns run against a helper that stalls ordinary frames (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:386-392).,high,keep,Only coverage of the drain's single-deadline contract; keep.,[],0.013s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 12.979208 at macOS-job.log:4299; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|captures%20exact%20native%20history%20at%20each%20conversation%20boundary|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,captures exact native history at each conversation boundary,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,100,114,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Two session_start announcements deliver frames carrying session_id native-a/native-b with session_file '/private/history/not-derived-from-id.jsonl' and '/private/history/second.jsonl' - the real history path, even when it does not derive from the id.","If the frame derived the file from the session id or cached the first history path, OVRCR would bind or resume the wrong conversation file, so a resumed Pi session would read and report another conversation's history.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,Binding the wrong conversation file means the receiver attributes a turn and its transcript to a conversation it does not own (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:94-104).,"It asserts the exact id/file pair for two distinct contexts, chosen so a derived path would be visibly different from the real one (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:100-114).",The OMP analogue (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:43-56) exercises a different extension module and an in-place switch; this file's announcement path is otherwise untested.,The real runtime registers its handlers into the fake ExtensionContext and each frame is delivered by a real helper child (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:80-97).,high,keep,Only coverage of the Pi announcement's history binding; keep.,[],0.073s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.073,0.073,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 73.422792 at macOS-job.log:4197; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|inert%20outside%20a%20managed%20invocation%3A%20registers%20nothing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,inert outside a managed invocation: registers nothing,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,116,122,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]",Without OVRCR_AGENT_SOCKET/OVRCR_AGENT_TOKEN the injected factory registers no handler at all.,"If the credential guard were dropped, every ordinary Pi launch would install reporting handlers and spawn helpers against a channel that does not exist, adding failure paths and retries to a plain session.",3,4,2,3,75,75,75,The guard keeps OVRCR out of unmanaged Pi sessions entirely; losing it makes an ordinary launch acquire a half-configured reporter (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:89-91).,"It asserts the empty registration list, which is the direct observable of the guard (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:116-122).","The OMP analogue asserts a wider inertness (both guards); this one is the Pi-side entry guard and the only test of it; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-124, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The production factory runs with the real guard condition and a fixture API; no process is spawned (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:117-121).,high,keep,Only test of the Pi entry credential guard; keep.,[],0.011s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 10.914583 at macOS-job.log:4203; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|queue%20overflow%20disables%20reporting%20and%20sends%20one%20content-free%20unavailable%20notice|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,queue overflow disables reporting and sends one content-free unavailable notice,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,239,252,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","258 concurrent agent_starts against a hanging helper overflow the bounded queue: at most two helpers complete, the last delivered frame is event 'unavailable' with reason 'overflow', and a following agent_settled delivers nothing more.","If the queue were unbounded, a stalled helper would accumulate every event with its bytes until memory or the receiver's bounds fail; if overflow did not disable, the producer would keep queueing after the notice.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,"This is the bounded-delivery guarantee: overflow must degrade to one notice the receiver can act on, not to unbounded buffering (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:107-125).","It asserts the notice's event and reason, the bound on completed helpers, and the silence after disabling (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:239-252); the exact 256-event boundary is not probed, only beyond it.","The OMP suite has no overflow row; this is the only test of the maxEvents/maxBytes guard; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:82-144, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real report() queue and real spawns run; the fixture helper is deliberately slow, and the record shows what actually completed (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:242-251).",high,keep,The only protection for the transport's bounded queue and its disable-on-overflow contract; keep.,[],0.917s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.917,0.917,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 917.438708 at macOS-job.log:4251; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,independent-extensions-check-1
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|cache-miss-relocated-profile-pin%3Aln239|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,cache-miss-relocated-profile-pin:ln239,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,239,239,"[""native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:239-239"", ""scripts/package-startup.sh:59-62""]","With the payload fingerprint still matching the local profile but the relocated expected-contract.json rewritten to local_development=false, requesting --local-development must miss the cache and reach the builder (exit 77), proving the cache hit revalidates the payload contract and does not trust source.sha256 alone.","A cache hit gated only on the source fingerprint, so a payload whose relocated contract no longer matches the requested profile is served without validation.",3,3,3,3,75,75,75,The cache may bypass a rebuild; if it also bypasses revalidation it serves a payload that fails its own profile pin (3).,"native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:239-239 asserts the builder is reached for the mismatched contract; scripts/package-startup.sh:59-62 shows the hit additionally requires the validator to pass, so dropping that clause fails the check.","Only test that payload revalidation, not only the fingerprint, guards a cache hit.","Real package-startup.sh, real validator invocation and a fake builder.",high,keep,Only evidence that a cache hit still revalidates the relocated contract rather than trusting source.sha256 alone.,[],"rewrites the contract, spawns package-startup.sh with a fake builder",,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-guards.py|entitlement-pin%3Aln35|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-guards.py,script-check,acceptance,entitlement-pin:ln35,local-development,native/bridge/check-guards.py,28,35,"[""native/bridge/entitlements.plist:1-5"", ""scripts/build-bridge.sh:136-142""]","The fixture bundle's Contents/Resources/OVRCRBridge.entitlements is a regular file whose SHA256 equals the repo-pinned entitlements.plist, decodes to exactly {com.apple.security.automation.apple-events: true}, and no legacy Contents/OVRCRBridge.entitlements exists.","A bundle whose shipped entitlement file differs from the pinned bytes, adds another entitlement, or carries a legacy copy where codesign could pick it up.",4,4,0,4,100,60,76,A wrong or extra automation entitlement changes what the signed bridge may do on the user's behalf (native/bridge/entitlements.plist:1-5).,"Asserts file identity, the exact SHA256 pin, the exact entitlement dictionary and absence of the legacy path (native/bridge/check-guards.py:28-35).","The identical block runs in both modes with no mode-dependent branch, so this execution adds no boundary over the production row (native/bridge/check-guards.py:28-35).",Hashes and decodes the real built bundle artifact from the staging pipeline.,high,consolidate,Identical statements in both modes; retain the production entitlement-pin row as the representative.,"[""python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-guards.py|entitlement-pin%3Aln35|production""]","[""reads and hashes the built bundle's entitlement file""]",,,,,unmeasured,"suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3646 (40 checks) '40 compiled-entry and bundle-layout guard checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no admitted request, IPC or native app lifecycle.' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets')",packaging-installers-001,independent-packaging-check-1
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-packaging.py|entitlement-pin%3Aln32|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-packaging.py,script-check,acceptance,entitlement-pin:ln32,local-development,native/bridge/check-packaging.py,25,32,"[""native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:20-89"", ""scripts/build-bridge.sh:115-145""]",The source bundle's entitlement resource is a regular file pinned to the repo entitlement SHA256 with exactly the automation entitlement and no legacy Contents/ copy.,A source bundle whose entitlement bytes differ from the pin or that carries an extra/legacy entitlement file.,4,4,0,4,100,60,76,The pin is what codesign will seal into the shipped app (native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:59-65).,"Asserts file identity, the SHA256 pin, the exact dictionary and the legacy path's absence (native/bridge/check-packaging.py:25-32).",Also pinned by check-guards on the input bundle and check-startup-package on the relocated payload; each stage can drift independently (native/bridge/check-guards.py:28-35).,Reads and hashes the real built bundle.,high,consolidate,Identical block in both modes; retain the production entitlement-pin row.,"[""python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-packaging.py|entitlement-pin%3Aln32|production""]","[""real copied bundle plus a validator subprocess""]",,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3645 (36 checks) '36 packaging checks passed under PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no signing/install/launch.' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-001,independent-packaging-check-1
