nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|real_process_discovery_failure_does_not_archive_the_record|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,real_process_discovery_failure_does_not_archive_the_record,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,2466,2513,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:838-849"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:1391-1401""]","When the real process-discovery command fails, closing a row reports failure, archives nothing, and keeps the actionable row in the active list.","A discovery failure treated as 'nothing running', archiving a row whose process may still exist.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"A failed discovery produces DiscoveryFailed ('process ownership is uncertain', crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:50-63) and the record keeps a row whose owning group was never proven stopped; the wrong-ownership consequence is bounded because nothing is signalled or deleted and unarchive restores the row, so this is 3 rather than a destructive or data-loss failure.","Injects a failing ps ahead of the server's PATH, asserts the CLI failure, an empty archive and the row still active (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2466-2513).",The discovery-failure branch is unique; the archived-uncertainty test covers a known archived row (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2019-2143).,"Real binary, a real wrapper process and the real ps command, so attached_subgroups() at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:838-849 executes its production error path; the OS discovery boundary is the subject.",high,keep,Only test of a real discovery command failure during close.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|workspace_removal_blocks_live_and_uncertain_rows_and_preserves_records_on_failures|default""]","[""A PATH wrapper and one close request""]",5.556,5.556,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1430 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-006,independent-integration-final-check-1
