nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_is_not_gated_on_the_claude_version|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_admission_is_not_gated_on_the_claude_version,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9963,9966,"[""src/report/admission.rs:88-190"", ""src/report/admission.rs:208-235""]","Two resume invocations are admitted on argv and hooks alone: one on 2.1.266 (below the former 2.1.267 floor) with -r and one whose `claude --version` prints ""not-a-version"".","A reintroduced version gate would refuse admission for an older or unparseable Claude build, leaving the agent unmanaged.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,An admission version gate silently disables managed reporting for valid installs (src/report/admission.rs:88-190).,"Assertions inside the helper cover argv/binding/usage; the row itself only varies the version inputs, and a malformed version is asserted only through admitting successfully (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9963-9966).",Only row asserting versions below the former floor and an unparseable version (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9963-9966).,Real native fixture printing the supplied version and real resume callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9370-9390).,high,keep,Grounded protection against reinstating a version gate.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_short_resume_on_2_1_268_preserves_argv_and_lifecycle|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_later_patch_preserves_resume_identity_and_lifecycle|default""]","[""two full admission helper runs"", ""real native fixtures"", ""env_lock serialization""]",10.405,10.405,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1446 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_later_patch_preserves_resume_identity_and_lifecycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_admission_later_patch_preserves_resume_identity_and_lifecycle,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9956,9958,"[""src/report/admission.rs:88-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]","The same resume flow with `-r` on Claude 2.1.274: argv, binding, usage collection and branch/clear transitions behave identically to the 2.1.268 case.","A patch version bump could silently change resume eligibility or argv handling, resuming wrongly or as a fresh session.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,"Resume regressions break conversation continuity, a major workflow failure; this row only varies the version string (src/report/admission.rs:88-190).","The helper asserts argv, binding, usage and lifecycle thoroughly, but those assertions duplicate the 2.1.268 short-resume row (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9450-9540).","The 2.1.274 release is a distinct above-floor patch input; the helper and assertions match the 2.1.268 row, but the retained not-gated row covers only 2.1.266 and an unparsable version, so this input is not fully subsumed (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9956-9958; src/report/admission.rs:21,206-221).",Real native fixture and real resume callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9370-9410).,high,keep,"Keep as a cheap version-boundary probe: the only difference is the diagnostic version constant, but it is a distinct input not covered by the 2.1.268 or not-gated rows.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_short_resume_on_2_1_268_preserves_argv_and_lifecycle|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_is_not_gated_on_the_claude_version|default""]","[""real native fixture"", ""resume callbacks"", ""env_lock serialization""]",4.802,4.802,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1444 (PASS attempt 1); run 424