nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_runtime_kill_reaches_owned_native_group|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_run_runtime_kill_reaches_owned_native_group,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,8561,8589,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1723-1740"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1560""]",KillSession on an agent-run session with a spawned native group leaves both the native group and the outer session group absent after the session reports Exited.,Server-side kill could reach only the session leader while the native agent group keeps running (orphaned provider process).,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,An orphaned native group keeps consuming provider quota and holds the workspace after the user killed the session (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1723-1740).,"Asserts both group absences, which is the decisive check; it does not assert what signal reached the native process (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8575-8588).",Only row for runtime kill of the native group (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8561-8589).,Real agent run with a real native process group and real signal path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8563-8575).,high,keep,Grounded and cheap protection against orphaned native groups.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term|default""]","[""real native process group"", ""kill and exit polling""]",4.453,4.453,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1456 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_ready_alerts_once_per_root_turn_with_unread_and_continuation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_ready_alerts_once_per_root_turn_with_unread_and_continuation,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,16926,17087,"[""src/report/claude.rs:44-80"", ""src/report/reporter.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:632-700""]","Claude: SessionStart alone is not Ready and does not alert; a fresh prompt yields Busy then Observed Ready with one turn, one host alert and Unread; duplicate Stop and child/wrong/missing/malformed Stops change nothing; a continuation under the same root turn returns Busy then Ready without a second alert or Unread; a later turn alerts again with a new Unread; stale Stop for the prior turn cannot create Ready; explicit R reviews only the presented identity.","A duplicate or stale Stop could re-alert or re-Ready, and a continuation could double-count Unread or clear it early.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"Repeated alerts for one completion train users to ignore them, and stale Ready misstates turn state (src/report/claude.rs:44-80 event normalisation).","Asserts alert-count checkpoints, activity/turn/quality and Unread identity across turns, with explicit equality after ignored Stops (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16940-17080).","Claude ready-alert row; codex and pi rows use different hook grammars (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13621-13721, :14902-14986).","Real claude alert fixture, dashboard host record and real PTY (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16928-16945).",high,keep,Grounded alert-once and continuation coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_exact_resume_reports_ready_unread_and_alert_without_historical_replay|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_ready_alerts_once_creates_unread_and_explicit_review_clears_only_presented|default""]","[""claude native helper"", ""dashboard host record"", ""CLI list call""]",5.860,5.860,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1467 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|cli_resolves_relative_project_paths_against_invocation_cwd_with_existing_server|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,cli_resolves_relative_project_paths_against_invocation_cwd_with_existing_server,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,7217,7253,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2152-2225"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1-120""]",The compiled CLI runs `project add relative . --workspace-root ../fixture-workspaces` from the fixture repo while a server is running; the persisted registry contains the canonical repo and workspace-root absolute paths.,"Relative paths could be resolved against the server working directory (usually elsewhere), registering the wrong project or workspace root.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Registering the wrong checkout or workspace root points every later operation at unintended directories (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2152-2225).,"Asserts both stored absolute paths against the fixture values, read back from the registry file (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7228-7250).",Only row covering CLI relative-path resolution with an existing server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7217-7253).,"Real compiled CLI child process, real server and real registry file (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7220-7248).",high,keep,Grounded path-resolution coverage with a durable-state read-back.,[],"[""spawns compiled CLI"", ""thread-hosted server"", ""registry read""]",2.015,2.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1470 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_missing_end_disables_overlap_without_native_failure|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,codex_managed_missing_end_disables_overlap_without_native_failure,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,11778,11831,"[""src/report/codex.rs:232-333"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:66-90""]","Two prompts are submitted without a Stop for the first; each callback leaves activity Busy and the session becomes Unavailable, while the native run still exits 17.",An unclosed turn could be treated as a valid overlap (wrong Ready) or could hard-fail the native agent.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Publishing Ready or the wrong turn for an unclosed cycle misreports the agent and corrupts Unread (src/report/codex.rs:232-333).,"Asserts Busy after every callback and Unavailable after the first overlapping prompt, plus native exit (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11790-11825).",Only row covering missing-end overlap disablement (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11778-11831).,Real native helper through the real server; proxy not involved (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11780-11790).,high,keep,Grounded overlap-guard assertions with native survival.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_lost_bind_receipt_recovers_before_busy|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_native_death_never_synthesizes_ready_and_removes_socket|default""]","[""real native helper and PTY"", ""repeated callback waits""]",3.839,3.839,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1477 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_native_death_never_synthesizes_ready_and_removes_socket|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,codex_managed_native_death_never_synthesizes_ready_and_removes_socket,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,11834,11866,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:1-120"", ""src/report/codex.rs:132-180""]","After a bound codex turn, SIGKILL of the native process yields CODEX_NATIVE_EXIT=137, the endpoint socket disappears, and health eventually leaves Connected while activity stays Busy; no Ready is synthesized.",Native death could synthesize Ready (claiming a response that never existed) or leave the private endpoint and lease behind.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"A synthesized Ready marks work complete that never finished, and a retained endpoint keeps reporting authority alive (src/report/reporter.rs:1-120).","Asserts the exit status, socket connect failure, pid absence and that activity remains Busy while health changes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11840-11864).",Only row asserting no-Ready on native death for codex (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11834-11866).,"Real native process killed with SIGKILL, real socket and pid observations (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11842-11855).",high,keep,Grounded negative Ready assertion plus endpoint cleanup.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_lost_bind_receipt_recovers_before_busy|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_managed_missing_end_disables_overlap_without_native_failure|default""]","[""SIGKILL of real native process"", ""socket/pid polling""]",3.253,3.253,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1478 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_unread_is_discarded_on_terminal_removal_and_server_restart|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,codex_unread_is_discarded_on_terminal_removal_and_server_restart,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,14831,14899,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:649-710"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:300-350""]","Closing a terminal archives it and drops Unread while retaining metadata; after Shutdown+restart the retained stopped Agent row survives with its kind and recovery-unavailable marker, no Unread and no live PTY, using the same registry.",Unread could be persisted as retained metadata (replaying stale attention after restart) or the Agent row could reopen as a shell / lose its kind.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A restart that resurrects a PTY or replays stale attention misstates live state and can mislead the user about running work (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:649-710 archive path).,"Asserts archived rows have no Unread and that the restarted row keeps Agent kind, unavailable recovery and non-live phase (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14835-14897).",Only row covering Unread across removal and restart (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14831-14899).,Real close/archive and a real server restart over the same registry (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14833-14870).,high,keep,Grounded retention-vs-runtime-state separation across restart.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_unread_real_cli_and_dashboard_review_preserve_native_reporting|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_doctor_inspects_identity_freeze_and_preserves_native_input|default""]","[""two server runs"", ""archive and restart"", ""real agent callbacks""]",4.489,4.489,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1482 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_unread_is_reviewed_by_the_next_prompt_typed_in_the_real_dashboard|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,codex_unread_is_reviewed_by_the_next_prompt_typed_in_the_real_dashboard,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,14783,14828,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:29-50"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320""]","In the real dashboard a Ready response shows ""1 ready""; selecting and focusing it does not review it; typing the next prompt into the session reaches the agent (Busy) and clears Unread, and the ready badge disappears.",Focusing/typing could fail to clear Unread (stale badge) or clear it before the prompt actually reached the agent.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Unread-driven attention is the mechanism by which a user finds finished work; a stale badge or premature clear misroutes attention (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320).,"Asserts the badge, full summary equality before typing, Busy activity and cleared Unread after, plus badge removal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14790-14825).",Only row asserting review by typing into the real dashboard (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14783-14828).,Real dashboard PTY with real key input and a real codex hook child (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14785-14800).,high,keep,Grounded interaction-level review coverage with real input.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_unread_real_cli_and_dashboard_review_preserve_native_reporting|default""]","[""dashboard PTY and key sequences"", ""real agent callbacks""]",4.318,4.318,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1483 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_shutdown_acknowledges_through_writer_before_teardown|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,dashboard_shutdown_acknowledges_through_writer_before_teardown,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,7178,7214,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:302-370"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:147-175""]","A dashboard sends Shutdown{kill:false}; the Ok response is observed on the dashboard connection itself, then the socket is removed and the server thread joins.","Shutdown could be acknowledged after tearing down the writer, so the dashboard hangs or reports a false failure while the server is gone.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A lost shutdown acknowledgement leaves the UI unable to distinguish a stopped server from a broken one (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:302-370).,Exact response equality plus socket removal and join; it does not assert the ordering internally beyond receiving the frame (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7184-7213).,Only row asserting the dashboard shutdown ack path; the disconnected-requester row uses a control socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2069-2094).,Real server thread and real dashboard connection with settings publication (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7179-7195).,high,keep,Grounded shutdown acknowledgement coverage on the dashboard writer.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_disconnected_requester_still_wakes_accept|default""]","[""real server thread"", ""dashboard socket and settings drain""]",2.255,2.255,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1496 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_focuses_existing_split_without_duplicating_target|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_focuses_existing_split_without_duplicating_target,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13125,13163,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:116-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:601-700""]","With a two-pane split already showing the target, a ready-ticket click focuses the existing pane, keeps both panes visible, creates no new session rows, and real input afterwards reaches the target and its callback.",Navigation could duplicate the target pane (recreating a session) or focus the wrong peer while claiming the jump succeeded.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A duplicated target pane or wrong focus sends the user input to an unintended session (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:116-190).,"Asserts row-set equality, both panes still visible, and a real callback after Enter proving focus (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13130-13160).",Only row covering split-pane focus without duplication (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13125-13163).,Real dashboard PTY with split layout and real bridge callback (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13128-13145).,high,keep,Grounded focus/identity assertions with a real input probe.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_lands_in_browse_without_reviewing_or_answering|default""]","[""real dashboard PTY"", ""bridge callback"", ""split layout interactions""]",6.902,6.902,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1503 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_never_starts_missing_server_and_old_lifetime_stays_invalid|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_never_starts_missing_server_and_old_lifetime_stays_invalid,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13412,13456,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-115"", ""src/cli/bridge.rs:334-357""]","After the server is shut down and its socket removed, a valid ticket is ignored and the socket is still absent (no auto-start). After an explicit restart, a ticket from the old lifetime is ignored while the new dashboard lists rows unchanged.","A notification click could auto-start a server (unexpected daemon) or accept a lifetime from before the restart, acting on unrelated new state.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A callback that starts a server or accepts a pre-restart lifetime can act on state the banner never described (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-113).,"Asserts ignore, socket absence, and after restart ignore plus row equality (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13420-13455).",Only row covering missing-server and post-restart lifetime invalidation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13412-13456).,"Real server process lifecycle (shutdown, restart) and real bridge callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13414-13450).",high,keep,Grounded lifecycle-boundary assertions for the callback path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_callback_rejects_malformed_versions_before_connecting|default""]","[""real server stop/start"", ""two dashboards"", ""bridge callbacks""]",10.369,10.369,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1507 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_slow_dashboard_recovers_after_finite_burst|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,history_slow_dashboard_recovers_after_finite_burst,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,5060,5146,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:481-540"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095""]","A dashboard selects then ignores a 200000-line burst; the server emits ScreenDirty for the session, a later Select recovers a screen, and HistoryBegin/Page still contains FINAL_HISTORY_MARKER.","A slow dashboard could permanently lose terminal output after the queue overflows, leaving a stale screen with no recovery signal.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Permanently stale terminal content after a burst is unusable until the session restarts (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:481-540).,"Asserts a dirty event, a recovered Select and the final marker in history, but not the recovered screen contents (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5090-5140).",Slow-dashboard recovery through HistoryConnection; the whole-connection variant asserts more (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5149-5292).,Real 200k-line PTY burst and real dashboard event queue (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5060-5090).,high,keep,Grounded slow-consumer recovery coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|slow_dashboard_recovers_after_output_burst|default""]","[""200000 line PTY burst"", ""event drain loop with 50ms polls"", ""history paging""]",2.814,2.814,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1541 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_backpressured_input_keeps_controls_available|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_backpressured_input_keeps_controls_available,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4284,4402,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:884-908"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:871-880""]","A 512KiB Input is blocked on a non-reading PTY and a SendTerminal is also blocked; PauseSession, List, ResumeSession and KillSession each answer within 3-5s and the session exits.",Backpressured input could block pause/resume/kill so a wedged session cannot be stopped or paused.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"A wedged session that cannot be paused, listed or killed requires killing the server (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:884-908).","Each control verb is asserted separately with a deadline; errors are asserted only as timeouts, not as specific blocking reasons (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4350-4395).",Distinct from the backpressure row because pause/resume run while input is blocked (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4284-4402).,Real blocked PTY and real concurrent control connections (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4286-4300).,high,keep,Grounded control-availability coverage under backpressure for the pause path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|backpressured_input_and_send_do_not_block_inspect_or_kill|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default""]","[""512KiB blocked input"", ""10ms/300ms timeout probes"", ""multiple control connections""]",4.388,4.388,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1554 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_control_races_converge|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_control_races_converge,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4065,4068,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:871-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1560""]","Pause, Resume and Kill are issued concurrently from three connections after a barrier; every response must be Ok or Conflict, and the session is then terminated with handlers run; a second session whose leader exited is paused (or refused OwnershipUncertain) and each branch still ends with the group gone and the row removable.","Concurrent control races could produce contradictory phases (e.g. pause after kill), a torn session, or a stuck ownership-uncertain row that cannot be cleaned.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A control race that leaves a session half-paused/mis-killed makes it unusable and blocks removal (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:871-880).,"Asserts the response envelope, eventual kill when nothing succeeded, and per-branch cleanup; the branchy ownership fallback weakens what any single run proves (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4090-4270).",Only row exercising concurrent control verbs from separate connections (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4065-4282).,Real concurrent sockets against a real server and real process groups (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4076-4100).,medium,keep,"Grounded race coverage; the ownership branch means the exercised path varies, so confidence stays medium.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers|default""]","[""barrier-synchronized threads"", ""branchy ownership fallback"", ""datagram acknowledgement collection""]",3.927,3.927,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1555 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_launch_admits_an_executable_whose_version_outlasts_the_probe|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_managed_launch_admits_an_executable_whose_version_outlasts_the_probe,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15827,15879,"[""src/report/pi.rs:26-79"", ""src/report/extension.rs:48-95"", ""src/report/admission.rs:208-240""]","A pi executable whose --version sleeps 2s still binds and reports Connected after session_start; doctor afterwards reports loaded_and_bound, session bound, probe unavailable and version unknown.",A slow version probe could refuse admission of a valid managed launch (no reporting) even though eligibility depends on argv only.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Probe-gated admission silently disables reporting on a loaded machine (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner admission path).,"Asserts binding and Connected after a >1s probe, then doctor probe_status unavailable with version unknown (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15835-15875).",Only row covering a version probe that outlasts the diagnostic budget (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15827-15879).,Real slow version fixture and real doctor CLI (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15829-15860).,high,keep,Grounded timing-boundary admission coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_launch_preserves_argv_exit_and_environment_and_plain_launch_is_untracked|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_doctor_reports_bound_lifecycle_activity_and_transport_loss|default""]","[""2s version sleep"", ""node pi host"", ""doctor CLI""]",3.886,3.886,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1563 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|selection_snapshot_precedes_later_quiet_tail_output|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,selection_snapshot_precedes_later_quiet_tail_output,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,6421,6498,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:574-660"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:254-320""]","A selected session waiting on input receives a newline; the dashboard first observes the Screen snapshot response, then an Output event carrying QUIET_TAIL.","Tail output produced right after the snapshot could be dropped (no later repaint) or the snapshot could be ordered after that output, leaving a permanent gap.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,A permanent one-frame gap leaves stale terminal content until unrelated output arrives (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:574-660).,"Asserts both the snapshot and the later output event are seen, but not their revision or byte continuity (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6465-6490).",Only row asserting snapshot-then-quiet-tail ordering for a single pane (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6421-6498).,"Real PTY with a child that prints only on input, real dashboard socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6425-6440).",medium,keep,Grounded ordering coverage; the exact delivery contract is only partly asserted.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|split_server_two_streams_resize_resync_and_detach|default""]","[""real PTY with gated child output"", ""dashboard event loop""]",2.973,2.973,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1576 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_disconnected_requester_still_wakes_accept|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,shutdown_disconnected_requester_still_wakes_accept,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2069,2094,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1988-2035"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:941-950""]","A control client writes Shutdown{kill:false} and immediately half-closes both directions; the socket disappears within 250ms without an extra connect, and the hosted server thread joins.","If the shutdown acknowledgement needs the requester socket, a disconnect could leave the accept loop blocked and the server orphaned with live sessions.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,An orphaned server holding sessions after shutdown is a major lifecycle failure (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1988-2035).,Asserts socket removal without the recovery connect and that the server joined; the fallback connect is only a diagnostic (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2069-2094).,Only row covering a requester that disappears mid-shutdown (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2069-2094).,"Real server thread, real Unix stream half-close and real socket removal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2070-2092).",high,keep,Grounded coverage of a shutdown race that ordinary tests would not produce.,[],"[""real server thread"", ""socket half-close"", ""250ms wait loop""]",1.285,1.285,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1577 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_kill_terminates_sessions_concurrently|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,shutdown_kill_terminates_sessions_concurrently,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2227,2251,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2035-2105"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1530""]","Six sessions that trap HUP and TERM are created, then Shutdown{kill:true} under a 500ms grace is answered Ok in under 2s, and every recorded process group disappears.",Serial termination would cost sessions x grace and time out the CLI; trapped signals could leave groups alive after shutdown.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Sessions surviving shutdown --kill leak processes and leave the instance half-stopped (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2035-2060).,"Uses a wall-clock bound to prove concurrency plus group-absence for every session; a slower but correct serial run would still fail, which is the intended claim (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2236-2250).",Only row asserting concurrent termination of stubborn groups (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2227-2251).,Six real PTY process groups that ignore HUP/TERM and a real shutdown path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2233-2245).,high,keep,Grounded concurrency coverage whose only observable is timing plus real group cleanup.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|backpressured_input_and_send_do_not_block_inspect_or_kill|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_shutdown_cleans_stopped_groups|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|fifty_sessions_survive_detach_and_leave_no_process_groups|default""]","[""six real PTY process groups"", ""500ms grace override"", ""wall-clock concurrency bound""]",2.980,2.980,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1579 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|slow_dashboard_recovers_after_output_burst|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,slow_dashboard_recovers_after_output_burst,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,5149,5292,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:138-175"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:481-540""]","After asserting event and dispatch queue capacities are 64, a burst is released only after the dashboard selects; exactly one ScreenDirty is observed, the follow-up Select returns the final marker, and no further dirty frames arrive in the quiet window.","Recovery could emit repeated dirty storms or, conversely, never recover, and queue capacities drifting from the tested bound would change overflow behaviour.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,ScreenDirty storms or permanent staleness both degrade the terminal for a slow dashboard (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:481-540).,"Asserts capacity constants, one dirty frame, the recovered screen bytes and a quiet period (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5153-5280).",Stronger than the HistoryConnection variant in the same contract; the two differ only in connection plumbing (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5060-5146).,Real PTY burst and real dashboard queue with the production capacity constants (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5149-5170).,high,keep,Grounded recovery coverage including the dirty-count invariant.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_slow_dashboard_recovers_after_finite_burst|default""]","[""200000 line PTY burst"", ""quiet-window polling"", ""capacity constant assertions""]",3.781,3.781,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1581 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_keeps_shared_existing_socket_directory_and_secures_the_socket|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,startup_keeps_shared_existing_socket_directory_and_secures_the_socket,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,1572,1595,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:145-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:472-540""]","A pre-existing socket parent directory created 0755 is left 0755 after the server starts, while the socket file itself is mode 0700; a graceful stop removes the socket.",Startup could chmod a directory it did not create (breaking a shared or user-owned layout) or leave the socket readable/writable by others.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Rewriting permissions on a caller-owned directory is a destructive wrong-target action on durable state (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:472-540).,"Two exact mode assertions (directory unchanged, socket private) on real metadata (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1572-1595).",Distinct from the private-directory test: this checks non-modification of an existing directory (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1572-1595).,Real server startup and real filesystem modes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1573-1594).,high,keep,"Decisive boundary between creating and reusing a socket directory, observed on the real filesystem.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_socket_directory_is_private|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_refuses_symlinked_socket_directory|default""]","[""real server start"", ""filesystem mode reads"", ""graceful shutdown""]",1.298,1.298,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1588 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
