 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acorrupt_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::corrupt_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,781,794,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:239-254""]",A malformed legacy config.toml is surfaced as a toml parse error and the file's bytes are left exactly as they were.,"Treating an unparseable registry as empty/default and overwriting it, destroying the user's only copy of a recoverable project list.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"Silently replacing the identity file is irreversible loss of the project/workspace list (config.rs:239-254), so the protected behavior is durable-state integrity at C=3.","The error must downcast to toml::de::Error and the file must still read back byte-identically (config.rs:785-793); that rejects replace-on-error, though it does not check that no sidecar database was created.","The corrupt-input counterpart to nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Apresent_empty_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default; different input state (parse error versus empty document), both needed because an empty parse is a distinct case. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:797-810.",Real file through production load_registry (config.rs:205-212) (F=4).,high,keep,Precise non-destruction assertion on the real legacy path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Apresent_empty_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default""]",temp file plus TOML parse,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2369 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Apresent_empty_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::present_empty_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,797,810,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:239-254""]","A present-but-empty legacy config.toml is reported as a TOML error instead of being read as a default registry, and the empty file is not replaced.","Treating an empty document as 'no registry' (Registry::default) and then creating or overwriting storage, erasing the evidence of a truncated/damaged instance.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"An empty file is ambiguous between a fresh install and damaged storage; replacing it would destroy the only record of a damaged instance (config.rs:239-254), so durable-state integrity at C=3.",The error downcast plus the byte-identical empty file (config.rs:801-809) reject the default-on-empty behavior; it does not assert the error message names the file.,"Distinct from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acorrupt_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default because empty input can parse successfully as a default, which the parse-error test cannot catch. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:781-794.",Production load_registry on a real file (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:239-254.,high,keep,Covers the empty-document branch that parse-error assertions miss.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acorrupt_registry_is_reported_and_not_replaced|default""]",temp file plus TOML parse,0.030,0.030,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2378 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aregistry_round_trip_preserves_projects_and_workspaces|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::registry_round_trip_preserves_projects_and_workspaces,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,753,778,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:256-263"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:595-673""]","A registry with one project and one workspace (id, path, branch, git_identity, setup_pending) survives save_registry_atomic then load_registry with full struct equality, including the empty-registry case.",A read/write pair that drops or defaults a workspace field (git_identity or setup_pending) or loses ordering/projects when persisting.,3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"The registry is the durable record of every project and worktree (config.rs:595-673); a field dropped on round-trip loses tracked work state, so C=3.","`assert_eq!(load_registry(&path).unwrap(), registry)` (config.rs:772) compares the whole struct including git_identity Some(""1:2"") and setup_pending true, so a silently defaulted field fails; it does not exercise a partially invalid registry.","Only config.rs test covering the registry struct round-trip end to end; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoffline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating|default covers the legacy shape read, not the write path. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:813-880.","Production save_registry_atomic and load_registry against a real SQLite file (config.rs:256-263, 205-212) (F=4).",high,keep,Full-struct equality over real storage is the right protection for the registry contract.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoffline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating|default""]",temp dir plus rusqlite write/read,0.410,0.410,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2380 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aa_task_after_double_dash_is_never_retained_for_resume|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,recovery::tests::a_task_after_double_dash_is_never_retained_for_resume,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/recovery.rs,132,159,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/recovery.rs:18-70"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:25-52"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/extension_recovery.rs:46-115""]","For Claude, Codex, Pi and Omp, a launch argv ending in `-- <task>` retains the approval flag but never the task text.","Replaying the user's previous task prompt when a session is resumed, re-executing an old instruction or exposing a private prompt in the new session.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,"A retained task is re-sent as the native command's one message on resume (recovery.rs:129-133); re-running an old prompt can repeat a destructive instruction in the user's checkout, wrong-target action at C=3.",All four providers are asserted with exact resulting vectors that exclude the task (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/recovery.rs:137-158).,Each provider's prompt dropping is also asserted by that provider's own recovery test (nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration|default and codex/extension siblings); this adds the shared `--` boundary across all four providers. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:189-220.,Direct calls to the four production launch_options functions (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/extension_recovery.rs:46-115.,high,keep,The cross-provider `--` boundary is unique even though per-provider prompt cases overlap.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration|default""]",argument vectors only,0.013,0.013,1,0,hos