nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areusable_name_migration_preserves_high_water_when_all_rows_were_deleted|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,retained::tests::reusable_name_migration_preserves_high_water_when_all_rows_were_deleted,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs,1295,1317,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:117-177"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:345-440"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:601-642""]","A schema-27 registry whose retained_sessions rows were all deleted, then reopened, still allocates rowid 101 for the next session rather than reusing 1.","A reusable-name migration that resets the AUTOINCREMENT high water when the table is empty, so a new session reuses a deleted session's id that stale conversation references still name.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"Reused ids would alias a new session onto an old session's references (retained.rs:117-177, 601-642), wrong identity/ownership of durable session state, C=3.",One exact `last_insert_rowid() == 101` after a crafted delete-all plus PRAGMA user_version=27 (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:1300-1316); the boundary is precise but only for the empty-table case.,"Distinct from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areusable_name_migration_preserves_references_and_deleted_id_high_water|default, which keeps rows and references; no other test covers the empty-table high water. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:1320-1415.",Real SQLite registry through production open_writable_registry and create (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:601-642.,high,keep,The deleted-id reuse boundary is only covered here.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areusable_name_migration_preserves_references_and_deleted_id_high_water|default""]","temp registry, raw SQL schema/version crafting",0.026,0.026,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2465 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-002,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aagent_models%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areplaced_or_unmarked_worktree_is_refused_before_catalog_spawn|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,server::agent_models::tests::replaced_or_unmarked_worktree_is_refused_before_catalog_spawn,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs,889,954,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:276-310"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:182-193""]","For a real git repository whose captured identity marker is either rewritten or deleted, discover_capabilities returns empty models with a reason containing 'registered Git worktree', and the PATH-resolved native claude script that would write a marker file is never executed.","Dropping or reordering the worktree revalidation so model discovery proceeds, and the native agent runs, inside a worktree whose recorded generation no longer matches.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:302-306 refuses a changed worktree before any catalog spawn; bypassing it runs agent work against a replaced checkout, which is wrong-target work and can lose changes (3).","crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:917-954 checks the error reason and the absence of the native-call marker for two distinct identity failures (replaced and unmarked), rejecting both a missing check and a check ordered after the spawn.",This is the only fixture that drives the pre-spawn worktree revalidation through discovery with a real repository and a spawn sentinel.,"Real git init, real identity marker manipulation, real temp-dir files and the production discover_capabilities; the abort happens exactly at the claimed boundary.",high,keep,Only evidenced protection for the spawn-order invariant around worktree identity.,[],runs git init subprocess twice; writes and deletes identity marker files,0.075,0.075,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2475 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-server-session-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Abuild_identity%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acaptured_record_requires_private_file_current_socket_and_peer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,server::build_identity::tests::captured_record_requires_private_file_current_socket_and_peer,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs,373,394,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:137-145"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:186-201""]","A published record reads back for the publishing pid; the same read fails for pid+1, fails after the record mode is widened to 0644, and fails after the socket is removed and rebound at the same path.","Accepting a record that belongs to another process or an old socket inode, or accepting a world-readable identity file.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,The record is the proof that an existing server is the one the client connected to; accepting another peer or socket inode means acting on wrong ownership (3).,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/build_identity.rs:373-394 asserts three independent refusals plus the accepted baseline; the socket-rebind case directly rejects matching on path instead of device and inode.,"Only test binding the record to peer pid, private mode and current socket inode together.",Real Unix socket with a real rebind plus real files and the production read_server_build.,high,keep,Only coverage of the peer and socket binding invariant.,[],"binds a Unix socket, chmods the record and rebinds a replacement socket",0.291,0.291,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2482 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-server-session-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,server::delegation::archive::tests::archive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs,849,888,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160""]","After an archive is admitted, a reason padded to the remaining byte budget still validates, 64 more bytes are refused, and a maximally sized future owner (max epochs/session ids, 128-256 byte identifiers) still serializes under CONTINUATION_BYTES.","Reserving too few bytes for the future continuation receipt, so a later owner with a long instance/controller name cannot record the filing and the archive is lost.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,"The reservation must cover the worst-case successor principal, not just the current one (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:76-100).","Exact remaining-budget arithmetic then boundary assertions: ok at the computed limit, error 64 bytes later (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:860-860), maximal successor strictly below CONTINUATION_BYTES (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:887-887).",The branch at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160: same capacity contract as nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_last_slot_until_atomic_successful_continuation|default; the distinct input is the maximal future owner shape rather than slot pressure.,Production validate_archive_storage plus real serde sizing of the maximal receipt (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160).,high,keep,"Quantified reserve with a worst-case successor, no timing input.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_last_slot_until_atomic_successful_continuation|default""]","[""one nextest process; real serialization of a maximal receipt""]",0.025,0.025,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2513 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-delegation-001,independent-runtime-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_last_slot_until_atomic_successful_continuation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,server::delegation::archive::tests::archive_reserves_last_slot_until_atomic_successful_continuation,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs,784,823,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:190-220""]","With 62 control intents already stored, admitting an archive consumes the 63rd slot and a further control intent is refused by validate_archive_storage; once a continuation receipt is present and the barrier retired, storage validates, no archive is pending and the original receipt is unchanged.","Spending the last operation slot on unrelated control so a pending archive continuation can never be recorded, or treating the archive as filed while its barrier is still open.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,"The reserved slot is what allows an archive continuation to be recorded at all; losing it strands a child in an unfilable archive state (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160, crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:190-220).","Exhausted validate_archive_storage errors before the refusal is attempted (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:801-801), and after the continuation the same validation passes with pending none and receipt equality (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:821-822).","The branch at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160: same capacity contract as nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner|default and nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aserialized_near_full_records_protect_slots_and_bytes_until_their_own_continuation|default, but the distinct input is the slot drained by control intents rather than bytes.",Production admit_archive and validate_archive_storage run on a real Record; the constants are the module's (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:8-13).,high,keep,Boundary at exactly one free slot with a positive completion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner|default""]","[""one nextest process; 62 generated intents""]",0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2512 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-delegation-001,independent-runtime-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astop_certification_spends_original_outcome_headroom_without_spending_continuation_bytes|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,server::delegation::archive::tests::stop_certification_spends_original_outcome_headroom_without_spending_continuation_bytes,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs,826,846,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160""]","A stop certification reuses the original outcome's growth headroom: the record validates at the exact byte budget, still validates after the outcome grows to StoppedArchivePending, and one further byte is refused.","Certifying a stop that consumes the bytes reserved for the future continuation, so the owner can record the stop but never the follow-up that completes the archive.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,Byte reservation protects a future owner's ability to record the continuation (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:76-100).,"Exact-boundary assertions: validate ok, transition ok, then exactly one more byte errors (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:845-845), rejecting both an off-by-one and an unbounded reservation.","The branch at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:36-160: same byte-accounting contract as nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner|default, distinct input (outcome growth during stop certification).",Production validate_archive_storage with the real constants (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_archive.rs:8-13).,high,keep,Single precise boundary with a positive and a negative side.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Aarchive%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aarchive_reserves_bytes_against_later_record_writes_and_future_owner|default""]","[""one nextest process; exact byte arithmetic""]",0.064,0.064,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2515 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-delegation-001,independent-runtime-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Afollowups%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_followup_keeps_original_digest_without_gaining_current_authority|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,server::delegation::followups::tests::legacy_followup_keeps_original_digest_without_gaining_current_authority,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_followups.rs,1161,1184,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:16-45"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_followups.rs:60-88""]","A legacy followup intent without expected_control_epoch deserializes to epoch 0, fails require_controller, and re-serializes to exactly the original JSON with only that field absent.","Migration granting a legacy followup the current control epoch, letting a stale intent pass the controller fence.",3,4,2,4,75,80,78,Without a captured epoch the intent must not satisfy the controller fence (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:16-45).,"expected_control_epoch 0, require_controller error, and exact JSON equality after removing the new field (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_followups.rs:1171-1180).",The branch at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:16-45: sibling nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Acontrol%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_metadata_preserves_receipt_digests_without_inventing_initial_authority|default covers legacy control fields; this one covers the followup intent's epoch default.,"Production serde default plus require_controller (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_followups.rs:60-88, crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:16-45).",high,keep,Exact round-trip equality and a fence failure.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Adelegation%3A%3Acontrol%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_metadata_preserves_receipt_digests_without_inventing_initial_authority|default""]","[""one nextest process""]",0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evid