nextest|Test|ovrcr|service%3A%3Adashboard_startup_tests%3A%3Adashboard_service_checks_executable_and_manager_ownership_for_both_platforms|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,service::dashboard_startup_tests::dashboard_service_checks_executable_and_manager_ownership_for_both_platforms,default,src/service.rs,868,942,"[""src/service.rs:214-290"", ""src/service.rs:597-625"", ""src/service.rs:642-666"", ""src/client.rs:406-415""]","dashboard_service_with returns the installed launchd or systemd definition only when its ProgramArguments or ExecStart is the intended executable and the OVRCR_SOCKET assignment appears exactly once; it refuses a duplicated definition, a different executable, and a listener whose peer pid is not the loaded manager's MainPID.","Without the peer-pid and manager check the Dashboard would take over - shut down and replace - a socket served by an unmanaged or foreign OVRCR process, killing sessions it does not own; without the executable check it would adopt a definition another install pointed at a different binary.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,Taking over a listener it does not own destroys another instance's running sessions - wrong ownership and a threat to durable session state (src/service.rs:280-290).,"Four assertions cover the definition echo, the duplicate-assignment refusal, the executable mismatch text and the peer-pid mismatch (src/service.rs:890-941), and the manager stub returns the exact launchctl and systemctl output formats; the socket-path mismatch branch (src/service.rs:240-243) and the O_NOFOLLOW symlink refusal are untested.","tests/service.rs:264-280 covers the install path's refusal through managed_connection (src/service.rs:629-640); the Dashboard startup variant, its executable match and its duplicate-assignment rule are asserted only here.","Real definition files, a real Unix socket pair whose kernel peer credentials are read through src/client.rs:406-415, and real ServiceConfig resolution are used; only the launchctl/systemctl process is a stub script, which is the external boundary tests cannot own.",high,keep,"The only direct coverage of the Dashboard's service ownership guard, whose regression kills another instance's sessions; keep.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aservice|install_refuses_to_take_over_an_unmanaged_server|default""]",0.052s one hosted attempt; a real Unix listener and stream pair per platform plus a stub manager script executed for print/show and is-active,0.052,0.052,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:677 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,
