python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-packaging.py|production-profile-from-local-rejected%3Aln137|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-packaging.py,script-check,acceptance,production-profile-from-local-rejected:ln137,local-development,native/bridge/check-packaging.py,137,137,"[""native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:20-89"", ""scripts/build-bridge.sh:115-145""]","A copy of the local-development source bundle with its OVRCRBridgeLocalDevelopment marker removed and the production identity written in (com.ovrcr.bridge / OVRCR) is rejected by validate-bundle.py when the local profile validates it: validate(production, False) at check-packaging.py:137 defaults local=local_development=True, so the validator runs with --local-development.","If the local-profile validator accepted a marker-less production-identity artifact, a local packaging copy could be validated as if it were the fixed local build, and the local pin requiring the exact marker/identity would no longer hold.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"The local profile pin is what stops a local artifact from carrying the production identity; losing it confuses which profile an artifact belongs to (native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:44-57, native/bridge/check-packaging.py:130-137).","It asserts a non-zero validator exit for the production-identity copy under the local profile (native/bridge/check-packaging.py:130-137); the pristine local baseline is the separate validate(source) row at native/bridge/check-packaging.py:36-37, so this negative carries no positive control of its own and S=3 rather than 4 is the honest score.","It is the only row where a production-identity artifact meets the local-profile validator; the accepted direction is the neighbouring validate(production, True, local=False) row (native/bridge/check-packaging.py:138).","A real copied bundle and the real validator run as a subprocess (native/bridge/check-packaging.py:130-137, native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:44-57).",high,keep,"Distinct profile-mismatch direction with no equivalent coverage; corrected description and S score, kept.",[],"[""real copied bundle plus a validator subprocess""]",,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3645 (36 checks) '36 packaging checks passed under PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no signing/install/launch.' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-001,independent-packaging-check-1
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|local-contract-profile-pin-rejected%3Aln116|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,local-contract-profile-pin-rejected:ln116,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,116,117,"[""native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:116-117"", ""native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:32-56""]",The local payload's Info.plist is rewritten to production metadata while its expected-contract.json still pins local_development=true; the local-profile validator must still exit nonzero.,"A validator that trusts the plist metadata over the pinned contract, so production metadata overrides the contract's local-development pin.",3,3,3,4,75,80,78,"The contract is the release pin; if metadata can override it, a payload whose contract says local is shipped as production (3).","native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:116-117 rejects either invocation on the mutated payload and counts the check; native/bridge/validate-bundle.py:32-34 and :47-56 assert contract/marker consistency, so a wrong pass is rejected.",Only this script mutates the expected-contract.json profile pin; the installer suite does not test contract-field precedence.,"Real payload copy with a rewritten Info.plist and contract, through the production validator.",high,keep,Only test that the pinned contract's profile outranks rewritten plist metadata in the relocated validator.,[],copies a payload tree; rewrites plist/contract; spawns the validator twice,,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,independent-report-check-2
python-unittest|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-installer.py%3A%3AInstallerTests|test_local_refuses_production_artifact|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-unittest,native/bridge/check-installer.py::InstallerTests,unittest,acceptance,test_local_refuses_production_artifact,default,native/bridge/check-installer.py,753,760,"[""scripts/install-bridge.sh:100-157""]",A local install of a source converted to the production identity exits 1 before staging.,Installing a production artifact through the local path.,3,4,2,4,75,80,78,"The real installer script decides what is signed, staged and published; a wrong decision ships an untrusted or broken app (scripts/install-bridge.sh:100-157).","Runs the real install-bridge.sh with the fake codesign/ditto dispatcher and asserts the exact operation sequence, exit code, artifact snapshots and absence of publication or staging.",This unittest targets 'test_local_refuses_production_artifact' with its own fixture state; no other row stages the same authority state (native/bridge/check-installer.py:753-760).,The real shipping installer runs against a real private filesystem; only the external signer/copier/CLI tools are deterministic fakes that record their arguments.,high,keep,Grounded installer boundary with exact artifact/permission assertions; no equivalent coverage.,[],"[""real install-bridge.sh under a private HOME"", ""fake codesign/ditto dispatcher recording every call"", ""fixture snapshot and process-group checks""]",,,,,unmeasured,no per-method timing; unittest prints one aggregate: macOS-job.log:3631 'Ran 33 tests in 10.080s' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-001,
