nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|conversation_subjects_use_retained_provider_histories_and_survive_restart|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,conversation_subjects_use_retained_provider_histories_and_survive_restart,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,605,713,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:109-124"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:852-926"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302""]","For each of Pi, Omp, Codex and Claude, creates an agent session, retains a provider-specific history file whose first line carries the conversation identity, waits for the display name to become Fixture Topic, then requires exactly four title calls and after a kill-shutdown plus restart requires every display name to be Fixture Topic again.","Any provider's history parser failing to bind the retained conversation (no subject), a provider firing more than one call, or subjects not being persisted across restart so a restarted server shows creation names.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Titles are the user's navigation identity for retained sessions; losing them on restart or misparsing one provider's history silently degrades the whole dashboard for that provider.,"Four distinct header formats are exercised, the total call count is pinned to four and the restart loop re-asserts every display name through the public List API.",Only restart-persistence test spanning all four provider formats; per-provider deep tests cover rename/mismatch behavior.,"Real server binary, real SQLite registry and real history files; only the model provider is a fake script, which is the appropriate external fixture.",high,keep,Unique cross-provider persistence contract with an exact call-count budget; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_matching_session_meta_shows_subject_replacing_creation_name_until_rename|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|claude_matching_mode_and_session_id_shows_subject_replacing_creation_name_until_rename|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|terminal_with_retained_agent_does_not_spawn_title_pi|default""]","[""starts and restarts the server"", ""four sessions plus four fake-pi calls"", ""12.66 s observed""]",12.660,12.660,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:709 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|identical_subject_reply_does_not_count_as_replacement|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,identical_subject_reply_does_not_count_as_replacement,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2073,2133,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:784-850"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:240-242""]","Titles a session, appends history so the provider repeats the same topic (asserting accepted/attempt 1/2 and an unchanged display), then appends again so the provider returns a clearer topic and asserts accepted/attempt 2/3, the new display and unchanged identity.","An identical reply being counted as an accepted replacement (burning the second revision and ignoring the real revision), or the third attempt no longer being accepted.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The accepted/attempt distinction keeps a repetitive model from consuming the revision budget, which would make the title permanently stale.","The (1,2) then (2,3) counter sequence pins both branches of the topic-equality condition in one body.",Only test isolating the identical-topic branch; the retained unit test mirrors it at store level.,"Real server, SQLite and fake provider; the provider reply content is scripted on call count.",high,keep,Precise counter evidence for a subtle equality branch; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|one_later_subject_may_replace_once_then_window_closes|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aidentical_subject_reply_is_not_a_new_accept_but_spends_an_attempt|default""]","[""provider script keyed on call count"", ""200 ms settle plus waits"", ""SQLite reads""]",8.433,8.433,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:710 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|one_later_subject_may_replace_once_then_window_closes|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,one_later_subject_may_replace_once_then_window_closes,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1999,2070,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:240-242"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:784-850""]","Titles a session (accepted/attempt 1/1), appends history to earn one replacement (2/2), then appends again and asserts after five seconds that the call count is unchanged, the second topic is still displayed and identity is unchanged.","A third accepted subject or an extra provider call after the replacement window closes, or losing the revision accounting so a legitimate second topic is rejected.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,An open window means repeated provider calls carrying private history and titles that flip on every turn.,"Exact accepted_count/attempt_count pairs are read from SQLite before and after the window closes, and the call count must freeze.",Replacement-window accounting is distinct from the identical-reply case (row 34) and the failure cap (row 35).,"Real server, SQLite and fake provider.",high,keep,Exact counter assertions are a decisive invariant for the two-revision contract; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|identical_subject_reply_does_not_count_as_replacement|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|three_failed_title_attempts_close_window_and_survive_restart|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aone_subject_revision_is_allowed_then_further_replies_are_ignored|default""]","[""provider script counts invocations"", ""5 s settle"", ""SQLite reads""]",11.421,11.421,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:715 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|rename_keeps_manual_title_and_drops_late_subject|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,rename_keeps_manual_title_and_drops_late_subject,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2233,2279,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1330-1395"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:784-800"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-380""]","Starts a title call whose provider sleeps two seconds, renames the session from the dashboard, waits for the rename event and then three more seconds, asserting the manual name is still displayed, identity is unchanged and zero subject rows were written.","A late model reply overriding an explicit user rename, or a subject row being stored for a conversation the user already renamed.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,A user's explicit rename must win over an in-flight automatic title; otherwise user intent is silently discarded.,"The dashboard change event pins the rename before the result arrives, and both the display name and the subject-row count are checked after the late reply.",Rename race is distinct from clear (row 38) and recorded-switch (row 40) races.,"Real server, dashboard stream, SQLite and fake provider.",high,keep,Covers a user-intent race with a DB-level no-write assertion; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_archive_is_not_saved_or_shown|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|clear_restores_original_dismisses_current_subject_and_keeps_other|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arename_hides_subject_and_late_save_is_dropped_without_changing_identity|default""]","[""provider sleeps 2 s"", ""3 s settle"", ""SQLite read""]",8.219,8.219,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:716 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|terminal_with_retained_agent_does_not_spawn_title_pi|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,terminal_with_retained_agent_does_not_spawn_title_pi,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1308,1419,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:780-800"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:240-242""]","Creates a terminal session with a retained Pi conversation and no pinned title, asserts pinned_title is null and the recovery conversation matches, then creates a control Pi agent and asserts it is titled with exactly one total call while the terminal keeps its creation name and has zero subject rows.","Titling a terminal session from its retained agent history (sending shell transcript content to a model), or requiring a manual title to exclude terminals so a later Clear re-enables titling.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Terminal sessions are the user's shell; titling them from retained history transmits shell content without consent, and the exclusion must be independent of a pinned title.","The pinned_title null check removes the alternative explanation, the control agent proves the worker is active with exactly one call, and the terminal has both a name and row-count assertion.",Only terminal-kind exclusion test with retained history and a positive control; row 20 covers it without a model.,Real server and PTY; the fake provider is the controlled dependency.,high,keep,Positive control plus two negative invariants make this the authoritative terminal-exclusion test.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_model_missing_mismatches_terminal_and_grok_do_not_spawn_pi|default""]","[""server spawn, terminal and two agent sessions"", ""3 s settle"", ""fake-pi call log""]",8.607,8.607,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:721 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|three_failed_title_attempts_close_window_and_survive_restart|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,three_failed_title_attempts_close_window_and_survive_restart,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2136,2230,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:746-782"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:240-242"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-400""]","Drives three failing provider calls, waits for accepted/attempt (0,3), asserts no further call after another history change, then restarts the server and asserts the window stays closed, the name is unchanged and the counters are still (0,3).","Retrying after three failures (unbounded provider cost and repeated excerpts), or forgetting the failure count across restart so a restarted server reopens the window.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Without a persisted cap, every server restart and every history change re-sends private content to a provider.","Attempt counts are read before closing, the call count is frozen after the window closes, and the same assertions are repeated after a restart.",Failure-cap plus restart persistence is unique; row 33 covers the accepted cap.,"Real server, SQLite, restart and fake provider.",high,keep,Persisted negative invariant across restart; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|one_later_subject_may_replace_once_then_window_closes|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Athree_failed_attempts_close_the_title_window|default""]","[""provider exits 2 per call"", ""two server runs"", ""5 s settles"", ""22.8 s observed""]",22.799,22.799,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:723 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_failures_mismatches_and_missing_binary_do_not_change_rows_or_retry|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_failures_mismatches_and_missing_binary_do_not_change_rows_or_retry,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,787,958,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-400"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:900-925"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:746-782""]",Exercises three independent failure classes: a provider exiting 2 leaves the name unchanged with attempt_count 1 and no retry; a history whose session header names a different conversation spends no attempt and produces zero subject rows while the call log stays exactly `call`; and a missing Pi executable is not retried in the same process even after the history changes and the executable later appears.,"Retrying a failed title call every poll (provider cost and repeated private excerpts), writing a subject for a mismatched conversation identity, or retrying a missing-binary condition after the environment changes.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Mismatched identity can attach another conversation's topic to a session, and unbounded retries repeatedly send private content to a provider.","Attempt counts, zero subject rows, the exact single call marker, and the absence of later calls after a history change and executable creation are all asserted, each against a separate fixture.",Three failure classes in one body; other rows cover the attempt cap and provider-specific mismatches rather than failed-call retry suppression.,"Real server, SQLite registry, history files and fake provider; appropriate fixture.",high,keep,Strong negative coverage of retry and identity-binding failures; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|three_failed_title_attempts_close_window_and_survive_restart|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|codex_mismatched_first_line_does_not_produce_subject_or_spend_attempt|default""]","[""three server fixtures plus one restart-free second server"", ""multiple 3 s settles"", ""wait_file polling""]",20.824,20.824,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:726 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_prompt_and_excerpt_stay_out_of_server_log|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_prompt_and_excerpt_stay_out_of_server_log,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1259,1305,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:395-420"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:680-700""]","Runs a successful title flow whose retained history contains EXCERPT_SECRET_9f3a, asserts the provider prompt contains the secret and the prompt sentence, then asserts the server log and the raw registry database bytes contain neither the secret nor the prompt sentence.","Writing the excerpt or the composed prompt into server.log or the SQLite registry, which would persist conversation content beyond the intended transient call.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Conversation content is private; persisting it in a log or the registry creates a durable privacy exposure outside the retained-history model.,"A positive check proves the secret was actually in flight, and two negative scans read the real log and the raw DB file, so a silent leak is caught rather than inferred.",Only normal-path leak scan; row 22 covers the failure-path log.,"Real server, real log and real database file; fake provider is the external dependency.",high,keep,Positive-then-negative secrecy assertion on the normal path; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_save_failure_while_live_leaves_subject_unsaved|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Atitle%3A%3Atests%3A%3Atitle_decisions_are_events_and_omit_the_excerpt|default""]","[""server spawn and fake provider"", ""reads the whole SQLite file as bytes"", ""4.25 s observed""]",4.251,4.251,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:727 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_subject_storage_archive_and_exclusions_cover_live_paths|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_subject_storage_archive_and_exclusions_cover_live_paths,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1026,1115,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:852-926"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:969-983"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302""]","Retains a 300 KiB Pi history whose oldest message sits before the tail window, asserts the prompt for the title call contains the tail reply but not the old message, closes the terminal and reads the archived row through the CLI while asserting its display name, then creates a Hermes session and asserts the call log does not change.","Reading the head instead of the tail so a stale prompt is sent, dropping the subject when the session is archived, or routing a Hermes session through the Pi title call.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Sending the wrong excerpt leaks older conversation content and produces a bad title, and losing a subject on archive removes the user's only handle on a stopped session.","Positive tail content and negative old-message assertions, plus an archived CLI read and a call-count equality for Hermes, cover three separate contracts in one flow.",Archive listing plus Hermes exclusion plus tail content is unique; row 24 measures the read bound exactly.,"Real server, real CLI archive read and real histories; fake provider is appropriate.",high,keep,Multi-contract coverage with concrete negative assertions; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_history_read_stops_at_256_kib|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_archive_is_not_saved_or_shown|default""]","[""spawns the CLI for the archived listing"", ""writes a 300 KiB history"", ""3 s settle""]",9.343,9.343,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:732 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
