 script installed"", ""3.19 s observed""]",3.185,3.185,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:737 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_silent_for_sixty_seconds_times_out_and_the_process_is_gone|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,integration,claude_probe_silent_for_sixty_seconds_times_out_and_the_process_is_gone,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,351,353,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:18-18"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:330-375"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:384-394""]","Delegates to assert_probe_deadline(""silent"", PROBE_TIMED_OUT), which waits up to 75 s for a QuotaChanged with that reason, requires at least 60 s elapsed, Unavailable state, and the recorded provider pid to be gone.","A silently hung probe never timing out, or the deadline being reported without killing the PTY child (a leaked provider process per refresh).",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,An unbounded hidden provider process holds resources and blocks every later quota refresh until restart.,"The elapsed lower bound, exact reason, state and ESRCH-style liveness check make both the deadline and cleanup observable.",No-callback timeout path; row 59 is the callback-then-hang path and rows 56/57 are immediate classifications.,"Real 60 s deadline, real PTY child and real pid check.",high,keep,Expensive but decisive deadline-plus-cleanup invariant; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_startup_without_usage_reaches_the_deadline_and_the_process_is_gone|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_that_exits_is_unavailable|default""]","[""60 s real deadline per run"", ""75 s read timeout"", ""PTY provider"", ""62.91 s observed""]",62.912,62.912,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:788 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_startup_without_usage_reaches_the_deadline_and_the_process_is_gone|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,integration,claude_probe_startup_without_usage_reaches_the_deadline_and_the_process_is_gone,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,356,358,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:330-375"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:384-394""]","Delegates to assert_probe_deadline(""no-limits-hang"", PROBE_MISSING_USAGE), requiring at least 60 s elapsed, Unavailable state with the missing-usage reason (not timed out) and a dead provider pid.","A probe that received a startup callback and then hung being classified as timed out rather than missing usage, or not being killed at the deadline.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The distinction decides the user-visible repair (provider usage unavailable versus probe timeout), and the process must not leak.","The shared helper asserts elapsed >= 60 s, the exact PROBE_MISSING_USAGE reason, state Unavailable and the probe pid gone (tests/claude_quota_probe.rs:378-388); a misclassification never matches and the 75 s loop panics, the same strength as the silent-mode sibling.",Callback-then-deadline branch is distinct from the silent timeout in row 58.,Real 60 s deadline and PTY child.,high,keep,Complements row 58 on the received-callback edge; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_silent_for_sixty_seconds_times_out_and_the_process_is_gone|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_without_rate_limits_is_unavailable|default""]","[""60 s real deadline"", ""PTY provider in hang mode"", ""62.92 s observed""]",62.920,62.920,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:789 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_waits_for_usage_after_the_startup_callback|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,acceptance,claude_probe_waits_for_usage_after_the_startup_callback,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,279,315,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:330-360"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:433-456"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/claude_allowance.rs:10-11""]","In cold-start mode, waits for a Current Probe-sourced row while asserting the state is never Unsupported, requires the provider log to show COLD_CALLBACK_ACKNOWLEDGED, exactly two windows with the 5h window at 8800 basis points, exactly one probe, and a dead process.","Classifying the startup callback as final (Unsupported or Current without usage), restarting the probe on each callback, or publishing only one window.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"A wrong classification permanently mislabels a subscription, and a restarting probe would repeatedly spawn a provider process.","`assert_ne Unsupported` runs inside the event predicate, and window contents, probe count and liveness are asserted after the row settles.",Cold-start callback semantics are distinct from row 56's exit classification and row 58's no-callback timeout.,"Real server, PTY provider fixture and real status-line callback.",high,keep,Covers the callback-versus-usage distinction with exact window values; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_without_rate_limits_is_unavailable|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aquota_probe%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astartup_callbacks_wait_for_usable_subscription_usage|default""]","[""PTY provider in cold-start mode"", ""window-count and process polling"", ""4.66 s observed""]",4.661,4.661,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:741 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acodex_initial_prompt|codex_models_come_from_the_current_dashboard_workspace_app_server|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::codex_initial_prompt,integration,acceptance,codex_models_come_from_the_current_dashboard_workspace_app_server,default,tests/codex_initial_prompt.rs,236,319,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:1-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:998-1055""]","Runs a fake codex app-server, queries models for the dashboard workspace, and asserts one model (gpt-5.4 alias/resolved), a binding, exact app-server argv, exact request method order, explicitGatewayOauth, exact startup-config argv, and no thread/turn requests.","Model discovery using the wrong workspace cwd or argv, reordering or dropping protocol requests, or starting a thread/turn during a read-only catalog query.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Model catalogs drive the launch picker; wrong models or a stray thread start mislead the user and may create provider work.,"Exact argv, request order, model fields and two negative request assertions make the protocol conversation fully observable.",Only model-catalog integration test; agent_models unit tests cover resolution rules without the app-server exchange.,Real server and a fake codex app-server standing in for the provider; the catalog protocol is real.,high,keep,Full protocol transcript assertions; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aagent_models%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amodel_catalog_refuses_a_client_launcher_that_differs_from_server_resolution|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aagent_models%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aconfigured_origin_never_reaches_native_model_discovery|default""]","[""server spawn"", ""fake app-server child"", ""catalog query""]",4.468,4.468,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:870 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-002,
