nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abridge_expired_permission_recovers_only_through_an_explicit_status_check|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::desktop::tests::bridge_expired_permission_recovers_only_through_an_explicit_status_check,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs,3880,4079,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:311-352"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:363-425"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1183-1350""]","For each of available, denied, not_determined and permission_pending replies after an expired authorization, only an explicit O Status check recovers: the palette names the real action, the checking notice clears on completion, bindings change with the resulting status, and disabling desktop notifications permits no recovery traffic.","An expired authorization silently restarting polling or opening a second permission prompt, a completed check leaving the checking notice, or recovery controls surviving with notifications disabled.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Permission recovery after expiry decides whether the user can restore banners (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:311-352); a wrong state machine leaves a permanently unconfirmed channel or repeats OS consent prompts.,"Four-way reply matrix with exact request sequences, palette text renders, binding names, unconfirmed predicates, notice absence and a notifications-off negative case (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:3880-4076).",Broader than the denial and pending-poll rows: it is the only test checking all four post-expiry statuses and the notifications-off recovery guard together.,"Production Dashboard recovery, palette and keymap paths with a fake bridge client supplying each status; native notification permission itself is out of scope for a deterministic test.",high,keep,Grounded matrix with precise positive and negative assertions; high value for the most complex recovery state machine here.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abridge_denial_has_persistent_recovery_and_settings_only_runs_explicitly|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abridge_pending_polls_are_bounded_and_never_repeat_authorization|default""]","[""four status iterations each spawning the fake bridge client"", ""wait_bridge polling"", ""120x40 TestBackend renders for palette text""]",2.618,2.618,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2951 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abridge_outbound_banners_use_only_manual_or_original_identity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::desktop::tests::bridge_outbound_banners_use_only_manual_or_original_identity,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs,3587,3681,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:640-701"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:830-862""]","Outbound bridge Deliver requests for Ready and Input alerts carry only the fixed title, a subtitle from manual_title or the session name, and a project/workspace/name(#id) body; generated conversation titles, labels, invocation ids, turn ids, paths and bidi controls are excluded, and identity text is clipped to 80 characters with byte caps.","A generated private conversation subject, workspace path, invocation or turn id reaching the native notification payload, or a bidi or control character surviving identity sanitisation into the banner text.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The protected property is privacy of session identity leaves crossing to macOS notifications (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:836-862); a leak exposes private titles and filesystem paths to a persistent outbound payload, though not message bodies or credentials.","Positive assertions pin title, navigation validity, session id and the exact body, plus 80-char and byte caps, and negative scans reject PRIVATE_GENERATED, PRIVATE_LABEL, PRIVATE_CONVERSATION, PRIVATE_INVOCATION, /private/path and turn- in the outbound file (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:3610-3650).",Distinct from the desktop-only identity export test and from the native input payload test because it exercises the bridge Deliver serialisation with a manual title containing bidi characters; no other reviewed test inspects the bridge outbound file for identity leaks.,"Runs the real notification observation and bridge delivery path with a fake shell client (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:2606-2640), so Dashboard composition and payload construction are production code; native provider acceptance of the banner is not proven, as expected of a fake client.",high,keep,"Grounded, decisive privacy assertions with no equivalent named coverage; cost is modest and does not affect value.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adesktop_ready_requires_new_accepted_root_identity_and_only_exports_identity|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Anative_input_notification_payload_excludes_dynamic_question_and_answer_content|default""]","[""fake bridge shell client spawned per outbound operation"", ""wait_bridge polling with a 3 s deadline"", ""tempdir request and status files""]",0.567,0.567,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2946 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aevent_loop%3A%3Aoperator_loop_tests%3A%3Aoperator_quick_production_dispatch_keeps_key_paste_mouse_resize_off_pty|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::event_loop::operator_loop_tests::operator_quick_production_dispatch_keeps_key_paste_mouse_resize_off_pty,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs,1912,2161,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:553-608"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/operator.rs:411-489"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/operator.rs:1240-1520""]","With Quick open, Ctrl-o, control chords, paste including an OSC52 sequence, mouse and resize produce no socket request and no PTY bytes; Ctrl-c clears only the Quick draft; Enter sends exactly one Create, and the Created receipt yields exactly one Submit with the captured text and no Input or AssignedHumanInput.","A Quick-composer keystroke or paste escaping into the PTY (Ctrl-C interrupting an agent, OSC52 writing the clipboard), or Enter emitting Create plus PTY input.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Input leaking from the modal into the agent PTY can interrupt or drive a running agent (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:553-608) and inject clipboard controls; that is a wrong action rather than a cosmetic one.,"Asserts no readable frame after every editing, mouse and resize event, that Ctrl-c clears only the draft, one Create on Enter, one Submit with the exact text, and no Input or AssignedHumanInput (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:1912-2158).","Complements the real-socket-reader row: this covers the Quick modal's dispatch immunity, while the other covers stream separation and Stop identity.","Runs the real reader thread, dispatch loop, terminal writer and vt100 parser against a UnixStream pair; only the server is scripted.",high,keep,Grounded at the real dispatch boundary with decisive negative assertions; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aevent_loop%3A%3