nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aone_revision_set_numbers_every_observation_kind_in_order|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::one_revision_set_numbers_every_observation_kind_in_order,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,167,198,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:656-683""]","One publisher numbering activity, input and health yields revisions 1, 2 and 3 with the health report at revision 3, so all observation kinds share one monotonic counter.","Per-kind revision counters that disagree, causing the server to reject a valid report as stale or accept an older sample.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The server keeps a watermark per kind; a disagreeing counter drops or reorders observations, corrupting the reported state (3).","src/report/reporter/tests.rs:167-198 asserts the exact revision vector [1,2,3] and the single Unavailable health entry, which a per-kind counter fails.",Only revision-set test; the bind-reset row covers generation resets.,Production Reporter over the scripted supervisor socket.,high,keep,Single-counter invariant is load-bearing for every publish path.,[],scripted supervisor run,0.038,0.038,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:666 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoperator_uses_watched_lease_and_validates_exact_journal_receipts|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::operator_uses_watched_lease_and_validates_exact_journal_receipts,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,584,714,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:169-240""]","Against a server thread that mirrors operator request validation, operator_start returns the identity, a batch with the wrong sequence is an error, a refused retire is an error, and a retire with stop proof succeeds; the observed command sequence is exactly Start, Retire, Stop.","Accepting a mismatched batch receipt as commit proof or a refused retire as stop proof, recording operator work that did not commit or a stop that did not happen.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Operator batches and stop proof are the durable authority over an operator turn; a wrong accept loses or forges turn state (3).,"src/report/reporter/tests.rs:584-714 asserts the two error cases and then the exact three-command sequence, with the server asserting auth and identity on every request.",Only operator reporter test; it also watches the lease's request ordering.,Real Unix socket with the production InvocationLease and reporter methods; the server responses are a test thread mirroring the runtime checks.,high,keep,Only coverage of the operator reporter's receipt validation.,[],spawns a server thread over a UnixStream pair with a 5s timeout,0.029,0.029,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:667 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aretention_retry_cannot_retarget_a_new_binding|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,integration,report::reporter::tests::retention_retry_cannot_retarget_a_new_binding,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,491,534,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:443-520""]","A retention for binding 'a' that fails stays pending for a; after a bind to 'b' the pending write is dropped, a retention for 'b' succeeds, a delayed retry for 'a' fails, and after binding 'a' again only the new 'a' retention succeeds, producing exactly generations 1..3 with a, b, a.","Resubmitting the old pending retention under the new binding, or letting a delayed retry persist metadata against a generation it does not belong to.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Retention metadata tells a restarted session which provider history to resume; retargeting it attaches the wrong conversation (durable-state and ownership, 3).","src/report/reporter/tests.rs:491-534 asserts the exact retained (generation, identity) sequence, which any retarget or dropped retry changes.",Only retention-retarget test.,Production Reporter with a scripted supervisor alternating refuse and accept.,high,keep,Only evidence that a pending retention cannot follow a new binding.,[],six scripted answers over the supervisor socket,0.061,0.061,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:670 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20print-mode%20child%20emits%20no%20approval%20or%20question%20frames|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,a print-mode child emits no approval or question frames,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,340,348,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","In mode 'print', approval and ask-tool events produce no frames and no helper record.","If the mode guard did not cover the tool handlers, a child's approvals would be reported as the root's pending prompts, so the human would be asked to approve a tool call in a session the dialog does not belong to.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Cross-mode reporting is the same wrong-session input state as the foreign-id case (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:108-108).,It sends all three event kinds through a print-mode host and asserts an empty record (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:340-348).,"The print-mode inertness row covers lifecycle events; this row covers the tool/approval handlers, which are separately guarded by report()'s mode check; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:107-109, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport in print mode; the absence of the record file proves no helper ran (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:345-348).,high,keep,Covers the mode guard on the tool handlers specifically; keep.,[],0.006s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.006,0.006,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 6.403583 at macOS-job.log:3813; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|a%20print-mode%20reattach%20delivers%20nothing%2C%20spawns%20no%20helper%2C%20and%20says%20it%20is%20unavailable|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,"a print-mode reattach delivers nothing, spawns no helper, and says it is unavailable",default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,166,174,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Running ovrcr-reattach in mode 'print' creates no record file, delivers no frame, and notifies 'OVRCR reporting is unavailable' at warning level.","If reattach ignored the mode guard, a child session would spawn a helper and announce itself as a producer, giving the receiver a second owner for the root's conversation.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"A child-session producer would compete with the interactive root for the same conversation, i.e. a duplicate authority over one session's reporting (src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:147-149).","It asserts the absence of the file itself, not just an empty frame list, plus the exact warning notice (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:166-174).",Only OMP has this print-mode reattach branch; the Pi reattach row covers a tui-mode producer (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:365-380).,The real command handler and real transport run with mode 'print'; the fixture observes the filesystem to prove no helper ran (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:170-174).,high,keep,Only test of the print-mode reattach refusal; keep.,[],0.004s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.004,0.004,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 3.949667 at macOS-job.log:3747; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20approval%20from%20another%20session%20id%20or%20with%20none%20emits%20nothing|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an approval from another session id or with none emits nothing,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,219,228,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","An approval or resolution whose sessionId is 'other-session', or is the empty string, produces no frame at all, while the root session's own id is required.","If the root check were dropped, an in-process task or advisor child's approval would be reported as the interactive root's, so the user would see and could answer a prompt belonging to a different session.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,This is the authority boundary between the interactive root and its in-process children; crossing it attributes input requests to the wrong session (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:82-84).,"Both foreign cases are asserted against an empty frame list, including the empty-string variant OMP actually sends (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:219-228).","No other test presents a foreign session id to the approval handlers; the print-mode row covers the mode guard, not the id guard; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real root() predicate runs against synthesized events; the negative assertion is on the recorded frames (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:224-227).,high,keep,The only test of the child-versus-root approval authority guard; keep.,[],0.002s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.002,0.002,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 2.044792 at macOS-job.log:3765; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20approval%20opened%20during%20a%20question%20keeps%20both%20requests%20and%20their%20order|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an approval opened during a question keeps both requests and their order,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,269,283,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","With a question q1 open, an approval c1 opens and closes inside it, and the question closes last: the four frames appear in exactly that order with their own request ids.","If the extension kept one current request, the approval would replace the question id, so the question's close would mismatch and the human's answer would be attributed to the approval.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Two independent namespaces must coexist while one dialog is nested in another; collapsing them misroutes the human's input (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105).,"The exact four-frame id order (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:269-283) is a complete ordering invariant for nesting, and it would fail on any shared-id implementation.","Distinct from the two-overlap row: here the requests belong to different namespaces and nest, which the receiver's dialog stack depends on; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-105, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real handlers and transport; ordering read from the delivered record (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:275-282).,high,keep,Complete invariant for nested request identities; keep.,[],0.023s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.023,0.023,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 23.10275 at macOS-job.log:3789; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20approval%20opens%20and%20closes%20one%20namespaced%20request%20and%20carries%20no%20reason|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an approval opens and closes one namespaced request and carries no reason,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,196,207,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A tool_approval_requested for toolCallId c1 emits input_open with namespace approval, request_id approval:c1 and kind approval, and the resolution emits input_close with the same request_id and no kind, while the approval reason text never reaches the record.","If the request id dropped the namespace or used the tool name, the close would not match the open, leaving a permanent pending approval on the session; copying the reason would send host approval text down the reporting channel.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The open/close pair is what the Dashboard uses to show a session waiting for input; an unmatched close leaves the session looking blocked forever (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:86-93). The receiver derives the namespace from the request-id prefix and IGNORES an open whose id does not carry it (src/report/extension.rs:396-420, src/report/extension.rs:688-696), so a wrong id or a mismatched close leaves the prompt invisible while the child blocks on the human answer.","Exact event/namespace/request_id/kind tuples plus a byte-level reason exclusion (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:196-207) reject a wrong id, a wrong namespace and a content leak.","The Pi provider reports prompt spans, not OMP approvals (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:134-141); this approval namespace has no other test.",The real handlers run through the fake ExtensionContext and the frames are produced by the real transport and helper; only the host event is synthesized (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:200-206).,high,keep,Only coverage of OMP's approval request identity; keep.,[],0.020s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.020,0.020,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 19.907375 at macOS-job.log:3753; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20in-place%20session%20switch%20re-announces%20the%20conversation%20and%20closes%20any%20open%20cycle|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an in-place session switch re-announces the conversation and closes any open cycle,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,418,440,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A startup, an open run 1, then a resume switch re-announces session-b with previous sess-a and run null, and the next start is run 2 (cycle numbering is per instance, not per conversation), with no .jsonl text in any frame.","If the switch kept run 1, the receiver would reject the repeated instance:run identity as a continuation of the published cycle, and a per-conversation counter would reopen run 1 in the new conversation.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Cycle identity is what the receiver deduplicates on; reusing a run across an in-place switch corrupts the published sequence for the conversation it now names (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:35-48, 49-57).",The four-frame tuple set (event/session/run/reason/previous) plus the .jsonl exclusion (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:418-440) rejects both a kept run and a reset counter.,"The history-boundary row covers the identity fields alone; this row adds the cycle reset, which no other OMP test asserts; the handler it drives is src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:47-48, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real announce/agent_start handlers with synthesized events; frames delivered by the real helper (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:427-439).,high,keep,Only test of the per-instance cycle numbering across an in-place switch; keep.,[],0.022s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 21.871 at macOS-job.log:3837; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|inert%20outside%20a%20managed%20invocation%20and%20outside%20the%20terminal%20UI|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,inert outside a managed invocation and outside the terminal UI,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,58,74,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Without OVRCR_AGENT_SOCKET/OVRCR_AGENT_TOKEN the factory registers no handlers; with the channel present but mode 'print' a child session emits session_start, agent_start, agent_end and session_shutdown and spawns no helper at all.","If the mode guard or the channel guard were dropped, in-process task and advisor children of an OMP session would report their own cycles and shutdowns as the interactive root, and the extension would spawn helpers from child sessions.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Child-session reporting is attributed to the interactive root session, i.e. state written to a session that does not own it, and helper spawns escape the managed channel (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:20-24, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:107-109).",It checks both guards with the negative evidence that matters - empty registration list and a record file that was never created (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:58-74) - not just an empty frame list.,The Pi provider's analogue asserts only the no-credentials case (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:116-122); the print-mode half for OMP's in-process children is unique to this row.,"The materialized production module runs with the real transport and a real helper path; only the ExtensionContext is faked, and the assertion is that no child process is created, which the fixture can observe truthfully (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:68-73).",high,keep,"The only test of OMP's two inertness guards, with a spawn-level negative assertion; keep.",[],0.006s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.006,0.006,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 5.882375 at macOS-job.log:3711; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|session%20switches%20capture%20OMP%27s%20exact%20native%20file%20and%20ephemeral%20identity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,session switches capture OMP's exact native file and ephemeral identity,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,43,56,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A session_start then an in-place session_switch deliver two frames whose session_id/session_file are the native ids the host had at emit time: ['native-a', '/private/omp/arbitrary-file.jsonl'] and ['native-b', null] for the ephemeral conversation.","If frame() read the session manager at delivery time (after the emit) or derived the file from the id, the switch frame would carry the previous conversation or an invented path, so OVRCR would bind or pause the wrong native conversation.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Wrong native identity binds reporting to another conversation, so lifecycle state and input requests land on a session OVRCR does not own (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:47-48, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:65-80).","It asserts the exact id/file pair per announcement plus the real-path-versus-null distinction (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:43-56), so a delivery-time read or a derived path both fail.","The transport's synchronous frame capture is also exercised by the Pi provider (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:100-114), but that file drives a different extension module; the OMP switch/history binding has no other test.","The real extension module is materialized from src with the binary token replaced and driven through the fake ExtensionContext, and each frame is delivered by a real /bin/sh helper child (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:21-37) - the spawn boundary is real; the OMP host itself is the fixture.",high,keep,"Grounded, decisive coverage of the provider's native-identity binding with no other test; keep.",[],0.024s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.024,0.024,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 23.614458 at macOS-job.log:3705; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fomp_reporting_extension.mjs|the%20ask%20tool%27s%20lifetime%20is%20one%20question%20request%20keyed%20by%20its%20tool%20call%20id|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,the ask tool's lifetime is one question request keyed by its tool call id,default,tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs,246,258,"[""src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:1-137"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","A tool_execution_start for the ask tool emits input_open with namespace question, request_id question:q1 and kind select, and its end emits input_close with the same id, while the question text and answer never reach the record.","If the question namespace were shared with approvals or the id were derived from the tool name, the close would not match and the Dashboard would show a stuck question; copying args/result would leak the question text and the model's answer.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The ask tool is the model's only question channel; a mismatched request leaves the human prompt unresolved and blocks the child's turn (src/omp-reporting-extension.mjs:98-105). The receiver derives the namespace from the request-id prefix and IGNORES an open whose id does not carry it (src/report/extension.rs:396-420, src/report/extension.rs:688-696), so a wrong id or a mismatched close leaves the prompt invisible while the child blocks on the human answer.","Exact open/close tuples plus two content exclusions (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:246-258) reject a wrong namespace, a wrong id and any body leak.","The Pi side has no ask-tool lifetime hook (its questions are tool calls in the runtime, src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:613-616); this is OMP-specific behaviour with no counterpart.",Real tool_execution handlers run with synthesized events; the frames come from the real transport and helper (tests/omp_reporting_extension.mjs:251-257).,high,keep,Only test of the ask-tool question lifetime; keep.,[],0.023s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.023,0.023,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 22.54625 at macOS-job.log:3777; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|a%20late%20startup%20reply%20cannot%20restore%20a%20retired%20factory|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,a late startup reply cannot restore a retired factory,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,66,76,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","A startup Recover that resolves after session_shutdown leaves state null, a 'retired' gap and no appended pointer.","If the generation fence were missing, a reply arriving after shutdown would restore a retired factory's state and the next factory would inherit authority from a session that no longer exists.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"A retired producer restoring state is duplicate/stale authority over the workflow, exactly what the receiver's fences are meant to prevent (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, 70-70).","It holds the reply open, shuts the module down, then resolves and asserts the post-condition (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:66-76), which a missing `active/generation` check cannot pass.","The explicit-new row covers a competing session_start; this row covers shutdown-then-reply, which no other test exercises; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:70-70, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real reconcile/restore fence runs with a deferred fake call (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:31-38).,high,keep,Only test of the shutdown retirement fence; keep.,[],0.0002715s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.0002715,0.0002715,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.2715 at macOS-job.log:3897; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|a%20pointer%20with%20only%20legacy%20gaps%20preserves%20the%20real%20gap%20without%20invented%20authority|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,a pointer with only legacy gaps preserves the real gap without invented authority,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,89,96,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","When recovery returns no workflows but one legacy gap, state stays null, the gap carries the real reason, it contains no TypeError or undefined, and the context still surfaces it.","If the module synthesized a workflow or an `undefined` authority from a gap-only response, the session would believe it owns a workflow it never recovered.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Inventing authority from a gap is the failure the whole pointer discipline exists to prevent; the test asserts the absence of invented authority and of crash artefacts (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:33-45).,"It asserts null state, the reason substring, the absence of TypeError/undefined and the context content (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:89-96).","The workflow-plus-gaps row always has a workflow; the gap-only branch is distinct and no other row reaches it; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real reconcile returns early on no rows with the recovery-gaps object, and the real context builder renders it (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:33-45, 71-79).",high,keep,Only test of the gap-only reconciliation branch; keep.,[],0.0002895s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.0002895,0.0002895,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.2895 at macOS-job.log:3909; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|actual%20startup%20and%20both%20compaction%20outcomes%20reconcile%20the%20original%20workflow%20without%20effects|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,actual startup and both compaction outcomes reconcile the original workflow without effects,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,15,31,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","A real startup and both compaction outcomes each issue exactly one Recover for the saved workflow; the reconciled state keeps authority epoch 4 and both handles, and the before_agent_start message carries the objective and decision references without the in-memory source capability.","If compaction dropped or re-ran recovery against a different workflow, the resumed Pi would continue with a stale or foreign authority, and an appended pointer containing the auth source would persist a capability into the transcript.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Restoring the wrong authority after compaction means the session can resume work with the wrong controller/instance, i.e. a workflow it does not own (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, 47-62).","Three events, one Recover each, exact authority and handle state, content assertions on the injected context, and an exclusion of the auth source from the appended entry (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:15-31).","The compaction hooks and the context injection are asserted only here; the other continuation rows cover fork/new, malformed pointers, publication failure and retirement; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:28-45, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The production continuation module runs with a fake control `call` standing in for the Server and a fake pi that records hooks and appendEntry; the extension-side logic is the real code, the transport is not (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:6-13).",high,keep,Only coverage of the compaction reconciliation and context injection; keep.,[],0.004s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.004,0.004,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 3.523792 at macOS-job.log:3867; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
