node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|Archive%20persists%20an%20exact%20private%20intent%20before%20transport%20and%20reconciles%20a%20lost%20reply|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,Archive persists an exact private intent before transport and reconciles a lost reply,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,546,604,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","ovrcr_archive persists a private intent before transport (the control stub re-reads it to prove durability), a lost reply returns Unknown with no invented receipts, replaying the original request reproduces the identical payload and reconciles a receipt, and authoritative Conflict/Internal failures map to Refused/Unknown without rewriting the intent; a foreign handle refuses without transport.","If the intent were written after transport, a lost reply would leave no exact payload to reconcile and the caller would have to resend; if an Internal error were reported Refused, the caller could duplicate a delivery the Server may have recorded.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Archive records durable delivery/archive state; misclassifying an unknown outcome as Refused invites a duplicate declaration, and losing the intent makes reconciliation impossible (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:436-461).","It asserts the Unknown-with-no-receipts result, the byte-identical replay, the unchanged intent bytes across recovery and both error codes, plus the durable-intent check inside the control stub (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:546-604).","The two rows share a body and differ in operation, private-intent prefix and response shape; Archive's reconciliation is exercised only here.","The real tool, the real private intent directory and a real control child that verifies the intent exists before answering (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:553-575).",high,keep,Coverage of Archive intent durability 