node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|an%20awaited%20old%20private%20intent%20cannot%20reacquire%20auth%20after%20fork|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,an awaited old private intent cannot reacquire auth after fork,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,503,543,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","A pending ovrcr_start holding an intent read when session_start 'fork' arrives rejects with 'previous Pi context', leaves the intent bytes unchanged and never spawns even a Reconcile call.","If the tool re-acquired auth after the fork, it would advance an assignment belonging to the pre-fork context under the new context's authority.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The auth closure's routing check is the only barrier between a stale in-flight tool and fresh authority (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:177-181, 326-350).","It forces the read to be in flight at the fork, then asserts the rejection, immutable bytes and the absence of any control spawn (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:503-543).","The queued-tool row fences a tool that had not started; this row fences one mid-read, which is the harder interleaving; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:177-181, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real read path (fs/promises prototype interposed) and the real requireRouting/auth closures (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:177-181).,high,keep,Only test of authority reacquisition blocking mid-intent; keep.,[],0.112s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.112,0.112,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 112.16925 at macOS-job.log:3981; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|failed%20registered%20collection%20releases%20pending%20follow-up%20without%20accepting%20either%20result|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,failed registered collection releases pending follow-up without accepting either result,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,352,419,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","With publication A pending an outstanding continuation and B arriving behind it, a failed Collect (server InvalidRequest) rejects and releases the consumed continuation so a second wake carries exactly ['B']; every control call is Observe or Collect.","If a failed collection swallowed the wake, the parent would never learn about B; if it marked A handled or accepted, a publication the user never saw would be recorded as handled.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Collecting is how the parent consumes a publication; a failure that consumes without releasing loses the next publication, and marking handled would fake handling (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:607-612, src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:110-110).","It asserts the first wake ['A'], the second wake ['B'] after the failure, the exact followUp options, and that no call is anything but Observe/Collect (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:352-419).","The observation suite covers wake coalescing without a failing Collect; the acknowledge-on-failure path through the tool wrapper is unique here; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:607-612, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real ovrcr_collect tool, the real observer and a real control child that serves Observe and refuses Collect (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:256-273, 607-612).",high,keep,Only coverage of continuation release after a failed collection; keep.,[],0.388s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.388,0.388,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 387.5175 at macOS-job.log:3963; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|followup%20recovery%20retains%20exact%20private%20request%20after%20a%20lost%20reply|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,followup recovery retains exact private request after a lost reply,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,294,349,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","A lost Followup reply returns Unknown with no receipts; replaying with only handle+request sends byte-identical operation identity and payload, the private intent holds no capability, a legacy intent without expected_control_epoch is only observed via Reconcile (epoch 9, Applied) and its bytes are preserved, and a symlinked intent is Refused without contacting control.","If recovery created a new request, the child could receive the same follow-up twice; if a legacy intent were advanced to a fresh epoch, it would claim input authority the caller never captured.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Follow-up input is delivered into a running child; a duplicate or an invented epoch is wrong-target input to a live session (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:540-585).,"It asserts identical records for the replay, the capability-free intent bytes, the Observe-only legacy path, the preserved immutable bytes and the symlink refusal with the call count unchanged (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:294-349).","The lost-Prepare rows cover launch recovery; the legacy-intent observe-only rule is unique here; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:274-350, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real followup tool, real intent files and a real control child that can lose its first reply (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:559-585).",high,keep,Covers follow-up recovery and the legacy observe-only rule; keep.,[],0.190s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.190,0.190,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 190.181125 at macOS-job.log:3957; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|managed%20Pi%20exposes%20research%20assignment%20and%20explicit%20collection%20tools|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,managed Pi exposes research assignment and explicit collection tools,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,11,86,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","With a managed channel the extension registers twenty-seven tools whose parameter roots are all type object (including every anyOf/oneOf branch), publishes the exact required fields and bounds for ovrcr_start/coding/dependencies/review/followup/accept/confirm_return, refuses malformed followup and accept calls locally with dispatch Refused/transport NotSent, and refuses Claude coding or review with the provider-specific reasons before any transport.","If a root schema had a non-object union branch, hosts such as Grok would reject the tool; if the required-field or action checks were lost, a call could reach Prepare without the exact authority fields, or a Claude coding request would be forwarded to a provider that cannot honour it.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"This is the delegation control surface: schemas and local refusals decide what can reach Prepare, and a permissive schema lets a call start or accept work without the exact identity the Server requires (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:256-273, 472-513, 593-606).","It asserts the exact tool list, object-ness of every root and union branch, several exact required/limit schemas, and both Refused/NotSent refusals with provider-specific reasons (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:11-86), which is far beyond a smoke check.","The other delegation rows exercise transport paths; the schema surface and local refusals are asserted only here. The Rust questions/delegation suites cover the Server side, not the Pi tool schemas; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:256-273, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The materialized extension and runtime register into the fake host, and the tool callbacks are the production ones; the control transport is never reached for refusals, so the refusal evidence is complete (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:20-23).",high,keep,Only coverage of the Pi delegation schema surface and pre-transport refusals; keep.,[],0.095s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.095,0.095,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 95.375458 at macOS-job.log:3927; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
