node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_interrupt_extension.mjs|only%20the%20loaded%20native%20Escape%20binding%20is%20supported|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,node,unit,only the loaded native Escape binding is supported,default,tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs,15,21,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:1-59"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:106-112""]","inspectPiInterruptBinding returns 'Escape' when app.interrupt is bound to escape, 'Unsupported' when it is bound to [] or ctrl+c/ctrl+x, and 'Escape' again when escape is one of two bindings.","If the check ignored the loaded binding and assumed Escape, OVRCR would offer a native interrupt that Pi delivers to another action, so the user would believe an agent was interrupted while it keeps running.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,The result gates whether OVRCR claims a byte-level interrupt is possible; a false Escape claim misrepresents control over a running agent (src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:41-54).,Four manager configurations including the empty and multi-binding cases plus the positive baseline (tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs:15-21) reject a static assumption.,"No other test feeds a custom app.interrupt binding; the fullscreen/clipboard row covers the preempting actions instead; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-interrupt.ts:41-54, which no other reviewed case exercises.","The real inspectPiInterruptBinding runs; the application manager is a fixture implementing getDefinition/getKeys/matches, so Pi's actual key decoder and override loading are not exercised (tests/pi_interrupt_extension.mjs:5-13).",high,keep,Only coverage of the interrupt binding claim; keep.,[],0.001s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.001,0.001,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 1.299125 at macOS-job.log:4029; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_observation_extension.mjs|content-free%20publication%20wake%20uses%20Pi%20followUp%20API%20and%20coalesces%20outstanding%20work|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,node,unit,content-free publication wake uses Pi followUp API and coalesces outstanding work,default,tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs,71,94,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:1-147"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:236-239""]","A publication wakes once with customType ovrcr_wake, display false, options triggerTurn/followUp, details.handles ['a'] and no digest in the content; while one continuation is outstanding a second handle does not wake, and after acknowledge the second handle wakes alone; a handled publication queues nothing.","If the wake were not coalesced, every observation would trigger a follow-up turn and the agent would converse with itself; if the digest entered the content, result identity would be copied into the conversation.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"The wake is what makes the parent reconcile; uncoalesced wakes create runaway turns, and a missed wake leaves work unhandled (src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:25-40).","It asserts the message shape and options, the single-outstanding rule across two handles, and the no-duplicate case after a handled publication (tests/pi_observation_extension.mjs:71-94).","The question row asserts coalescing for question facts; this row asserts the API shape (followUp, display false) and the outstanding-continuation rule for publications; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:43-67, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The production deliver() runs against a recording pi.sendMessage that also models the triggerTurn call (src/ovrcr-delegation-observer.mjs:25-40).,high,keep,Only coverage of the wake's API shape and outstanding-continuation coalescing; keep.,[],0.089s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.089,0.089,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 88.638791 at macOS-job.log:4065; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
