node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_reporting_extension.mjs|an%20outer%20prompt%20span%20opens%20and%20closes%20one%20Input%20request%3B%20the%20title%20never%20leaves|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,node,integration,an outer prompt span opens and closes one Input request; the title never leaves,default,tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs,293,312,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-170"", ""src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:1-160""]","Two ui_prompt spans (select then editor) each emit input_open with kind and a request id shaped '<instance>:p1'/':p2' and a matching input_close; request ids differ between spans, and title, question, context, choices, scope and answer text never appear.","If the prompt counter were absent, both spans would share an id and the second close would resolve the wrong request; if any prompt field were copied, user prompt content and answers would enter the reporting channel.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Prompt spans are the human-input signal for Pi; unmatched ids leave a phantom pending prompt, and prompt bodies are content the channel is designed never to carry (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:130-141).","Exact event/run/kind tuples, id equality and inequality checks, the id shape, and six content exclusions (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:293-312) make this a complete positive/negative invariant.","The OMP suite reports approvals and the ask tool, not prompt spans; the two providers' input channels are separate handlers; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:130-141, which no other reviewed case exercises.",Real ui_prompt handlers and transport with a real helper child; the assertions read the delivered bytes (tests/pi_reporting_extension.mjs:303-311).,high,keep,Complete invariant for the prompt-span identity and redaction; keep.,[],0.030s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.030,0.030,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 30.15775 at macOS-job.log:4269; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-002,
python-check|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-startup-package.py|cache-miss-production-profile%3Aln234|local-development,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated macOS startup assets,python-check,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,script-check,acceptance,cache-miss-production-profile:ln234,local-development,native/bridge/check-startup-package.py,234,234,"[""native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:234-234"", ""scripts/package-startup.sh:26-62""]","Requesting the production profile against a payload built for local development misses the cache: package-startup.sh exits 77, calls the intercepted builder exactly once with the profile flag and --callback-executable, leaves the payload byte-identical, cleans the stage and leaves no process in the group.","A fingerprint that omits the profile from the hash, so a local build is reused as the production payload instead of rebuilt.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,Serving a local-profile payload to a production request ships the wrong artifact to users (3).,"native/bridge/check-startup-package.py:196-220 checks the expected 77 exit, the exact recorded builder argv, the byte-identical payload and the cleaned stage/process group, so both a false hit and a wrong builder invocation fail.",Only profile-participation cache test.,"Real package-startup.sh and real relocation; the builder is the documented intercepted fake, so the build itself is not exercised.",high,keep,"Only evidence that the profile participates in the source fingerprint, preventing a local build being reused as production.",[],spawns package-startup.sh with a fake builder; compares payload hashes and ps output,,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3644 (28 checks) '28 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,
python-unittest|Relocated%20pinned%20Cursor%20dependency%20and%20passive%20CLI%20diagnostics|tests%2Fcursor_bridge_install.py%3A%3AInstallation|test_install_and_relocate_exact_official_archive_without_notification_collision|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics,python-unittest,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py::Installation,unittest,acceptance,test_install_and_relocate_exact_official_archive_without_notification_collision,default,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py,28,40,"[""tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:28-40"", ""scripts/install-cursor-bridge.py:44-78""]","The real installer is run against the pinned archive; the destination archive's SHA-256 equals the source archive, relocating the version directory preserves the bytes, an existing notification asset elsewhere under ~/.local/lib/ovrcr keeps its content, and a reinstall returns 0.","An installer that writes a different artifact, collides with the notification assets directory, or fails on a second run after the archive was relocated.",3,4,3,3,75,85,81,The installed SDK archive is the dependency later launched for cloud runs; writing the wrong or colliding content is a wrong-target durable write (3).,"tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:28-40 asserts returncode, the printed destination, digest equality with the source archive, post-relocation bytes, notification content and a repeat install.",Only relocation/collision test for this installer.,Runs the production install-cursor-bridge.py against a real pinned archive in a temp HOME.,high,keep,Only relocation and notification-collision test for the pinned-archive installer.,[],runs the installer twice in a temp HOME; hashes the archive,,,,,unmeasured,no per-method timing; unittest prints one aggregate: macOS-job.log:3669 'Ran 6 tests in 2.076s' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics'),packaging-installers-002,
python-unittest|Relocated%20pinned%20Cursor%20dependency%20and%20passive%20CLI%20diagnostics|tests%2Fcursor_bridge_install.py%3A%3AInstallation|test_missing_or_tampered_source_preserves_previous_installation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics,python-unittest,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py::Installation,unittest,acceptance,test_missing_or_tampered_source_preserves_previous_installation,default,tests/cursor_bridge_install.py,64,73,"[""tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:64-73"", ""scripts/install-cursor-bridge.py:60-78""]","After a good install, installing from a missing archive and from a tampered archive both return nonzero and leave the previously installed bridge.tar.gz byte-identical.",An installer that overwrites or removes the working installation when the new source is missing or fails the pinned checksum.,3,4,3,3,75,85,81,"Clobbering a verified installation with a failed source destroys the working dependency (durable-state loss, 3).","tests/cursor_bridge_install.py:64-73 iterates the two failure sources and asserts nonzero plus byte equality of the destination, which the current 'stage then rename' order must preserve.",Only source-failure preservation test for this installer.,Real installer and real archive file; failure sources are real files on disk.,high,keep,Only source-failure preservation test; guards the previous installation against a missing or tampered archive.,[],runs the installer three times and compares installed bytes,,,,,unmeasured,no per-method timing; unittest prints one aggregate: macOS-job.log:3669 'Ran 6 tests in 2.076s' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated pinned Cursor dependency and passive CLI diagnostics'),packaging-installers-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_stale_concurrent_attempts_leave_one_surviving_server|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,startup_stale_concurrent_attempts_leave_one_surviving_server,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,1872,2024,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:145-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:540-557""]","With a stale socket present, two `ovrcr server` children are spawned; exactly one exits during startup, the survivor answers a Shutdown, and the socket is removed; diagnostics capture worker pids, stderr and public paths.","Two real server processes could both acquire the instance, or neither could survive, destroying the single-owner guarantee after a crash.",4,3,2,4,100,70,82,Violating the one-server guarantee splits ownership of sessions and registry state (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/startup.rs:540-557).,"Asserts exactly one of two workers exits and that the survivor serves shutdown, though it does not verify the loser failed for the lock reason (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1940-1965).",Distinct process-level stale-socket race within the one-server contract already covered by the thread-level test (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1629-1685).,"Two real compiled server processes, real stale socket and filesystem observation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1880-1940).",high,keep,Process-level evidence for the one-server invariant that the thread-level test cannot provide.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_concurrent_attempts_leave_one_server|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|startup_stale_socket_is_recovered|default""]","[""spawns two compiled servers"", ""stale socket fixture"", ""verbose failure diagnostics"", ""2s startup observation window""]",1.881,1.881,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1591 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aworkspace_identity|a_repository_root_cannot_be_removed_through_another_projects_workspace|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::workspace_identity,integration,acceptance,a_repository_root_cannot_be_removed_through_another_projects_workspace,default,tests/workspace_identity.rs,1063,1099,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2641-2670"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2220-2285""]",A checkout that another project registers as its repository root cannot be removed as a workspace of the first project; its .git survives.,"Removing a registered repository root through another project's workspace, deleting .git.",4,2,3,4,100,70,82,Deleting a repository checkout destroys the user's repository (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2641-2670).,One error assertion plus the surviving .git file (tests/workspace_identity.rs:1063-1099).,The cross-project root protection is unique (tests/workspace_identity.rs:704-723 covers unregister).,Real binary and two project registrations (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2641-2670).,high,keep,Pins cross-project repository-root protection.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aworkspace_identity|unregistering_a_project_keeps_its_protected_repository_checkout|default""]",Two workspace creations and one removal,2.839,2.839,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2136 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-007,independent-integration-final-check-1
