cting the non-ad-hoc rule at the install path.","[""python-unittest|Relocated%20macOS%20startup%20assets|native%2Fbridge%2Fcheck-installer.py%3A%3AInstallerTests|test_production_still_refuses_ad_hoc_identity|default""]",copies a payload tree; spawns install-bridge.sh subprocess,,,,,unmeasured,suite aggregate only: macOS-job.log:3634 (12 checks) '12 relocated startup payload checks passed; pinned entitlement SHA256 c479446ccc1537f8b64d0bc2c4a7b5a64f80753659d0cdf5450c2927df8eb29b; no install or app launch' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Relocated macOS startup assets'),packaging-installers-002,independent-report-check-2
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_doctor_checks_supplied_hooks_without_certifying_trust|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,acceptance,codex_doctor_checks_supplied_hooks_without_certifying_trust,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,715,803,"[""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:37-53"", ""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:236-340"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:254-265""]","Generates a fresh Codex composition, mutates it six ways (matcher-filtered Stop, legacy SessionStart filter, async handler, non-command type, valid base, invalid TOML) and asserts configuration.status, the exact legacy issue list, release_status hooks_only, hook_trust/delivery unverified, file non-mutation and no secret in either the doctor output or setup's rejection stderr.","Certifying a filtered, async or wrongly typed handler, accepting the legacy `startup|resume|clear|compact` matcher, claiming trust or delivery is proven from file presence, rewriting the supplied file, or echoing the invalid TOML while reporting it.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,The certification predicate decides whether a user believes Codex reporting is configured; a false positive leaves every prompt untracked while the UI looks healthy.,"Six cases carry independent expectations, including the exact single-issue list for the legacy filter and a byte-equality check on the unchanged file, plus a secret scan on two commands.",Only Codex supplied-file certification matrix with the exact issue list; row 7 is the Claude counterpart.,Real CLI and real TOML files; no provider process is needed for the claim.,high,keep,Grounds the Codex certification predicate and trust/deilvery honesty; no retained equivalent.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr|cli%3A%3Acodex_setup%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aconfiguration_presence_requires_unfiltered_synchronous_exact_command|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|doctor_does_not_certify_filtered_hooks_wrong_types_or_statusline_suffixes|default""]","[""seven doctor spawns plus one setup"", ""temp HOME and settings.toml""]",0.267,0.267,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:678 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_preserves_handlers_trust_and_quotes_noop_helper|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,acceptance,codex_setup_preserves_handlers_trust_and_quotes_noop_helper,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,532,623,"[""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:34-54"", ""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:55-133"", ""src/cli/codex_setup.rs:191-212""]","Runs setup against a config.toml that has a projects trust table, a hooks.state trust hash, two existing Stop handlers and one PermissionRequest approval handler, then asserts the file is untouched, those native values/ordering are preserved, every one of eight events ends with an `exec '<quoted path>' report codex --stdin` handler, executes each emitted command through sh with an event payload (success, empty stdout), and reruns to assert idempotence.","Dropping or reordering the user's approval handler or trust tables, emitting an unquoted path so the hook fails under sh, letting a hook print anything (Codex treats stdout as an approval decision), omitting an event, or appending duplicate reporters on rerun.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"An emitted hook that writes stdout can auto-approve or block tool calls, and trust-table loss forces the user to re-trust every project; both are consequences beyond a cosmetic name.","All eight emitted commands are executed for real with success and empty-stdout assertions, native tables and handler order are compared structurally, the input file is compared byte-for-byte and the rerun must be a fixed point.",Only row executing every emitted Codex hook; rows 15 and 16 cover repair and comment preservation rather than composition.,"Real copied binary, real TOML file and real /bin/sh execution of the emitted commands.",high,keep,High-value security-relevant composition contract with an execution-level assertion; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_repairs_stale_owned_handler_and_preserves_comments|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|codex_setup_repairs_inline_filtered_hooks_once_without_changing_native_approvals|default""]","[""copies the compiled binary"", ""spawns eight sh helpers"", ""temp HOME""]",0.215,0.215,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:686 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
