001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_preserves_settings_and_external_renderer_bytes_once|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,integration,setup_preserves_settings_and_external_renderer_bytes_once,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,59,103,"[""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:266-310"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:311-470"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:445-470"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:10-31""]","Runs `agent setup claude --print --settings` on a 0600 settings file that already carries permissions, two SessionStart groups and a user statusLine whose command is a shell renderer; then executes the emitted statusLine command with a JSON payload and asserts the renderer runs once, receives the exact original bytes and prints its own output; then re-runs setup on the emitted document.","Setup overwriting or reordering the user's permissions/hook groups, writing the input file (asserted byte-identical, mode 0600), dropping statusLine.padding, invoking the user renderer twice or re-encoding its stdin, losing the manual removal/notes text, or wrapping the renderer again on a second run.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,src/cli/agent_setup.rs:311-470 composes statusLine and hooks over user-owned Claude settings; a lost permission/hook or a corrupted renderer silently breaks both the user's configuration and managed reporting.,"src/cli/agent_setup.rs:445-470 is print-only, yet the test pins the input file byte-identical with mode 0600, executes the emitted command through /bin/sh, compares passthrough bytes and renderer call count, and requires an exact fixed point on rerun.",The only row executing an external renderer end to end and measuring its bytes and invocation count; setup_migrates_only_exact_legacy_statusline... and setup_repairs_stale_owned... cover migration and repair branches instead.,"Real compiled CLI (CARGO_BIN_EXE_ovrcr), real settings file on disk, emitted shell command executed by /bin/sh, so no part of the claimed boundary is simulated.",high,keep,Grounded high-signal coverage of a destructive settings rewrite plus renderer passthrough; no retained test asserts byte-identical file preservation and single renderer invocation.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_migrates_only_exact_legacy_statusline_and_marks_hooks|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|setup_repairs_stale_owned_claude_statusline_without_wrapping_it|default""]","[""spawns the compiled ovrcr binary two plus one sh child"", ""creates a temp HOME and a 0600 settings file"", ""executes an emitted shell command""]",0.083,0.083,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:694 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
