lled_across_dashboard_reconnect|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|empty_workspace_and_generated_names_preserve_explicit_titles|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|session%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aapplication_titles_are_consumed_without_changing_titles_or_output|default""]","[""PTY session and shell program"", ""dashboard stream plus SetView fence"", ""5 s transitions"", ""3.84 s observed""]",5.218,5.218,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:720 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|workspace_launch_failure_retains_worktree_and_retry_uses_existing_workspace|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,workspace_launch_failure_retains_worktree_and_retry_uses_existing_workspace,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,3121,3182,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/lifecycle.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1070-1100""]","Creates a workspace with a launch pointing at a nonexistent executable, asserts PartialFailure, that the registered workspace still has a real .git file, that no session exists, that a retry CreateWorkspaceWithLaunch is AlreadyExists, that an explicit CreateSession in that workspace succeeds, and that reopening an unknown session id is NotFound.","A failed launch discarding or orphaning the freshly created worktree/registration (lost work), a retry creating a second workspace, or a fabricated session for the failed launch.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Worktree retention after a partial failure is the difference between a retryable mistake and lost user work.,"Five independent assertions span error code, on-disk repository, session list, duplicate rejection and recovery by explicit creation.",Only partial-launch-failure test in this file; workspace creation elsewhere does not assert retention.,"Real git worktree, real server and real CLI.",high,keep,Concrete lost-work invariant with an end-to-end retry path; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|stable_workspace_launch_titles_rename_reset_and_reopen_keep_identity_and_reset_output|default""]","[""git worktree creation"", ""five protocol requests"", ""3.69 s observed""]",3.690,3.690,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:731 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr-gui|close_request_leaves_the_dashboard_running_until_outside_the_frame|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr-gui,bin,acceptance,close_request_leaves_the_dashboard_running_until_outside_the_frame,default,src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs,636,690,"[""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:453-480"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:444-451"", ""src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:620-633""]","App::show only records closing = true when the viewport reports a close request and never stops the PTY inside the egui pass; App::close, called from on_exit, stops the dashboard and then the demo root.","Stopping the Terminal inside show() would join the PTY reader while the egui context lock is held; the reader's Context::request_repaint then blocks until epaint's 10s deadlock panic, so every window close would freeze or panic and could leave the dashboard child running.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A close that blocks the frame or panics is a major workflow failure of the GUI itself (the user force-quits and the dashboard child may survive), though it does not lose server-side sessions (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:453-468).","It asserts the elapsed frame time, that the Terminal is still present, that closing was recorded, that no error surfaced, and that app.close() then removes the demo root (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:674-689), which separates the deadlock from a correct deferral.","This is the only test of the close and on_exit path: tests/gui.rs:385-422 exercises Demo cleanup but never App::show's close handling (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:453-468), so the lock-ordering defect has no other protection.","It runs the real App::show inside a real egui Context with a real spawned dashboard on a PTY and a real temp root (src/bin/ovrcr-gui.rs:637-660), i.e. the full lifecycle boundary.",high,keep,"The only protection for a close-path deadlock in the GUI host; high-signal and high-fidelity, keep.",[],"6.576s one hosted attempt; spawns a real ovrcr demo dashboard on a PTY, waits for it to become ready, then runs one closed-viewport egui frame",6.576,6.576,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2344 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-core-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Abin%2Fovrcr|cli%3A%3Abridge%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acallback_stream_preserves_fragmented_owner_response_under_one_deadline|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::bin/ovrcr,bin,integration,cli::bridge::tests::callback_stream_preserves_fragmented_owner_response_under_one_deadline,default,src/cli/bridge.rs,456,499,"[""src/cli/bridge.rs:278-303"", ""src/cli/bridge.rs:220-223""]","On macOS, a peer writes a framed BridgeOwner response in three-byte fragments with short parks; the client reads it under one absolute CALLBACK_BUDGET and returns the exact response, and the peer sees request id 9 with Request::Inspect.","The callback stream losing bytes or resetting its deadline per read, so a fragmented owner response times out and notification routing reports unavailable.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,src/cli/bridge.rs:278-303 and 220-223 implement the fragmented read path under one deadline; failure breaks bridge owner resolution.,Fragmented real frames plus exact response equality.,Only fragmentation test; row 8 covers silent/expired peers.,Real UnixStream pair and production framing on the macOS path that ships.,high,keep,Grounded behavioral protection with no complete subsumption; keeps its place.,[],spawned thread; socketpair,0.215,0.215,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2159 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-cli-001,independent-protocol-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_cancel_reaps_an_exited_group_before_confirming_absence|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_reporting,integration,acceptance,collector_cancel_reaps_an_exited_group_before_confirming_absence,default,tests/claude_reporting.rs,548,586,"[""src/report/collector.rs:212-260"", ""src/report/collector.rs:284-300""]","Kills the helper's process group, waits until `ps` reports a zombie, calls cancel with a 2 s deadline, drops the controller, and asserts the pid becomes ESRCH while this parent stays alive before finally checking the group is gone.","Cancellation confirming success while the exited child stays an unreaped zombie, or a group left anchored by a zombie leader.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Zombie accumulation across collect runs is a process-table leak for the life of the server.,"The zombie state is established first, then ESRCH-while-parent-alive proves a wait happened; result Ok is also required.",Already-exited-group cancellation is distinct from the stalled and expired-deadline rows.,"Real SIGKILL, real `ps` state, real reaping.",high,keep,Precise ownership proof that cancel reaps rather than only signals; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_drop_is_bounded_for_a_stalled_helper|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_expired_deadline_transfers_reaping_ownership|default""]","[""ps invocation"", ""3 s polling"", ""0.04 s observed""]",0.046,0.046,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:746 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_expired_deadline_transfers_reaping_ownership|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_reporting,integration,acceptance,collector_expired_deadline_transfers_reaping_ownership,default,tests/claude_reporting.rs,383,432,"[""src/report/collector.rs:212-260"", ""src/report/collector.rs:284-300""]","SIGSTOPs the helper, calls cancel with an already-expired deadline (asserting it returns an error), drops the controller, and then polls until the pid is ESRCH while this parent process stays alive, proving the child was reaped rather than left a zombie.","An expired cancellation that drops ownership without reaping, leaving a zombie or leaked group, or reporting success from the deferred path.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Zombie accumulation across reporting sessions is a process-table leak that survives until the server exits.,"The error return, the ESRCH-while-parent-alive proof and the cleanup bound are all asserted, with an explicit comment that fixture cleanup cannot turn the assertion green.",Only test of the deferred/reaping-ownership branch.,"Real expired deadline, real drop and real wait verification.",high,keep,"Proves reaping rather than mere killing, which no other row does; keep.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_stalled_helper_is_nonblocking_and_owned_group_cleanup_is_bounded|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_reporting|collector_drop_is_bounded_for_a_stalled_helper|default""]","[""SIGSTOP"", ""expired deadline"", ""ESRCH polling"", ""0.04 s observed""]",0.035,0.035,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:750 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
