nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_current_owner_confirms_original_interrupt_and_transfer_preserves_tombstone|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,cancellation::production_current_owner_confirms_original_interrupt_and_transfer_preserves_tombstone,default,tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs,535,646,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_recovery.rs:1085-1200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:90-131"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_cancellation.rs:158-260""]","Transfers workflow authority to a successor parent, asserts the retired owner cannot confirm the pending interrupt, lets the successor recover/inspect and confirm with the same control evidence and receipt, then cancels after transfer capturing epoch 2 against controller epoch 1, transfers back, recovers, and reproves the same cancellation capture with only the authority epoch advancing.","A retired parent confirming or clearing an interrupt after transfer, a transfer that rewrites the pending receipt/control, or a cancellation capture that changes on replay after transferring back.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Authority transfer plus interrupt confirmation decides which parent may settle a live child; a stale owner acting is wrong ownership of an irreversible native signal (tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:535-646).,"Asserts retired-owner refusal, identical control and receipt under the successor, exact captured epochs, and capture equality after transfer-back while the authority epoch alone advances; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:628-629.","Distinct transfer-boundary interaction from other recovery tests: no other row combines interrupt confirmation, cancellation capture, and transfer-back identity; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_cancel_wins_queued_launch_and_blocks_original_accepted_launch_resume|default at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:650-742; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:628-629.","Real parent/successor agent sessions, real child PTY, and real workflow transfer through public tools; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/observation.rs:14-85.",high,keep,Unique transfer-preserved tombstone and confirmation-authority coverage; no equivalent.,[],"[""real successor parent session"", ""real managed child PTY"", ""transfer/recover tool round trips""]",6.243,6.243,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1034 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_interrupt_delivery_requires_fresh_settlement_and_keeps_same_child_followup|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,cancellation::production_interrupt_delivery_requires_fresh_settlement_and_keeps_same_child_followup,default,tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs,197,199,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_interrupt.rs:1-111"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_interrupt_effects.rs:1-180"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:39-60""]","Delivers one Escape (written_bytes 1, no submit), records an Applied interrupt receipt and barrier, proves duplicate interrupt is idempotent, refuses early confirmation and followups during the barrier, refuses a mismatched interrupted-request confirmation, then after settlement confirms, bumps control epoch, keeps the original receipt, collects the late result, and follows up on the same child/run at version 2 without replaying the old interrupt bytes.","A duplicate interrupt writing a second Escape, a confirmation that clears the barrier without matching the original request, a followup bypassing the barrier, or a settlement that rewrites the delivery receipt.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Interrupt authority gates further native input; wrong confirmation or replay can signal the wrong turn in a live child (tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:197-199 via interrupt_then_confirm).,"Asserts exact byte deltas, receipt fields (written_bytes, submit_written), barrier equality, refusal paths, epoch advance, and receipt identity across duplicate/replay/recovery; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:223-227.","The Applied-delivery baseline is distinct from the unknown-outcome variant, but both share the same scenario body and assertions with one expected outcome swapped; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_unknown_interrupt_never_replays_and_confirmation_preserves_original_receipt|default at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:203-205; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:223-227.","Real child PTY, real Escape consumption visible in terminal text, production interrupt tool and control receipts; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/observation.rs:14-85.",high,keep,"Grounded delivery-and-settlement coverage; the variant split with the unknown test is a real branch, so both rows are retained.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_unknown_interrupt_never_replays_and_confirmation_preserves_original_receipt|default""]","[""real managed child PTY"", ""filesystem polling at 10ms"", ""20s deadline loops""]",5.885,5.885,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1035 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_question_answer_respects_interrupt_barrier_until_explicit_settlement_confirmation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,cancellation::production_question_answer_respects_interrupt_barrier_until_explicit_settlement_confirmation,default,tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs,120,194,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_questions.rs:1-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_interrupt.rs:1-111"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_interrupt_effects.rs:1-180""]","Interrupts a child while a question is published, asserts answer_question is Refused with no new input bytes during the barrier, read-only question evidence still collects, native settlement alone does not authorize, and only an explicit confirm_interrupt followed by answer delivers exactly one Applied AnswerQuestion receipt at the same version and one attempt.","A human answer injected into a child while an interrupt barrier is unsettled, a barrier that never clears after confirmation, or duplicate answer receipts in one turn.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Delivering human authority into an interrupted child is wrong-target input/authority; the barrier also protects the question evidence record (tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:120-194).,"Each stage asserts exact Refused dispatch, unchanged byte totals, barrier presence, and after confirmation a single Applied receipt with version and attempt stability; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:153-156.",Distinct question-answer-under-barrier path from the interrupt delivery tests; no other coverage combines question publication with interrupt settlement; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_interrupt_delivery_requires_fresh_settlement_and_keeps_same_child_followup|default at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:197-199; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:153-156.,"Real managed child PTY, real interrupt Escape bytes, registered tools through the production control CLI, and a fixture question script; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/observation.rs:14-85.",high,keep,Precise barrier and authority sequencing with byte-level and receipt-level assertions; sole coverage of answer-after-interrupt.,[],"[""real managed child PTY"", ""native Escape consumption polling at 10ms"", ""fixture question publication script""]",5.731,5.731,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1036 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_unknown_interrupt_never_replays_and_confirmation_preserves_original_receipt|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,cancellation::production_unknown_interrupt_never_replays_and_confirmation_preserves_original_receipt,default,tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs,203,205,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_interrupt_effects.rs:1-180"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:168-260"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:39-60""]","Injects interrupt-after-write so the Escape is delivered but the reply unknown; asserts an Unknown receipt with written_bytes 1, the same barrier, duplicate request returning the identical receipt without a second byte, refusal of confirmation until the original settlement, and preservation of the original receipt through confirmation and later followup.","Treating an unknown interrupt as unsent and replaying the Escape, or a confirmation that rewrites/clears the unknown receipt instead of preserving it.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"An uncertain interrupt that is replayed signals a second Escape into the child, changing its turn, while a rewritten receipt destroys durable delivery evidence (tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:203-205 via interrupt_then_confirm).","Distinguishes Unknown from Applied by fault injection, then asserts written_bytes, duplicate receipt equality, byte stability, and epoch advance after confirmation; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:311-315.","The unknown-outcome branch is exercised only here; other interrupt tests expect Applied or rejection, so the boundary is distinct despite the shared body; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_interrupt_delivery_requires_fresh_settlement_and_keeps_same_child_followup|default at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:197-199; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/cancellation.rs:311-315.","Real fault injection at the write boundary, real child PTY, and production control receipts; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/observation.rs:14-85.",high,keep,Only unknown-interrupt non-replay evidence; keep as an independent boundary from the applied variant.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|cancellation%3A%3Aproduction_interrupt_delivery_requires_fresh_settlement_and_keeps_same_child_followup|default""]","[""acceptance-diagnostics feature"", ""fault file injection"", ""real managed child PTY""]",5.763,5.763,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1037 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|claude%3A%3Apublic_claude_sealed_policy_replacement_refuses_real_read_and_publication|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,claude::public_claude_sealed_policy_replacement_refuses_real_read_and_publication,default,tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs,793,817,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_delegation.rs:115-182"", ""src/cli/delegation_publisher.rs:100-180""]","Starts a Claude child, lets it replace the settings policy and issue a real MCP read at publication time; asserts the read is refused, the publication is refused Conflict without a 'sent' marker, identity is unchanged, no submission/publication/acceptance reference appears, the result file is absent, and acceptance stays pending.","A real read or result publication succeeding after the policy file was replaced, or a refusal that reports a successful send.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Publication and read authority depend on the sealed policy; a tampered policy producing accepted evidence is an authority bypass (tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:793-817).,"Asserts both the read refusal and the publication refusal with code and absence of 'sent', plus durable state preservation; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:809-810.",Distinct publication-time policy fence from the followup fence and stale-publication; only this row exercises a real read under replaced policy; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|claude%3A%3Apublic_claude_stale_publication_and_tampered_file_remain_uncollectable|default at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:380-438; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:809-810.,"Real MCP read frames, real result gate, real server publication verification, scripted Claude host; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:39-86.",high,keep,Unique read+publication policy-tamper boundary with durable negative evidence; keep.,[],"[""settings replacement fixture"", ""scripted Claude host"", ""result gate polling""]",4.857,4.857,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1055 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|claude%3A%3Apublic_claude_stale_publication_and_tampered_file_remain_uncollectable|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,claude::public_claude_stale_publication_and_tampered_file_remain_uncollectable,default,tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs,380,438,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1993-2100"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_files.rs:1-120"", ""src/cli/delegation_publisher.rs:100-180""]","Makes the Claude child publish a version with a bumped contract so the publication is refused as Conflict with attempted_identity recorded; then writes partial, empty, and parseable-but-unauthenticated result bytes and asserts collect refuses each while reconcile keeps identity/version and pending acceptance.","Accepting a stale-contract or tampered result file as evidence, or letting an unauthenticated parseable payload become a submission.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Publication identity binds evidence to the exact contract; accepting stale or tampered bytes delivers wrong work under a valid identity (tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:380-438).,Four distinct tamper shapes plus the stale attempted identity and unchanged reconcile state reject both identity and content forgeries; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:433-436.,Extends the large acceptance test's corrupt-byte case with stale contract identity and a parseable-but-unauthenticated payload; distinct inputs; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|public_dispatch_recovery_preserves_receipts_when_result_is_corrupt_and_run_replaced|default at tests/pi_delegation.rs:2534-2598; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:433-436.,"Real result files, real server publication verification, and a scripted Claude host emitting the stale payload; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation/claude.rs:39-86.",high,keep,Precise stale/tampered publication matrix; complements rather than duplicates the symlink/partial checks.,[],"[""scripted Claude host"", ""result gate file polling"", ""filesystem permission changes""]",4.864,4.864,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1056 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Acombined_workspace_launch_refusal_retains_exact_registered_git_generation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,coding::combined_workspace_launch_refusal_retains_exact_registered_git_generation,default,tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs,753,860,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2363-2420"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/lifecycle.rs:474-500"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:150-260""]","Creates a workspace with a launch whose executable is absent; asserts PartialFailure naming the surviving worktree path, the workspace exists with a stable non-empty generation at the requested base, no child, AlreadyExists on repeat, identical workspace lookup/generation afterwards, inventory delta one, and root README untouched.","A combined create+launch failure losing the registered worktree or its generation, retrying the same request creating a second workspace, or leaking an unregistered worktree.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Retaining the exact registered git generation is required for later retry and ownership; losing or duplicating it corrupts durable workspace identity (tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:753-860).,"Asserts PartialFailure with path in the message, generation/head equality, AlreadyExists on repeat, identical workspace row, inventory delta, and untouched root; assertion at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:814-817.",Only combined CreateWorkspaceWithLaunch failure boundary; other rows test coding launch or CreateWorkspace alone; compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Apublic_coding_lost_launch_reply_reconciles_one_workspace_and_one_child|default at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:350-395; distinguishing assertion at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:814-817.,"Real git worktree, real server lifecycle job, real registry; only the launch executable is absent; real boundary at tests/pi_delegation.rs:1509-1600.",high,keep,Unique combined c