691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_private_claude_route_binds_once_and_clear_leave_retains_lease|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_admission_private_claude_route_binds_once_and_clear_leave_retains_lease,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9345,9349,"[""src/report/admission.rs:16-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]",A root prompt binds the private Claude route once; SessionEnd(clear) retires turn state while health stays Connected and the binding is retained; a later root keeps the same binding; another session cannot be admitted with the old token and the old UUID payload is ignored.,Clear could either drop the lease (forcing a new startup) or accept the old token/UUID in a replacement invocation (cross-invocation authority).,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Cross-invocation token acceptance reuses reporting authority across runs (src/report/admission.rs:16-190).,"Asserts health across clear, old endpoint refusal, stale-token write returning empty and old-UUID payload ignored (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9840-9930).","Clear-leave branch is distinct from the freeze branch, which is its own row (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9345-9349).","Real token endpoints, real CLI reports and a second real invocation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9840-9930).",high,keep,Grounded authority-retention coverage with stale-token negatives.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_branch_freezes_without_replacement_or_reopening|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_interrupted_resume_keeps_reporting_healthy_and_delivers_new_ready|default""]","[""two real invocations"", ""stale token and UUID probes"", ""compiled CLI report runs""]",5.632,5.632,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1447 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_round_trip_survives_dashboard_reconnect|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,agent_hook_round_trip_survives_dashboard_reconnect,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,953,1086,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:31-73"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:958-1000"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:186-260""]","Hook child reports Busy; first dashboard hello shows Busy; sending ""w"" makes the child report WaitingInput; after dashboard drop a reconnect hello shows WaitingInput; Select returns a screen containing HOOK_READY and none of the hook protocol identifiers; KillSession then terminates it.","Activity could be recomputed per connection instead of retained, so a reattached dashboard shows stale Unknown; hook wire bytes could leak into the terminal.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"State lost on reattach misreports agent state to the only UI, a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:31-73).",Asserts both snapshot values across reattach and an explicit forbidden-substring list over the reconstructed screen (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:965-1060).,Only row asserting state retention plus terminal cleanliness across a dashboard reconnect for agent hooks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:953-1086).,"Real socket reconnect, real PTY child and vt100 reconstruction of server bytes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:971-1040).",high,keep,Grounded reattach coverage with a decisive leak-negative assertion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_startup_registration_is_visible|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|context_snapshot_survives_dashboard_reattach|default""]","[""ignored test-binary hook child"", ""dashboard reconnect with real socket"", ""vt100 screen parse"", ""polling identity marker file""]",2.745,2.745,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1450 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_hook_sequence_does_not_regress_state|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,agent_hook_sequence_does_not_regress_state,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,701,803,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:228-249"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:958-1000"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:439-458""]","A hook child session accepts sequenced Busy(1), then rejects receipt-mode reports, replay of sequence 1, and sequence 0 with Conflict while activity stays Busy; sequence 2 Idle is accepted; after KillSession the same capability is rejected and the group is gone.",A late or replayed activity report could overwrite newer state (stale Idle masking Busy) or a report could be accepted after the session exited.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Regressed activity state misreports whether an agent needs attention, a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:968-990).",Positive and negative reports are each paired with an unchanged-state assertion and exact Conflict codes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:710-790).,Only row asserting the receipt-mode/sequenced ordering transition and post-exit rejection together (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:701-803).,Real PTY child that speaks the hook protocol over the server socket; full process boundary (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5867-5935).,high,keep,Grounded coverage of the report-ordering invariant with corrective assertions after each rejection.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|context_report_rejects_old_and_invalid_samples|default""]","[""spawns test binary itself as an ignored hook child"", ""real PTY and Unix socket"", ""polling waits for markers""]",2.873,2.873,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1451 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_channel_failure_releases_reservation_before_native_fallback|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_run_channel_failure_releases_reservation_before_native_fallback,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,8592,8644,"[""src/report/admission.rs:16-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120""]",With TMPDIR pointing at a regular file the private reporting channel cannot be created; the native fallback runs with all agent/hook env removed (the child exits 99 if any leaks) and prints FALLBACK_READY; a second `agent run` then succeeds (epoch 2) and the native exit 17 is preserved.,A channel-setup failure could retain the reservation (blocking later runs) or leak outer agent credentials into the untracked native fallback.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A leaked reservation blocks every later agent run, and leaked tokens give the fallback reporting authority it should not have (src/report/admission.rs:16-190).","Assertions cover epoch 2, the child-side env guard, FALLBACK_READY and exit 17 (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8610-8640).",Only row covering channel-creation failure and credential scrubbing on the fallback path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8592-8644).,Real compiled agent run with a real blocked TMPDIR and a real child guard (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8596-8620).,high,keep,Grounded failure-path coverage of reservation release and credential scrubbing.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|fresh_pty_does_not_inherit_outer_managed_reporting_channel|default""]","[""blocked TMPDIR fixture"", ""real compiled CLI runs"", ""env-leak guard child""]",4.502,4.502,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1453 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_native_exec_does_not_inherit_supervisor_lease|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_run_native_exec_does_not_inherit_supervisor_lease,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,8002,8096,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120"", ""src/report/admission.rs:16-160""]","A native exec fixture enumerates every open descriptor: stdio are character devices, and neither the supervisor watch socket nor the private listener socket is inherited; its callback binds the conversation, receives stdin, exits, and its group disappears.","Native exec could inherit the supervisor watch or private listener descriptor, letting a child hold the reporting lease open or spy on the admission channel.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Inheriting the lease socket keeps reporting ownership alive past the supervisor and can wedge later runs (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120).,Enumerates real fds with fstat/getpeername and asserts both specific sockets absent plus stdio tty-ness (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8020-8060).,Descriptor-level variant of the lease-release contract; the crash row covers supervisor death instead (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7738-7999).,Real exec through agent run with a helper enumerating the real descriptor table (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8020-8060).,high,keep,Decisive descriptor-inheritance assertions on a real process.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_supervisor_sigkill_releases_reporting_watch|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term|default""]","[""real exec with descriptor enumeration"", ""real PTY and helper process group"", ""socket path probing""]",4.653,4.653,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1454 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|backpressured_input_and_send_do_not_block_inspect_or_kill|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,backpressured_input_and_send_do_not_block_inspect_or_kill,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2254,2435,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:884-908"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:849-905"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1723-1745""]","A 512KiB Input to a session that never reads its PTY does not complete; a SendTerminal on another connection also does not complete; Inspect, List and KillSession on fresh connections still answer; kill succeeds, then sessions are shut down.","PTY backpressure could serialize the control plane, so a wedged session cannot be inspected or killed and the server appears hung.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,An inspector/kill path blocked by one wedged session makes the terminal unusable for that instance (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:884-908).,Pairs each blocked request with successful control requests on separate connections and asserts kill Ok (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2320-2420).,Only row asserting control-plane independence under PTY write backpressure for Input and SendTerminal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2254-2435).,Real PTY with a genuinely blocked reader and real concurrent Unix connections (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2256-2280).,high,keep,Decisive independence assertions between the data path and control path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_backpressured_input_keeps_controls_available|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default""]","[""512KiB blocked input"", ""multiple concurrent sockets"", ""timeout-based negative assertions""]",3.596,3.596,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1458 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17090,17345,"[""src/report/claude.rs:44-80"", ""src/report/extension.rs:230-343""]","Claude input lane: PermissionRequest/Notification(generic)/PreToolUse alone open nothing; verified permission_prompt yields WaitingInput, approval:A, one alert and no Unread; duplicate open and child/wrong/stale notifications change nothing; PostToolUse closes and restores Busy; a later turn opens approval:B and alerts; Stop closes it and yields Ready/Unread; a request on top of Ready keeps Unread and restores on close; an open request at reattach is a baseline and a new one there alerts once.","PermissionRequest or idle notifications could be mistaken for approvals, a duplicate could double-alert, or a reattach could replay a pending prompt.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Opening an approval from the wrong event or turn prompts the user to answer something that is not pending (src/report/claude.rs:44-80 classification).,"Alert-title vectors across six checkpoints, exact request ids/kinds, underlying-sample assertions and reattach baseline (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17100-17340).","Claude input-lane row; codex and omp rows cover different grammars/multiplicity (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13724-13972, :16025-16336).","Real claude hooks, dashboard host record and CLI list (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17102-17125).",high,keep,Grounded negative and positive input-lane assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_input_request_shows_waiting_alerts_once_and_restores_the_underlying_activity|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_ready_alerts_once_per_root_turn_with_unread_and_continuation|default""]","[""claude helper callbacks"", ""dashboard host record"", ""CLI list""]",7.468,7.468,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1462 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_interrupted_resume_keeps_reporting_healthy_and_delivers_new_ready|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_interrupted_resume_keeps_reporting_healthy_and_delivers_new_ready,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9366,9368,"[""src/report/admission.rs:88-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1-120""]","A resume whose transcript contains a synthetic interrupted assistant entry (no requestId) keeps reporting Connected with no failure reason, counts only the real usage once, and delivers a real desktop alert titled ""OVRCR · response ready"" for the new turn.","An interrupted assistant entry could be counted as a metered API response (inflating usage) or trip a health failure, and the ready alert could be missed.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Inflated usage and a false health failure misreport a healthy resumed session (src/report/admission.rs:88-190).,"Asserts exact 60/6 totals, Connected health with no reason, ResponseReady activity and the exact alert title via a real dashboard (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9480-9610).",Only row covering synthetic interrupted transcript entries plus desktop alert delivery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9366-9368).,"Real transcript entries, real reporting and a real spawned desktop-alert dashboard fixture (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9470-9490).",high,keep,Grounded coverage of the interrupted-entry accounting rule and alert delivery.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_explicit_resume_preserves_argv_and_collects_conversation_usage|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_delivery_failure_disconnects_without_stopping_native|default""]","[""synthetic transcript entry"", ""desktop alert dashboard fixture"", ""metric polling""]",6.509,6.509,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1461 (PASS attempt 1); run 4