nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_missing_initial_file_preserves_activity_and_recovers_same_path|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_metrics_missing_initial_file_preserves_activity_and_recovers_same_path,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,10370,10372,"[""src/report/claude_metrics.rs:48-120"", ""src/report/collector.rs:436-459""]","When the initial transcript file is absent, a prompt still shows activity Busy with context 20 while health becomes Unavailable; creating the transcript afterwards on the same path recovers Connected metrics without a new invocation.","A missing transcript could drop all metrics permanently or reopen from a different path, losing prior activity.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Permanent metrics loss for a valid run hides context and usage until a new agent run (src/report/collector.rs:436-459).,"Asserts Unavailable plus preserved Busy/context before recovery, then Connected metrics after create-transcript (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10440-10480).",Only row covering a missing initial transcript and same-path recovery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10370-10372).,Real native run with a delayed transcript file and real retained metrics (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10385-10410).,high,keep,Grounded missing-source recovery coverage with preserved activity.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_route_collects_partial_usage_and_finalizes_native_exit|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_finalization_recovers_original_receipt_after_lost_ack|default""]","[""delayed transcript file"", ""real native helper"", ""metrics polling""]",3.492,3.492,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1464 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_unsupported_fork_freezes_components_and_prevents_reader_reopening|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_metrics_unsupported_fork_freezes_components_and_prevents_reader_reopening,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,10374,10376,"[""src/report/claude_metrics.rs:48-130"", ""src/report/claude_metrics.rs:188-350"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:217-260""]","With clear=true, a bare fork SessionStart freezes metrics after an initial statusline sample; branch/grow-transcript/statusline-unknown/root all preserve the same metrics and binding while health is Unavailable, and native exit finalises as Partial with reason unfinalized_release and an unchanged context stamp.","A forked conversation could keep publishing metrics under the old binding: stale usage/context stamped as current, and an unfinalized release could be reported as complete accounting.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Retained usage/cost accounting for the wrong conversation misstates spend and remaining context, a major integrity failure (src/report/claude_metrics.rs:188-350 accumulator).","Four post-freeze callbacks each assert metrics equality, binding identity and Unavailable health; finalize asserts Partial coverage plus unchanged context stamp (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10696-10790).",Only row covering the freeze/unsupported-fork branch of the metrics finalizer; baseline and lost-ack rows in the sibling shard differ (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10374-10376).,Real compiled agent run with statusline callbacks over the real reporting socket; only the provider binary is scripted (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10383-10410).,high,keep,Precise freeze assertions on a distinct branch; no equivalent retained protection identified.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_route_collects_partial_usage_and_finalizes_native_exit|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_finalization_recovers_original_receipt_after_lost_ack|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_metrics_missing_initial_file_preserves_activity_and_recovers_same_path|default""]","[""real compiled agent run and PTY"", ""statusline callback sequence"", ""metrics polling"", ""env_lock serialization""]",4.095,4.095,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1466 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_supported_conversation_switches_rebind_ready_and_input_without_unread_ack|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,claude_supported_conversation_switches_rebind_ready_and_input_without_unread_ack,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17348,17592,"[""src/report/claude.rs:44-80"", ""src/report/admission.rs:240-300""]","Claude conversation switches: A readies and opens an approval; a clear keeps Connected, closes requests, retains Unread and the same binding; clear-replace to B binds generation 2 and keeps Unread; late A frames (including explicit conversation suffixes) cannot open or Ready on B; the Ready on B creates a new Unread; resume back to A is generation 3; a late B Stop cannot Ready; C readies; compact changes nothing; a bare branch freezes to identity_transition_unavailable while Running.","Late frames from the left conversation could Ready or open approvals on the new one, and a switch could acknowledge Unread.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Cross-conversation frame leakage misattributes activity and can prompt for work in another conversation (src/report/admission.rs:240-300 conversation identity).,Asserts generation/request/alert vectors after every transition and full snapshot equality for compact (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17355-17585).,"Claude switch row; codex/omp variants carry different clear/resume grammars (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14222-14447, :16339-16570).",Real claude fixture with real conversation ids and server state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17350-17375).,high,keep,Grounded late-frame rejection across three generations.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_supported_conversation_switches_rebind_ready_and_input_without_unread_ack|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_in_place_transitions_rebind_reload_and_refresh_without_a_new_producer|default""]","[""long claude callback sequence"", ""dashboard host record""]",6.423,6.423,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1469 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|client_with_wrong_protocol_version_is_refused|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,client_with_wrong_protocol_version_is_refused,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,1738,1808,"[""src/client.rs:39-70"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/codec.rs:18-70""]","Clients claiming versions 68, 69, 70 and current+1 receive the server preamble and are then refused (write or read fails); a fake newer server produces a ""protocol version mismatch"" error naming its version and the shutdown --kill remedy; a peer that closes before a preamble produces the ""older OVRCR build"" error.",A server could serve a client with an incompatible wire layout (mis-decoded session control) or report a version mismatch without the remedy.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Serving an incompatible client can mis-drive sessions through mis-decoded frames (crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/codec.rs:18-70).,Four divergent versions plus both mismatch directions are each asserted with explicit error text (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1738-1808).,Only row covering protocol-version refusal from both the server and client side (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1738-1808).,"Real Unix sockets on both sides, including fake peers implementing the handshake (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:1745-1800).",high,keep,Decisive protocol-compatibility coverage across four version boundaries.,[],"[""thread-hosted real server"", ""raw preamble writes"", ""fake peer listener threads""]",1.175,1.175,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1471 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_exact_resume_reports_ready_unread_and_alert_without_historical_replay|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,codex_exact_resume_reports_ready_unread_and_alert_without_historical_replay,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13621,13721,"[""src/report/codex.rs:150-175"", ""src/report/codex.rs:232-300"", ""src/report/reporter.rs:1-120""]","A codex exact resume: a historical Stop before certified resume invents no binding, Ready or alert; SessionStart(source=resume) attaches (attached=true) with Unknown activity and no alert; a new prompt produces Busy then Observed Ready with Unread and exactly one response-ready alert; a duplicate Stop adds no alert.","A historical Stop could replay a Ready alert on attach, and resume attach could invent Unread or bind the wrong conversation.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Replayed or fabricated Ready on a resumed conversation misstates agent state and notifies for work already seen (src/report/codex.rs:232-300 source transitions).,"Asserts no binding/unread plus zero host calls before attach, then exact alert-titles vector and single-alert duplicate behaviour (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13635-13715).",Only row covering codex resume attach without historical replay (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13621-13721).,"Real codex resume native fixture, dashboard host record and real PTY (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13625-13650).",high,keep,Grounded replay-negative assertions with exact alert counts.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_reopened_path_follows_switch_and_handles_genuine_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_ready_alerts_once_per_root_turn_with_unread_and_continuation|default""]","[""real codex resume fixture"", ""desktop host record"", ""alert polling""]",4.193,4.193,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1473 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,codex_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13724,13972,"[""src/report/codex.rs:232-333"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]","A codex session: PreToolUse alone opens nothing; a verified PermissionRequest yields WaitingInput, one approval:A request, one input-needed alert and no Unread; duplicate open, child and wrong-turn requests change nothing; PostToolUse closes; Stop yields Ready/Unread; a later turn opens approval:B and alerts again; Stop closes it; a request on top of Ready keeps Unread and restores on close; an open request at reattach is a baseline, then a genuinely new request alerts once.","An input request could be duplicated, opened by a child/stale turn, or replayed as a new alert on reattach, and closing it could clear Unread or the underlying sample.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A phantom or replayed approval can prompt the user to approve work that already resolved, and clearing Unread loses the response signal (src/report/codex.rs:300-333 approval correlation).",Twelve alert-count checkpoints plus request-vector equality and underlying-sample assertions (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13740-13960).,Only row covering codex approval correlation across reattach and overlapping Request-on-Ready states (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13724-13972).,"Real codex hooks, real dashboard host record and real CLI list output (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13725-13745).",high,keep,Dense positive/negative assertions with independent expectations.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each|default""]",