nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_hello_carries_the_servers_settings_and_toggles_save_through_the_request|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,dashboard_hello_carries_the_servers_settings_and_toggles_save_through_the_request,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,19928,20084,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1-140"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:250-290""]","The dashboard hello carries the server reading of the document named only by OVRCR_DASHBOARD_CONFIG (path, settings, rows, findings), proving the default config path is unused; N/S/L each send one SetSetting and the document grows by exactly that line; launch_choices merge one project entry while preserving comments and other projects; invalid edits name the expected type or unknown key and leave the document unchanged.","The dashboard could read or save the wrong settings document, merge launch choices destructively, or accept invalid settings silently.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Saving the wrong document or corrupting launch choices changes how every later session launches (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1-140).,"Asserts the full reading vs an independently loaded document, per-key document growth, comment-preserving merge and specific refusal messages (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19940-20080).",Only row covering hello settings provenance plus toggle saves through requests (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19928-20084).,Real binary server with a real document path in its environment and real dashboard key handling (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:19930-19960).,high,keep,Grounded document-provenance and merge coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|settings_set_without_a_server_writes_the_document_a_later_server_loads|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|settings_edit_while_attached_republishes_only_real_changes|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_settings_sources_authorize_and_failed_saves_preserve_opt_ins|default""]","[""real binary server"", ""multiple SetSetting round trips"", ""document comparisons""]",1.856,1.856,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1491 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_authorizes_enabled_startup_before_any_alert|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_authorizes_enabled_startup_before_any_alert,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18079,18127,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520"", ""src/cli/bridge.rs:75-130""]","With notifications enabled and permission not_determined at startup, the dashboard issues exactly status+authorize before any alert, records no delivery; then an input-needed event and a response-ready event each deliver once, giving operations [status, authorize, deliver, deliver] and no startup alert.",Startup could skip the explicit permission authorization (later silent failures) or treat startup as an alert; a permission flow could double-authorize.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Without explicit authorization the OS drops alerts silently, so the user believes notifications are on when they are not (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520 emit_bridge_control).","Asserts the exact ordered operations list, no record at startup, and one delivery per event (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18090-18120).",Only row covering startup authorization ordering before alerts (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18079-18127).,"Real dashboard PTY, real bridge host fixture recording requests (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18081-18095).",high,keep,Decisive ordered-operation assertion on the authorization boundary.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_denied_settings_are_explicit_and_never_modal_or_automatic|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_pending_permission_does_not_repeat_or_block_input|default""]","[""dashboard PTY"", ""bridge request record""]",4.844,4.844,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1497 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_callback_rejects_malformed_versions_before_connecting|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_callback_rejects_malformed_versions_before_connecting,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13460,13519,"[""src/cli/bridge.rs:17-45"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/bridge.rs:1-80""]","With no server running, five malformed tickets (wrong schema, wrong wire, invalid lifetime, relative socket, relative callback executable) each make the callback fail with empty stdout, and no socket appears.","A malformed or foreign ticket could be accepted and drive a connection (or claim an activation), forging navigation authority.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Ticket validation is the only authority check before connecting; accepting a bad digest/schema/lifetime forges navigation (src/cli/bridge.rs:17-45).,"Each malformed field is a separate case asserting non-success, empty stdout and no server start (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13465-13515).",Only row covering malformed-ticket rejection at the CLI boundary (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13460-13519).,Real bridge CLI invocations reading real stdin tickets with no server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13462-13475).,high,keep,Decisive negative coverage of the ticket-validation boundary.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_old_ticket_cannot_select_an_explicitly_reopened_run|default""]","[""five bridge CLI processes"", ""server shutdown setup""]",5.853,5.853,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1498 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_each_in_flight_lane_and_preserves_the_persistent_host|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_each_in_flight_lane_and_preserves_the_persistent_host,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18636,18708,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:86-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130""]","A persistent host pid is established; a blocked Ready client is cancelled when the next prompt starts, and a blocked Input client is cancelled when the tool resolves, while the persistent host stays alive; with another Input client hung, real shell input, render and detach still work, the client dies on detach, and the persistent host survives.",A preference/state change could cancel the persistent host itself (killing all notifications) or leave hung clients after detach.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Killing the app host would disable all desktop notifications until relaunch, a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130 host lifecycle).","Asserts per-lane client absence with persistent-host presence, input round trip under a hung client, and post-detach survival (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18650-18700).",Only row covering in-flight lane cancellation with a persistent host (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18636-18708).,"Real separate host process group, real dashboard PTY and real detach (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18638-18660).",high,keep,Grounded lane/host lifetime separation.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_queued_ready_and_input_without_replay|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_host_failure_and_blocking_never_block_input_or_detach|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_sound_in_flight_preference_changes_cancel_clients_without_replay_and_keep_host_alive|default""]","[""persistent host process"", ""blocked clients"", ""detach wait""]",7.617,7.617,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1499 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_can_inspect_exited_original_run_without_recovery|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_can_inspect_exited_original_run_without_recovery,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13362,13408,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-115"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1466-1515""]","After the bound session exits (run unchanged), a ticket for that original run still applies: the dashboard lands in Browse showing the retained output, and the session summary and row set are unchanged (no recovery, reopen, acknowledge or review).",Navigation could reopen/recover an exited run (starting a new process) or refuse to inspect a legitimately retained exited run.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A navigation-triggered recovery would resurrect a process and change run identity from a notification click (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1466-1515 reopen path).,Asserts applied result plus full session-summary equality and row-set equality after the click (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13370-13405).,Only row covering navigation to an exited original run without recovery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13362-13408).,"Real dashboard PTY, real bridge callback and real exited native process (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13364-13400).",high,keep,Grounded no-side-effect assertion for the retained-run case.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_lands_in_browse_without_reviewing_or_answering|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default""]","[""real native exit sequence"", ""bridge callback"", ""dashboard PTY""]",6.971,6.971,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1501 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_discards_transient_drafts_and_releases_capture|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_discards_transient_drafts_and_releases_capture,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13167,13247,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:116-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:601-700""]","With palette, rename, copy and history overlays each holding unsent text, a valid ticket click still lands in Browse; each overlay closes, no draft text is submitted or restored, no session row changes, Unread stays, and manual_title remains None.",Navigation could leave a transient draft in place (later submitted by accident) or restore an unsent palette search.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Retained drafts after navigation can be submitted into the wrong session, and a stale rename could alter identity (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:601-700).","Four overlay cases each assert screen absence of the draft tokens plus row/unread/title equality, and a reopened palette starts empty (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13170-13240).",Only row covering transient-draft discarding across four overlay types (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13167-13247).,Real dashboard PTY with real key input and bridge callbacks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13169-13200).,high,keep,Grounded multi-overlay negative assertions with durable identity check.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_lands_in_browse_without_reviewing_or_answering|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_focuses_existing_split_without_duplicating_target|default""]","[""four bridge callbacks"", ""real dashboard PTY and key sequences""]",10.796,10.796,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1502 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_lands_in_browse_without_reviewing_or_answering|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_lands_in_browse_without_reviewing_or_answering,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13046,13121,"[""src/cli/bridge.rs:17-45"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:116-190""]","A ready-ticket click from Browse selects the target into Terminal mode, then a second run with an open Input request: clicking enters Browse and selects it without marking Unread reviewed, answering the request, or creating/replacing any process; a historical ticket still navigates without replaying its alert.","Navigation could acknowledge Unread or answer a pending approval, and a stale ticket could replay an old alert or duplicate a session.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Navigation must move focus only; acknowledging or answering as a side effect misreports state and can approve work the user never saw (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:116-190).,Asserts unread/agent/row equality after each click plus the retained historical ticket navigation and stable delivery count (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13060-13115).,Only row asserting that Browse entry on Ready and Input banners does not review/answer (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13046-13121).,"Real bridge CLI callback, real dashboard PTY and real server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13050-13070).",high,keep,Grounded side-effect-negative assertions with real ticket capture.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_preserves_queued_wip_shutdown_questions|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_focuses_existing_split_without_duplicating_target|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_can_inspect_exited_original_run_without_recovery|default""]","[""real dashboard PTY and bridge callback"", ""ticket extraction from host record""]",9.960,9.960,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1504 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_old_ticket_cannot_select_an_explicitly_reopened_run|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_old_ticket_cannot_select_an_explicitly_reopened_run,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13523,13618,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-115"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1466-1515""]","A ticket is captured, the session is killed, and an explicit ReopenSession creates run 2 (verified by the spawn record); the old ticket is ignored, the dashboard does not show the new run, rows are unchanged, and the provider is not invoked again.","An old notification click could select or restart an explicitly reopened run, mixing a stale ticket with a new run identity.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Selecting a new run from an old ticket crosses run authority, and re-invoking the provider could spawn a duplicate agent (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1466-1515).","Asserts spawn-record equality, rows equality, ignored result and absence of the new run on screen (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13530-13615).",Only row covering explicit reopen versus an old ticket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13523-13618).,"Real server binary, real reopen through the compiled CLI/server and real bridge callback (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13525-13560).",high,keep,Grounded run-identity isolation with a spawn-side-effect check.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_can_inspect_exited_original_run_without_recovery|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_never_starts_missing_server_and_old_lifetime_stays_invalid|default""]","[""real binary server"", ""session reopen via provider"", ""bridge callback"", ""spawn record""]",7.734,7.734,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1505 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_denied_settings_are_explicit_and_never_modal_or_automatic|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_denied_settings_are_explicit_and_never_modal_or_automatic,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18264,18345,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:840-880""]","With permission denied at startup, the dashboard shows an explicit denied notice and only a status check; input works; input-needed and response-ready each produce one delivery attempt (which the host denies) and Unread appears; a Browse recovery key is the sole Settings launch request, no Confirm modal appears, repeated recovery re-checks status, a failed settings open reports manual action, and a later allow clears the notice without a delivery or fallback.","Denied permission could be retried automatically or hidden, or Settings could be launched without explicit user action (and possibly modally).",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Automatic or modal permission escalation takes over the screen and bypasses explicit consent (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520).,"Asserts ordered control operations, absence of Confirm and fallback, input round trip under denial, and clearing after allow (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18270-18340).",Only row covering denied-permission UX and explicit recovery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18264-18345).,Real dashboard PTY with a host fixture returning denied/settings statuses (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18266-18280).,high,keep,Grounded consent-UX assertions with explicit-operation checks.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_authorizes_enabled_startup_before_any_alert|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_settings_sources_authorize_and_failed_saves_preserve_opt_ins|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_expired_permission_check_recovers_without_reauthorization|default""]","[""dashboard PTY"", ""bridge control record"", ""input round trip""]",5.351,5.351,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1508 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_host_failure_and_blocking_never_block_input_or_detach|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_host_failure_and_blocking_never_block_input_or_detach,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,17887,17978,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1080-1130"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1123-1155""]","With the host in fail mode, delivery fails, a sticky unavailable notice appears with no private stderr text, and activity stays Ready; toggling works. With the host blocking on a second completion, real terminal input still renders while the host process is alive; detach succeeds and kills the blocked host group; the session stays Running.",A failing or hung host command could block dashboard input/detach or leak host stderr into the UI.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A blocking notification host that stalls input or detach freezes the UI on the critical path (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1123-1155 run_host).,"Asserts private stderr absence, a real input round trip while the host group is alive, group death after detach, and Running phase (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17900-17970).",Only row covering host failure/blocking on the input/detach path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17887-17978).,"Real dashboard PTY, real blocked host process group and real shell session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:17889-17905).",high,keep,Decisive non-blocking assertions with real hung processes.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_managed_completion_reaches_host_once_including_visible_sessions|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_cancels_each_in_flight_lane_and_preserves_the_persistent_host|default""]","[""blocked host process group"", ""dashboard input round trip"", ""detach wait""]",6.457,6.457,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1516 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|detected_claude_model_launch_revalidates_alias_and_workspace_identity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,detected_claude_model_launch_revalidates_alias_and_workspace_identity,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,100,467,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:276-345"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:604-698"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:589-620""]","Dashboard QueryAgentModels against a fake native Claude catalog returns alias opus to claude-opus-fixture-v1 plus a launch binding; an explicit create with that binding splices --model opus; after the native resolution file changes, the same binding is refused with a ""resolution changed"" InvalidRequest and no session; after the worktree identity file changes, create fails with ""Git worktree changed"" and the fake catalog is never invoked; a HarnessDefault launch omits --model.","A stale model alias, or a workspace whose git worktree identity changed after the binding was issued, could launch Claude with a model or checkout the user never verified; a HarnessDefault launch could silently acquire --model.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Wrong model in a replaced worktree is wrong-ownership/major workflow failure; the server refuses both drift cases at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:604-698.,"Positive and negative legs assert AgentModels content, resulting terminal argv, absence of the fake catalog-call file, and exact rejection messages at tests/server_lifecycle.rs:186-260, :300-330, :360-430.","Only reviewed test that chains catalog discovery, alias revalidation, git-identity revalidation and HarnessDefault argv through the real server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:100-467).","Compiled ovrcr server process, real Unix dashboard socket and real PTY; only the native Claude binary is a scripted stand-in (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:104-140).",high,keep,Grounded high-signal acceptance coverage; no other row asserts both alias drift and worktree-identity drift before launch.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|harness_default_claude_launches_without_catalog_or_model_override|default""]","[""spawns detached compiled server with a fake claude on PATH"", ""real PTY plus Unix dashboard socket"", ""polls terminal text and catalog-call marker file"", ""sleep-based terminal polling""]",3.863,3.863,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1527 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_drops_saved_lines_a_repaint_erases|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,history_drops_saved_lines_a_repaint_erases,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4892,4951,"[""crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/history.rs:83-160"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095""]","A session prints 60 ERASED lines, waits, then repaints with ESC[H ESC[2J ESC[3J and 40 REPAINTED lines; the History rows contain no ERASED_ line, contain REPAINTED_0000 exactly once, and include the tail and done markers.","An erase-display repaint could stack the erased transcript into History, so a user scrolling back sees every repaint duplicated.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Duplicated ghost transcript corrupts the durable scrollback users rely on (crates/ovrcr-terminal/src/history.rs).,"Asserts the negative substring, an exact single occurrence count, and the tail markers (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4930-4947).",Only row covering erase-display history compaction (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4892-4951).,Real PTY emitting the exact repaint escape sequence parsed by production vt100 history (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4895-4905).,high,keep,Decisive negative and count assertions for a subtle repaint defect.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default""]","[""real PTY with raw escape sequences"", ""history paging"", ""vt100 history parser""]",2.174,2.174,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1537 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_frozen_page_survives_eviction_and_exit|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,history_frozen_page_survives_eviction_and_exit,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4954,5057,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:246-330""]","HistoryBegin freezes a snapshot; after the shell emits 640 more lines and exits, paging the same snapshot returns byte-identical rows, while a new HistoryBegin reflects the final output and no longer contains OLD_VISIBLE.","A frozen snapshot could mutate as the terminal advances or be lost on exit, breaking a slow client reading history.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A mutating snapshot makes paged history inconsistent and can drop rows mid-read (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095).,Asserts equality of the entire row vector before/after exit plus the new snapshot contents (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4980-5045).,Only row covering snapshot immutability across eviction and exit (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4954-5057).,Real PTY progress and the real history protocol with frozen snapshots (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4954-5057).,high,keep,Decisive immutable-snapshot invariant with a contrasting fresh snapshot.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default""]","[""640 line PTY output"", ""two history sessions"", ""vector equality on rows""]",2.406,2.406,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1539 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,history_reattach_reads_retained_output,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,4797,4887,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:246-330"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:643-700""]","After a dashboard detaches and the shell runs 600 lines plus 40 offscreen tail lines then exits, a new dashboard Select shows FINAL_HISTORY_MARKER but not the evicted offscreen line, and HistoryBegin/HistoryPage returns the retained rows containing DETACHED_OFFSCREEN_000 and the final marker; the first page stays within PAGE_BYTES.","Detached output could be lost from History, or a reattach could show only the visible screen without the retained scrollback.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Lost detached output destroys the transcript a user reattaches to inspect (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095).,"Asserts both the live screen exclusion and the retained-row inclusion, plus page size bound (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4800-4880).",Only row covering reattach history retention with an eviction boundary (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4797-4887).,Real PTY producing 640 lines and real history protocol over a socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:4797-4887).,high,keep,Grounded history coverage distinguishing visible screen from retained rows.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_frozen_page_survives_eviction_and_exit|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_slow_dashboard_recovers_after_finite_burst|default""]","[""600+40 line PTY output"", ""history page loop"", ""screen parse""]",2.565,2.565,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1540 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_reattach_recovers_a_paused_reporter_during_an_input_wait|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,omp_reattach_recovers_a_paused_reporter_during_an_input_wait,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,16677,16866,"[""src/report/extension.rs:200-280"", ""src/report/extension.rs:230-260""]","With the approval open dropped, the following close exposes a gap that clears the standing request set; doctor reports paused_recoverable/Unavailable with recovery available and an omp-specific /ovrcr-reattach remediation; running reattach recovers generation 2 Connected Idle from the API with no requests and no Unread invented; a new question alerts once; a late close for the pre-reattach request cannot clear the new question; closing the last request restores Idle.","Recovery could clear a newer request with a stale close, or baseline Idle without any API evidence.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A stale close clearing a live request hides a pending decision from the user (src/report/extension.rs:230-260 request ownership).,"Doctor fields, generation/activity after recovery, request-vector equality after the stale close, and restored activity (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16690-16860).",Only row covering omp reattach during an input wait with stale-close fencing (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16677-16866).,"Real omp host with recovery command, real doctor CLI and dashboard host record (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16679-16700).",high,keep,Grounded recovery-plus-fencing coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_command_recovers_a_paused_reporter|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default""]","[""doctor CLI"", ""dashboard host record"", ""node omp host""]",4.813,4.813,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1553 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,omp_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,16573,16674,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-260"", ""src/report/extension.rs:98-140""]","A dropped approval close (sequence 4) changes nothing until the next approval frame exposes the hole; then health is Unavailable/source_gap, requests clear, binding and generation hold, later frames apply nothing, and a later agent_start recovers generation 2 with Busy, followed by a normal Ready/Unread in generation 2.",A lost close could be assumed applied (leaving a phantom approval) or could pause forever without boundary recovery.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A phantom approval or a permanently paused reporter misstates whether the agent is waiting (src/report/extension.rs:230-260).,"Asserts snapshot equality before detection, cleared requests with retained binding, quiet-state equality, and recovery generation plus later Unread (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16580-16670).",Omp gap variant at an approval close; pi rows cover dialog/other boundaries (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15434-15526).,Real omp transport dropping one frame and real server state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16582-16600).,high,keep,Grounded frame-loss detection and recovery assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_reattach_recovers_a_paused_reporter_during_an_input_wait|default""]","[""dropped-frame omp host"", ""callback waits""]",4.077,4.077,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1552 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,3931,4010,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1560"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1723-1740""]","Killing a paused group delivers SIGTERM to both stopped leader and descendant, collects TERM_ACK and final descendant output, retains the pre-exit markers, and leaves the group absent; a group externally SIGSTOPped (row still Running) is also killed with handlers run.","Terminating a stopped group could send SIGTERM without SIGCONT so handlers never run, or only the leader receives it, losing final output.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A stopped group that never handles SIGTERM survives until SIGKILL, losing graceful handler output (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1466-1520).","Requires TERM_ACK from both peers, descendant final bytes, terminal markers at first Exited observation, and group absence (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:3935-4005).",Only row asserting handler execution (not just death) for a paused and an externally stopped group (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:3931-4010).,Real stopped process groups with handler scripts reporting over a datagram channel (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2913-2990).,high,keep,Decisive coverage that stop-state termination still runs handlers.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_shutdown_cleans_stopped_groups|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_control_races_converge|default""]","[""stopped real process groups"", ""datagram acknowledgement collection"", ""SIGSTOP injection""]",4.502,4.502,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1556 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_server_refuses_removal_and_late_mutation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_server_refuses_removal_and_late_mutation,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2725,2896,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:871-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:621-626""]","PauseSession publishes a Paused SessionChanged and List shows Paused; Input and SendTerminal are refused Conflict; RemoveSession is SessionRunning; ResumeSession publishes Running; then kill, acknowledge and removal of workspace/project succeed.","A paused session could accept input (writing to a stopped PTY) or be removed while still live, and phase transitions could fail to publish.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Admitting input or removal while paused leaves a live session unusable or wrongly destroyed (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:871-880).,"Asserts events, List phase, both refusal codes, and the post-resume Running state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2740-2860).",Covers the dashboard event + Phase removal gates; the group-level pause behaviour is covered by the pause harness rows (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2725-2896).,"Real server, real PTY shell and real dashboard socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2727-2750).",high,keep,Grounded state-machine coverage of pause/resume through the dashboard path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers|default""]","[""real PTY shell"", ""dashboard event loop"", ""full teardown sequence""]",4.145,4.145,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1558 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pause_resume_stops_group_and_rejects_input,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,3832,3928,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:884-897"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1736-1750""]","A real leader and descendant in one PTY group both enter state T after PauseSession; Input is refused with the exact paused message; RemoveSession and non-kill shutdown are refused; after ResumeSession the screen is byte-identical, pid/phase are unchanged, and injected bytes reach the PTY.","Pause could stop only the leader (descendants keep running), input could be written to a stopped group, or resume could replace the session and lose its screen.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A half-stopped group keeps producing output while the UI claims paused, and input to a stopped group wedges (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880).","Asserts ps state of both peers, exact screen equality across resume, identity preservation and delivered PTY bytes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:3836-3915).",Only row asserting the whole-group SIGSTOP plus screen-preserving resume with a descendant peer (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:3832-3928).,Real leader and descendant processes with a datagram control channel and real PTY (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2913-2990).,high,keep,Grounded process-group pause coverage with byte-level resume check.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_server_refuses_removal_and_late_mutation|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_kill_runs_group_handlers|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pause_resume_backpressured_input_keeps_controls_available|default""]","[""two real PTY peers with datagram channel"", ""ps state polling"", ""SIGSTOP/SIGCONT signalling""]",2.956,2.956,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1559 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_input_request_shows_waiting_alerts_once_and_restores_the_underlying_activity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_input_request_shows_waiting_alerts_once_and_restores_the_underlying_activity,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,14989,15185,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-343"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]",Pi dialog frames: ui_prompt_start opens a Select request with WaitingInput while Busy stays underneath and no Unread; answering restores Busy without a second alert; a second outer span is a new request id; Ready/Unread is a separate lane; a request on top of Ready keeps Unread and restores Ready; reattach baselines an open request; after reporter loss requests clear while Unread survives.,"A dialog close could clear the wrong request or leave a stale request, and a reattach could replay an alert for a request already on screen.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A stale dialog request prompts the user to answer something no longer pending, and losing the underlying activity misreports the agent (src/report/extension.rs:230-343 request lifecycle).","Asserts request kinds/ids, underlying samples, alert-title vectors across reattach, and cleared-set-with-Unread on loss (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15000-15180).",Only row covering pi Select request identity and restore-under-Ready semantics (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14989-15185).,Real pi host dialogs and real dashboard host record (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:14991-15005).,high,keep,Grounded request-lane coverage distinct from ready alerts.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default""]","[""node pi host"", ""dashboard host record"", ""many callback steps""]",6.165,6.165,1,0,hosted-single-run,evi