nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_launch_preserves_argv_exit_and_environment_and_plain_launch_is_untracked|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_managed_launch_preserves_argv_exit_and_environment_and_plain_launch_is_untracked,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,11542,11629,"[""src/report/extension.rs:48-95"", ""src/report/pi.rs:26-79"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120""]","A picker-shaped pi launch gets exactly one prepended -e extension path, keeps the user argv (--model x/y hello world), passes no hook env, exits 17 without binding, and the materialized extension directory is removed; RPC mode runs native with reporting unavailable and no binding; a plain launch has no channel at all.","argv rewriting could run a different command, a stray -e could be duplicated, or the private extension file/directory could survive the invocation.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Rewritten or duplicated launch argv changes what the user runs, and a surviving extension leaks the reporting entrypoint (src/report/extension.rs:48-95 materialize/cleanup).","Asserts exact argv prefix and tail, absence of hook variables, exit code, extension removal and the ineligible-mode notice (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11542-11629).",Only row asserting managed-launch argv preservation and extension cleanup for pi (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11542-11629).,Real compiled agent run and a scripted native pi that records its argv and environment (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11544-11600).,high,keep,Grounded launch-shape and cleanup assertions with a negative environment check.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|picker_shaped_claude_and_codex_launches_use_the_managed_reporting_route|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_managed_launch_inserts_its_extension_and_removes_it|default""]","[""real compiled CLI launches"", ""scripted native pi"", ""extension directory polling""]",3.457,3.457,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1564 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_command_recovers_a_paused_reporter|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_reattach_command_recovers_a_paused_reporter,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15664,15745,"[""src/report/extension.rs:200-280"", ""src/cli/managed.rs:250-280""]","A paused reporter (source_gap) is reported by doctor as paused_recoverable with recovery available and an /ovrcr-reattach remediation; running that command in the loaded extension recovers generation 2, Connected, Idle from its own API, empty requests, prints the reattach notice, and needs no fresh native launch.","A paused reporter could be unrecoverable without restarting the whole agent, or recovery could baseline from silence (Idle invented).",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Irrecoverable reporting after one lost frame forces a native restart and loses the conversation context (src/report/extension.rs:200-280 recovery path).,Asserts doctor delivery/recovery/remediation plus recovered generation/health/activity/requests and the notice (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15670-15740).,Only row covering the explicit reattach recovery command from a paused state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15664-15745).,"Real pi host executing the production recovery command, real doctor CLI (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15666-15690).",high,keep,Grounded in-place recovery coverage reviewed against its branch.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_on_a_healthy_reporter_is_a_fresh_generation_and_the_next_cycle_readies|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_reattach_recovers_a_paused_reporter_during_an_input_wait|default""]","[""doctor CLI"", ""node pi host"", ""callback waits""]",3.482,3.482,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1565 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_on_a_healthy_reporter_is_a_fresh_generation_and_the_next_cycle_readies|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pi_reattach_on_a_healthy_reporter_is_a_fresh_generation_and_the_next_cycle_readies,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15594,15661,"[""src/report/extension.rs:200-280"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320""]",A reattach command on a healthy reporter (idle:false) becomes generation 2 with Unknown activity (not Idle/Ready) and keeps the first Unread; the next cycle reusing run 1 still Readies as a new Unread in generation 2.,"Reattach could reuse the generation so the next cycle is dropped as a duplicate (never Ready), or it could baseline as Idle/Ready and misstate state.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A dropped post-reattach Ready loses the only completion signal for that cycle (src/report/extension.rs:200-280 reattach generation).,"Asserts generation, Unknown state, Unread preservation and the new Unread after the next cycle (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15600-15655).",Only row covering healthy-reporter reattach generation reset (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15594-15661).,Real pi host running the reattach command through the loaded extension (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15596-15610).,high,keep,Grounded identity-reset coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_replacement_binds_the_foreground_conversation_and_rejects_the_retired_producer|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_command_recovers_a_paused_reporter|default""]","[""node pi host"", ""callback waits""]",3.492,3.492,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1567 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reload_closes_the_open_request_before_retiring_the_producer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_reload_closes_the_open_request_before_retiring_the_producer,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15188,15278,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-290"", ""src/report/reporter.rs:1-120""]","With a Select dialog open, `agent doctor pi` reports WaitingInput and [Select]; a session_shutdown(reload) retires the producer, publishes the empty request set against the owning binding, restores Busy, keeps Connected (reload is not transport loss) and leaves Unread None.","A reload could leave a stale dialog published against a retired producer, or be misclassified as transport loss and pause reporting.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A dialog left open after reload points the user at a session state that no longer exists (src/report/extension.rs:230-290 retire_requests).,"Asserts doctor activity and request kinds, then the retired snapshot fields including Connected and restored Busy (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15195-15275).",Only row covering reload retiring an open request before the producer (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15188-15278).,"Real pi host, real compiled doctor CLI and real server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15190-15220).",high,keep,Grounded retirment path with doctor cross-check.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_replacement_binds_the_foreground_conversation_and_rejects_the_retired_producer|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default""]","[""doctor CLI run"", ""node pi host"", ""callback steps""]",3.523,3.523,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1568 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_recovers_at_a_continuation_start_and_still_readies|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pi_source_gap_recovers_at_a_continuation_start_and_still_readies,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15529,15591,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-270"", ""src/report/extension.rs:290-343""]","With the input_open dropped, the hole is detected at the following close, then a repeated agent_start for the same run recovers the receiver: generation 2, Connected, Busy with a turn identity; the cycle then Readies and its Unread belongs to generation 2.","A continuation start after a gap could fail to recover (leaving reporting paused) or recover without the cycle identity, so the response never becomes Ready.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A recovery that loses the cycle identity permanently hides the response the agent is producing (src/report/extension.rs:290-343 continuation handling).,"Asserts reason before recovery, generation/turn after, and the Unread binding generation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15535-15585).",Distinct recovery boundary (continuation start) from the ordinary-start gap row (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15434-15526).,Real pi host with a dropped frame and real server state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15531-15550).,high,keep,Grounded continuation-recovery assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default""]","[""dropped-frame pi host"", ""callback waits""]",4.847,4.847,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1571 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_delivery_failure_disconnects_without_stopping_native|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,private_claude_activity_delivery_failure_disconnects_without_stopping_native,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,10050,10052,"[""src/report/admission.rs:16-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:66-90""]","With activity delivery rejected by the proxy, the reporter flips to Unavailable and the activity revision stays 0; a later prompt still produces no admission of activity, the binding is unchanged, and the native run continues printing ACTIVITY_FINISHED.",A failed activity delivery could leave the reporter claiming Connected (silently dropping all future activity) or stop the native agent.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Silently connected-but-undelivered reporting hides agent state indefinitely (src/report/admission.rs:16-190).,"Asserts Unavailable within a deadline, revision 0, preserved binding and native continuation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10240-10270).",Delivery-failure variant of the activity contract; the value table row covers normal delivery (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10050-10052).,"Real proxy rejecting a production frame, real native helper and real PTY output (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9674-9730).",high,keep,Grounded coverage of the delivery-failure disconnect path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_tracks_only_current_root_prompt_observations|default""]","[""admission proxy thread"", ""real native helper"", ""deadline polling""]",3.696,3.696,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1573 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|resource_terminal_requests_preserve_background_state_and_close_cleanly|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,resource_terminal_requests_preserve_background_state_and_close_cleanly,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,5412,5642,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:546-570"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1406-1420"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:649-700""]","A background session at 40x120 acknowledges sends with bracketed pastes while another session is selected; ReadTerminal rejects max_lines 0 as InvalidRequest and an unknown id as NotFound; max_lines 1 returns exactly TAIL; closing twice is Conflict after the first close, and the pid group is gone.","Sending to a non-selected session could resize its PTY (corrupting a background agent), truncation bounds could be ignored, or a closed session could be closed again.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Resizing a background session corrupts an agent TUI (bounded but major for that workflow), and unknown-session handling must not touch state (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:546-570).","Asserts size stability, exact paste hex, exact max_lines output, both error codes and idempotent-close refusal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5440-5600).",Only row covering background-send geometry plus ReadTerminal bounds together (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5412-5642).,"Real PTYs, real dashboard socket and real process-group disappearance (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:5415-5445).",high,keep,Grounded multi-boundary resource/terminal coverage with exact assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|concurrent_terminal_sends_are_serialized_as_complete_pastes|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default""]","[""two real PTY sessions"", ""dashboard select + sends"", ""exact hex and line assertions""]",3.509,3.509,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1574 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|shutdown_without_kill_allows_retained_exited_records|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,shutdown_without_kill_allows_retained_exited_records,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,2187,2224,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1988-2035"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1736-1775"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:643-700""]",A session that printed and exited is retained as an exited row; Shutdown{kill:false} still returns Ok; after restarting the same instance the row is acknowledged with run 1 and removed with Ok.,"Retained exited rows could block a non-kill shutdown (making the CLI unusable), or the run identity could reset across restart so the row cannot be acknowledged.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A shutdown that cannot complete without killing live work is a major workflow failure; run identity must survive restart (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1988-2035).,Crosses a server restart and asserts acknowledgement with the original run plus successful removal (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2200-2224).,Only row asserting retained-row lifecycle across a restart (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2187-2224).,"Real server restarted over the same registry and socket, real PTY session (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:2196-2220).",high,keep,Grounded persistence coverage with a restart boundary.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|fast_exit_session_is_retained_as_exited|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|control_lifecycle_enforces_every_removal_gate|default""]","[""two server starts on retained storage"", ""real exiting session"", ""acknowledge/remove requests""]",3.961,3.961,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1580 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|transcript_reads_only_the_retained_conversation_and_rejects_stale_pages|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,transcript_reads_only_the_retained_conversation_and_rejects_stale_pages,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,20592,20837,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/transcript.rs:88-260"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:643-700""]","For both Claude and Codex retained conversations, a control client and a dashboard read the same page; a different run is NotFound; a page before the start or a wrong conversation identity is Conflict; a same-run reference change after retention cannot splice pages; provider history files are never written; the session stays live and acknowledges terminal input.","A transcript page could mix a moved/renamed provider file with the retained conversation (showing another conversation's text) or could write to provider history, and stale pages could splice unrelated content.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Splicing another conversation into a retained transcript is a privacy/integrity breach of conversation content (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/transcript.rs:88-260).,"Asserts exact entry vectors, identity equality per page, and NotFound/Conflict for stale run, page and identity, with byte equality of the history file (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20640-20820).",Only row covering transcript paging identity and stale-page rejection for both providers (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20592-20837).,"Real retained conversation files, real control/dashboard sockets and real agent children (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20597-20640).",high,keep,Grounded identity and staleness assertions with file-immutability evidence.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_unread_real_cli_and_dashboard_review_preserve_native_reporting|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_generated_subject_and_private_history_never_leave_the_application|default""]","[""two provider conversations"", ""real sockets and PTYs"", ""supervisor reserve/bind/retain""]",3.575,3.575,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1598 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
