nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|explicit_non_default_takes_effect|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,unit,explicit_non_default_takes_effect,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,622,642,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-260""]","For every declared setting, a valid non-default value (proven different from the default) produces no findings and the expected row value/source across all backgrounds.","An accepted but ignored setting (silent no-op), so a user change such as quota.enabled or delegation limits never takes effect.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,A silently ignored setting can leave consent or delegation policy unapplied (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-260).,"Asserts no findings, the sample differs from the default, and the exact expected row for every setting and background.",full_document_sets_every_setting_with_document_source sets all settings at once; per-setting effect isolation is unique (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1050).,Runs the production loader over generated documents.,high,keep,Only per-setting non-default effect matrix.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afull_document_sets_every_setting_with_document_source|default""]","[""generated document matrix over the loader""]",0.072,0.072,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2880 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime%3A%3Asettings_matrix|wrong_type_reports_one_finding_and_disables_invalid_cursor_source|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime::settings_matrix,integration,unit,wrong_type_reports_one_finding_and_disables_invalid_cursor_source,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/tests/settings_matrix.rs,645,674,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-300""]","For every setting, its wrong type in every background yields exactly one finding naming the key and line, only that setting falls back to its invalid row, and a malformed Cursor state_db disables the Cursor reader instead of selecting the default account.","A wrong-typed setting silently defaulting (no finding), or an invalid Cursor database path falling back to the default account's database and reading it.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,Silent defaulting can misapply consent/policy settings; a wrong Cursor source would report another account's usage (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:107-300).,"Asserts one finding per case with key/line, the invalid row for every other row, and the explicit Cursor-reader-disabled check.",one_wrong_type_defaults_only_that_setting_with_one_finding covers one setting; invalid_explicit_cursor_database... covers the Cursor sub-claim (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/mod.rs:1246).,Runs the production loader over generated wrong-typed documents.,high,keep,Only all-settings wrong-type matrix with the Cursor source sub-assertion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aone_wrong_type_defaults_only_that_setting_with_one_finding|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainvalid_explicit_cursor_database_never_selects_default_account|default""]","[""generated wrong-typed matrix""]",0.073,0.073,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2885 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|catalog_process%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areaped_group_uncertainty_is_read_only_until_descendant_exit|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,catalog_process::tests::reaped_group_uncertainty_is_read_only_until_descendant_exit,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/catalog_process.rs,880,923,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/catalog_process.rs:278-330""]","With the group leader reaped but a descendant still holding the group, resolution refuses while the group is present and sends no signal; after the descendant exits, resolution succeeds and both leader and group are absent.","Signalling or reaping a process group whose leader is already gone and whose membership is uncertain, which can target a recycled pid, or declaring the group resolved while a descendant still runs.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The read-only-until-absent rule prevents acting on a process group whose ownership cannot be proven (catalog_process.rs:278-330); the worst regression is a wrong-target signal to a recycled group, so ownership/durable-process integrity at C=3.","It asserts the leader was waited, the descendant started and stayed present during refusal, the refusal itself, then recovery and group/leader absence (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/catalog_process.rs:909-922) — a precise state-preserving transition with a real held descendant.",The group-only uncertainty state is covered only here; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|catalog_process%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aunknown_nonmatching_child_blocks_repeated_spawns_until_it_is_waited|default covers an un-waited nonmatching child instead. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/catalog_process.rs:804-877.,"Real shell leader, background descendant, real pgid probes and production owner methods (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/catalog_process.rs:278-330.",high,keep,The only test that proves refusal is read-only (no signal) on a real held group.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|catalog_process%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aunknown_nonmatching_child_blocks_repeated_spawns_until_it_is_waited|default""]","spawns a shell with a background descendant, polls files and pgid",0.253,0.253,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2343 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aassigned_read_policy_recovery_retains_disabled_builtins_and_one_exact_mcp_file|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,claude_recovery::tests::assigned_read_policy_recovery_retains_disabled_builtins_and_one_exact_mcp_file,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs,256,292,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115""]","A saved read policy keeps `--tools """"` (builtins disabled), `--strict-mcp-config` and exactly one canonical --mcp-config file path in position, and a missing MCP file makes recovery fail.","Resuming a delegated read-only session without `--tools """"` or without strict MCP scoping, which would re-enable built-in tools or admit every configured MCP server.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"This argv is the delegated session's tool/MCP authority fence (claude_recovery.rs:48-115 and launch_options' refusal list at 202-219); losing `--tools """"` or strict MCP scoping expands what a resumed delegated agent may execute, so C=3.","Exact vector equality including the empty tool list, the strict flag and the canonicalized MCP path (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:256-282), plus the missing-file Err (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:283-291), reject any dropped or reordered authority flag.","The delegated read-policy restoration is not covered by the other two Claude recovery tests, which assert prompt dropping and settings files. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115.","Real temp MCP file, canonical path emitted by production launch_options (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/claude_recovery.rs:48-115.",high,keep,Preserves a security-relevant authority fence with exact argv assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration|default""]",temp file create/canonicalize/delete,0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2351 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_delegation%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_startup_requirements_only_allow_a_proven_plugins_off_override|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,codex_delegation::tests::dashboard_startup_requirements_only_allow_a_proven_plugins_off_override,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs,990,1007,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:227-258""]","A startup config is accepted only when requirements are absent, when featureRequirements.plugins is exactly false, when only other features are named, or when requirements are empty; it is rejected for a missing appServerVersion, plugins true, featureRequirements true, and requirements 42.","Starting the dashboard app server when the startup config does not prove plugins are disabled (or when the config shape is unreadable), so user plugins could run inside the probe.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Plugins are user/third-party code that the probe must not execute; the checker is the precondition for starting the app server (codex_delegation.rs:227-258), a side-effect/authority boundary at C=3.","Four accept and four reject shapes (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:990-1006) pin both the permission and the fail-closed behavior, including type confusion in featureRequirements.",The only test of the plugins-off requirement parser; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_delegation%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_catalog_refuses_managed_plugins_enabled_before_app_server_warmup|default asserts the integration refusal after a real startup config. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:1254-1282.,Direct call to production dashboard_plugins_override_is_compatible (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:227-258.,high,keep,Exact accept/reject matrix for the precondition that gates plugin execution.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_delegation%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_catalog_refuses_managed_plugins_enabled_before_app_server_warmup|default""]",JSON parsing only,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2363 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aexact_history_header_is_required_and_missing_history_is_unavailable|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,codex_recovery::tests::exact_history_header_is_required_and_missing_history_is_unavailable,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs,343,392,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:53-113"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:114-150"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/recovery.rs:18-56""]","validate_history accepts a history file only when its first session_meta line carries the exact conversation id, rejects a missing file, another id or a truncated/absent header, reports a history-less reference as unavailable with a history message, and resume_argv refuses non-canonical UUID identities with 'canonical UUID'.","Resuming from a history file that belongs to a different Codex conversation, or passing --last/a display name/an uppercase UUID as the resume identity.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The exact conversation identity is what a resumed session continues (codex_recovery.rs:91-113); attaching another conversation's history mixes contexts and reports the wrong conversation's state, so wrong conversation ownership at C=3.","Four history states are asserted in sequence (missing, other id, exact id, then no history) and unavailable/resume_argv are checked for their message (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:343-391); a validator that accepted any session_meta or any UUID case fails.",Codex history identity is unique; Grok's history test uses its own first-line schema and Claude recovery has no history-file rule. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:53-113.,Real temp JSONL files plus the production validators and message builder (recovery.rs:18-56) (F=4).,high,keep,Exact identity checks across four file states with the unavailable path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|grok_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahistory_identity_is_the_first_update_line_and_nothing_else|default""]",temp JSONL files written and rewritten,0.019,0.019,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2366 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arecovery_preserves_controls_but_drops_prompts_and_rejects_unsafe_options|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,codex_recovery::tests::recovery_preserves_controls_but_drops_prompts_and_rejects_unsafe_options,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs,267,340,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:25-52""]","Codex launch_options keeps model, profile, sandbox (-s), approval (-a), --no-alt-screen/--approve-for-me/--no-daemon/--strict-config and legacy --full-auto, drops a trailing prompt and everything after `--`, and errors for --config=, --remote, --last, --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust and a relative -C.","Dropping the sandbox or approval flags when resuming, replaying a private prompt, or admitting options that would let the resumed process bypass hook trust or attach to another session.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"`-s read-only` and `-a on-request` are the sandbox and approval controls of a resumed Codex session (codex_recovery.rs:25-52); losing them restores default authority, and --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust is refused, so C=3.","Two exact vectors plus the legacy --full-auto vector, the empty post-`--` result and five per-option errors (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:267-339) reject each control loss and each unsafe admission by name.",Codex's control vocabulary and legacy alias differ from the Claude and Pi/Omp tests; this is the only place --full-auto compatibility and the bypass/remote refusals are pinned. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:25-52.,Direct call to production launch_options over constructed argv (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_recovery.rs:25-52.,high,keep,Exact argv assertions on sandbox/approval controls and refusal of authority-bypassing options.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|claude_recovery%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asaved_launch_options_drop_task_prompts_and_refuse_inline_configuration|default""]",argument vector construction only,0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2368 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_cloud_authority_survives_offline_read_and_upgrade|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::legacy_cloud_authority_survives_offline_read_and_upgrade,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,883,1001,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","For schemas 23, 24, 25 and 26, an offline read leaves the version unchanged; initialize_registry upgrades to schema 28, preserves the cloud_creations metadata byte-for-byte, keeps the private payload bytes, and creates empty Operator tables.","A cloud-creation upgrade that rewrites or drops an unparsed legacy metadata blob, deletes the private payload, or leaves a partially-upgraded Operator schema.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The metadata records a claimed cloud creation and its account/receipts (config.rs:883-999); losing it abandons an in-flight paid resource, so durable-state integrity at C=3.","Byte-exact metadata equality (config.rs:979-995), payload byte equality (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:996-999) and the version gate before/after upgrade (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:970-976) reject normalization, truncation or premature migration across four legacy layouts.",Unique boundary for the cloud_creations table across schemas 23-26; the sibling schema tests target delegations/registry tables instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212.,Hand-built legacy SQLite databases and real private files upgraded by production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Four-version loop with byte-preservation assertions; no equivalent protection.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eight_upgrade_preserves_delegation_authority_and_evidence|default""]",four temp databases with hand-written legacy rows and files,0.061,0.061,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2374 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amigrate_copies_legacy_db_and_tasks_once_without_deleting|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::migrate_copies_legacy_db_and_tasks_once_without_deleting,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,728,750,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:142-189""]","migrate_instance_layout copies the legacy database bytes to registry.sqlite3 and config.tasks to tasks/, keeps both legacy originals, and a second pass with changed legacy bytes is a no-op.","A migration that moves instead of copies, overwrites a modern database from stale legacy bytes, or re-runs and replaces already-migrated storage.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"This is the upgrade path for an existing instance's projects and task state (config.rs:142-189); deleting or overwriting the legacy source loses the user's durable work, so C=3.","Byte equality of the copied database (config.rs:738), presence of both originals (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:740-744), and the second-pass no-op with a changed legacy file (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:747-749) are precise positive and negative state assertions.",The only test of the legacy-layout copy; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afresh_home_uses_registry_sqlite3_not_legacy_siblings|default covers the fresh-install layout instead. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:716-725.,Real temp directories and files through migrate_instance_layout (config.rs:142-189); the filesystem layout is exactly the subject (F=4).,high,keep,Assertions preserve the legacy source and prove idempotence; no equivalent coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Afresh_home_uses_registry_sqlite3_not_legacy_siblings|default""]",temp directories plus file copies,0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2375 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Anewer_schema_refusal_preserves_delegation_metadata_and_private_evidence|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::newer_schema_refusal_preserves_delegation_metadata_and_private_evidence,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1395,1443,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:463-503"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237""]","A database one schema newer than this build makes both load_registry and initialize_registry fail with 'incompatible registry database', leaves user_version at the newer value, and preserves the delegation metadata and private evidence bytes.","A downgrade path that opens a newer database, rewrites its schema to the older version, or migrates/replaces it — destroying data written by a newer build.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Refusing a newer schema is what prevents an older binary from corrupting a newer build's durable authority (config.rs:463-503); a silent downgrade is irreversible loss, C=3.","Both entry points must error with the exact incompatibility text (config.rs:1415-1426), and the version plus metadata plus evidence bytes are re-read unchanged (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1427-1442), a decisive negative invariant.",Only test of the newer-schema refusal branch; the schema-23..26 tests cover upgrades upward. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:463-503.,Real SQLite file at SCHEMA_VERSION+1 through both production entry points (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.,high,keep,Protects the data of newer builds from an older binary; no equivalent assertion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_cloud_authority_survives_offline_read_and_upgrade|default""]",temp dir plus SQLite pragma bump,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2376 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoffline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::offline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,813,880,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:205-212"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:595-642"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:505-511""]","A read-only load of a schema-5 database whose workspaces table has `name` reads that column as the workspace id, reports no git_identity and setup_pending=false, and leaves user_version 5 and the `name` column untouched.","An offline read that migrates (or assumes the modern `id`/`git_identity` columns), which would either fail inspection or alter a database owned by a running server.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The read-only path inspects another process's live registry (config.rs:204-212); mutating it offline can corrupt the running server's durable state, so C=3.","Assertions pin id, branch, the two absent columns' defaults, user_version 5 and the still-present `name` column (config.rs:867-879), rejecting both wrong decoding and any migration.",Only test of the read-only/no-migrate mode; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_migrates_id_and_assigns_git_identity|default covers the writable upgrade of the same schema. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1446-1557.,"Real SQLite database built with the legacy schema on disk, read through production load_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:505-511.",high,keep,Precise assertions that offline inspection never writes.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_migrates_id_and_assigns_git_identity|default""]","temp dir, hand-built SQLite schema, read-only open",0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2377 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eight_upgrade_preserves_delegation_authority_and_evidence|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_eight_upgrade_preserves_delegation_authority_and_evidence,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1004,1064,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:463-503""]","Upgrading a schema-8 database preserves the delegation_instance id and the raw delegation metadata (including an Unknown receipt) exactly, keeps three immutable evidence files, and a second initialize does not duplicate or recreate delegation rows.","An upgrade that regenerates the instance identity, normalizes unknown receipt outcomes out of the metadata, or appends duplicate rows when reopened.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Delegation metadata carries authority and receipts for a running workflow (config.rs:1004-1063); changing it silently changes who may act, so wrong ownership/durable state at C=3.","The instance id equality (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1032-1038), raw metadata equality (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1039-1048), three evidence-file byte checks (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1049-1054) and the reopen row count (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1055-1063) are exact positive and negative assertions.",The schema-8 identity/evidence boundary is covered only here; later schema tests seed higher versions and different tables. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.,Real SQLite upgrade through production initialize_registry with on-disk evidence (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:463-503.,high,keep,Direct byte and identity preservation over the real migration path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Alegacy_cloud_authority_survives_offline_read_and_upgrade|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, hand-inserted row and evidence files",0.063,0.063,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2382 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_native_proof_policy_and_dependency_bytes|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_native_proof_policy_and_dependency_bytes,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1291,1337,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-18 database preserves the native model request/resolution/profile/binary digest, native policy recipe/settings/mcp, dependency witnesses, review base and an Unknown receipt byte-for-byte, plus four native evidence files.","An upgrade that drops or rewrites native policy/digest metadata or the private native evidence, making a later native proof unattributable.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Native model digests and policy bytes are the proof that a delegated run used the attested native binary (config.rs:1291-1336); rewriting them destroys proof, so C=3.","One exact metadata string comparison (config.rs:1322-1330) and four file byte checks (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1331-1336) after the version gate (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1318-1321) reject normalization, truncation or file loss.",The native-proof columns of schema 18 are covered only here; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_original_review_records_and_private_bytes|default covers the review-record columns at the same version. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1340-1392.,Real SQLite row and files through production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Exact preservation of the native proof boundary; distinct from the review-record test at the same schema.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_original_review_records_and_private_bytes|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, hand-inserted row and four native evidence files",0.052,0.052,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2381 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_original_review_records_and_private_bytes|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_original_review_records_and_private_bytes,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1340,1392,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-18 database preserves the review rounds/repairs metadata and previous_versions contract digest exactly, plus five immutable review evidence files.","An upgrade that rewrites review rounds or discards the old round/candidate/acceptance files, losing the audit trail behind an acceptance decision.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Review rounds and their immutable files are the audit trail for accepting a candidate (config.rs:1340-1391); losing them removes the evidence a human or parent reviews, so C=3.",Exact metadata equality (config.rs:1370-1379) and five file byte checks (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1380-1391) after the version gate (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1361-1367) reject any rewrite or deletion.,Same schema version as nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_native_proof_policy_and_dependency_bytes|default but a different record family (review rounds/repairs versus native policy); both are needed because the migration touches distinct columns and files. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1291-1337.,Real SQLite row and files through production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Distinct record family at the same schema; preservation is asserted byte-exactly.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_native_proof_policy_and_dependency_bytes|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, hand-inserted row and five evidence files",0.042,0.042,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2384 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eleven_upgrade_keeps_question_intents_and_unknown_answer_receipts_exact|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_eleven_upgrade_keeps_question_intents_and_unknown_answer_receipts_exact,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1067,1095,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-11 database leaves the delegation metadata — question intents with handled=false and answer receipts with outcome Unknown — byte-identical, and the offline read leaves version 11.","A migration that drops questions or answer obligations it cannot interpret, or that rewrites Unknown outcomes into a normalized form.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Question/answer receipts encode whether a child may still be answered (config.rs:1067-1094); dropping them loses obligation state and can silently orphan a waiting child, so C=3.",Byte equality of the exact metadata string (config.rs:1091-1094) after the version gate (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1080-1082) rejects any normalization or drop.,The unanswered-question boundary of schema 11 is unique; the schema-15 test covers coding deliveries and archive receipts instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.,Real SQLite row inserted and upgraded through production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,One exact byte-preservation invariant on the real migration.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_fifteen_upgrade_preserves_coding_delivery_and_uncertain_receipts|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, hand-inserted row",0.035,0.035,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2383 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_fifteen_upgrade_preserves_coding_delivery_and_uncertain_receipts|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_fifteen_upgrade_preserves_coding_delivery_and_uncertain_receipts,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1098,1168,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-15 database preserves the delegation metadata (coding base/generation, obligation revision, StopUnknown archive receipt) and the delegation_workflows delivery metadata, plus five immutable evidence files.","An upgrade that rewrites coding delivery or workflow delivery metadata, or deletes the accepted coding evidence while adding the newer schema.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Coding delivery and acceptance evidence decide whether a delegated coding result is accepted (config.rs:1098-1167); losing it destroys review provenance, so C=3.",Two byte-exact metadata comparisons (config.rs:1136-1155) and five file byte checks (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1156-1167) after a version gate (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1128-1134) reject normalization or evidence loss.,The schema-15 coding-delivery boundary is only covered here; the schema-17 test adds dependency witnesses and review publications instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.,Real SQLite with two tables and on-disk evidence upgraded by production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Grounded byte-preservation over the real migration.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_seventeen_upgrade_preserves_dependency_witnesses_and_review_publications|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, two hand-inserted rows and evidence files",0.039,0.039,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2385 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_seventeen_upgrade_preserves_dependency_witnesses_and_review_publications|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_seventeen_upgrade_preserves_dependency_witnesses_and_review_publications,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1219,1288,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-17 database preserves delegation dependency witnesses/acceptance metadata and delegation_workflows dependency edges, plus the input baseline, review submission and acceptance files byte-for-byte.","An upgrade that drops dependency edges or witnesses, which would let a successor start without its predecessor's accepted input.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Dependency witnesses gate successor execution (config.rs:1219-1287); losing them means work can be published against a missing predecessor, so durable-state/ownership at C=3.",Two byte-exact metadata comparisons (config.rs:1262-1281) and three file byte checks (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1282-1287) after the version gate (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1254-1260) reject dropped edges or rewritten evidence.,"Dependency witness preservation is unique to this schema; sibling tests cover cloud, coding and review records. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.",Real SQLite rows and files through production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Direct preservation assertions on the dependency boundary.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_fifteen_upgrade_preserves_coding_delivery_and_uncertain_receipts|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, two hand-inserted rows and evidence files",0.038,0.038,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2386 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 