nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_sixteen_upgrade_preserves_typed_fallback_and_immutable_history|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::schema_sixteen_upgrade_preserves_typed_fallback_and_immutable_history,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1171,1216,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","Upgrading a schema-16 database preserves the typed ParentRecovery acceptance target, previous_versions history, captures and recoveries metadata, plus the legacy acceptance-v1, typed acceptance-v2 and parent-fallback-r2-v2 files byte-for-byte.","An upgrade that rewrites the typed fallback target or replaces a versioned acceptance file, breaking the immutable history a parent relies on after a lost reply.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Parent recovery decisions are immutable publication history (config.rs:1171-1215); rewriting them changes which child result is authoritative, so durable-state/ownership at C=3.",Exact metadata equality (config.rs:1200-1209) and byte equality for three versioned files (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1210-1215) after the version gate reject normalization and file replacement.,Only test of the typed ParentRecovery fallback publication; the schema-18 review-record test uses different metadata and files. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:233-237.,Real SQLite row and files through production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Exact history-preservation assertions on the migration path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aschema_eighteen_upgrade_preserves_original_review_records_and_private_bytes|default""]","temp dir, SQLite pragma downgrade, hand-inserted row and three evidence files",0.031,0.031,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2387 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_inaccessible_path_does_not_commit_null_identity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::writable_v5_inaccessible_path_does_not_commit_null_identity,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1683,1717,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:543-570"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","An existing workspace whose parent directory is mode 000 makes initialize_registry fail and leaves user_version 5, rather than treating the inaccessible path as missing and committing a null identity.","Classifying PermissionDenied as NotFound, which would commit a null git identity for a workspace that is actually present but temporarily unreadable.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Confusing an unreadable checkout with a deleted one permanently drops its generation marker (config.rs:543-570), threatening later ownership decisions on the user's worktree — C=3.",The failure plus `schema_version == 5` (config.rs:1711-1716) rejects the specific EACCES-as-missing defect; the permissions are restored before the assertion so it is deterministic.,"Distinct failure mode from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_rolls_back_present_identity_failure_then_retries|default: that test hides .git (identity capture fails), this one makes symlink_metadata itself fail. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1649-1680.","Real directory permissions and SQLite, production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.",high,keep,Precisely targets the error-kind classification that would corrupt identity state.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_rolls_back_present_identity_failure_then_retries|default""]","temp dir, chmod 000, SQLite open",0.118,0.118,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2388 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_migrates_id_and_assigns_git_identity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::writable_v5_migrates_id_and_assigns_git_identity,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1446,1557,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:513-593"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","A writable open of a schema-5 registry renames workspaces.name to id, assigns the present checkout's git identity, leaves a missing checkout with no identity and setup_pending=false, and leaves user_version at the current schema with no name column.","An upgrade that fails to rename the column, assigns an identity to a vanished checkout, or marks an archived workspace setup_pending.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"git_identity is the generation marker that decides whether a worktree still belongs to this instance (config.rs:513-593); a wrong or missing marker causes wrong-ownership operations on the user's checkout, C=3.","The root identity is compared against production git::worktree_identity (config.rs:1537-1541), the archived row must have None and setup_pending false (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1542-1549), and the schema rename is asserted both ways (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1550-1556).",The writable v5 upgrade boundary; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoffline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating|default asserts the read-only counterpart. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:813-880.,Real git repository and SQLite database migrated by production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.,high,keep,Identity assignment and schema rename are both asserted on the real migration.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoffline_v5_reads_name_as_id_without_migrating|default""]","temp git repository, SQLite schema 5 seeded by hand",0.142,0.142,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2389 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_recovers_missing_worktree_identity_from_admin_metadata|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::writable_v5_recovers_missing_worktree_identity_from_admin_metadata,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1720,1773,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:557-564"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:183-240""]","When a registered worktree's directory is gone but its Git admin metadata survives, initialize_registry recovers the identity from that metadata and commits it with the current schema.",Leaving a surviving worktree without a generation marker (or failing the whole upgrade) when only the checkout directory is missing.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The recovery marker is what allows the user to later restore or remove the worktree correctly (config.rs:557-564); losing it breaks ownership of the surviving admin entry, C=3.","The recovered value is compared with production recover_worktree_identity and asserted Some (config.rs:1766-1771), plus the final schema version (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1772), rejecting both a wrong digest and a null fallback.","The recovery branch (directory missing, admin present) is unique; the other v5 tests cover present, hidden and inaccessible paths. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:557-564.",Real git worktree whose directory is removed while .git/worktrees metadata remains; production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs. The recovery helper exercised is crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:198-240.,high,keep,Directly exercises the recovery fallback and its exact digest.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_unavailable_repository_defers_migration_until_it_returns|default""]","temp git repo with an added worktree, then remove_dir_all",0.181,0.181,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2392 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_rolls_back_present_identity_failure_then_retries|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::writable_v5_rolls_back_present_identity_failure_then_retries,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1649,1680,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:513-593"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","With the checkout's .git hidden, initialize_registry fails and leaves user_version 5; after .git returns the retry commits the upgrade and records the real worktree identity.","A migration that commits a null identity when capture fails (or partially migrates), and a retry path that cannot recover after the transient failure.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A committed null identity would leave the workspace without a generation marker, so later operations cannot tell whether the checkout is the one this instance owns (config.rs:513-593) — durable-state/ownership at C=3.","`failed.is_err()` plus `schema_version == 5` (config.rs:1667-1672) prove rollback, and the retry asserts the exact worktree identity and final schema (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1674-1679) — a decisive transition invariant.",The rollback-and-retry branch is unique; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_inaccessible_path_does_not_commit_null_identity|default covers a different failure (permission denied) that must also not be read as missing. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1683-1717.,"Real git repo with .git temporarily renamed, real SQLite, production initialize_registry (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.",high,keep,Transactional rollback and retry are both observed on real storage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_inaccessible_path_does_not_commit_null_identity|default""]","temp git repository, directory rename, SQLite open",0.126,0.126,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2391 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_unavailable_repository_defers_migration_until_it_returns|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,config::tests::writable_v5_unavailable_repository_defers_migration_until_it_returns,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs,1776,1823,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:543-570"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441""]","With the repository volume renamed away, initialize_registry fails and leaves user_version 5; after the volume returns the migration succeeds, preserves the branch, and the restored worktree remains removable.","Migrating (or half-migrating) while the repository is unavailable, and a retry that cannot use the restored checkout — either of which strands the workspace.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A non-retryable migration failure on an unmounted volume would leave the user's workspaces unmanageable (config.rs:543-570), so deferral is durable-state integrity at C=3.","The failed attempt keeps version 5 (config.rs:1808-1812), then the retry asserts branch feature/work and that git::remove_worktree succeeds (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:1813-1822) — a complete failure-then-recovery transition.",The unavailable-volume failure mode is unique among the v5 tests; the others fail identity capture or path inspection. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:543-570.,"Real git repository on a renamed volume path, production initialize_registry and remove_worktree (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/config.rs:265-441.",high,keep,Proves the migration is retryable and the restored checkout is usable.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|config%3A%3Atests%3A%3Awritable_v5_recovers_missing_worktree_identity_from_admin_metadata|default""]","temp git repo, volume directory renamed and restored",0.273,0.273,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2398 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Abaseline%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acomplete_inherited_untracked_bytes_do_not_expand_successor_write_authority|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,git::candidate::baseline::tests::complete_inherited_untracked_bytes_do_not_expand_successor_write_authority,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/baseline.rs,323,367,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/baseline.rs:46-120""]","A successor candidate validates against an input baseline when it carries the inherited file unchanged plus its own file; changing the inherited bytes or removing the entry fails, and declaring the inherited path in the successor's own scope makes it valid again.","Letting a successor rewrite inherited input bytes or omit them while still presenting itself as based on the baseline, or silently widening its write authority to inherited paths.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The baseline pins what a successor inherited versus what it may write (baseline.rs:46-120); a changed inherited file breaks provenance for the dependency chain, wrong authority/durable state at C=3.","One accept, a changed-bytes reject, a removed-entry reject and a scope-widened accept (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/baseline.rs:345-366) pin both the invariant and its exact relaxation.",The only test of InputBaseline::validate_candidate in this shard; no sibling asserts the inherited-versus-owned split. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/baseline.rs:46-120.,Direct call to production validate_candidate with protocol-shaped values (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/baseline.rs:46-120.,high,keep,Precise accept/reject pairs around inherited bytes.,[],JSON value construction only,0.029,0.029,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2397 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aexact_context_is_explicit_complete_bounded_and_never_reads_mutable_checkout|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::candidate::review::tests::exact_context_is_explicit_complete_bounded_and_never_reads_mutable_checkout,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs,164,202,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:4-85""]","context reads caller and a symlink at the committed base (original bytes and target), refuses a missing path, a binary file, an unsafe symlink, .git/config, two files exceeding MAX_BYTES, 33 paths, and the non-oid 'HEAD', and leaves the mutable checkout's unstaged content unchanged.","Reading the mutable checkout instead of the base (reviewing content that is not in the candidate), following an unsafe link, or reading unbounded data for a review request.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The exact-context read is the reviewer's evidence (review.rs:4-85); returning mutable or out-of-scope bytes makes the review decision apply to the wrong content, integrity at C=3.","Two exact content results and six independent refusals plus the unchanged-checkout assertion (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:183-201) cover the base read, the bounds and the no-mutation rule.","Distinct from nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areadable_review_images_preserve_committed_staged_unstaged_untracked_deletion_modes_and_link|default: this covers explicit bounded path selection at a base, that one covers the full image set per change class. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:91-161.",Real Git repository with staged/unstaged edits at a fixed base through production context (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:4-85.,high,keep,Bounds and base-vs-mutable separation are both asserted on real git state.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areadable_review_images_preserve_committed_staged_unstaged_untracked_deletion_modes_and_link|default""]",git repo with commits and staged/unstaged edits,0.431,0.431,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2399 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,independent-storage-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acapture_includes_mode_only_change_under_core_filemode_false_without_config_mutation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::candidate::tests::capture_includes_mode_only_change_under_core_filemode_false_without_config_mutation,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs,665,703,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505""]","With core.filemode=false and README chmod 755, `git diff --name-only` reports nothing (fixture premise), yet capture records README with base_mode 0o100644, mode 0o100755 and identical bytes, and the worktree's core.filemode remains false afterwards.","Relying on git diff for mode-only changes (dropping the executable bit from the candidate), or fixing detection by rewriting the user's repository configuration.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"A dropped mode change publishes a candidate that differs from the worktree (git/candidate.rs:408-505), and mutating core.filemode changes the user's durable repository config; both are integrity issues at C=3.","The fixture proves git hides the change (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:678-684), then the exact mode pair, byte equality and unchanged config (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:687-702) reject both omission and config mutation.",The mode-only hidden-change case is unique; the index-flag test covers --assume-unchanged/--skip-worktree instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505.,Real Git worktree from capture_fixture with real chmod and production capture (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505.,high,keep,Pins both the captured mode and the absence of a config side effect.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acapture_refuses_index_flags_that_hide_tracked_edits|default""]","creates a git repo and worktree, chmod, capture",0.455,0.455,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2400 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acapture_refuses_index_flags_that_hide_tracked_edits|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::candidate::tests::capture_refuses_index_flags_that_hide_tracked_edits,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs,706,726,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505""]","For both --assume-unchanged and --skip-worktree, a tracked README edit is hidden from `git diff --name-only` (fixture premise) and capture fails with an error containing 'assume-unchanged or skip-worktree'.","Capturing a snapshot that silently omits a tracked edit hidden by an index flag, so the published candidate lacks the real change.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"An omitted tracked edit means the reviewer approves a candidate that does not contain the worktree's change (git/candidate.rs:408-505), durable-state/work-integrity at C=3.","Both flags are exercised, each with the hiding premise and an exact error substring (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:706-725), so a detector that trusts git diff fails.",Index-flag hiding is distinct from the mode-only and submodule hiding mechanisms covered by siblings. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505.,Real Git worktree with update-index flags through production capture (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-505.,high,keep,Two flag variants with the premise and refusal asserted.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asubmodule_changes_cannot_be_hidden_by_repository_diff_settings|default""]","creates a git repo and worktree, update-index, capture",0.486,0.486,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2410 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aimmutable_manifest_rejects_tampering_duplicates_modes_and_scope|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,git::candidate::tests::immutable_manifest_rejects_tampering_duplicates_modes_and_scope,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs,550,587,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:75-135""]","A well-formed candidate snapshot validates; changing content after the digest, duplicating a path, setting mode 0, validating against another scope, or replacing the base oid with a branch name each make validate fail.","Accepting a manifest whose bytes no longer match the recorded digest, whose paths repeat, or whose base is not an object id — i.e. publishing bytes different from the reviewed ones.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"CandidateSnapshot::validate is the immutability check on the bytes a reviewer approved (git/candidate.rs:75-135); accepting a tampered manifest defeats review and publishes different code, so integrity at C=3.","Five independent mutations are asserted against one accepted baseline (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:550-586), each targeting a distinct field (content digest, duplicate path, mode, scope, base oid).","The only manifest-integrity test; the review-image test covers how the images are built, not tamper rejection. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:75-135.",Direct call to production CandidateSnapshot::validate (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:75-135.,high,keep,Distinct tamper cases each with their own expected failure.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areadable_review_images_preserve_committed_staged_unstaged_untracked_deletion_modes_and_link|default""]",JSON struct construction only,0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2402 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ascope_rejects_traversal_and_prefix_confusion|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,unit,git::candidate::tests::scope_rejects_traversal_and_prefix_confusion,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs,516,532,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:136-169""]","validate_scope refuses empty, absolute, parent-traversal, doubled-slash, dot-segment and newline paths, allows '.', and `allowed` admits src/main.rs for scope src while refusing src-private/key.","A scope check that treats 'src-private' as inside 'src' or lets ../, an absolute path or a newline through, so a candidate can collect or write outside its declared paths.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The scope decides which paths a delegated candidate may capture and publish (git/candidate.rs:136-169); a bypass reaches files outside the assignment's authority, so wrong-scope access at C=3.","Seven invalid paths plus the prefix-confusion pair and the '.' case (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:516-531) reject traversal, absolute paths and prefix matching by name; a scope containing only whitespace is not covered.",The only test of path-scope validation; nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aprivate_paths_and_unsafe_git_paths_are_refused|default tests the separate private-file filter and NUL-separated path parser. Counterpart assertions: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:534-548.,Direct calls to production validate_scope and allowed (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:136-169.,high,keep,Exact positive and negative scope boundaries including prefix confusion.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aprivate_paths_and_unsafe_git_paths_are_refused|default""]",string computation only,0.013,0.013,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2404 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Asubmodule_changes_cannot_be_hidden_by_repository_diff_settings|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::candidate::tests::submodule_changes_cannot_be_hidden_by_repository_diff_settings,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs,589,622,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:247-269"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-461""]","With diff.ignoreSubmodules=all, a child-repository edit is invisible to `git diff --name-only` (asserted as the fixture premise) but changed_paths still reports 'nested' and scan refuses a base containing submodules with 'refuses base submodules'.","Trusting the repository's diff settings for change detection, so a submodule edit is silently omitted or a snapshot is produced from a base with submodules.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"An omitted submodule change means the published candidate differs from the reviewed worktree (git/candidate.rs:247-269); losing a child repository's change is missing work, C=3.","The test first proves the setting hides the edit, then asserts changed_paths returns {nested} and scan errors with the exact reason (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:607-621) — the premise and both outcomes are pinned.",The only submodule-boundary test; the mode-only and index-flag tests cover other hidden-change mechanisms. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:247-269.,"Real Git repository with a nested clone and a modified diff setting, production changed_paths/scan (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:408-461.",high,keep,Distinguishes the repository's view from the trusted change detector.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Atests%3A%3Acapture_includes_mode_only_change_under_core_filemode_false_without_config_mutation|default""]",creates a git repo and a nested clone,0.353,0.353,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2414 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Adiagnostics%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aprivate_file_noclobber_and_invalid_scope_remain_unqualified|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::diagnostics::tests::private_file_noclobber_and_invalid_scope_remain_unqualified,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs,250,268,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:47-99""]","The journal file is mode 0600, a second Journal::open in the same directory fails and leaves the bytes unchanged, a 0755 directory is refused, an invalid run name containing .. is refused, and no journal file is created in that directory.","Clobbering another run's evidence, creating the journal in a world-readable directory, or accepting a traversal-shaped run identifier that writes outside the directory.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The journal records process evidence and private command data (diagnostics.rs:47-99); clobbering it or exposing it in a 0755 directory defeats the evidence/privacy boundary, C=3.","Exact 0600 mode, byte-identical file after the refused open, refused 0755 directory, and the absence of a file for the invalid run (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs:256-267) cover each boundary.",The only no-clobber/scope test for the journal; sibling tests cover content and seal health. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:47-99.,Real directories and file modes with production Journal::open (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:47-99.,high,keep,Asserts both the refusal and the absence of side effects.,[],"temp dirs, chmod, file reads",0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2409 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Adiagnostics%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aspawn_and_wait_failure_never_create_success_or_expose_error_body|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::diagnostics::tests::spawn_and_wait_failure_never_create_success_or_expose_error_body,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs,222,247,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:263-307"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:100-198""]","A missing program propagates NotFound and records a spawn_error row; an injected wait error records original_wait=false, pipes_drained=false and a failed seal; neither the program path nor the wait error body appears in the journal.","Recording an error as a successful wait, or writing the private program path/error message into diagnostic evidence.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The journal is durable diagnostic evidence that may be attached to a report; leaking a private path/error body there is a bounded privacy exposure (C=3), and a false success is integrity-relevant. Protected path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:263-307.","It asserts the io error kind, the spawn_error and non-original wait rows, failed=true, and two forbidden strings in the raw file (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs:232-246).",The only test of the spawn/wait failure rows; the redaction test covers argv/env/stderr values on successful runs. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:263-307.,"A real missing executable and the real Journal state machine, with a classification-only wait error (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:100-198.",high,keep,Covers failure evidence and its redaction; complements the success-path redaction test.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Adiagnostics%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aoutput_stdin_eof_nonzero_signal_status_and_private_content_are_preserved|default""]","attempted spawn of a missing path, journal writes",0.079,0.079,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2411 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Adiagnostics%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aterminal_health_rejects_pending_unavailable_late_and_duplicate_finish|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::diagnostics::tests::terminal_health_rejects_pending_unavailable_late_and_duplicate_finish,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs,345,372,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:199-262"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:32-46""]","finish_diagnostics succeeds once and fails on a duplicate finish, fails with a pending call, fails for an unavailable journal, and after a healthy seal plus a write failure begin() returns None and finish fails while the healthy seal row still says failed=false.","Qualifying a run twice, qualifying with a call still pending, or claiming a terminal seal when the journal never wrote one.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"These are the terminal-health rules for accepting a run's evidence (diagnostics.rs:199-262); a false qualification fabricates a completed proof, integrity at C=3.","Four independent health states each with the expected finish result, plus the late-write-failure case asserting begin None and the unchanged healthy row (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics/tests.rs:345-371).",The only test of the terminal health matrix; the sync-failure test covers the write path. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:199-262.,Real journals and the production health state machine (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/diagnostics.rs:32-46.,high,keep,All four rejection states are asserted directly.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Adiagnostics%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aterminal_sync_failure_cannot_qualify_healthy_seal_bytes|default""]","four journals, one unavailable state",0.033,0.033,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2412 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
