nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aadmit_fences_gaps_retired_producers_and_an_unobserved_replacement|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,report::reporter::tests::admit_fences_gaps_retired_producers_and_an_unobserved_replacement,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,47,75,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:817-857""]","The producer fence accepts only an announcing frame for an unknown instance, ignores duplicates and lower sequences, reports a hole once and then accepts the next frame, reports an unobserved replacement as LostClose and retires the old instance, and never re-admits a retired A however high its sequence.","Accepting a stale, replayed or retired producer's frames, or admitting an unknown instance without a session_start.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Producer fencing decides which provider process may mutate session reporting; a wrong accept mixes generations and resurrects a retired producer (wrong ownership, 3).",src/report/reporter/tests.rs:47-75 drives a nine-step sequence asserting every Fence outcome including gap-then-accept and A-to-B-to-A rejection.,Only end-to-end fence sequence; the retire() row covers the explicit retirement call.,Direct production Reporter state machine.,high,keep,Core fence sequence; the explicit-retire row depends on this contract being right.,[],pure state transitions,0.022,0.022,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:662 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Athe_identity_budget_answers_duplicates_before_capacity|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,report::reporter::tests::the_identity_budget_answers_duplicates_before_capacity,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,96,125,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:859-915""]","A fresh cycle identity is charged and published, its repeat is Ignored even with zero capacity left, and a new identity with the budget exhausted returns UNAVAILABLE, closes the reporter, and leaves the already-published identity set unchanged.",Charging capacity before the duplicate check (so a repeat can exhaust the budget and disable a healthy reporter) or evicting published identities to make room.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Identity exhaustion disables reporting; a duplicate-triggered disable loses reporting for a healthy session, and eviction loses duplicate detection (3).","src/report/reporter/tests.rs:96-125 asserts the duplicate path with charged set to the limit, closure on the next identity, and exact cycles-set equality.",Only duplicate-before-capacity test.,Direct production Reporter budget logic.,high,keep,Protects a healthy reporter from being disabled by replays.,[],pure state transitions,0.025,0.025,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:671 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Areporter%3A%3Atests%3A%3Athe_identity_budget_counts_fences_and_cycles_against_one_ceiling|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,report::reporter::tests::the_identity_budget_counts_fences_and_cycles_against_one_ceiling,default,src/report/reporter/tests.rs,128,164,"[""src/report/reporter.rs:859-915""]","MAX_IDENTITIES-1 cycles are admitted, a producer fence takes the final slot, and the next cycle is UNAVAILABLE with the retained set unchanged; separately, identities sized to cross MAX_IDENTITY_BYTES trigger UNAVAILABLE at the computed byte boundary and the charged total never exceeds the ceiling.",Two separate ceilings (fences and cycles counted independently) or byte accounting that lets retained strings exceed the declared memory bound.,3,4,3,4,75,90,84,The shared ceiling bounds reporter memory against unbounded provider strings; a split or leaking ceiling allows unbounded growth (3).,"src/report/reporter/tests.rs:128-164 computes the byte boundary independently from string sizes rather than setting the counter, and asserts exact set equality after exhaustion.",Only test of the shared fence-and-cycle ceiling and the byte accounting.,Direct production budget logic.,high,keep,Only evidence for the single shared ceiling that the duplicate test assumes.,[],pure state transitions up to the identity and byte ceilings,0.598,0.598,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:679 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,independent-report-check-2
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_continuation_records.mjs|malformed%20or%20overflowing%20pointers%20report%20a%20gap%20without%20contacting%20control|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,node,unit,malformed or overflowing pointers report a gap without contacting control,default,tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs,43,52,"[""src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:1-99"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:240-255""]","A stored pointer with an extra field is rejected before any Recover, leaving a Malformed gap; validatePointer also throws for version above MAX_SAFE_INTEGER and for a truncated digest.","If validatePointer accepted extra or out-of-range fields, a hand-edited or truncated transcription of a pointer could be treated as authority and recover a workflow from invented data.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"The pointer is the only durable claim of workflow ownership; accepting a malformed one can resume a workflow from a corrupted record (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:4-7, 15-23).",It asserts the no-contact gap on the integration path and two direct validatePointer throws for the exact bounds (tests/pi_continuation_records.mjs:43-52).,"The exact-key-set and numeric/digest bounds are asserted only here; no other test feeds a malformed pointer; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:4-7, which no other reviewed case exercises.","validatePointer is a pure production function called directly, and restore() runs unmodified with a fake call that must not be reached (src/ovrcr-delegation-continuation.mjs:4-7, 15-23).",high,keep,Direct boundary coverage of the pointer validator plus its no-contact consequence; keep.,[],0.000329875s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.000329875,0.000329875,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 0.329875 at macOS-job.log:3885; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Installed%20Pi%20package%20through%20production%20materialization|tests%2Fpi_package_installed.mjs|installed%20package%20plus%20real%20injected%20entry%20keeps%20one%20runtime%20registration%20owner%20across%20reload|production,cargo-test|Installed%20Pi%20package%20through%20production%20materialization|ovrcr%3A%3Alib|production_materializer_loads_local_package_with_one_injected_owner|production,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Installed Pi package through production materialization,node-test,tests/pi_package_installed.mjs,node,acceptance,installed package plus real injected entry keeps one runtime registration owner across reload,production,tests/pi_package_installed.mjs,74,148,"[""pi/extension.ts:1-6"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-77"", ""pi/skills/ovrcr-orchestrator/SKILL.md:1-62""]","With the package and a production-materialized injected entry both loaded, exactly two extensions are discovered and exactly one owns ovrcr-reattach, ovrcr_start, ovrcr_dependencies, ovrcr_review and the agent_settled handler; the package contributes only a single session_start diagnostic; the installed SDK's validateToolArguments accepts valid start/review payloads and rejects mixed handle+new, bad actions and over-limit context; after a reload the retired tool rejects and one owner remains.","If the package entry also registered the runtime, one session would have two reporters and two tool sets, so events and results would be duplicated and the retired tool could still act; a schema the installed validator rejects would break delegation entirely.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,"Two runtime owners for one session duplicate reporting and control; the single-owner assertion is what keeps the package diagnostic-only (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-77, pi/extension.ts:1-6).","It asserts per-tool and per-handler owner counts (one), the diagnostic-only package handler, the installed SDK's accept/reject results for six payloads, and the post-reload retirement (tests/pi_package_installed.mjs:74-148).","The child-tools row asserts the catalog; this row asserts the single-owner and installed-validator contract, which no other test covers; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-77, which no other reviewed case exercises.","It uses the installed SDK's resource loader and its own validateToolArguments, plus a real materialized entry from the production materializer (tests/pi_package_installed.mjs:16-24, 90-96).",high,keep,Decisive single-owner and installed-validator coverage; keep.,[],0.106s reported for this case; nested case whose runtime is included in the parent's reported duration (timing_source is the parent's TAP output),0.106,0.106,1,0,hosted-single-run,nested TAP duration_ms 106.068458 at macOS-job.log:4404 inside parent 'production_materializer_loads_local_package_with_one_injected_owner' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Installed Pi package through production materialization'),extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Installed%20Pi%20package%20through%20production%20materialization|tests%2Fpi_package_installed.mjs|local%20installed%20package%20discovers%20one%20valid%20promoted%20skill%20and%20confined%20links|production,cargo-test|Installed%20Pi%20package%20through%20production%20materialization|ovrcr%3A%3Alib|production_materializer_loads_local_package_with_one_injected_owner|production,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Installed Pi package through production materialization,node-test,tests/pi_package_installed.mjs,node,acceptance,local installed package discovers one valid promoted skill and confined links,production,tests/pi_package_installed.mjs,46,72,"[""pi/extension.ts:1-6"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:69-77"", ""pi/skills/ovrcr-orchestrator/SKILL.md:1-62""]","A real package install of the repository discovers exactly one skill (ovrcr-orchestrator) with model invocation enabled, its baseDir resolves to pi/skills/ovrcr-orchestrator, every relative markdown link in SKILL.md and the four references stays inside the repository, settings are persisted, exactly one package is configured, and removal leaves no skills.","If link confinement were lost, the skill could instruct the model to read a file outside the package (an injection surface); if the install discovered extra skills or persisted extra settings, an unrelated profile would be promoted into every session.",3,4,3,4,75,90,84,The promoted skill is instruction content loaded into the model's context; an escaping link or an extra discovered skill changes what the agent is told to do (pi/skills/ovrcr-orchestrator/SKILL.md:1-62).,"It asserts the single skill name, its baseDir realpath, every relative link target's containment, the diagnostics list, the persisted package list and the post-removal emptiness (tests/pi_package_installed.mjs:46-72).","No other test installs the package and inspects link confinement; the bootstrap rows only diagnose metadata; the handler it drives is pi/skills/ovrcr-orchestrator/SKILL.md:1-62, which no other reviewed case exercises.",It runs the real DefaultPackageManager.installAndPersist and DefaultResourceLoader against the installed Pi 0.87.1 SDK and the real repository tree (tests/pi_package_installed.mjs:25-45).,high,keep,Only coverage of the packaged skill promotion and link confinement; keep.,[],1.233s reported for this case; nested case whose runtime is included in the parent's reported duration (timing_source is the parent's TAP output),1.233,1.233,1,0,hosted-single-run,nested TAP duration_ms 1233.015542 at macOS-job.log:4398 inside parent 'production_materializer_loads_local_package_with_one_injected_owner' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Installed Pi package through production materialization'),extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
