nextest|Test|ovrcr-protocol|wire%3A%3Awire_snapshot%3A%3Ainitial_prompt_wire_debug_redacts_prompt_text|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-protocol,lib,unit,wire::wire_snapshot::initial_prompt_wire_debug_redacts_prompt_text,default,crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/wire.rs,1029,1055,"[""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/wire.rs:349-363""]","The Debug rendering of Request::CreateAgentSessionWithPrompt with prompt ""  keep this\nexactly  "" does not contain the prompt and does contain ""redacted"".",The manual Debug for InitialPromptLaunchRequest printing the private prompt text into logs or diagnostics.,4,3,3,3,100,75,85,"crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/wire.rs:349-363 redacts prompt text; the prompt is private user/agent content, so a leak is a privacy breach.","Absence of the exact prompt and presence of ""redacted""; other launch fields and recovery bytes are not asserted.",Only prompt-redaction Debug test; rows 20 and the snapshot cover behavior and encoding.,Production Debug implementation.,high,keep,C=4 prompt privacy guard.,[],one Debug rendering,0.010,0.010,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2325 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,protocol-terminal-002,independent-protocol-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aquota%3A%3Atests%3A%3Anative_error_reason_is_classified_without_its_body|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,server::quota::tests::native_error_reason_is_classified_without_its_body,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs,1932,2031,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:893-944"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:731-808"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:969-1004""]","Rpc::call classifies JSON-RPC error replies into Unavailable, NotSignedIn and Unsupported with fixed OVRCR reasons, clamps retryAfterSeconds, and reports expired deadlines and missing executables without reading native text.","Echoing the native error message/data (account email and provider text) into the quota reason, mapping 401 to a retryable Unavailable, accepting retryAfterSeconds=0 so the worker spins, or serving a buffered reply past the request deadline.",4,4,2,3,100,75,85,"The reason is shown in the dashboard and event log; the fixture body contains an account email, so a regression is a privacy leak (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:893-944).","Seven error shapes each assert state, exact reason, deterministic flag and retry_after, and every reason is checked free of 'secret' and '@'; timeout and not-found paths are separate assertions (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:1932-2031).","Acceptance tests already assert HTTP 503, unsupported, unrecognized, timeout and missing-executable outcomes through the real server; only the 401 branch and the 5s->60s Retry-After clamp are distinct here (tests/provider_quota.rs:1270-1288).","Real child process and pipe bytes feed the production Rpc::call, but the peer is /bin/cat with a preloaded buffer rather than a native app-server.",high,keep,"Covers branches the acceptance suite leaves out, including the retry clamp and 401 classification.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aprovider_quota|unknown_method_or_unrecognized_reply_not_a_version_is_unsupported|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aprovider_quota|missing_executable_is_not_found_with_next_check_at_the_cap|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aprovider_quota|unrelated_native_messages_cannot_extend_the_account_request_deadline|default""]","[""spawns /bin/cat once per error case"", ""in-memory pipe buffers, no network""]",1.569,1.569,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2634 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-server-session-002,independent-runtime-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Apalette%3A%3Alaunch_tests%3A%3Aclose_confirm_does_not_submit_after_run_replacement|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::palette::launch_tests::close_confirm_does_not_submit_after_run_replacement,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs,13720,13753,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:2963-3082"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:6713-7032""]","An open close confirm for run 1, after the hierarchy advances to run 4, must not send CloseTerminal for the old confirmation; submit either does nothing or requires a new confirm.","Closing a replaced run terminates the wrong/new session, which is destructive and irreversible.",4,3,3,3,100,75,85,"A close sent for a replaced run can terminate the wrong session, destructive and irreversible (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:2963-3082,6713-7032).",Asserts the confirm's captured run and the absence of CloseTerminal after the hierarchy advances (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:2963-3082).,Only close-confirm run-replacement guard (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:6713-7032).,"Real hierarchy event, submit and request drain. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/palette.rs:2963-3082.",high,keep,Destructive wrong-target guard; keep.,[],[],0.024,0.024,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3152 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-004,independent-tui-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aan_unconfigured_gateway_refuses_tailnet_requests|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::an_unconfigured_gateway_refuses_tailnet_requests,default,src/remote/mod.rs,800,809,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:144-166"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:80-96""]","With login = None, authorized() still accepts loopback Hosts but refuses every non-loopback Host, even when the request carries a tailscale-user-login header.",A regression treating an unconfigured login as 'no gate' (returning true when login is None) would expose the gateway over tailscale with no identity check at all: every tailnet peer could read screens and transcripts and drive keystrokes.,4,3,3,3,100,75,85,This is the fail-closed default for the remote surface when no operator identity is configured; losing it is an unauthenticated privacy and control breach of every session (src/remote/mod.rs:80-100 resolves the login from --login or OVRCR_REMOTE_LOGIN).,"The positive loopback case plus the refuse-anyway tailnet case with a login header pin the 'unconfigured means loopback-only' rule exactly (src/remote/mod.rs:800-809); no IPv6 loopback or host-with-port variant is included, and the same host-parse hole as the loopback test remains.","It covers a different branch of authorized() - login absent, src/remote/mod.rs:144-166 - from the configured-login test, and no other suite (tests/remote_web.rs:80-86 starts a gateway with no login) exercises an unconfigured gateway's refusal of a tailnet caller.","Gateway::authorized is the real decision function; the request is hand-built, so the parsed-header layer is again out of the path (src/remote/mod.rs:761-773).",high,keep,Protects the fail-closed default for a high-criticality gate in a distinct authority state from the configured-login test; keep.,[],"0.015s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:561 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr|remote%3A%3Atests%3A%3Atailnet_requests_need_the_configured_login|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,remote::tests::tailnet_requests_need_the_configured_login,default,src/remote/mod.rs,782,797,"[""src/remote/mod.rs:144-166"", ""src/remote/mod.rs:75-96""]","With a configured login, authorized() refuses a non-loopback Host that carries no tailscale-user-login, refuses one carrying a different login, and accepts one carrying the configured login.","If the non-loopback branch stopped comparing the caller login, any device on the tailnet could read /api/state and POST send, key, kill and transcript to every session - an unauthenticated remote control of terminals and their content.",4,3,3,3,100,75,85,"The behaviour is the identity gate on remote access to all sessions: a regression is a privacy breach of transcripts and keystrokes plus a wrong-target control capability, matching the rubric's top band (src/remote/mod.rs:144-166).","Three cases cover the branch's real shape - missing header, wrong login, right login (src/remote/mod.rs:782-797) - so the login comparison itself is pinned. Missing: the served login is normalized at src/remote/mod.rs:79 (inside serve, 75-82; the record cited 80-85), so a case-varied caller login is untested, and host_is_loopback (src/remote/mod.rs:703-710) accepts any Host that merely starts with ""[::1]"", so a tailnet request with Host: [::1].example passes the loopback branch with no login at all; no row exercises that spoofed host, and a host without a port is also untested.","No other test presents a tailscale-user-login header (src/remote/mod.rs:144-166): the only end-to-end suite, tests/remote_web.rs:23-56, binds and calls 127.0.0.1, so the tailnet branch's authority states are protected only by the three gate tests.","The production Gateway::authorized runs, but the tests construct the request struct directly, so the header-parsing layer that produces those names is not in the path (src/remote/mod.rs:761-773).",high,keep,High-criticality authority assertion with no equivalent coverage elsewhere; it must be retained even though it is a small unit test.,[],"0.018s one hosted attempt; unit test in the ovrcr lib target, no sockets or child processes",0.018,0.018,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:565 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-remote-001,independent-shared-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|clear_restores_original_dismisses_current_subject_and_keeps_other|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,clear_restores_original_dismisses_current_subject_and_keeps_other,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2282,2352,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1330-1360"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:858-890"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302""]","Titles the active conversation, inserts a second conversation's subject directly in SQLite, pins then clears the title, and asserts the display returns to the creation name, the active conversation's subject is dismissed while its topic is retained, and the other conversation is not dismissed.",Clear dismissing every recorded conversation (silently disabling titles for conversations the user did not clear) or leaving the active subject visible after clear.,3,4,4,3,75,95,87,Dismissal scope is per-conversation authority over automatic naming; over-dismissal removes the feature for unrelated conversations.,"Two conversations with independent dismissed flags and preserved topics pin the scope exactly, and the dashboard event confirms the restored name.",Only test asserting scoped dismissal; row 38 covers a late result after clear.,"Real server and dashboard, with a direct SQL fixture row for the second conversation.",high,keep,Precise two-conversation scope assertion; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_clear_is_dropped|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aclear_restores_original_name_dismisses_current_subject_and_keeps_other|default""]","[""dashboard stream"", ""SQLite insert and two reads"", ""fake provider""]",4.883,4.883,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:702 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|recorded_pi_switch_shows_stored_subjects_without_new_title_calls|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,recorded_pi_switch_shows_stored_subjects_without_new_title_calls,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,2402,2496,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:250-345"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:289-302""]","Titles conversation A, records a supervisor switch to B (titled, second call), switches back to A and then to B again, asserting each stored subject is shown immediately and the call count stays fixed after both return switches, with identity unchanged.","Switching back to a conversation that already has a stored subject firing a new provider call, or showing the previous conversation's subject after a recorded switch.",3,4,4,3,75,95,87,Stored-subject reuse is the core cost/privacy invariant for recorded switches: each redundant call re-sends private history.,"Call-count equality is asserted twice after two return switches, and dashboard events pin which subject is shown at each step.",Only test of stored-subject reuse on recorded switches; row 40 covers the late-reply race.,"Real server, protocol supervisor messages and fake provider.",high,keep,Serialization of switch state and call budget with no equivalent coverage; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|late_title_result_after_recorded_switch_is_dropped|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|retained%3A%3Atests%3A%3Arecorded_switch_shows_each_conversations_subject_and_keeps_identity|default""]","[""supervisor bind/retain cycles"", ""dashboard events"", ""5 s waits"", ""17.6 s observed""]",17.647,17.647,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:717 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|second_session_due_during_title_call_gets_subject_after_first_ends|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,second_session_due_during_title_call_gets_subject_after_first_ends,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,3185,3361,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:250-345"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:55-100""]","Titles two sessions by retaining both histories; the first provider call blocks on a gate, and the test asserts the second has not started, that a due session observed while the first is in flight still shows its creation name, then releases the gate and asserts both subjects appear and the call log is strictly start-1 < end-1 < start-2 < end-2, with the second history's length and mtime unchanged.","Concurrent title calls (interleaved excerpts and provider overload), a due session forgotten because its file never changes again, or re-reading the history to title the second session later.",3,4,4,3,75,95,87,"Strict serialization protects the single-worker assumption and the provider budget, while the due set is the only thing preventing a silently untitled session.","Ordered provider log markers, the pre-release absence of start-2, unchanged file metadata and both DB rows make serialization and retention directly observable.",Only test of the due-queue/serialization contract; no other row observes two in-flight sessions.,Real server with two sessions and a fake provider that gates on a file.,high,keep,Decisive ordered-log invariant for serialization and due retention; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|conversation_subjects_use_retained_provider_histories_and_survive_restart|default""]","[""two sessions and a gated provider"", ""3 s observation while blocked"", ""file metadata read"", ""9.08 s observed""]",9.076,9.076,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:718 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_call_keeps_pi_stdin_open_until_the_run_settles_and_names_failures|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_call_keeps_pi_stdin_open_until_the_run_settles_and_names_failures,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,3441,3517,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:430-520"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:600-660"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:720-736""]","Uses a fake provider that treats stdin EOF before its reply as an orderly shutdown, asserts the successful call yields Settled Topic and that argv contains `--mode rpc` and `--no-session`; then makes the provider fail and requires the events log to contain the exact `call failed: Pi exited with code 1: ...` line and not the generic timeout text or the excerpt.",Closing provider stdin after sending the prompt makes Pi dispose the in-flight run so every title fails; omitting --no-session leaks the excerpt into a Pi session file; and reporting a generic failure hides the provider's reason.,3,4,4,3,75,95,87,This is the documented Pi RPC lifecycle assumption (#310); getting it wrong makes the whole feature fail while looking like a provider problem.,"The fake provider makes EOF observably fatal, argv is asserted, the success title is required and the failure event text is matched exactly with a negative excerpt scan.",Only test asserting stdin lifetime and the --no-session flag end to end; the unit test covers the reply loop without the process boundary.,"Real process, real pipes and real EOF behavior; the provider script replicates the documented Pi semantics.",high,keep,Historical regression (#310) with an exact failure-message contract; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Atitle%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astdin_stays_open_until_the_rpc_run_settles|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Atitle%3A%3Atests%3A%3Api_exit_before_reply_names_the_reason|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Atitle%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aprovider_error_reaches_the_event|default""]","[""fake provider reads stdin and forks a reader"", ""12 s event-log polling"", ""8.87 s observed""]",8.870,8.870,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:722 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_save_failure_while_live_leaves_subject_unsaved|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_save_failure_while_live_leaves_subject_unsaved,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,961,1023,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:355-390"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:784-850"", ""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:555-600""]","Gates a title call on a file so the session is still live, installs a SQLite trigger that aborts every insert into conversation_subjects, releases the gate, waits for the save-failure log line, and asserts the row is still live and unarchived, keeps its original name, has zero subject rows, and that server.log contains neither the excerpt, the prompt sentence nor the generated topic.","A failed subject insert leaving a partial row, archiving or stopping the session, changing its name, or logging the excerpt/prompt/topic while reporting the error.",3,4,4,3,75,95,87,This protects durable session state and the confidentiality of conversation content when persistence fails.,"A real DB trigger forces the exact production error path; after it, live phase, archived flag, display name, row count and three log substrings are asserted, so a silent success, a rollback failure and a leak are all rejected.",Only row exercising the save-error path end to end; retained unit tests cover save rules but not server error handling and logging.,"Real server, real SQLite trigger and real server log; only the model provider is faked.",high,keep,Decisive state-preservation plus secrecy assertions on a failure path with no other coverage.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_prompt_and_excerpt_stay_out_of_server_log|default""]","[""fake provider gated on a file and read loop"", ""SQLite trigger creation"", ""log polling""]",4.515,4.515,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:728 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_cadence_and_refresh_cooldown_follow_the_fake_clock|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,acceptance,claude_probe_cadence_and_refresh_cooldown_follow_the_fake_clock,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,393,448,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:23-23"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:75-137"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:100-143"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:436-447""]","Uses a file-backed clock to attach, run one probe, refresh for a second probe, then assert a second immediate refresh returns QuotaCooldown with a remaining range and starts nothing; advances 31 s to allow a third probe, advances 29 minutes to assert the 30-minute cadence does not fire, then 31 minutes to assert it does.",Ignoring the refresh cooldown (unbounded provider spawns from repeated clicks) or firing the recurring probe inside its 30-minute cadence and never after it.,3,4,4,3,75,95,87,Cadence and cooldown bound how often a hidden provider process runs; a bypass is a provider-abuse and cost defect.,Exact probe counts after each clock step plus the QuotaCooldown remaining range make the timing behavior directly observable without real waits.,Only cadence/cooldown test with a controllable clock; the generic cooldown is unit-tested in quota.rs:2034-2070 but not the probe cadence.,Real server reading a real clock file; the probe itself is the real hidden-process path with a fixture provider.,high,keep,Deterministic timing coverage of both the cooldown and the cadence; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aquota%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amanual_refresh_has_a_server_cooldown_and_excludes_claude|default""]","[""fake clock file rewritten four times"", ""400 ms settle"", ""probe processes"", ""6.56 s observed""]",6.559,6.559,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:735 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acursor_cloud|managed_busy_prompt_is_rejected_retained_and_requires_manual_resubmission|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::cursor_cloud,integration,acceptance,managed_busy_prompt_is_rejected_retained_and_requires_manual_resubmission,default,tests/cursor_cloud.rs,1631,1702,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/cursor_cloud/run.rs:101-160""]","Pauses send, enters a second prompt while busy, asserts the retained-locally text and exactly one Send, then releases and uses `/resubmit` to assert a second Ready with two Sends total.",A busy prompt being queued and automatically replayed (a second unintended remote turn) or dropped without retention.,3,4,4,3,75,95,87,Automatic replay would send a prompt the user was told was rejected; dropping it loses their input.,"The Send count before and after release, the retention text and the explicit `/resubmit` transition are all asserted.",Only busy/manual-resubmission path.,Real server/PTY and paused scripted bridge.,high,keep,No-replay invariant plus explicit resubmission; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acursor_cloud|managed_send_uncertainty_and_malformed_evidence_never_retry_or_become_ready|default""]","[""PTY session"", ""pause file"", ""0.40 s observed""]",8.179,8.179,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:874 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-003,
