nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Ahermes%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ahook_notice_drops_prompt_and_transcript_fields|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr,lib,unit,report::hermes::tests::hook_notice_drops_prompt_and_transcript_fields,default,src/report/hermes.rs,450,471,"[""src/report/hermes.rs:106-160"", ""src/report.rs:586-598""]","A post_llm_call hook payload carrying user_message, assistant_response and conversation_history is parsed into a Notice retaining only the event, session id, turn id, model, state_db and numeric fields; the serialized notice contains none of the secret prompt, answer or history text.","Retaining and re-serializing prompt or transcript fields, copying user conversation content into the reported notice and whatever consumes it.",4,3,3,4,100,80,88,The notice is the data that leaves the hook; carrying prompt or transcript text is a direct privacy leak of conversation content (4).,"src/report/hermes.rs:450-471 asserts the encoded notice does not contain 'secret' and pins the retained identity fields, so both over-retention and under-parsing fail.",Only redaction test for the Hermes hook parser.,Direct production notice_from_hook over a JSON payload.,high,keep,Only evidence for the Hermes prompt/transcript drop.,[],pure JSON parsing,0.016,0.016,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:655 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,app-report-002,independent-report-check-2
