nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aagent_setup|doctor_interrupt_cleans_its_owned_version_probe_before_exit|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::agent_setup,integration,acceptance,doctor_interrupt_cleans_its_owned_version_probe_before_exit,default,tests/agent_setup.rs,404,470,"[""src/cli/agent_setup.rs:644-673"", ""src/report/admission.rs:222-303""]","For SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGQUIT the test spawns doctor with a fixture claude that publishes its pid and sleeps 60, signals doctor, and asserts the fixture is its own process-group leader, that the group is gone (ESRCH) within the 3 s bound, and that doctor's exit status carries the same signal.","Doctor exiting on an interrupt while leaving the version probe or its descendants running, cleaning up the wrong process group, or hanging past the bound instead of restoring the pending signal.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Every interrupted doctor invocation would otherwise leak a sleeping provider process; leaked probe groups accumulate across repair attempts and can hold the provider lock/PTY.,"Real signals are delivered, the group leader relation is checked with getpgid, absence is proven by ESRCH, and the whole cleanup is bounded by a deadline with a status.signal assertion.",Only signal-cleanup test for the doctor probe; report::admission unit tests cover a different probe caller.,Real OS processes and signals: the process-group boundary is exactly the subject.,high,keep,Decisive OS-level cleanup invariant that no other reviewed test asserts.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Aadmission%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ablocked_version_probe_reaps_the_exact_group_within_budget|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr|report%3A%3Aadmission%3A%3Atests%3A%3Ainitial_admission_probe_cleans_descendants_after_leader_exit|default""]","[""four spawn/signal cycles with a 60 s sleeping fixture"", ""polling at 2 ms"", ""4.165 s observed""]",4.165,4.165,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:698 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 12