nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_history_read_stops_at_256_kib|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::automatic_titles,integration,acceptance,title_history_read_stops_at_256_kib,default,tests/automatic_titles.rs,1192,1256,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:13-13"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:969-983"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/title.rs:938-967""]","Builds a 300 KiB history with a JSON secret placed outside the tail window, launches the server with a DYLD-interposed read() that counts bytes read from that exact file, and asserts the server read exactly the first line plus 256 KiB, that the secret never reaches the prompt and that the tail reply does.","Reading the whole history (unbounded latency and memory, and a prompt containing content the contract excludes) or skipping the identity header line while reading only the tail.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,An unbounded history read blocks the single title worker and can transmit far more private content than the contract allows.,"The exact byte count comes from a real interposed read() against the canonical file path, so any extra or missing read changes the number; content assertions independently reject head leakage.",Only exact read-bound measurement in the suite; row 23 checks tail content but not the byte budget.,"Real macOS read boundary via DYLD interposition, real server process and real file; the OS read is the subject rather than a stand-in.",high,keep,"A decisive, instrumented invariant with no equivalent coverage; keep.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aautomatic_titles|title_subject_storage_archive_and_exclusions_cover_live_paths|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Atitle%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abounded_tail_extracts_provider_messages|default""]","[""compiles a C dylib with clang"", ""writes a 300 KiB file"", ""DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES server launch"", ""12.64 s observed""]",12.643,12.643,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:724 