nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_ownership|natural_leader_exit_with_attached_job_requires_ack_before_reopen|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_ownership,integration,acceptance,natural_leader_exit_with_attached_job_requires_ack_before_reopen,default,tests/retained_ownership.rs,360,407,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:262-272"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1476-1560""]",A leader exiting while a detached attached job survives yields exited plus requires_ack; reopen refuses OwnershipUncertain and the survivor stays alive until the test reaps it.,Reopening over a live descendant (duplicate shell) or reaping the survivor.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Reopening over a surviving descendant is a wrong-owner acknowledgement guard: the stale owner must be acknowledged before a fresh shell reuses the row, which protects ownership and workflow state rather than a credential or a destructive wrong-target action (tests/retained_ownership.rs:360-407; crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:262-272).","Real setsid survivor pid, phase/recovery assertions, refusal and liveness.",Leader-exit-with-surviving-job ownership is unique.,Real processes/setsid and server state.,high,keep,"Keep: Real setsid survivor pid, phase/recovery assertions, refusal and liveness. Leader-exit-with-surviving-job ownership is unique.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_ownership|same_boot_crash_with_surviving_descendant_requires_ack_before_fresh_shell_reopen|default""]","[""real processes""]",3.976,3.976,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1410 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,independent-integration-mid-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_ownership|same_boot_crash_with_surviving_descendant_requires_ack_before_fresh_shell_reopen|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_ownership,integration,acceptance,same_boot_crash_with_surviving_descendant_requires_ack_before_fresh_shell_reopen,default,tests/retained_ownership.rs,658,773,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:262-272"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1476-1560""]","After SIGKILL of the server pid, the surviving descendant remains; restart restores interrupted/requires_ack with no live work; reopen refuses; after reaping/ack the fresh shell runs in the recorded cwd without the old command.",Restart reaping/ignoring a live descendant and launching a second shell over it.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"After a same-boot server crash the surviving descendant must be acknowledged before a fresh shell reopens; this is a wrong-owner/durable-state guard, and the failure only withholds a spawn, so it is C=3 rather than a destructive wrong-target or credential protection (tests/retained_ownership.rs:658-773; crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:262-272).","Real SIGKILL, descendant liveness, interrupted state, refusal and fresh-shell identity/cwd.",Same-boot crash ownership with a descendant is the deepest reconciliation case.,"Real processes, sqlite and restarts.",high,keep,"Keep: Real SIGKILL, descendant liveness, interrupted state, refusal and fresh-shell identity/cwd. Same-boot crash ownership with a descendant is the deepest reconciliation case.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_ownership|natural_leader_exit_with_attached_job_requires_ack_before_reopen|default""]","[""real SIGKILL""]",5.617,5.617,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1412 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,independent-integration-mid-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|automatic_recovery_rechecks_ownership_disposition_and_identity_on_server|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,automatic_recovery_rechecks_ownership_disposition_and_identity_on_server,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,1604,1709,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1476-1512"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/session.rs:116-131""]","Seven mutated authority states (same/missing/malformed boot, stopped, archived, unarchived, invalid identity) each make RecoverSession fail without starting work, and no launch occurs across restarts.","A dashboard/cached recovery bypassing the server's ownership, disposition or identity re-check and launching anyway.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"The server rechecks boot identity, disposition and conversation identity before auto-recovery; this is a wrong-owner/authority guard whose failure only withholds recovery, so it is C=3 rather than destructive wrong-target or data-loss protection (tests/retained_sessions.rs:1604-1709; crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/session.rs:116-131).","Seven-case mutation matrix with error, no groups and unchanged argv after each restart.",Server-side re-check of all recovery authority states is the decisive invariant.,"Real sqlite mutations, server restarts and PTY.",high,keep,"Keep: Seven-case mutation matrix with error, no groups and unchanged argv after each restart. Server-side re-check of all recovery authority states is the decisive invariant.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|automatic_recovery_failure_requires_explicit_retry_even_after_reconnect|default""]","[""real sqlite+restarts""]",16.940,16.940,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1421 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,independent-integration-mid-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|displayed_interrupted_claude_recovers_through_real_dashboard_and_coalesces_duplicates|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,displayed_interrupted_claude_recovers_through_real_dashboard_and_coalesces_duplicates,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,1385,1545,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1670-1696"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1476-1512"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1538-1562""]","Displaying an interrupted Claude row makes the real dashboard emit exactly one RecoverSession; queued explicit/recover duplicates reuse run+1, post-publication duplicates still reuse it, a reconnect/redraw emits none, and a late recover after close does not restart the session.","Duplicate recover launches, or a display-driven recovery after close/late redraw restarting a closed session.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Duplicate and late Dashboard recovery requests are coalesced and a closed row is not respawned; this is wrong-owner/duplicate-launch protection, so it is C=3 rather than a wrong-target destructive or credential protection (tests/retained_sessions.rs:1385-1545; crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1476-1512).","Real dashboard request stream, receipt counting/run equality, argv equality, request-count equality and post-close check.",Dashboard-driven automatic recovery coalescing is unique.,"Real dashboard, server, PTY and sqlite.",high,keep,"Keep: Real dashboard request stream, receipt counting/run equality, argv equality, request-count equality and post-close check. Dashboard-driven automatic recovery coalescing is unique.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|automatic_recovery_failure_requires_explicit_retry_even_after_reconnect|default""]","[""real dashboard+socket""]",9.661,9.661,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1423 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,independent-integration-mid-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|grok_managed_launch_retains_its_history_file_for_titles_without_resume|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,grok_managed_launch_retains_its_history_file_for_titles_without_resume,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,305,476,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/grok_recovery.rs:58-90"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:156-158""]","Grok launch records only conversation+history path, marks resume unavailable, validates history-file identity before use, never stores prompt/output, and survives two restarts with the same reference; resume is refused.","Advertising resume Grok cannot do, losing the history reference, or persisting private text.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Wrong resume/reference can read another conversation's private history.,"Exact argv/reference/store row, identity validation both ways, restart equality, privacy byte scans and refusal.",Grok history-only retention is unique.,Real server/PTY/sqlite; native Grok is a fixture. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/grok_recovery.rs:58-90.,high,keep,"Keep: Exact argv/reference/store row, identity validation both ways, restart equality, privacy byte scans and refusal. Grok history-only retention is unique.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|codex_reopen_uses_exact_identity_without_prompt_across_two_restarts|default""]","[""real restarts+sqlite""]",7.692,7.692,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1427 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-005,independent-integration-tail-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_admission_ineligible_argv_and_probe_failures_preserve_native_arguments|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_admission_ineligible_argv_and_probe_failures_preserve_native_arguments,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9969,10043,"[""src/report/admission.rs:88-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120""]","Seven cases (foreign --resume= form, --resume/-r on 2.1.268, unknown mode, doctor, --model with blocked or missing TMPDIR): the native argv is exactly the ineligible argument plus --dangerously-skip-permissions, no agent binding exists, the child prints NATIVE_UNCHANGED, and it exits 19; the version-probe timeout leaves no process group.","An ineligible argv could be rewritten or partially consumed before native exec (the user runs the wrong mode), or a hung version probe could leak a process group and block admission.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Rewriting an ineligible native argv runs a different command than the user typed (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120).,"Asserts the exact argv file for every case, absence of binding, the native marker, exit 19 and probe-process cleanup (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9985-10040).",Only row covering ineligible-argv pass-through and probe failure/timeout preservation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9969-10043).,Real native fixture cases and real compiled agent run invocations (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9970-9995).,high,keep,Grounded table of distinct ineligible inputs with exact argv preservation.,[],"[""seven session creations"", ""real native fixture"", ""probe timeout case""]",4.606,4.606,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1443 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,8360,8558,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1454-1560""]",agent run gives the native child its own process group and terminal foreground; Ctrl-C reaches it once; Ctrl-Z stops both native and launcher; pause/resume works; a second concurrent `agent run` is refused with no stdout; SIGTERM to the launcher exits 23 and restores termios; a failed missing-binary launch releases the lease so a third invocation succeeds (epoch 3) and the endpoint is gone.,"A failed native launch could keep the reservation, blocking every later agent run in the session; terminal modes could be left altered after a forwarded termination.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,A retained reservation after failure permanently blocks agent runs in that session (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120).,"Asserts epochs 1 and 3, the refused concurrent spawn, termios equality, endpoint removal and group absence (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8400-8545).",Only row covering lease release after a failed exec plus double stop (Ctrl-Z) handling (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8360-8558).,"Real native groups, real stop signals and real compiled CLI invocations (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8362-8400).",high,keep,Grounded lease-release and job-control coverage with epoch assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|hermes_supervision_preserves_job_control_failure_and_peer_isolation|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_runtime_kill_reaches_owned_native_group|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_channel_failure_releases_reservation_before_native_fallback|default""]","[""real native and launcher groups"", ""Ctrl-Z/SIGTERM injection"", ""multiple compiled CLI runs"", ""termios snapshots""]",5.918,5.918,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1455 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_supervisor_sigkill_releases_reporting_watch|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,agent_run_supervisor_sigkill_releases_reporting_watch,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,7738,7999,"[""src/report/admission.rs:16-160"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:66-90"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120""]","An agent run under a fault-free proxy is SIGKILLed; the server flips health to Unavailable with reason supervisor_disconnected, the collector group disappears, coverage stops being Complete, and the native process and outer shell survive; a replacement invocation binds, and late old reports/releases are rejected.",A dead supervisor could leave reporting ownership wedged (no new invocation can bind) or take the native process down with it; a stale release could clear the replacement binding.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Wedged reporting ownership blocks all later agent runs in the session and misstates health, a major workflow failure (src/report/admission.rs:16-160).","Asserts health reason/state, partial coverage, collector group absence, native/shell survival, replacement binding and two late-write rejections (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7820-7950).",Only row covering supervisor crash recovery and stale-lease rejection (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7738-7999).,"Real supervisor process killed with SIGKILL, real collector and native process groups, real proxy on the socket path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:7748-7800).",high,keep,High-value crash-recovery coverage with real process deaths.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_channel_failure_releases_reservation_before_native_fallback|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_tracks_only_current_root_prompt_observations|default""]","[""real supervisor/native/collector process groups"", ""SIGKILL injection"", ""admission proxy"", ""ps-based collector discovery""]",4.222,4.222,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1457 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
