ral compiled CLI runs"", ""150+ line body""]",8.729,8.729,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1487 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,13251,13358,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-115"", ""src/cli/bridge.rs:17-45""]","Tickets with a wrong server lifetime, a wrong run, or a missing session are each ignored with row-set equality; a fresh valid ticket then applies (ordering barrier); after the dashboard drops the same ticket is ignored; a replacement dashboard applies it; after CloseTerminal archives the run, both the original and run-updated archived ticket are ignored.","Accepting a stale lifetime/run/session could select or resurrect a session that the banner no longer refers to, possibly after archival.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Selecting an archived or replaced run on stale authority targets work that is no longer live (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:64-113 lifetime/run/disposition checks).,Three stale-ticket cases plus live/absent/replacement-dashboard/archived cases each assert ignored results and unchanged rows (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13260-13355).,Only row covering all navigation validation dimensions including archive disposition (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13251-13358).,"Real compiled server binary, real bridge CLIs and real dashboard processes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:13253-13265).",high,keep,The most complete ticket-revalidation coverage; decisive for the authority boundary.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_can_inspect_exited_original_run_without_recovery|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_never_starts_missing_server_and_old_lifetime_stays_invalid|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_callback_rejects_malformed_versions_before_connecting|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_old_ticket_cannot_select_an_explicitly_reopened_run|default""]","[""multiple bridge CLI callbacks"", ""dashboard restart"", ""archive operations""]",14.978,14.978,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1510 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_settings_sources_authorize_and_failed_saves_preserve_opt_ins|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,desktop_notifications_bridge_settings_sources_authorize_and_failed_saves_preserve_opt_ins,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,18131,18260,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:205-260"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:1-120""]","A failed settings save (read-only document) shows a concrete error, leaves the document byte-identical, does not authorize, and does not expand consent; a later real save path through the Settings editor authorizes before any alert; server SetSetting and external document reload each drive status+authorize; a failed opt-out preserves both saved opt-ins and a later real delivery.","A failed save could authorize or enable the channel anyway, or could drop the saved sound opt-in; external reloads might bypass permission checks.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Consent expanded without a saved opt-in, or a permission requested without a user action, breaks the notification authorization contract (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:205-260).","Asserts document equality after failures, ordered control sequences across three sources, and loaded settings after each path (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18135-18255).",Only row covering all three settings sources and failed-save preservation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18131-18260).,"Real dashboard PTY, real read-only filesystem, real settings editor and real host record (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:18133-18150).",high,keep,Grounded consent-preservation across every settings source.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_authorizes_enabled_startup_before_any_alert|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_denied_settings_are_explicit_and_never_modal_or_automatic|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_hello_carries_the_servers_settings_and_toggles_save_through_the_request|default""]","[""dashboard PTY"", ""read-only document chmod"", ""bridge request record"", ""settings editor input""]",8.884,8.884,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1515 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|hermes_supervision_preserves_job_control_failure_and_peer_isolation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,hermes_supervision_preserves_job_control_failure_and_peer_isolation,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,8213,8357,"[""src/report/hermes.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/agent_runner.rs:29-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880""]","A hermes agent run owns its process group and terminal foreground; Ctrl-C increments native interrupts; pause stops it and refuses input, resume delivers input; SIGTERM to the launcher makes the wrapper exit 23, restores the outer shell termios, removes the native group and private endpoint, and a peer session stays usable.","The native child could run outside the managed group/foreground (Ctrl-C and pause hitting the wrong processes), or a failure could leave termios altered and the private endpoint behind.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Wrong process-group/foreground ownership misroutes interrupts and pause signals, breaking job control (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:852-880).","Asserts pgid==pid, foreground pgid, interrupt counter, termios equality, group/endpoint absence, exit 23 and peer usability (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8240-8350).",Only row covering hermes wrapper job control alongside peer isolation (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8213-8357).,"Real native process group, real termios snapshots and real datagram/datagram-free probes (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:8219-8240).",high,keep,Grounded job-control coverage with termios and peer-isolation assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|agent_run_owns_native_group_and_restores_terminal_after_forwarded_term|default""]","[""real native process group and stty snapshots"", ""SIGTERM forwarding"", ""peer session round trip""]",3.973,3.973,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1536 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|iterm_setup_real_palette_requires_separate_opt_in_and_uses_current_owned_dashboard|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,iterm_setup_real_palette_requires_separate_opt_in_and_uses_current_owned_dashboard,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,20377,20537,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:444-520"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:190-300""]","iTerm setup requires a second explicit opt-in: palette with iterm_focus off records no setup and a control-client PrepareITermFocus returns None; after enabling, the palette records exactly one setup whose target names the current dashboard pid/IQ identity and an owner ticket the server and CLI both confirm; disabling makes the server answer iterm_focus false; detach invalidates the ticket; a replacement dashboard gets its own setup and the old owner is rejected.","Setup could be initiated by a control client or stale dashboard (authorizing the wrong terminal), or an old owner ticket could survive and activate an unrelated window.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Authorizing exact iTerm control for the wrong dashboard/owner can activate or type into an unrelated terminal window (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/navigation.rs:190-300 owner confirmation).,"Asserts setup counts, target pid/identity/focus, server and CLI owner confirmations, invalidation after detach and rejection after replacement (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20385-20530).",Only row covering iTerm setup opt-in and owner binding end to end (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20377-20537).,"Real dashboard PTY with a real iTerm identity environment, real bridge CLI and real host record (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:20379-20420).",high,keep,Grounded authorization-binding coverage for a terminal-control feature.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|iterm_setup_real_palette_denial_and_missing_identity_preserve_notification_preferences|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|desktop_notifications_bridge_click_revalidates_lifetime_run_target_and_current_dashboard|default""]","[""dashboard PTY and replacement dashboard"", ""bridge CLI owner runs"", ""iTerm host record""]",9.582,9.582,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1543 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|native_claude_quota_reaches_sidebar_through_real_reporting_and_dashboard_socket|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,native_claude_quota_reaches_sidebar_through_real_reporting_and_dashboard_socket,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,9153,9342,"[""src/report/admission.rs:16-190"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/quota.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:1-120""]","A real Claude-shaped native run reports through real reporting and the dashboard socket; the quota row is Checking with a session source, flips to NotSignedIn when the fixture signs out, and two statusline callbacks make the sidebar render 58% and 82% windows plus plain-language detail text with no internal provenance.","Quota snapshots could be dropped between reporting and the sidebar (or shown from the wrong source), and internal identifiers could leak into user-visible text.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"A missing or wrong-source quota row hides remaining allowance, a major workflow failure (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/quota.rs:1-120).","Asserts protocol snapshot state/reason/source, rendered sidebar percentages and forbidden internal strings in details (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9210-9335).",Only row driving real reporting into the real TUI renderer for quota (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9153-9342).,"Real server, real reporting socket, real native fixture and real ratatui TestBackend render (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9157-9200).",high,keep,Grounded end-to-end quota coverage including rendered output.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_tracks_only_current_root_prompt_observations|default""]","[""real native helper reporting"", ""dashboard socket event drain"", ""ratatui TestBackend render"", ""env_lock serialization""]",3.582,3.582,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1546 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_in_place_transitions_rebind_reload_and_refresh_without_a_new_producer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,omp_in_place_transitions_rebind_reload_and_refresh_without_a_new_producer,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,16339,16570,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-343"", ""src/report/extension.rs:637-700""]","In-place omp transitions: startup binds generation 1; a switch with an approval open clears requests, binds generation 2 Connected, Idle with no turn, keeps Unread; compaction changes nothing; A to B to A is generation 3; a same-conversation reload keeps generation 3 but abandons the cycle (Idle, no turn); plugin_refresh changes nothing; tree navigation yields Unknown then Idle; the next cycle Readies in generation 3; a switch naming an unseen previous conversation pauses with transition_mismatch keeping the binding and Unread; the next boundary recovers as generation 4.","A reload or refresh could fabricate a rebind, a mismatched transition could rebind silently, or a cycle could be reused across generations (identical Ready identities).",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Fabricated transitions or silent rebinding report the wrong conversation as current (src/report/extension.rs:637-700 transition_mismatch).,"Asserts conversation/generation pairs, activity states, health reasons and Unread across nine transitions (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16350-16560).",Only row covering omp in-place reload/refresh/mismatch transitions (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16339-16570).,Real omp producer through the materialized extension (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16341-16360).,high,keep,The most complete in-place transition coverage; decisive.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_replacement_binds_the_foreground_conversation_and_rejects_the_retired_producer|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_supported_conversation_switches_rebind_ready_and_input_without_unread_ack|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_supported_conversation_switches_rebind_ready_and_input_without_unread_ack|default""]","[""node omp host"", ""~20 callback steps""]",5.542,5.542,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1547 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,16025,16336,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-343"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]","Omp keeps two input requests open at once (approval:c1 then question:q1, oldest first); each alerts once; CLI list reports both kinds with no Unread and no secret text; doctor names both and the question tool-lifetime capability; denying c1 leaves the question and WaitingInput; closing q1 restores Busy; reopening c1 after close is a new request and alerts again; a foreign approval is refused; Ready/Unread is a separate lane and a switch clears requests while keeping Unread; reporter loss clears requests and keeps Unread.","A denial could be treated as ending the whole wait, a closed id could be reused without a new alert, or a foreign child approval could open a root request.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Conflating multiple simultaneous approvals/questions leaves the user answering a stale dialog or missing a live one (src/report/extension.rs:230-343 request set).,"Ordered request-vector equality at every step, alert-title sequence, CLI/doctor shapes and secret negatives (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16040-16330).",Only row covering multiple simultaneous omp requests and id reuse (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16025-16336).,"Real omp host, real dashboard host record and real CLI output (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:16027-16045).",high,keep,Grounded multi-request lane coverage unique to omp.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|codex_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_input_request_shows_waiting_alerts_once_and_restores_the_underlying_activity|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_input_requests_wait_alert_once_each_and_restore_without_unread|default""]","[""node omp host"", ""dashboard host record"", ""CLI and doctor runs""]",5.571,5.571,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1548 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_managed_extension_reports_observed_ready_continuations_switches_and_child_inertness|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,omp_managed_extension_reports_observed_ready_continuations_switches_and_child_inertness,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15882,16022,"[""src/report/extension.rs:180-343"", ""src/report/omp.rs:24-47""]",An omp session walks 17 frames: session_start binds generation 1 Idle; continuations keep the same turn; an end without continuation settles Ready Observed with Unread; later error/aborted cycles keep the first Unread; print mode reports nothing; an in-process child start reports Idle; a session_switch rebinds sess-b generation 2 and its Ready replaces Unread; shutdown yields Unavailable with Unread retained.,"Continuation frames could be double-published or lost, and an in-process child could be mistaken for the root cycle, misreporting activity in the wrong conversation.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Wrong cycle/child attribution reports work that is not the foreground conversation (src/report/extension.rs:180-343 admit_cycle/switch).,"Per-step activity, quality, conversation and generation assertions with explicit Unread identity checks (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15900-16010).","Only row covering omp continuations, print mode and child inertness (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15882-16022).","Real omp host via the materialized extension, real PTY and socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15884-15900).",high,keep,Dense independent expectations; distinct omp protocol semantics.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_extension_reports_busy_ready_error_idle_and_fences_producers|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_in_place_transitions_rebind_reload_and_refresh_without_a_new_producer|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default""]","[""node omp host"", ""17 callback steps"", ""PTY marker waits""]",4.743,4.743,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1549 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_managed_extension_reports_busy_ready_error_idle_and_fences_producers|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,pi_managed_extension_reports_busy_ready_error_idle_and_fences_producers,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,11324,11539,"[""src/report/extension.rs:98-180"", ""src/report/extension.rs:230-343"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]",A pi managed session walks 25 extension frames: a foreign-parent helper cannot bind; Busy/Ready/Error/Idle and Observed/Confirmed quality follow the table; the first Ready is Unread and survives later errors and continuations; a continued cycle settles as a new Unread; reporter loss after native exit yields Unavailable while Unread remains.,"A producer that cannot be fenced could open or keep a wrong cycle, and continuation starts could either be double-published or lose their eventual Ready/Unread.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Cycle/Unread misattribution reports the wrong agent as needing attention (src/report/extension.rs:230-320 admit_cycle).,"Every step asserts activity, quality, binding conversation/provider and specific Unread identity transitions (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11360-11520).",Only row covering pi continuation cycles and producer fencing end to end (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11324-11539).,"Real pi host through the materialized extension, real PTY, real reporting socket (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:11250-11320).",high,keep,Dense independent expectations make most mapping defects fail; retention is clearly justified.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_managed_extension_reports_observed_ready_continuations_switches_and_child_inertness|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_input_requests_wait_until_the_last_closes_and_alert_once_each|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|claude_ready_alerts_once_per_root_turn_with_unread_and_continuation|default""]","[""node host process per callback"", ""real PTY and hook socket"", ""25-step terminal waits""]",6.023,6.023,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1562 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_replacement_binds_the_foreground_conversation_and_rejects_the_retired_producer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pi_replacement_binds_the_foreground_conversation_and_rejects_the_retired_producer,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15281,15431,"[""src/report/extension.rs:190-280"", ""src/report/reporter.rs:1-160""]","A pi session_replace to sess-b resumes as generation 2 with Connected and Idle/None turn, keeping Unread; same-conversation compaction changes nothing; returning to sess-a is generation 3; tree navigation after Busy yields Unknown with no turn, and after idle:true yields Idle; the next cycle Readies on generation 3 with a new Unread.","An announced replacement could be treated as an unexpected transition (pausing), reuse an old generation, or replay a historical response as new.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Generation reuse or a false pause breaks the reporting contract for the replacement producer (src/report/extension.rs:190-280 bind/rebind).,"Asserts conversation/generation pairs, health/reason, turn identity and Unread at every transition (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15290-15425).",Only row covering replacement/compaction/tree-navigation transitions for pi (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15281-15431).,Real pi host with a replacement-capable fixture (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15283-15300).,high,keep,Dense transition table with independent expectations.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_in_place_transitions_rebind_reload_and_refresh_without_a_new_producer|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_reattach_on_a_healthy_reporter_is_a_fresh_generation_and_the_next_cycle_readies|default""]","[""node pi host"", ""many callback waits""]",5.226,5.226,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1569 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,pi_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,15434,15526,"[""src/report/extension.rs:230-260"", ""src/report/extension.rs:637-700""]","A dropped input_close (sequence 7) leaves the snapshot unmoved until the next frame reveals a hole; then health becomes Unavailable with source_gap, the request set is cleared, Unread survives, later frames change nothing, and the next agent_start recovers as generation 2 with Busy and empty requests and a later cycle Readies normally.",A missed frame could be applied as if contiguous (believing a dialog closed) or could drop the session permanently instead of recovering at the next boundary.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Applying a gap as contiguous state publishes a wrong dialogue/activity view of a live agent (src/report/extension.rs:230-260 fence/gap).,"Frame-dropping fixture plus quiet-state equality, recovery generation, and a later Ready/Unread (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15440-15522).",Only row covering gap detection at a lost close and recovery at an ordinary start (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15434-15526).,"Real pi transport dropping one real frame, real PTY and server (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:15436-15450).",high,keep,Grounded gap-injection coverage with state-preserving assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|pi_source_gap_recovers_at_a_continuation_start_and_still_readies|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_source_gap_pauses_then_recovers_at_the_next_boundary|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|omp_reattach_recovers_a_paused_reporter_during_an_input_wait|default""]","[""pi host with dropped sequence"", ""many callback waits""]",5.862,5.862,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1570 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_tracks_only_current_root_prompt_observations|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,acceptance,private_claude_activity_tracks_only_current_root_prompt_observations,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,10046,10048,"[""src/report/admission.rs:317-430"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205""]","A 25-step activity table drives the private Claude route: only the current root turn opens Input (approval), stale Stop/Notification/PreToolUse callbacks for a prior turn leave state, Stop produces ResponseReady, StopFailure produces Error, and each step asserts the exact activity revision, activity state, turn and input_requests.","A stale callback from a previous turn could open Input or change activity for the wrong turn, misreporting that an agent needs approval.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Showing a phantom approval request or hiding a real one blocks or misleads the user at the only control point (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205).,"Per-step expected revision, state, turn and input_requests vector make almost any wrong mapping fail (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10090-10340).",Only row covering the full activity/Input state machine over the private route (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:10046-10048).,Real hook callbacks through the real private reporting channel and real server state (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:9674-9730).,high,keep,High-resolution state-machine coverage with independent per-case expectations.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|private_claude_activity_delivery_failure_disconnects_without_stopping_native|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|hermes_supervision_preserves_job_control_failure_and_peer_isolation|default""]","[""25 callback steps with terminal waits"", ""real native helper"", ""env_lock serialization""]",5.933,5.933,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1575 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,independent-lifecycle-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|split_server_two_streams_resize_resync_and_detach|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::server_lifecycle,integration,integration,split_server_two_streams_resize_resync_and_detach,default,tests/server_lifecycle.rs,6761,7119,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:574-700"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dashboard.rs:254-375""]",Two-pane views at revisions 1-5: SetView returns one Screen per pane then Ok; child stty sizes follow pane sizes and resizes; focus changes; a hidden session keeps 40x120; a 200k-line burst produces per-session ScreenDirty and recovery; detaching leaves all three groups alive; reattach rebuilds one and two panes with final output.,"Split view could return snapshots for the wrong pane, acknowledge before snapshots, resize wrong PTYs, emit old-revision frames after replacement, or kill sessions on detach.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Wrong pane snapshots/revisions corrupt the split dashboard and stale-revision frames overwrite replacement panes (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/dispatch.rs:574-700).,"Asserts snapshot-per-pane exactly once, ack ordering, revision equality on every frame, child-reported sizes, and post-detach group existence (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6660-7100).","Only reviewed row covering multi-pane DashboardView revisions, focus and resync (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6761-7119).","Real PTYs, real dashboard socket with a shrunk receive buffer, and real 200k-line bursts (tests/server_lifecycle.rs:6761-7119).",high,keep,The only split-view protection; precise revision and per-pane assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|dashboard_geometry_sizes_connected_empty_and_detached_sessions|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|selection_snapshot_precedes_later_quiet_tail_output|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|slow_dashboard_recovers_after_output_burst|default""]","[""three real PTY sessions"", ""two 200k-line bursts"", ""30s burst deadline"", ""SO_RCVBUF tuning"", ""revision tracking helpers""]",4.457,4.457,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1584 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_attention_ranks_accepted_reports_and_selects_the_real_destination|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,acceptance,agent_attention_ranks_accepted_reports_and_selects_the_real_destination,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,1262,1474,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320""]","Two agents get accepted reports: agent-a-unread has Unread, agent-z-input has WaitingInput. The Agents list shows both, ranks the input-needed session above the alphabetical Unread one, Enter lands in that session, input reaches only it, Unread survives and the input request remains after navigation.",Attention ordering could rank the wrong session (sending the user to the wrong agent) or navigation could clear Unread/resolve a pending request as a side effect.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Misranking attention sends the user to the wrong live session, and clearing requests on navigation fabricates a decision (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/reporting.rs:88-205).","Asserts effective activity, screen ordering by index of the two rows, destination delivery and full Unread/request equality after navigation (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1270-1470).",Only row covering attention ranking with real accepted reports and real jump destination (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1262-1474).,"Real supervisor reserve/hello/bind frames, real PTYs and a real dashboard PTY (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1264-1350).",high,keep,Grounded ranking and no-side-effect assertions with real reporting frames.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_search_selects_and_types_through_real_dashboard|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_search_navigates_fifty_live_sessions_through_real_dashboard|default""]","[""supervisor leases per session"", ""real dashboard PTY"", ""report frames""]",4.732,4.732,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1693 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_initial_prompt_reaches_fake_claude_as_one_literal_argument|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,integration,agent_initial_prompt_reaches_fake_claude_as_one_literal_argument,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,1669,1769,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:520-560"", ""crates/ovrcr-protocol/src/agent.rs:1-80""]","Creating an agent session with a multiline initial prompt through the New agent form reaches a fake claude: the prompt arrives as exactly one AGENT_ARG entry after an explicit `--` separator, is not used as the session name, and the branch child workspace exists.","A multiline prompt could be split into multiple argv items or shell-split, changing the instructions the agent receives (or letting prompt text inject arguments).",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"Prompt/argv confusion alters the agent's instructions and can inject flags, a major correctness/authority issue (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:520-560).","Asserts exactly one occurrence of the full prompt argument, its position after the separator, and the session identity (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1660-1760).",Only row covering initial-prompt argv fidelity through the branch child and compiled CLI (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1669-1769).,"Real dashboard form input, real compiled CLI/server and a scripted claude that prints its argv (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1671-1700).",high,keep,Decisive single-argument assertion for a security-relevant boundary.,[],"[""outer PTY form input"", ""branch child workspace"", ""30s form deadline""]",5.104,5.104,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1694 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_search_real_loading_input_is_discarded_and_never_replayed|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,acceptance,agent_search_real_loading_input_is_discarded_and_never_replayed,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,1194,1259,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:1-80""]","With the final SetView Ok withheld by a proxy, at the end of the search wait, keyboard and paste input are rejected with a visible notice and a queued cutover burst is also discarded; after release the dashboard enters Terminal mode and only post-gate input reaches agent-b; neither child ever sees the loading input.","Input typed while a pane is still loading could be buffered and replayed into the target, or lost with the game visible only as silent data loss.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Replaying loading-time input into a newly focused agent runs commands the user typed at a different screen (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320).,"Asserts rejection notices, absence of all four sentinel payloads in both sessions, consumed confirmation Enter, and post-gate delivery (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1200-1255).",Only row covering input discarding at the view-acknowledgement cutover (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1194-1259).,"Real view proxy holding the production Ok, real dashboard PTY and two real agents (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1196-1220).",high,keep,Decisive no-replay assertions across a real acknowledgement barrier.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|session_jump_single_digit%3A%3Asingle_digit_jump_selects_the_ninth_agent_through_the_compiled_dashboard|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|agent_search_selects_and_types_through_real_dashboard|default""]","[""view proxy holding SetView Ok"", ""real dashboard PTY"", ""64x burst input""]",4.860,4.860,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1696 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|assignment_control%3A%3Aassigned_child_is_view_only_until_explicit_dashboard_takeover_and_return|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,acceptance,assignment_control::assigned_child_is_view_only_until_explicit_dashboard_takeover_and_return,default,tests/terminal_acceptance/assignment_control.rs,135,402,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:1-140"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:805-820""]","An assigned child is view-only: a passive split/focus/resize/hide never changes its run, phase or default control, and a bracketed paste sent before takeover never reaches it. H (takeover) shows Human control, Enter enters Terminal mode, a marker reaches the child, then A (return) enters a pending reconciliation barrier and further input is rejected; afterwards the child's run and Running phase are unchanged with owner Controller, epoch 3 and a HumanReturn barrier.",Viewing could mutate control ownership or let input through before takeover; return could leave control unclaimed or let input race reconciliation.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,View-only enforcement is an ownership boundary: input before takeover or a stuck return can send commands to an agent the user does not control (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_control.rs:1-140).,"Asserts control equality before takeover, absence of the forbidden payload, and post-return owner/epoch/barrier plus run/phase stability (tests/terminal_acceptance/assignment_control.rs:150-400).",Only row covering the assignment-control takeover/return state machine end to end (tests/terminal_acceptance/assignment_control.rs:135-402).,"Real compiled dashboard, real assigned Pi child through delegation and real server control frames (tests/terminal_acceptance/assignment_control.rs:30-90).",high,keep,Grounded ownership invariants with real input attempts.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|session_jump_operator%3A%3Aoperator_control_jump_uses_the_live_agent_and_preserves_its_unsent_draft|default""]","[""delegation fixture with held settlement"", ""outer PTY dashboard"", ""split/resize interactions""]",6.654,6.654,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1699 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|copy_history_acceptance_emits_across_page_and_tile_boundaries|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,integration,copy_history_acceptance_emits_across_page_and_tile_boundaries,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,2192,2384,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/copy.rs:198-470"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/transcript.rs:1-60""]","A 40x125 historic page is copied through the dashboard: the cursor walks rows 1-16 and columns 1-126, selection extends to row 17 columns 128-130, y emits exactly the expected OSC52 payload spanning page and tile boundaries, the notice appears, and moving the cursor after copy does not re-emit.","Cross-page/tile selection could produce truncated, duplicated or misaligned clipboard text, and copying could re-emit on cursor movement.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Truncated or duplicated clipboard text silently corrupts what the user pastes into another program (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/copy.rs:198-470).,Byte-exact OSC52 expectation computed with the production writer across row/col boundaries plus a post-copy no-reemit check (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2300-2380).,Only row covering copy across page and tile boundaries with byte-exact output (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2192-2384).,Real history rows over the server protocol and a real dashboard PTY emitting OSC52 (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2194-2230).,high,keep,Byte-exact cross-boundary assertion; retain.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|copy_mode_acceptance_emits_selected_text_and_reattaches|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default""]","[""outer PTY dashboard"", ""126 col moves"", ""40 history rows""]",9.574,9.574,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1703 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|copy_mode_acceptance_emits_selected_text_and_reattaches|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,integration,copy_mode_acceptance_emits_selected_text_and_reattaches,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,2601,2795,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/copy.rs:69-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/keymap.rs:419-500""]","Copy mode from Browse: help/close and form cancel preserve the live session snapshot; [gv then six l then y emits exactly the OSC52 payload for WAITING, Escape returns to Browse; input then reaches the session; after reattach the retained screen is copyable at the same pane coordinates, and F12 clears the startup note without entering Terminal mode.","Copy selections could capture the wrong cells or the reattached view could mis-map coordinates, producing wrong clipboard text; cancelling forms could disturb the session.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Wrong copy output silently pastes incorrect text into other applications (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/copy.rs:69-200).,"Exact OSC52 bases for two selections, screen-coordinate reconstruction after reattach, and session-text equality after cancels (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2605-2790).",Only row covering copy-mode coordinate mapping across detach/reattach (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2601-2795).,"Real dashboard PTY, real session screen and real OSC52 output (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2603-2640).",high,keep,Grounded coordinate/selection assertions with durable screen checks.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|copy_history_acceptance_emits_across_page_and_tile_boundaries|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|pause_resume_dashboard_round_trip|default""]","[""outer PTY dashboard"", ""detach/reattach"", ""OSC52 capture""]",5.070,5.070,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1700 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|history_keyboard_reads_old_output_during_live_session|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,integration,history_keyboard_reads_old_output_during_live_session,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,2009,2189,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1200-1320""]",A live session's history: PageUp freezes history and older rows become visible; live output arriving while frozen marks 'new output' without moving the frozen rows; a resize keeps the frozen rows and reflows the status; leaving history shows the live output again.,"Frozen history could shift or lose rows when new output arrives or the window resizes, so the user reads a corrupted transcript.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,A frozen history page that moves under the user corrupts the transcript they are reading (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/session/mod.rs:1065-1095).,"Asserts old rows plus the new-output marker after live output, their persistence across resize, a changed status line, and live output after exit (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2015-2185).",Only row covering history freeze under live output and resize through the dashboard (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2009-2189).,"Real PTY producing 100 rows, real dashboard PTY and FIFO-driven live output (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:2011-2040).",high,keep,Grounded frozen-history stability assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_reattach_reads_retained_output|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|history_frozen_page_survives_eviction_and_exit|default""]","[""outer PTY dashboard"", ""FIFO live output"", ""500ms retries""]",5.547,5.547,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1706 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
