nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|split_terminal_acceptance_preserves_input_and_geometry|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::terminal_acceptance,integration,integration,split_terminal_acceptance_preserves_input_and_geometry,default,tests/terminal_acceptance.rs,1831,2006,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:1-120""]","A two-pane split is driven through the real dashboard: both panes receive their own input and show their own acknowledgements, pane headers and separators follow focus, resizes to 100x30 and 80x30 then 120x40 change the children's reported sizes exactly, closing one pane removes the separator, and a reattach restores one pane then rebuilds the split with both children otherwise untouched (same pids).","Split input could be routed to the wrong pane, resize could resize the wrong PTY (or not resize), and closing/reattaching could restart sessions or leave stale separators.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Misdirected split input or wrong PTY geometry makes multi-pane work unusable and can corrupt an agent TUI (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:1-120).,"Child-reported stty sizes, per-rect content assertions, separator checks and pid stability across detach/reattach (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1835-2000).",Only row covering split geometry and input routing through the outer PTY with real children (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1831-2006).,"Real dashboard PTY, two real shells reporting kernel PTY sizes, real detach/reattach (tests/terminal_acceptance.rs:1833-1860).",high,keep,Grounded multi-pane geometry and identity assertions.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aserver_lifecycle|split_server_two_streams_resize_resync_and_detach|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aterminal_acceptance|history_keyboard_reads_old_output_during_live_session|default""]","[""outer PTY dashboard"", ""two real shells"", ""multiple resizes""]",5.765,5.765,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1723 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,lifecycle-terminal-acceptance-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_delegation%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_catalog_uses_effective_app_server_without_starting_a_thread|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,codex_delegation::tests::dashboard_catalog_uses_effective_app_server_without_starting_a_thread,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs,1034,1105,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:331-430"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:897-960""]","Against a fake codex that logs every argv and request, the dashboard catalog returns the exact model choice, runs the startup-config and app-server with exactly '-c features.plugins=false app-server --stdio', uses the canonical workspace as cwd, sends only initialize/initialized/account/gatewayOAuth/read/model/list, never thread/start or turn/start, requests explicitGatewayOauth, and asks model/list for non-hidden entries with limit 128.","A catalog that starts a Codex thread/turn (consuming a turn or creating conversation history in the user's account), or that drops the plugins=false override, the workspace cwd, or the explicit gateway capability.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"The probe must not create a Codex conversation or run a turn in the user's account (the test asserts no thread/start or turn/start, codex_delegation.rs:331-430); a regression performs hidden account side effects, C=3.","Exact argv for both invocations, canonical cwd, the full method sequence, the two forbidden methods, and two request parameters (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:1061-1104) reject every plausible protocol deviation.","The only test pinning the app-server conversation-free protocol sequence and its parameters; the sibling tests cover cleanup, cancellation and preconditions instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:331-430.","A fake codex executable that records the real argv/requests driven by production dashboard_catalog; the claim is OVRCR composition, so the fake provider is appropriate and cannot prove native acceptance (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/codex_delegation.rs:897-960.",high,keep,Decisive no-side-effect and exact protocol assertions over the real spawn path.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|codex_delegation%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_catalog_removes_residual_same_group_child_before_reaping_leader|default""]","fake codex script, real spawn and stdio protocol, files as records",0.359,0.359,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2365 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areadable_review_images_preserve_committed_staged_unstaged_untracked_deletion_modes_and_link|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,git::candidate::review::tests::readable_review_images_preserve_committed_staged_unstaged_untracked_deletion_modes_and_link,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs,91,161,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:4-46"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:79-85"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:462-505""]","A worktree with a committed candidate, staged, unstaged, untracked, deleted, mode-only and symlink changes yields seven review images; each live path carries the expected bytes and passes readable_image, the deleted path keeps its base preimage with mode 0 and no content, and re-parsing the snapshot after a later checkout edit returns the identical snapshot.","A review image missing a change class (so the reviewer never sees staged/untracked/deleted work), the wrong bytes for a path, or a snapshot that changes when the mutable checkout changes.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"These images are what a human approves (review.rs:4-46); a missing or wrong image means approving code that was never shown, an integrity failure at C=3.","Seven files are counted, five live images are byte-compared and re-validated, the deletion and mode pairs are asserted exactly, and the immutability re-parse (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:156-160) rejects late mutation.",The only end-to-end test covering all review image classes (committed/staged/unstaged/untracked/deletion/mode/symlink) at once; the exact-context test covers bounded collection of explicit paths instead. No counterpart test in the inventory; production surface: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate/review.rs:4-46.,"Real Git worktree from capture_fixture, real files/symlinks, production capture and readable_image (F=4). Exercised production path: crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git/candidate.rs:462-505.",high,keep,The strongest review-provenance test in the shard.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|git%3A%3Acandidate%3A%3Areview%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aexact_context_is_explicit_complete_bounded_and_never_reads_mutable_checkout|default""]","git worktree with seven file states, capture and re-parse",0.724,0.724,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2405 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|settings%3A%3Awrite%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aedits_refuse_dangling_links_and_read_only_targets_and_keep_links|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-runtime,lib,integration,settings::write::tests::edits_refuse_dangling_links_and_read_only_targets_and_keep_links,default,crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs,1073,1131,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:397-465"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:18-63""]","A symlinked document whose target is dangling is refused and the link kept; a read-only target is refused with bytes and 0444 mode intact; a writable symlink target is edited through the link, keeping the link and its 0640 mode, with other launch choices preserved.","Replacing the user's symlink with a regular file (breaking dotfile management), rewriting a read-only config, or chmod'ing the target.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Losing the symlink or rewriting a read-only target damages durable user configuration in ways the user did not request (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:397-465).,"Asserts read_link identity, target bytes, target mode 0444/0640 and exact file counts for four edit paths across both read-only states, then a successful through-link edit.",No other test covers symlink and read-only preservation in the writer (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/settings/write.rs:1073-1131).,Real symlinks and permission bits on a real filesystem through the production save().,high,keep,Only symlink/read-only fidelity coverage.,[],"[""nine real symlink fixtures with mode changes""]",0.020,0.020,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2812 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,runtime-storage-settings-tasks-003,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aagents%3A%3Atests%3A%3Amanaged_agents_launch_through_the_agent_run_route|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::agents::tests::managed_agents_launch_through_the_agent_run_route,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs,359,451,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-38"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:72-122"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:124-174""]","Every MANAGED_AGENTS name is launched as launcher agent run <name> -- <detected path>, with the provider auto-trust flag for claude/codex/pi/omp; gemini stays bare; without a launcher claude and codex are bare; explicit overrides keep their stored argv.",Wrapping an unmanaged agent or omitting the launcher changes who owns and reports the session; a wrong or missing auto-trust flag leaves the agent at its trust prompt or passes a flag it rejects; rebuilding an override into the wrapper loses the user's command. Rejected by exact argv per name.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"This routing is what gives a launched agent OVRCR ownership and reporting (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-38,72-122); losing it makes sessions unmanaged, a major workflow regression.","A complete invariant over all seven managed names with exact argv, plus unmanaged, no-launcher and override negatives. Assertion anchor: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:402-447.","Only test asserting the full managed set, the unmanaged exclusion, the no-launcher baseline and override preservation together. Surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:26-38.",Real temp executables through production detect_agents; the auto-trust flags come from the production apply_default_auto_trust call site (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/agents.rs:88-96).,medium,keep,Strongest agent-launch test in the suite; retained as the canonical managed-route check. Confidence is medium because the flag mapping inside apply_default_auto_trust was not opened.,[],"[""tempdir with eight chmod stubs""]",0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2905 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Aattention%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aa_new_unread_moves_no_row_under_the_pointer|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::attention::tests::a_new_unread_moves_no_row_under_the_pointer,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs,488,528,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:102-114"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/state.rs:2968-3043"", ""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/render.rs:428-520""]","With no strip, agent-6's row is at y; a Ready for session 6 inserts the strip, leaves every row above y byte-identical, keeps `✓ agent-6` on row y, and a click on y still focuses session 6.","Inserting the strip above the tree shifts rows so the pending click lands on a different session, which can invoke a destructive row action on the wrong session; the prefix comparison and post-click focus reject it.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"A row shifted under the pointer turns one click into an action on the wrong session (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:488-528), a wrong-target risk.","Compares the full rendered prefix before and after and verifies the click target identity, not just the strip text. Assertion anchor: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:497-527.",Only test of pointer/row stability under an asynchronous layout change. Surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:102-114.,Real 120x30 render plus production mouse_action dispatch. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/attention.rs:102-114.,high,keep,Strongest wrong-target protection in the attention suite; unique and precise.,[],"[""two TestBackend renders"", ""mouse event dispatch""]",0.082,0.082,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2909 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-001,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Adesktop%3A%3Atests%3A%3Abridge_reaped_client_failures_do_not_signal_its_former_process_group|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::desktop::tests::bridge_reaped_client_failures_do_not_signal_its_former_process_group,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs,4203,4366,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1183-1350""]","For an invalid-sound-status reply, invalid JSON and a nonzero exit, run_bridge returns Failed and, after the client has already been reaped, does not SIGKILL the former process group: a directly owned witness that joined that group survives and exits cleanly with no signal.","run_bridge killing a reaped client's former PID or process group, which can hit an unrelated process that reused the group after the client exited, possibly destroying someone else's work.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,A stale process-group SIGKILL is a wrong-target destructive action against unrelated processes (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:1330-1349); this is the only protection for that reap-versus-signal ordering.,"Asserts the witness joined the client group, the client reached its expected exit, and that the witness survived with exit code 0 and signal None for three failure shapes (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/desktop.rs:4203-4363).",Unique failure mode: no other reviewed test covers signalling after reaping. The FIFO gate makes the reap-before-cleanup ordering observable rather than assumed.,"The process-group ownership and reaping behaviour is the subject, and the test uses real spawned processes, a real FIFO gate, getpgid and libc signal checks, so the OS boundary is genuine even though the client is a shell script.",high,keep,"Decisive, unique protection for a destructive wrong-target signal; keep regardless of cost.",[],"[""mkfifo gate with nonblocking open"", ""spawned witness in the client process group"", ""libc getpgid and mkfifo"", ""thread::scope plus poll loops with HOST_TIMEOUT""]",0.469,0.469,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:2952 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-002,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Astatus%3A%3Atests%3A%3Areporting_words_start_then_settle_without_false_alarms|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::status::tests::reporting_words_start_then_settle_without_false_alarms,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs,869,944,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:97-315""]","Before the first report the header says 'starting…' until grace, then 'status off' if never bound; a bound unasked agent says nothing after grace; real losses say 'status off' immediately; a first report ends 'starting…'; legacy rollup counts; terminals never; no start time says 'status off'; paused says nothing.",A startup reported as a loss (false alarm) or a real reporter loss hidden behind 'starting…' misleads the user about the session's health.,3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Alert/status wording prevents false alarms and hidden losses (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:97-315); a wrong health signal is a major workflow misread.,"Long exact matrix over reasons, the grace boundary and phases (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:97-315).",Only startup/loss reporting-words test. Surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:97-315.,Pure production SessionStatus::of. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:97-315.,high,keep,Grounded reporting lifecycle; keep.,[],[],0.011,0.011,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3282 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-005,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Astatus%3A%3Atests%3A%3Astatus_table|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::status::tests::status_table,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs,654,863,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:62-315""]","Fifteen phase/snapshot cases assert glyph, color, activity clause, header state, narrow state, reporting, pid, exited flag and no internal words, and busy() equals spinner membership.","Any disagreement between glyph, picker clause, header and redraw cadence makes the user act on a wrong Waiting/Ready/Working state.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"The single status model drives glyphs, headers and redraw cadence (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:62-315); a wrong state is a major workflow misread.",Complete table with exact fields plus the busy/spinner cross-check (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:62-315).,Only full status matrix; narrower bodies cover specific clauses. Surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:62-315.,Pure production SessionStatus::of and busy. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/status.rs:62-315.,high,keep,Canonical status table; keep.,[],[],0.012,0.012,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3283 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-005,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Atests%3A%3Adashboard_reader_reconciles_two_pane_burst_at_ack_boundary|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,integration,dashboard::tests::dashboard_reader_reconciles_two_pane_burst_at_ack_boundary,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs,253,388,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377""]",Sixty-two output events while unready are ignored; two Screen responses populate both panes; without Ok panes remain unready and tail output is withheld; the next batch with Ok makes both ready and applies TAIL_A/TAIL_B.,"Applying output before the ack boundary renders stale bytes, and never becoming ready stalls the panes.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,Ack-boundary input correctness (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377); wrong screen bytes corrupt the terminal view. Impact surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377.,Exact screen contents and readiness before/after (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377). Assertion surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377.,Only two-pane burst at the ack boundary. Surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377.,"Real channels, UnixStream and parsers. Production surface: crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:377-377.",high,keep,Protects the ack boundary for two panes; keep.,[],"[""62 output messages"", ""two panes""]",0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3316 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-005,
nextest|Test|ovrcr-tui|dashboard%3A%3Atests%3A%3Apanic_hook_ignores_non_main_threads|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr-tui,lib,unit,dashboard::tests::panic_hook_ignores_non_main_threads,default,crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs,1577,1630,"[""crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:157-187""]","A panic on a background thread writes nothing to the terminal writer, while a panic on the thread that installed the hook emits leave-alternate-screen, show-cursor and keyboard-reporting restore sequences; the previous hook is reinstalled.","A background panic restoring the terminal while the main loop still draws (corrupted display), or a main-thread panic leaving the terminal in the alternate screen with echo off.",3,4,4,4,75,100,90,"An unrestored terminal after a crash makes the user's shell unusable (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs:1600-1628), the unusable-terminal class.","Asserts an empty buffer for the background panic, three exact restore sequences for the main-thread panic, and hook restoration (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/tests.rs:1591-1628).","Only reviewed test of the thread gate on the panic hook; the terminal_guard rows cover the restore sequences themselves, not which thread may use them (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:157-187).","Uses real panics, catch_unwind and the real process-global hook, which is the boundary under test (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:157-187).",high,keep,"Kept: criticality 3 and derived usefulness 100 do not meet the prune gate, and no test named in the uniqueness note covers the same assertion and input (crates/ovrcr-tui/src/dashboard/event_loop.rs:157-187).",[],"[""installs a process-global panic hook"", ""static mutex serializes hook tests in-process""]",0.014,0.014,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:3349 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,tui-library-006,
