node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|prepare-only%20registered%20start%20reserves%20without%20effects%20and%20recovers%20none%20Prepare%20loss|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,prepare-only registered start reserves without effects and recovers none Prepare loss,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,644,673,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","With loss none, a prepare_only start never makes a Launch or SendInitial call and returns Prepared with null session/run, idempotent on repeat, one Prepare per call with an identical contract and auth, and no prepare_only field in the canonical intent; a later prepare_only:false launches and sends exactly once.","If prepare_only ever reached Launch or SendInitial, a request that promised reservation would start a child and type the initial task; if the replay created a new contract, the reservation would not be idempotent.",4,4,3,3,100,85,91,"prepare_only is the reservation-only mode: a leaked Launch/SendInitial is a real child process and terminal input created by a call that explicitly promised no effects (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-496, 326-330).","It asserts zero Launch/SendInitial rows before the explicit resume, Prepared with null identity, idempotent duplicate equality, one Prepare per call with identical contract and auth, the absent prepare_only marker and exact single Launch/SendInitial after resume (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:644-673).","The no-loss row is distinct: the first prepare_only call succeeds, so it pins the immediate Prepared/null-identity response and the idempotent repeat without entering the Unknown recovery path (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:644-673). The two lost-Prepare executions are redundant with each other because the prepareOnly branch returns call({Prepare}) without any Reconcile (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:326-327), so this row is the trio's baseline rather than a third recovery state.","The real ovrcr_start callback, the real advance() and a real control child implement the Prepare state machine (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:326-350, 472-513).",high,keep,The reservation-without-effects invariant is decisive (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:644-673) and this execution is the only no-loss baseline; keep.,"[""node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|prepare-only%20registered%20start%20reserves%20without%20effects%20and%20recovers%20before%20Prepare%20loss|default""]",0.408s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.408,0.408,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 407.830708 at macOS-job.log:3999; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_delegation_extension.mjs|registered%20start%20rejects%20invalid%20action%20authority%20before%20intent%20or%20transport|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,node,integration,registered start rejects invalid action authority before intent or transport,default,tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs,137,202,"[""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:171-350"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-656""]","Seven action-authority shapes (read+result_file, read+write, empty, null, review/coding with wrong action sets) are Refused with the exactly-read or coding reason and no handle, receipt or parent-intents directory; prepare-only handle replays with any extra key and mixed handle+new-field calls are refused with zero launches.","If the action check passed read+write to a research assignment, the child would gain write authority the caller did not request; if a handle replay accepted extra keys, it could silently change the original contract.",4,4,3,3,100,85,91,"The permitted-actions check is the child's authority boundary: accepting write or check authority for a research assignment would let a read-only child modify the workspace, a destructive wrong-target action (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:478-490).","It asserts zero process launches, the refusal shape, the absence of any persisted intent directory, and the handle-replay key checks (tests/pi_delegation_extension.mjs:137-202).","The schema row asserts the declared schema; this row asserts the callback-level enforcement, which a schema-only regression leaves open; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-513, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real ovrcr_start callback runs with all child-process entry points counted and the real private-intent directory observed (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:472-513).,high,keep,Covers callback-level action authority enforcement with no-effects evidence; keep.,[],0.015s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.015,0.015,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 14.79775 at macOS-job.log:3939; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Extension%20tests|tests%2Fpi_package_bootstrap.mjs|injected%20initialization%20rejects%20an%20unbound%20relative%20helper%20binary%20before%20registration|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Extension tests,node-test,tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs,node,unit,injected initialization rejects an unbound relative helper binary before registration,default,tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs,84,95,"[""pi/extension.ts:1-6"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:33-93""]",initializeOvrcr with entry 'injected' and binary 'ovrcr' rejects with 'binary path is unavailable' before any pi.on/registerTool/registerCommand call.,"If a relative helper path were accepted, spawn() would resolve it through PATH (or the process cwd), so reporting could execute an unintended program instead of the supervising ovrcr binary.",4,4,3,3,100,85,91,"The binary is spawned with the session's capability frames; a PATH-resolved helper is an arbitrary-execution boundary and can leak reporting credentials to the wrong program (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:88-92, src/ovrcr-reporting-transport.mjs:82-86).","It asserts both the rejection message and zero registrations (tests/pi_package_bootstrap.mjs:84-95), so no partial handler set is installed before the throw.","No other test supplies a relative or NUL-bearing binary; the package rows never reach initializeOvrcr's injected branch; the handler it drives is src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:88-92, which no other reviewed case exercises.",The real initializeOvrcr guard runs with a fixture Pi API that counts every registration attempt (src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:88-92).,high,keep,Protects the helper-path authority check with a hard no-registration assertion; keep.,[],0.002s reported for this case; ordinary node:test case in the 'Extension tests' batch,0.002,0.002,1,0,hosted-single-run,TAP duration_ms 1.720417 at macOS-job.log:4167; run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Extension tests',extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
