nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Apublic_coding_replaced_parent_directory_preserves_containment_and_unrelated_work|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,coding::public_coding_replaced_parent_directory_preserves_containment_and_unrelated_work,default,tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs,1854,1956,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:150-175"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:150-260""]","Replaces the workspace-root directory with a different inode while a coding launch is pending, then recovers; asserts the created resource either stays contained under the canonical root with a matching git identity and one child/input, or is Refused with no child and no git change, while the original parent directory bytes/generation and repository HEAD remain unchanged.","A replaced parent directory letting coding creation escape the canonical root, or mutating the unrelated parent checkout and repository while launching.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,"A replaced parent directory letting coding creation escape the canonical root, or mutating the unrelated parent checkout and repository while launching; the canonicalize-and-equality containment check is at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:150-166.","The decisive assertion is the 'must not let creation escape its canonical root' check at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1912-1915, which rejects the wrong outcome rather than smoke-testing.","Compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Apublic_coding_same_path_repository_replacement_refuses_before_creation|default at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1750-1851, which does not exercise this boundary; the distinguishing assertion here is at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1912-1915.","The real boundary is constructed by tests/pi_delegation.rs:1509-1600 (fixture spawns the binary server and managed PTY/provider gates), with no stand-in for the subject.",high,keep,Kept: C=4 and the exact containment/no-effect assertions make this the only coverage of a replaced workspace root; production_refs were corrected to the check at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:150-175.,[],"[""real git worktrees"", ""isolated server + managed PTY"", ""filesystem polling""]",4.223,4.223,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1092 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-002,independent-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Apublic_coding_same_path_repository_replacement_refuses_before_creation|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,acceptance,coding::public_coding_same_path_repository_replacement_refuses_before_creation,default,tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs,1750,1851,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:1-120"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:150-260""]","Starts coding through a repository path that was replaced by a different clone with a different Git identity, then recovers; asserts Refused with no session, no coding worktree, unchanged worktree count and workspace inventory, unchanged original identity; a direct second start also refuses before a Prepare intent row or workspace effect exists.","A same-path repository swap being accepted so coding work and a candidate are created inside an attacker-controlled clone, or a refused prepare leaving a delegation row or worktree.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,"A same-path repository swap being accepted so coding work and a candidate are created inside an attacker-controlled clone, or a refused prepare leaving a delegation row or worktree. The consequence is enforced at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:1-120.","The decisive assertion is the 'must not create an assignment' check at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1791-1795, which rejects the wrong outcome rather than smoke-testing.","Compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|coding%3A%3Apublic_coding_replaced_parent_directory_preserves_containment_and_unrelated_work|default at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1854-1956, which does not exercise this boundary; the distinguishing assertion here is at tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1791-1795.","The real boundary is constructed by tests/pi_delegation.rs:1509-1600 (fixture spawns the binary server and managed PTY/provider gates), with no stand-in for the subject.",high,keep,"Grounded coverage of a durable authority, evidence, or dependency invariant; no equivalent retained test subsumes it and the usefulness is well above the prune gate.",[],"[""real git worktrees"", ""isolated server + managed PTY"", ""filesystem polling""]",4.476,4.476,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1098 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-002,independent-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|independent_review%3A%3Apublic_review_capacity_refusal_retries_one_fresh_seat_without_duplicate_team|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::pi_delegation,integration,integration,independent_review::public_review_capacity_refusal_retries_one_fresh_seat_without_duplicate_team,default,tests/pi_delegation/review.rs,725,727,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_review.rs:1-200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation_coding.rs:537-648""]","At the declared-policy capacity boundary, refuses a review start with retryable capacity and zero attempts and no child; after the ordinary occupant frees a slot, the retry is Applied at attempt 2 for the same task with unchanged contract bytes and limits, exactly one collected evidence entry names the retried reviewer, and a duplicate start from the original assignment is Refused.",A capacity refusal allocating a reviewer or a retry losing the authenticated view.,4,4,3,4,100,90,94,A capacity refusal allocating a reviewer or a retry losing the authenticated contract would break the delegation admission rule; the live-child and minimum-free-slot refusal is enforced at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1427-1440.,"Asserts Refused with retryable_capacity_refusal and zero attempts, retry Applied at attempt 2 with identical contract bytes, exactly one evidence entry with the retried reviewer identity, and a duplicate start Refused (tests/pi_delegation/review.rs:949-953, tests/pi_delegation/review.rs:980-982).","Compared with nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|independent_review%3A%3Apublic_review_direct_capacity_retry_preserves_original_readable_view_and_round|default at tests/pi_delegation/review.rs:730-732, which runs the direct branch and asserts the readable-view bytes; this execution covers the declared-policy evidence count and duplicate-team refusal, with distinguishing assertions at tests/pi_delegation/review.rs:949-953.","The real boundary is constructed by tests/pi_delegation/review.rs:1-275 (binary server, managed PTY, fault gates or git/review fixtures), not replaced by a stand-in.",high,keep,"Kept: the declared-policy capacity variant asserts a boundary the direct variant skips, at crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1427-1440; only the decisive-assertion citation and the behavior wording were corrected.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Api_delegation|public_pi_research_assignment_launches_collects_and_fences_real_child|default""]","[""real git worktrees"", ""real managed PTY"", ""SQLite triggers"", ""node hashing"", ""20s loops""]",14.661,14.661,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1181 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,public-delegation-003,independent-delegation-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|archive_round_trip_survives_restart_and_rejects_old_recovery_without_deleting_history|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,archive_round_trip_survives_restart_and_rejects_old_recovery_without_deleting_history,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,2329,2463,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:936-1015"", ""tests/support/live.rs:1-80""]","A closed live row is archived without killing its owned group in the record; legacy unfenced removal and pre-archive recovery are refused, the archive survives two restarts and offline reads, unarchive yields a stopped row, rename works offline, and provider history survives final removal.","An archive deleted by legacy removal, an old recovery token crossing unarchive, or offline inspection spawning a server.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,Archives hold the only record of stopped work; deleting or resurrecting one loses data and can launch a stale run (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:936-1015).,"Asserts the owned group is gone, the archive record is byte-equal across an offline read and two restarts, every stale request errors, unarchive starts no process, and the history file is intact (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2329-2463).",The offline archive plus unarchive fencing path is unique; the close-only test does not restart (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2306-2326).,"Real binary, real process groups, real socket presence and real files; the full lifecycle boundary is the subject (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:936-1015).",high,keep,"The broadest archive-integrity test, including offline reads and stale tokens.","[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|close_exited_row_moves_it_to_the_archive_without_process_acknowledgement|default""]","Two restarts, offline CLI reads and a process group",11.317,11.317,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1419 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-006,independent-integration-final-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|workspace_removal_blocks_live_and_uncertain_rows_and_preserves_records_on_failures|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::retained_sessions,integration,acceptance,workspace_removal_blocks_live_and_uncertain_rows_and_preserves_records_on_failures,default,tests/retained_sessions.rs,2019,2143,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/retained.rs:996-1035"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:2641-2670"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/git.rs:175-200""]","Removing a workspace is refused while live or archived-uncertain sessions name it, and dirty, locked, storage-preflight and commit failures leave the checkout and every session record intact, ending with the workspace marked unavailable.","A removal deleting the checkout or session records before a later step fails, or silently discarding an archived row's uncertainty.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,"Removing a workspace deletes the user's checkout and session records; a partial failure must never destroy data (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1990-2040,2641-2670).","Walks SessionsRemain (naming the archived row), DirtyWorktree, a locked worktree, an archive SQL failure and a commit failure, asserting the dirty file, path existence and session list equality at each stage (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2019-2143).",The failure-ordering matrix for workspace removal is unique; the provider-history and project-removal tests cover other guards (tests/retained_sessions.rs:2146-2303).,"Real binary, real SQLite triggers, real git worktree locks and real files; the destructive boundary is the subject (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/mod.rs:1990-2040).",high,keep,The only test proving preflight ordering and record preservation across removal failures.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aretained_sessions|workspace_removal_protects_provider_history_inside_an_ignored_directory|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aworkspace_identity|a_repository_root_cannot_be_removed_through_another_projects_workspace|default""]","Real SQLite schema triggers, git locks and two restarts",6.774,6.774,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:1436 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-006,independent-integration-final-check-1
