node-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|tests%2Fpi_child_tools_installed.mjs|production%20coding%20argv%20exposes%20child%20publishers%20in%20the%20installed%20effective%20catalog|production,cargo-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|ovrcr%3A%3Alib|coding%3A%3Aproduction_assignment_argv_preserves_installed_sdk_child_publication_tools|production,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Installed Pi effective child tools through production assignment argv,node-test,tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs,node,acceptance,production coding argv exposes child publishers in the installed effective catalog,production,tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs,20,66,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1490-1496"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:655-656""]","The production coding assignment argv parsed by the installed Pi SDK yields a nonempty --tools list and exactly one injected extension; loading it through the real DefaultResourceLoader registers ovrcr_publish and ovrcr_publish_question, and a real AgentSession exposes exactly read/grep/find/ls plus both publishers plus write/edit/bash, both active and configured, with no other ovrcr_ tool.","A coding child missing write/edit/bash or either publisher cannot do its work or deliver a result, and a tool outside the declared catalog that survives in the configured set could be activated by a later tool change and act with the child's delegation capability.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,"The effective catalog is the coding child's authority: it must be exactly read/grep/find/ls/write/edit/bash plus the two publishers, and an extra configured tool is a capability the installed host could later enable with the child's delegation credential (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1490-1496).","It asserts the active and configured name sets exactly against the real SDK's parseArgs and AgentSession, plus that the only ovrcr_ tools are the two publishers (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:47-65).","The coding variant asserts the coding extra permissions (write/edit/bash); the pair is the whole catalog contract, and the Rust parent only captures the argv and the 2/2 TAP receipt (tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1961-2048).","It runs the installed @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 0.87.1 parser, resource loader, settings manager and AgentSession over the production-materialized entry - the packaged boundary itself (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:10-46).",high,keep,Decisive packaged-boundary coverage of the coding child's authority set (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:47-65); keep.,"[""node-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|tests%2Fpi_child_tools_installed.mjs|production%20research%20argv%20exposes%20child%20publishers%20in%20the%20installed%20effective%20catalog|production""]",0.136s reported for this case; nested case whose runtime is included in the parent's reported duration (timing_source is the parent's TAP output),0.136,0.136,1,0,hosted-single-run,nested TAP duration_ms 135.685375 at macOS-job.log:4465 inside parent 'coding::production_assignment_argv_preserves_installed_sdk_child_publication_tools' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Installed Pi effective child tools through production assignment argv'),extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
node-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|tests%2Fpi_child_tools_installed.mjs|production%20research%20argv%20exposes%20child%20publishers%20in%20the%20installed%20effective%20catalog|production,cargo-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|ovrcr%3A%3Alib|coding%3A%3Aproduction_assignment_argv_preserves_installed_sdk_child_publication_tools|production,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Installed Pi effective child tools through production assignment argv,node-test,tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs,node,acceptance,production research argv exposes child publishers in the installed effective catalog,production,tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs,20,66,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1490-1496"", ""src/ovrcr-pi-runtime.ts:655-656""]","The production research assignment argv parsed by the installed Pi SDK yields a nonempty --tools list and exactly one injected extension; loading it through the real DefaultResourceLoader registers ovrcr_publish and ovrcr_publish_question, and a real AgentSession exposes exactly read/grep/find/ls plus both publishers, both active and configured, with no other ovrcr_ tool.","If the child boundary were wrong, a research child could write files or run bash, or the publisher tools could be missing so the child's result never reaches OVRCR; if a disallowed tool survived only in the configured set, a later tool change could re-enable it.",4,4,3,4,100,90,94,"The effective tool catalog is the child's authority over the workspace: for research it must be exactly the declared set, and research gaining write/bash is a destructive wrong-target capability (crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/delegation.rs:1490-1496).","It asserts the active and configured name sets exactly against the real SDK's parseArgs and AgentSession, plus that the only ovrcr_ tools are the two publishers (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:47-65).","The coding execution at the same body and range (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:20-66) asserts the coding extras write/edit/bash; this research execution asserts their absence, and the pair is the whole catalog contract while the Rust parent only captures the argv and requires the 2/2 TAP receipt (tests/pi_delegation/coding.rs:1961-2048).","It runs the installed @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 0.87.1 parser, resource loader, settings manager and AgentSession over the production-materialized entry - the packaged boundary itself (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:10-46).",high,keep,Decisive packaged-boundary coverage of the research child's authority set (tests/pi_child_tools_installed.mjs:47-65); keep.,"[""node-test|Installed%20Pi%20effective%20child%20tools%20through%20production%20assignment%20argv|tests%2Fpi_child_tools_installed.mjs|production%20coding%20argv%20exposes%20child%20publishers%20in%20the%20installed%20effective%20catalog|production""]",0.366s reported for this case; nested case whose runtime is included in the parent's reported duration (timing_source is the parent's TAP output),0.366,0.366,1,0,hosted-single-run,nested TAP duration_ms 366.265625 at macOS-job.log:4458 inside parent 'coding::production_assignment_argv_preserves_installed_sdk_child_publication_tools' (run 42429838269 job 128576086691 step 'Installed Pi effective child tools through production assignment argv'),extensions-installed-pi-001,independent-extensions-check-1
