nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_output_does_not_contain_a_fixture_credential|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::claude_quota_probe,integration,acceptance,claude_probe_output_does_not_contain_a_fixture_credential,default,tests/claude_quota_probe.rs,617,658,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota_probe.rs:214-270"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/quota.rs:1374-1397""]","Runs an isolated HOME with a credentials file and the probe enabled, accumulates every QuotaChanged snapshot as Debug text, then asserts that the accumulated events, the server log and the final snapshot together contain no occurrence of the fixture bearer token.","The bearer token reaching Server output, events or logs, which would disclose a provider credential to any dashboard reader or log consumer.",4,4,4,3,100,95,97,"This is a credential disclosure boundary: the probe reads a bearer token and must never publish it, even in Debug-formatted events.","Positive proof that the probe produced a Current Probe-sourced row, then a single substring scan over the full accumulated event text, the server log and the snapshot.",Only credential-leak assertion on the probe path; row 62 covers the account-read path.,"Real server, real probe PTY and real credentials file; the provider and usage endpoint are fixtures, appropriate for the claim.",high,keep,Credential-exposure invariant with a whole-output scan; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|claude_probe_off_allows_an_account_read_without_spawning_a_probe|default"", ""nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Aclaude_quota_probe|a_live_managed_claude_session_suppresses_the_probe|default""]","[""isolated HOME fixture"", ""probe PTY plus loopback usage server"", ""3.32 s observed""]",3.318,3.318,1,0,hosted-single-run,evidence/macos-job.log:738 (PASS attempt 1); run 42429838269 job 128576086691,other-rust-integration-001,independent-integration-check-1
nextest|Test|ovrcr%3A%3Acodex_initial_prompt|codex_harness_default_and_explicit_prompt_use_the_shared_lifecycle_and_privacy_path|default,,992a1da5c59a865ebb48051e4d9d8ff7184c8dc5,Test,nextest,ovrcr::codex_initial_prompt,integration,acceptance,codex_harness_default_and_explicit_prompt_use_the_shared_lifecycle_and_privacy_path,default,tests/codex_initial_prompt.rs,322,506,"[""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/lifecycle.rs:130-235"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/connections.rs:1170-1200"", ""crates/ovrcr-runtime/src/server/agent_models.rs:1-120""]","Allocates a blank prompt intent and creates a harness-default session, then queries models, allocates an explicit-model intent with a multi-line private prompt, and asserts exact captured argv for both launches, intent snapshot/ack ordering, reconcile after dashboard reconnect returning the same snapshot, replay returning the same session/run with no third native process, and the prompt appearing in no settings, session metadata, events or database bytes.","The initial prompt being written to settings, metadata, events or SQLite (a durable privacy breach), the model policy not reaching argv, or an accepted intent replaying or creating a second process.",4,4,4,3,100,95,97,The prompt is private conversation content and this path guarantees it is not persisted; leaking it into the registry or events is durable exposure.,"Four independent storage scans (settings, inventory JSON, events JSON, raw database windows) plus argv block counts and replay identity cover both privacy and lifecycle.",Only initial-prompt lifecycle test; agent_models unit tests cover argv composition without intents or storage scans.,"Real server, dashboard protocol and a fake codex app-server; the lifecycle and storage are production code.",high,keep,Privacy invariant with raw-storage evidence plus exact replay semantics; keep.,"[""nextest|Test|ovrcr-runtime|server%3A%3Aagent_models%3A%3Atests%3A%3Aharness_default_preserves_the_complete_selected_launche